    ],
    "title": "**Task 1** (step 13)",
    "text": "**Task 1** (step 13): the Slice 1 checklist above, end to end.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Task 2** (step 14)",
    "text": "**Task 2** (step 14): (a) two blocks with an identical fresh path in the same doc are rejected, (b) a new block colliding with another live block's current `toPath()` is rejected, (c) a new block colliding with another live block's still-embedded anchor name is also rejected, (d) no false positive when paths are genuinely distinct.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Task 3** (step 15)",
    "text": "**Task 3** (step 15): deleting an anchor tag from a block's source text and re-ingesting drops it from `treeAnchor`/the graph, with no other block affected; a full-text safety search catches an old-style reference living in a file that isn't tracked/ingested, a case `kg:backlinks` alone misses.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ77F800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
