    "title": "00CDGTZHSR005",
    "text": "Cross-package imports go through each package's own `exports` map (`\"./*\": \"./src/*.ts\"`), not relative dot-paths — `import ... from '@aperas/core/apeironNgn/node'` instead of `'../apeironNgn/node'` — resolved by npm workspace symlinking, the same subpath shape the code already uses today, so the rewrite is a mechanical prefix swap, not a redesign. Root `package.json` no longer carries the old `kg:*` script names: once the `aperas` dispatcher (see [Architecture](#id/BlockNode:00CDDVBXHG005)) covered every verb through the same `run*`/`request()` calls the old scripts used, `npm run kg:X -- <args>` and `npm run aperas -- X <args>` were doing identical work, so the older aliases were dropped rather than kept indefinitely. The dogfooding workflow is `npm run aperas -- <verb> <args>` in a source checkout and the built `aperas <verb>` once installed — one command surface in dev and in production, not two. Two unused dependencies (`terminusdb`, `rehype-stringify`/`remark-rehype` — confirmed zero references anywhere in `src/`) are dropped rather than assigned to any package.",
