    "title": "`aperas service stop` (added afterward, on request)",
    "text": "`aperas service stop` (added afterward, on request): the explicit, graceful counterpart to finding the service's pid and `kill`-ing it by hand — same SIGTERM-and-wait `restart` already used as its own first half, factored out into a shared `stopIfRunning()` so `stop` and `restart` share one implementation. A no-op (with a status line) if nothing's running.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDXFWK3R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
