    ],
    "title": "**`aperas unfold` doesn't mark tombstoned children; both `unfold` and `tree` should hide them by default**",
    "text": "**`aperas unfold` doesn't mark tombstoned children; both `unfold` and `tree` should hide them by default**: `aperas tree --view <name>` appends a `(tombstoned)` suffix to a tombstoned node's line; `aperas unfold` showed the identical node with no marker at all, indistinguishable from a live sibling — confirmed live, see [Discussion](../discussion/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE8T49MR001). Proposed direction: don't just bring `unfold` in line with `tree`'s tag — suppress tombstoned nodes from both commands' default output, and add a `--tombstoned` flag to opt into seeing them. **Resolved exactly as proposed**: `TreeOptions.showTombstoned` (default `false`) gates every renderer — `kg:tree`'s plain and view-based paths, and `kg:unfold`'s own separate preview path — hiding a tombstoned node and its subtree entirely by default, tagged `(tombstoned)` only with `--tombstoned`. `kg:unfold` additionally refuses to unfold a tombstoned node directly without the flag, rather than returning something misleadingly empty. Verified live and in `verify.ts`. See [Discussion](../discussion/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE8T49MR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW63800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
