  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Implementation Plan",
    "text": "Restructure in place rather than rewriting from a blank file. Every existing item was paid for by a live incident, so the content is the asset and the arrangement is the defect — a fresh draft would silently drop hard-won specifics that no one would notice missing until the incident recurred.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8003",
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEA5M6S8003",
    "text": "The verbatim copy already dumped into the discussion doc is the working surface for the rewrite: each item is an addressable block, so the reorganisation can be discussed and tracked by citing blocks rather than line numbers in a file that is about to move.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004:links:Link:00CEA6RAGR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8004:links:Link:00CEA6RAGR000:props:StringProp:00CEA6RAGR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "114"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CEA5M6S8004",
    "text": "Order matters. The level assignment comes first and everything else follows from it, because an item's level (see [Architecture](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG003)) determines both where it lands and how it gets reworded — the same fact stated as philosophy and as mechanics is not the same sentence.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Task Breakdown",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
      "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG003",
      "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XR000",
      "BlockNode:00CR3XQKNG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006:props:StringProp:00CEA5M7QR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006:props:StringProp:00CEA5M7QR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8006:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDHR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS8002",
    "text": "Assign every one of the eighteen existing items to a level — philosophy, orientation, discipline, or mechanics — by asking what explains it, not where it was first noticed. Items that split across levels get split.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8007:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDHR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS8003",
    "text": "Restate the philosophy and orientation levels from the settled framing, so they read as the cause of what follows rather than as two more rules.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8008:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJ0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS8004",
    "text": "Rewrite each remaining item rule-first, with its originating incident attached rather than leading.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8009:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJ0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Mark every item's status explicitly where it stands",
    "text": "Mark every item's status explicitly where it stands: confirmed-current, superseded by a landed change, or unverified.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800A:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJ0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS8006",
    "text": "Harvest an example for each level in the kind that level takes — a contrast pair for philosophy, a traversal transcript for orientation, one full worked loop for discipline, a command plus its exact failure text for mechanics. Draw every one from a real recorded incident; synthesise nothing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800B:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJ0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS8007",
    "text": "Extract accumulated tool gaps out of the prose into tracked issues in the graph, leaving the skill with a pointer rather than a growing caveat list.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800C:props:StringProp:00CFAFGDJ8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "true"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CFAFGBS8008",
    "text": "Decide the scope boundary against `kg-doc-ingest` and against concern docs, and state it in the skill itself.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CFAMC7XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Verification Plan",
    "text": "The rewrite succeeds if an agent reading only the first two levels behaves correctly in the ordinary case — graph-first, traversal-first — without having reached any mechanics.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800E",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0001",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0002",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0003",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY0004",
      "BlockNode:00CEDFCMY8000",
      "BlockNode:00CFANC9KR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CEA5M6S800E",
    "text": "Two concrete checks, both available from this corpus rather than from judgement alone. First, every incident already recorded in this concern's discussion should be predictable from a statement at the philosophy or discipline level; one that isn't marks a gap at that level, not a missing gotcha. Second, the grep-instead-of-traverse failure specifically should be prevented by something a reader meets before any CLI verb appears, since that failure happened to a reader who had the rule available and still did not apply it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5M6S800D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
