        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CG9MPGVG001",
    "text": "**The provenance obligation is scoped to promotion, so a claim added to an entry already in place carries no source**: *Promotion links at the origin* describes the failure exactly — a formal entry paraphrasing a confirmed finding without linking it, complete-looking from its own side, with `aperas backlinks` returning nothing — but scopes itself to the moment a finding crystallizes up out of `discussion`. An edit that adds supporting evidence to an entry already in the doc is not a promotion, and nothing else in the skill covers it. Confirmed live: `planning/aperas-skill.md`'s trigger-accuracy item was edited to cite three recorded observations and came out with `links: 0`, caught only when a reader ran `backlinks` on it. The same uncovered gap let through two claims that were wrong in kind rather than merely unsourced — a version label inferred and written as recorded, and a task shape quoted as though it were a labelled prompt. Note this is [\"The skill states the citation-direction constraint but never the obligation that follows from it\"](#id/BlockNode:00CEA5Y5JG00J) resurfacing one case over, since that fix was scoped to the incident which produced it; and that the underlying notion is older than either — `archive/Aperas-design.md` defines deep read as provenance projection, a definition `SKILL.md` did not carry across. **Resolved in v1.4**: the rule is now *Every claim carries its source*, stated as a property of the claim rather than a step in the promotion ritual, requiring `aperas backlinks` to be run on what was just written, and grounded in the new Philosophy statement that a claim and its provenance are one object.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CG9X6PPG000",
