            "value": "61"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Discipline — identity preservation restated outcome-first",
    "text": "Supersedes: [the v1 move rule](#id/BlockNode:00CF46W4QR009), [its remove+insert caveat](#id/BlockNode:00CF46W4QR00A)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G000",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G004",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G005",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G000",
    "text": "[current] Stated by outcome, not by verb, because three different calls reach the same destruction and only one of them looks like a delete:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8800P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G001",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G002",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G001:props:StringProp:00CGA4ZQ1G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G001:props:StringProp:00CGA4ZQ1G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G001",
    "text": "`remove` + `insert` — the obvious one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G002",
    "text": "`aperas update` on a **parent heading** — reconciliation tombstones and remints the subtree as a *side effect*; nothing in the intent resembles deleting, and the word `remove` is never typed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G003",
    "text": "a full-list push whose items **change depth** — matching is defeated entirely, so every id is recreated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G004",
    "text": "`aperas insert <node-id> --after/--before <anchor>` with **no stdin piped** repositions that exact node — the anchor's current parent becomes its new parent, cross-parent moves included. It preserves the id, every backlink to it, and its place in history. Reach for anything else only when the wording is changing enough that it is genuinely not the same item any more — and even then, a move followed by a separate `--text-only` edit keeps the id while changing only what actually changed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8800P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G005",
    "text": "Zero backlinks is not a licence. The rule also protects a node's place in history, which backlink count has no bearing on.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8800P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Caught live twice",
    "text": "Caught live twice: promoting two findings into a new section via `remove` + `insert` left two needlessly tombstoned orphans for a relocation a plain move would have handled with zero churn; and regrouping a flat 17-item list under three new sub-headings as a single parent-heading `update` returned `0 matched, 20 added, 17 removed`. Redone as create-headings-with-anchors, then move each item, then set the run-leader props per batch — all 17 ids survived. See *Adding an item to an existing list* (Mechanics) for the matching promise this rule constrains.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8800P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007:links:Link:00CGRVD1DG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CF46W4QR00D",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007:links:Link:00CGRVD1DG000:props:StringProp:00CGRVD1DG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007:links:Link:00CGRVD1DR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CF46W4QR00E",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007:links:Link:00CGRVD1DR000:props:StringProp:00CGRVD1DR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "71"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Discipline — promotion links become every claim carries its source",
    "text": "Supersedes: [the v1 promotion corollary](#id/BlockNode:00CF46W4QR00D), [its do-it-at-promotion-time line](#id/BlockNode:00CF46W4QR00E)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G008",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G009",
      "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G00A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G008",
    "text": "[current] Philosophy's evidence rule, as something to do. Before leaving any text in a formal doc — `issues`, `design`, `planning`, `history` — check that each claim in it can be traced: provenance first, and every other relationship the text carries alongside it, each reified as a real link rather than described in prose. Then run `aperas backlinks <id> --text` on **what you just wrote**, not only on what you are about to read. A node whose claims rest on nothing returns nothing, and that silence is the entire signal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G009",
    "text": "Direction decides which end the link lives at, never whether it exists. When a finding crystallizes *up* out of `discussion` into `issues`/`design`/`planning`/`history`, the new entry cannot cite the discussion entry it came from — that is a down-citation. So the link is added at the **origin** instead: the discussion entry gains \"promoted to `issues/<concern>.md`\" with a real wikilink, pointing up. The provenance then surfaces from the new entry's side for free, as a backlink.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CGA4ZN8G00A",
    "text": "**This is a property of the claim, not a step in the promotion ritual**, and reading it as the latter is a live failure mode. An edit that adds supporting evidence to an entry already sitting in the doc is not a promotion, so a version of this rule scoped to promotions never reaches it. Caught live: a planning entry was edited to cite three recorded observations and came out with `links: 0` — complete-looking from its own side, caught only when a reader ran `backlinks` on it. The same unguarded gap passed an inferred version number written as recorded fact, and a paraphrase set in quotation marks as though it were a logged prompt. Every mechanical check in this file passed on that edit; all of them ask whether the write landed, none asks whether what was written is true.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Mechanics — show_node.py reads the on-disk mirror",
    "text": "It reads the **on-disk mirror**, so after an unflushed mutation it reports pre-flush state while `aperas unfold`/`tree` report the live service's. Flush first, or ask the CLI, when checking something you just changed. Caught live: a move and a tombstone were both invisible to it, producing a confident and wrong conclusion that the move had gone backwards.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN8G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Mechanics — the exact-key-matching promise gets its precondition",
    "text": "**That promise holds only while every item keeps its parent and its depth** — a precondition this section used to state unconditionally, which is exactly how it got read as licence for a restructure. A push that moves items to a new depth, regrouping a flat list under fresh sub-headings say, matches nothing and recreates everything; use moves for that instead (see *Preserve identity*, Discipline).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA5Y2P8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA5Y2P8001:links:Link:00CGA5Y4JG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA5Y2P8001:links:Link:00CGA5Y4JG000:props:StringProp:00CN3ZT1C0000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "844"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**v1.4 — rules re-keyed to outcomes, after the same defect produced three separate failures in one session**",
    "text": "**v1.4 — rules re-keyed to outcomes, after the same defect produced three separate failures in one session**: with v1.3's description finally firing on turn one, a session loaded the skill, consented to it, and still read an entire task out of the projections before editing code — so the trigger was never the last problem. Three rules failed in the same shape, each keyed to the operation that first surfaced it rather than to the result it was guarding: orientation keyed to \"editing the graph\" never fired for a read, identity preservation keyed to `remove` never fired for a parent-heading `update` that tombstoned seventeen nodes, and the provenance obligation keyed to \"promotion\" never fired for an edit adding evidence to an entry already in place. Recorded as [the v1.4 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88001), and nine issues moved to Resolved with their mechanisms named. The load-bearing addition is a Philosophy statement the founding design always implied and the skill had never carried: Aperas is an evidence-based documentation system, a claim and its provenance are one object — `archive/Aperas-design.md` defines deep read as provenance projection, while `SKILL.md` had reduced backward traversal to context and blast radius and used the word \"evidence\" exactly once, about something else. Notable for how it was caught: not by any check in the file, all of which passed, but by a reader running `aperas backlinks` on a claim and getting nothing back.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA8YGW8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA8YGW8001:links:Link:00CGRV9D30000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CGA4ZN88003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CGA8YGW8001:links:Link:00CGRV9D30000:props:StringProp:00CGRV9D30001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Top matter — Status line compacted, version rationale left to Discussion",
