    "title": "00CGG7BN40001",
    "text": "**Two approved engine fixes, plus a graph-repair sweep, following the v2 skill review**: (1) `astParser.ts` never stripped an inline `aperas-anchor` tag before storing a paragraph/listItem's `text` — `stripInlineAnchors` only ran at *comparison* sites (`reconcile.ts`'s `leafKey`, rename matching), never at the one place `block.text = text` is actually set. Copying an already-projected file's content back through `update`/`insert` therefore baked the anchor into stored text permanently, even though `hasIdAnchor`'s idempotency check kept the *rendered* output looking unchanged. Fix: wrap that single assignment in `stripInlineAnchors`, symmetric to how a heading already strips its own trailing anchor structurally at parse time. This retires `SKILL.md`'s \"never copy from an already-projected file\" caution as a fact about the engine rather than a rule to remember. (2) `findLeadInColonOffset` applies `MAX_LEAD_IN_WORDS`/`MAX_LEAD_IN_CHARS_JA` to the *entire* span before the accepted colon, bold text included — so a legitimate `**Bold Term**:` lead-in longer than the cap silently fails and the block's title falls back to its own raw id. Confirmed on real nodes from this session: `BlockNode:00CG9MDJF0001` (20-word bold lead-in) and `BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG003` (13 words), both showing their bare id as title in every `tree`/`unfold`/`backlinks` preview. Fix: when the text immediately preceding the candidate colon is *entirely* inside a single bold/strong span (nothing else before it), accept it unconditionally — no length cap; the cap continues to gate only the plain, non-bold colon heuristic, where a colon reached after a long run of ordinary prose is genuinely ambiguous. (3) Sweeping for the same pre-fix \"wikilink never resolved\" staleness [an old `discussion/linking.md` entry names](../discussion/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1276D0001) — `resolveBlockLinks` used to run only from `kg:ingest`, not `kg:update`/`kg:insert` — found 20 live nodes graph-wide still carrying a resolvable `](...#...)` link with empty `.links`, all predating that fix. Confirmed the remedy is just re-touching each one (`aperas update <id>` piping its own unchanged text back) under the now-fixed code; done for `issues/core.md`'s Sub-Parts list (3 nodes, including the one that had left [issues/linking.md's Open Issues](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV5A8002) without an incoming link). The other 17 (mostly `discussion/aperas-skill.md`'s own frozen verbatim snapshots, plus a few in `linking`/`documentation`/`packaging`) are left for a separate pass — touching a snapshot's links doesn't touch its text, but it's a broader sweep than this task asked for.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ37GPRR009",
