    "title": "**Tier 1 — silent corruption on ordinary writes, highest priority**",
    "text": "**Tier 1 — silent corruption on ordinary writes, highest priority**: [`aperas update` never re-derives a non-heading title, and can tombstone real children as a side effect](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGFE4SV0002) — proven live this session, not hypothetical, and hits the single most common write (`update` on a leaf). [A parent-heading list-push reassigns live content onto the wrong id once a tombstoned sibling is interleaved](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG003) and [`update`'s reconciliation can silently match fresh content onto an already-tombstoned id without reviving it](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG004) — both live in the same matching machinery (`diffChildren`'s `matchKeyed`/`gestaltMatchingBlocks`), and the first item's own text already notes \"one fix in `reconcile.ts` likely closes\" both of these plus [item 3](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG005) — meaning a single fix here has 3x leverage, the highest of anything reviewed. **Misplaced on first pass, moved up here after direct diagnosis**: [the GFM task-list marker leak](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1GW638007) was filed in Tier 5 as \"likely non-reproducible\" — it reproduces every time a checkbox's content doesn't start with plain text (bold, italic, code, or a link lead-in all qualify), and it silently bakes the leftover marker into stored `.text` as literal prose on an ordinary `update`/`insert`, exactly the same failure shape as the rest of this tier: a write that looks clean and corrupts content nobody asked it to touch. Confirmed live on this session's own plan checkboxes before being caught.",
