    "title": "**Tier 1/2/3 fix plan — six issues, approved to implement now**",
    "text": "**Tier 1/2/3 fix plan — six issues, approved to implement now**: investigated all six down to the exact mechanism before writing this. One finding changes the record: [issues/core.md#1's root-cause note](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG003), added earlier this session, was **wrong** — it blamed `diffChildren`'s `matchKeyed`/`gestaltMatchingBlocks` (Stage A, leaf-only), but `listItem` is a `CONTAINER_TYPE`, not a `LEAF_TYPE`, so it never goes through Stage A at all. The real mechanism is Stage B's per-type container alignment, which zips old/new by raw array position with **zero content comparison** — confirmed by direct reproduction (a 4-item list, item 2 tombstoned-but-present, piped without it: item 3's content lands on item 2's dead id, item 4's content lands on item 3's id, item 4's real id gets tombstoned — a full one-slot cascade). That note was corrected as part of item 2, moved with the rest of this checklist below. The seven items themselves, and their execution order, moved wholesale into [planning/core.md's Archive](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XP4XK0001) as its own [Batch 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CGK2C16G001) — that doc already tracked this exact reconcile-fix effort, sketched before `reconcile.ts` was actually read and never followed as written, so the old sketch was retired (tombstoned, kept for history) rather than reconciled line-by-line against what actually happened. This entry keeps only the investigation reasoning that led here.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
