    "title": "**2. Stage B's container alignment is positional, not content-keyed — the real cause of [core.md #1](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG003) and [#2](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG004)**",
    "text": "**2. Stage B's container alignment is positional, not content-keyed — the real cause of [core.md #1](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG003) and [#2](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG004)**: fix by keying `listItem`-typed buckets through the same `matchKeyed`+`leafKey` machinery Stage A already uses for leaves, instead of a plain `Math.min(old.length, new.length)` zip — reproduced above, a real diff not a hypothetical. Alongside it: exclude every tombstoned old candidate from every matching pool (Stage A's `oldLeafIdx`/heading buckets *and* Stage B's container buckets) — today nothing stops live new content being matched onto an already-dead id without reviving it (core.md #2's exact complaint), and it turns out Stage A has the identical exposure for headings/paragraphs, not only Stage B for list items. A dead slot should never be reused; new content lands on a fresh id instead. Corrects the wrong root-cause note above once landed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGK2C16G001",
