    ],
    "title": "**5. Multi-artifact `kg:ingest` isn't transactional** ([issues/core.md](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG008))",
    "text": "**5. Multi-artifact `kg:ingest` isn't transactional** ([issues/core.md](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG008)): `ingestArtifacts`/`ingestAllArtifacts` loop per file with no try/catch, so one file's failure mid-batch leaves earlier files' writes already committed with no rollback, and later files never attempted. True all-or-nothing would need a store-wide snapshot/rollback primitive that doesn't exist here — a bigger undertaking than this item's scope. Chosen design instead: isolate per file, matching the pattern `ingestAllArtifacts` already uses for `untracked` — wrap each `ingestArtifact` call in try/catch, collect `{path, error}` for failures, keep going, return successes *and* failures both, so a bad file no longer silently aborts every file after it in the same batch, and the caller gets an accurate report instead of a mid-loop throw. Flagging this design choice explicitly since a true-rollback alternative existed and wasn't picked.",
