    "title": "**Tier 4/5 fix plan — approved to implement now**",
    "text": "**Tier 4/5 fix plan — approved to implement now**: every genuine code-level item in Tiers 4-5 investigated and fixed. `matchLeftoverByAbstract`'s position-sensitivity and the dead-container-never-tombstoned gap (Tier 4) were already tracked as [planning/core.md's Batch 2](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CGK3AH60001), now done. Insert always spawning a fresh run-leader (Tier 4) had no plan anywhere — designed and fixed, see [issues/list-consumption.md](../issues/list-consumption.md#id/BlockNode:00CE32GRZG002). The four `treeview` Tier 5 items (unfolds staleness, bare-unfold mutation, no raw inspection command, unfold's missing tombstone marker) are all done — see [planning/treeview.md's Task Breakdown](../planning/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1GW7CG003), which also picked up two items that were never actually tracked there before (the tombstone-hide-by-default direction, and `aperas show`, both scoped and built in this same batch). The two `archive-migration` Tier 5 items are process/decision notes with nothing to implement, left as-is. Two unplanned findings surfaced while doing this bookkeeping, not part of the original Tier 4/5 scope: `issues/core.md`'s and `issues/linking.md`'s own `ArtifactNode` titles had been silently corrupted by `aperas update`'s non-heading title re-derivation (added earlier this session) never excluding artifact-root targets — root-caused, fixed, and both instances repaired; see [issues/core.md](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CGM54FX0001). A pre-existing, unrelated `verify.ts` failure (Slice 1's own anchor-emission check, \"re-projecting an already-anchored list item to not duplicate its id-anchor\") was also found still failing on a clean checkout with none of this batch's changes applied — not investigated further, flagged here rather than left silent.",
