    "title": "**Link integrity is now a standing, three-layer check, not a one-time hand sweep**",
    "text": "**Link integrity is now a standing, three-layer check, not a one-time hand sweep**: a per-write sweep after every `update`/`insert`/`remove`, a corpus-wide sweep at startup and on `reload`, and an end-of-batch sweep folded into the skill's own discipline. See [issues/linking.md](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGN6GJVG000) for the mechanism and Freeflow below for how it was built. All three report; none repairs automatically — `aperas check-links --repair` stays a manual step.",
