    "title": "00CJ3E5ER0001",
    "text": "**`check-links --repair` is not the safe recovery path its own design assumed — confirmed live, twice, while editing this very doc.** Editing [`BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001`](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CGMWQ6T0001) (the \"Links silently fail...\" parent item) with `update --text-only` — an edit to an *ancestor*, touching no link-bearing text directly — dropped `.links` from its own two just-repaired children, reproducing item (3)'s exact symptom live, in real time, while writing item (3) up. Running `check-links --repair` on the resulting 2 discrepancies then made things dramatically worse: discrepancies went from 2 to **16**, spanning nearly every link-bearing block in `issues/linking.md`. Root cause traced directly in `linkIntegrity.ts`/`artifacts.ts`: `repairLinkIntegrity` correctly scopes `pendingLinks` to only the *named* discrepant blocks (the fix already recorded in [issues/linking.md](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CHYM4Z1G001)'s Resolved section), but still builds `oldWikilinksByBlock` from the *whole artifact* via `collectOldWikilinksByBlock(artifactNode, ...)`. `resolveBlockLinks`'s own block-iteration loop unions `codesByBlock.keys()` with `oldWikilinksByBlock.keys()` — so every link-bearing block in the artifact gets reprocessed, but any block *not* in the narrower `pendingLinks` set has no codes to resolve and ends up with `block.links = undefined`, wiping correct links wholesale. The 00CHYM4Z1G001 fix narrowed one side of this pair and not the other, so the \"re-mints every id\" symptom it actually fixed was replaced by a strictly worse \"wipes every other block's links\" symptom, undetected until now because no prior repair happened to touch an artifact with other untouched link-bearing content nearby. Recovered by hand: the 2 originally-dropped links were restored via per-block `update --text-only` (which scopes correctly, per `kgUpdate.ts`'s own `collectOldWikilinksByBlock(target, ...)` call against the single target rather than the whole artifact) rather than `--repair`; a first restore attempt using a carelessly-captured shell pipe (a stray `> tsx ... --text` header line surviving into the piped content) additionally corrupted 16 blocks' own `.text` by parsing that header line as a blockquote — caught by comparing every restored block byte-for-byte against a pre-session dump, and fixed by removing the 32 spurious children and re-piping verified-clean text. Not yet fixed in code — reported, not repaired, pending the user's decision on the fix.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGMX88R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Q48PR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ3Q48PR000:props:StringProp:00CJ3Q4B2R000",
