    "title": "**No safe, identity-preserving rename primitive exists for an ArtifactNode**",
    "text": "**No safe, identity-preserving rename primitive exists for an ArtifactNode**: scoped `kg:ingest --track <paths>` doesn't rename at all — it just creates a fresh ArtifactNode and orphans the old one, live but detached from the tree; the only real Gestalt-match rename detection lives in the full, path-less corpus sweep, which has no `archive/` exclusion and aborts on the first pre-existing collision it finds there. See [Incident: artifact rename has no working path yet](#id/BlockNode:00CDEB141G001) below. The later `cli-packaging.md` → `packaging.md` rename that did succeed used a manual multi-step recipe (retitle each H1 directly, fix each cross-reference bullet one at a time, then `git mv` + scoped `--track`), not this primitive — so the underlying gap is still open even though a workaround exists.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ5ET5Z8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ5FATY8002",
