      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG006:props:StringProp:00CJ6TGT10001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The webapp is a third thin wrapper over `@aperas/core`**",
    "text": "**The webapp is a third thin wrapper over `@aperas/core`**: the UI-projection tier, alongside `cli` and anticipated by name in [cli's settled scope](../discussion/cli.md#id/BlockNode:00CF2AEMER007). It owns presentation and interaction, not graph semantics — every rule it renders (fold tiers, canonical position, zoom) is computed in core and consumed here.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The ApeironNgn service remains the sole writer**",
    "text": "**The ApeironNgn service remains the sole writer**: the webapp never opens the store, reaching the graph only through the service, which keeps single-writer discipline, the lock file, the code-fingerprint check and conflict reporting exactly as they are for CLI callers.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Transport is an HTTP listener inside the service**",
    "text": "**Transport is an HTTP listener inside the service**: not a separate bridge process and not a Node-hosted shell. Live notification can only honestly originate in the service, because it is the sole writer and the only thing that knows when the store changed. The unix socket is untouched and remains the CLI's path; the listener is an addition beside it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The listener exposes an explicit op allowlist**",
    "text": "**The listener exposes an explicit op allowlist**: not a proxy onto the service protocol — deep read, plus a single-node text update. This bounds the blast radius of any auth failure and is the part that cannot be retrofitted cheaply.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Auth rests on five controls**",
    "text": "**Auth rests on five controls**: a custom `X-Aperas-Token` header on every request, which forces a CORS preflight and so prevents a cross-origin request being sent at all, independent of the token's value; a `127.0.0.1` bind; a per-run `randomBytes(32)` token stored in the existing run directory beside the lock and socket at mode 0600, compared with `timingSafeEqual`; a `Host` check against the loopback address, which is the specific anti-DNS-rebinding control; and an `Origin` allowlist as defence in depth, never reflected back.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Change notification is a bare tick**",
    "text": "**Change notification is a bare tick**: the service pushes *the store changed*, and the UI refetches its current apex. The tick is idempotent and stateless, so no delta format exists and none is needed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The tick stream is NDJSON over a streaming `fetch()` response**",
    "text": "**The tick stream is NDJSON over a streaming `fetch()` response**: read with `ReadableStream` rather than `EventSource`, which cannot set a request header and so cannot carry the token without falling back to a cookie or a URL ticket. NDJSON is already the service's framing on the unix socket, so no second wire format is introduced.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`buildRenderTree` is core's structured render**",
    "text": "**`buildRenderTree` is core's structured render**: the CLI's text output becomes a projection of it. `renderTreeWithView` already runs two passes — `discoverCone` builds the render plan, and only then does `emitNode`/`emitLinkLine` flatten it to strings; pass 1 is what a UI wants, pass 2 is the only part that assumes text. Extracting the plan as a tree of render items, and redefining the text render as `toText(buildRenderTree(...))`, keeps the existing verification suite as the guarantee that nothing changed — the text output must stay byte-identical.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A single `updateText(id, text)` hides the write-path's rules**",
    "text": "**A single `updateText(id, text)` hides the write-path's rules**: on the host side, per node type — an existing list item takes bare text with no bullet marker, a heading needs `--text-only` — so the UI encodes none of it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYG005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Topology",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSX8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR001",
