        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`FolderDiv`'s three slots are the three render tiers**",
    "text": "**`FolderDiv`'s three slots are the three render tiers**: which is why the port is a port and not a rewrite.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A link renders at two sites sharing one identity**",
    "text": "**A link renders at two sites sharing one identity**: its own text inside the block's prose, and an endnote in the link list after the children. Wikipedia's `cite-ref`/`cite-note` scheme without the superscript marker — a wikilink already carries the words the reader is looking at, so the link text *is* the marker. That an endnote exists below is carried by styling: a link that resolved to a graph node is styled as one, a dangling link is not.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR003:links:Link:00CJ6TGT2R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE1GW4YG006",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR003:links:Link:00CJ6TGT2R000:props:StringProp:00CJ71R7K8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "134"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR003:links:Link:00CJ6TGT2R002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE1GW4YG004",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR003:links:Link:00CJ6TGT2R002:props:StringProp:00CJ71R7WG000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "346"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Both sites obey canonical position**",
    "text": "**Both sites obey canonical position**: rather than re-deriving it — how a link's target renders is a property of where that target's [structural home](treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1GW4YG006) sits relative to the current render, not a property of the link. Three states: the home is nowhere in the render, and the link renders the target itself ([rule a folded, rule b unfolded](treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1GW4YG004)); the home is in the render, even as a title-only breadcrumb, and the link collapses to the `[*see <path>]` pointer plus a jump; the target sits above the apex, and it renders as `(outside view)` plus a zoom-out. Both sites read one shared verdict, so they cannot disagree with each other or with `aperas tree`. This also makes link-following cycle-safe without a visited set.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**One target cited twice is one `Link`**",
    "text": "**One target cited twice is one `Link`**: with two positions. Resolution groups by distinct target, so identity is the target alone and each occurrence contributes a `position` — the endnote is therefore per-`Link`, with one back-reference per position, Wikipedia's `^ a b`, already the stored shape.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The apex is recorded, not merely local**",
    "text": "**The apex is recorded, not merely local**: zooming (a tree click, a backlink zoom, a breadcrumb, or the root button) sets the local apex immediately and persists it as the current view's `root` alongside it (`/api/zoom`) — the same field `aperas zoom` sets from the CLI (design/treeview.md's \"root records the current zoom\"). A bare `?view=<name>` deep link with no `path` at all resolves from that recorded root, not the corpus root; an explicit `path=.` still means the corpus root regardless of what root a view carries.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Workflows",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSX8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR007",
      "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR008",
