        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Slice 8 — shallow write**",
    "text": "**Slice 8 — shallow write**: host-side `updateText(id, text)` choosing the per-type input form, link-sweep results surfaced.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Verification Plan",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8008",
      "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8009",
      "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800A",
      "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800B",
      "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800C",
      "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800D",
      "BlockNode:00CNS7K630001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8008:props:StringProp:00CJ6V6CJR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8008:props:StringProp:00CJ6V6CJR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Slice 1 is verified by the existing suite**",
    "text": "**Slice 1 is verified by the existing suite**: the text render must stay byte-identical across the extraction — any diff is a regression, and no new assertion is needed to catch it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slice 2 is verified by file mode and lifetime**",
    "text": "**Slice 2 is verified by file mode and lifetime**: the token file exists at 0600, its value changes across a service restart, and the old value stops being accepted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slice 3 is verified adversarially**",
    "text": "**Slice 3 is verified adversarially**: not just positively — a request with no token, with a wrong token, with a foreign `Origin`, and with a non-loopback `Host` must each be rejected; a cross-origin `fetch` from a scratch page must fail at the preflight rather than reaching a handler. An op outside the allowlist must be refused even with a valid token.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slice 4 is verified by killing the service mid-stream**",
    "text": "**Slice 4 is verified by killing the service mid-stream**: the client must reconnect, refetch unconditionally, and — once the token from the previous run is rejected — surface the 401 state rather than retrying silently.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slices 5 to 7 are verified against `aperas tree --view`**",
    "text": "**Slices 5 to 7 are verified against `aperas tree --view`**: the same view rendered by the UI and by the CLI must agree on tier, canonical-position verdict and hidden counts for every node, since both now read the same render tree.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Slice 8 is verified by round-tripping an edit**",
    "text": "**Slice 8 is verified by round-tripping an edit**: text typed in the UI, stored, projected and re-parsed must come back byte-identical, and a write whose links fail to persist must be visible in the UI rather than swallowed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6CH8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
