    ],
    "title": "**2026-09-18: bare relative-path links (no fragment) now resolve**",
    "text": "**2026-09-18: bare relative-path links (no fragment) now resolve**: a `[title](../folder/file)` reference with no `#fragment` — described in [Topology](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T8007) as valid \"cross-file navigation,\" but never actually implemented — was invisible to link resolution entirely, not merely dangling: `collectLinkCodes` (`astParser.ts`) never extracted it as an occurrence at all. Fixed by also extracting a `./`/`../`-leading href with no fragment, resolved via a new `resolveBarePathCode` (`apeironNgn/artifacts.ts`) straight to the target's own `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` — the same OS-relative path arithmetic the fragment form already uses, no anchor-matching gate needed. `check-links --repair` found and fixed 2 pre-existing corpus instances of the same gap once the resolver landed. See [Resolved](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJAV2W1R001) and [Projected/Pre-Ingestion Context](../design/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CDBYV4T800C).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBZ7698003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJAVRF90001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CJAVRF90001:links:Link:00CJAVRHYG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJAVGNJG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
