            "value": "74"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**2026-09-18: bare-path corpus links made navigable in the render tree**",
    "text": "**2026-09-18: bare-path corpus links made navigable in the render tree**: [design/linking.md's bare relative-path form](../history/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJAVGNJG001), fixed the same day, resolves in the graph now — but the webapp's `Inline.tsx` has no server round trip of its own to learn a link's target; it only ever recognizes a `#id/<Kind>:<id>` fragment already sitting in the href text, so a correctly-resolved bare-path link still rendered inert. Fixed with `bakeResolvedLinkIds` (`apeironNgn/node.ts`): before truncating a node's `abstract`/a link's `targetAbstract` for the render tree, it splices `#id/<target>` onto any `./`/`../`-leading href, using each `Link`'s own stored occurrence `position` — render-tree-only, the stored text and every projected file stay untouched. Verified live in a real browser: clicking `design/linking.md`'s `**Discussion**`/`**Planning**` links now navigates to their target `ArtifactNode`s, breadcrumbs and content updating correctly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6N9R003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
