    ],
    "title": "**The node-kind tag is a glyph, not a bracketed type name**",
    "text": "**The node-kind tag is a glyph, not a bracketed type name**: `📂`/`📄`/`§`/`¶`/`🔗` for `FolderNode`/`ArtifactNode`/heading/paragraph/link — the handful of kinds a reader actually orients by — and no tag at all for anything else (`listItem`, `code`, `table`, ...), rather than falling back to the old `[type]` text. A silent per-kind opt-in, not a universal re-skin: unmapped kinds stay exactly as bare as a plain list item always read.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
