        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The arrow and its stem are one control, not two**",
    "text": "**The arrow and its stem are one control, not two**: hovering or clicking either the fold arrow or the guide line below it is the same action, ported from the original vanilla `FolderDiv.js` sketch's single `<label>` wrapping both (`UniinfoNotes/assets/HTML/FolderDiv.js`, outside this repo). The stem's own position falls out of sharing the arrow's fixed-width column rather than from a separately-guessed margin — the earlier `.fd-children` border-left had no actual relationship to the arrow's position, which is what made it misaligned. Hovering recolors the arrow and the line together; it never washes the row with a background highlight, which read as an unrelated hover box rather than part of the control.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CJE11FRR000",
