    "title": "**`ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode.text` is a stale, heuristic copy that can't be baked — found via a folder-listing link that stayed inert after the fix meant to cover it**",
    "text": "**`ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode.text` is a stale, heuristic copy that can't be baked — found via a folder-listing link that stayed inert after the fix meant to cover it**: `design/linking.md`'s own `**Discussion**:` line rendered `inline-link-inert` in the \"design\" folder's listing, even after the bare-relative-path resolver fix and `bakeResolvedLinkIds` render-time fix ([history/linking.md](../history/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CJAVGNJG001), [history/webapp.md](../history/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CJAVRF90001), both 2026-09-18) were verified working for the direct case. Root cause: the folder-listing preview reads the `ArtifactNode`'s own `.text`, which is a *copy* of its first content-bearing descendant's text (`extractAbstract`), made once at hydration time — the descendant's real `Link` (confirmed already correctly resolved via `aperas show`) is never duplicated onto the container, so `bakeResolvedLinkIds` has nothing to bake with for this render path specifically. Deeper problem underneath: this copy is never refreshed by an ordinary deep edit either — `kgUpdate.ts`'s `target.text = text` never touches an ancestor's own `.text`, only a full re-hydration or the one-time holder-promotion path ever recomputes it — so the preview can go stale independent of this specific bug too. Direction agreed (see [discussion/core.md](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CKE4FFF0001)'s 2026-09-20 Freeflow entry for full rationale): retire the copy/heuristic entirely; give `ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` a real `description` field in their own YAML frontmatter, with its own genuinely-owned `Link`s, edited via `aperas update` extended to accept `FolderNode` and to consume `frontmatter` — the corpus's long-standing \"update as a scoped reconciliation\" pattern, not a new bespoke channel. Implemented in `e66996b`, but only partly: the `description` prop and its bakeable links landed, while one of the two preview paths still reads the copy this issue exists to retire — see [the follow-on](#id/BlockNode:00CN7V9BX0001).",
