    ],
    "title": "**The gesture is chosen by the state it lands on, not fixed per key**",
    "text": "**The gesture is chosen by the state it lands on, not fixed per key**: bare click always does the obvious thing to whatever is in front of it — unfold when folded, stash when open, unstash when stashed, unpin at a leaf, zoom at a depth cut-off — so one click reads as \"close this\" wherever the row looks closed and \"open this\" wherever it looks open, and never needs a second gesture to mean the same intent. Modifiers rank by how often they are wanted: shift steps the level, ctrl zooms, alt is the plain non-recursive `fold`, alt+shift the recursive pair. Bare click therefore never removes a node from `unfolds` except at a leaf — click is \"remember\", alt is \"forget\". Ctrl applies on the arrow and the stem as well as the row, which the [arrow has never actually honoured](../issues/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWN0XDG001). [The full gesture matrix and its transition diagram](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CMWMP6X8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6TGSYR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
