    ],
    "title": "**A checkbox's checked state never reaches any renderer, console or webapp**",
    "text": "**A checkbox's checked state never reaches any renderer, console or webapp**: `astParser.ts:705-706` stores it correctly as a `checked` prop and strips the literal `[ ]`/`[x]` from `.text`/`.title` so it isn't duplicated as text, and `project.ts` re-emits it correctly on the way back to `.md` — but `RenderNodeItem` (`node.ts`) has no `checked` field at all, and `buildNodeItem` never reads the prop, so every reader downstream of the render tree sees a plain listItem with no marker anywhere: not `aperas tree`, not `aperas unfold`'s own preview, not the webapp. The round trip through disk is correct; only the *reading* path drops it, the mirror image of [the table/code gap above](#id/BlockNode:00CMX4NCW8001) — that one loses structure already present in the abstract string, this one never puts the value in the string's carrier (`RenderNodeItem`) to begin with. Fix is additive: a `checked?: boolean` field, read via `getProp` the same way `holder`/`starred` already are, surfaced as a real glyph rather than folded into title text (a `- [ ]`/`- [x]` prefix would collide with `.fd-title`'s own bold styling the way it collides with nothing today).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V6370002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CMZPC898000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-22T03:08:48.801Z",
    "title": "00CMZPC898000",
    "text": "**Frontmatter sweep across every live concern doc — testing the `description`-frontmatter feature end to end, 2026-09-22.** Exercises [the frontmatter-backed `description` design](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CKE4FFF0001) against real content for the first time since it landed: every doc in the corpus was ingested before that feature existed, so `description` is unset everywhere and every artifact/folder listing still falls back to `.text`. Scope: the 44 live concern docs under `design/`, `discussion/`, `issues/`, `planning/`, `history/` for `aperas-skill`, `archive-migration`, `cli`, `core`, `documentation`, `linking`, `list-consumption`, `packaging`, `treeview`, `webapp`, plus `artifacts/README.md` itself (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`). `archive/` is deliberately excluded — superseded content, not worth the churn. The goal is exercising the mechanism, not polishing prose: each file gets one brief, genuinely-considered description (not a mechanical first-sentence copy), authored across the whole batch, then reviewed by the user as a batch at the end rather than file-by-file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CMZPC898001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-22T03:08:50.360Z",
    "title": "Per-file loop, run to completion before moving to the next",
    "text": "Per-file loop, run to completion before moving to the next: (1) read the file, draft a one-line `description:` frontmatter value; (2) prepend `---\\ndescription: <text>\\n---` to the file on disk; (3) `aperas ingest <path> --track --flush`; (4) `aperas project <path> --flush`; (5) round-trip check — `aperas show <ArtifactNode-id>` (or `git diff`) confirms `description` landed as a real prop, any markdown links in it resolved to real `Link`s, and the re-projected file's frontmatter/body matches what was intended (no corruption, no dropped content). `aperas check-links` once at the end of the whole batch, not per file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
