    "title": "00CMZPWSCR000",
    "text": "**Frontmatter sweep across every live concern doc — testing the `description`-frontmatter feature end to end, 2026-09-22.** Exercises [the frontmatter-backed `description` design](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CKE4FFF0001) against real content for the first time since it landed: every doc in the corpus was ingested before that feature existed, so `description` is unset everywhere and every artifact/folder listing still falls back to `.text`. Scope: the 44 live concern docs under `design/`, `discussion/`, `issues/`, `planning/`, `history/` for `aperas-skill`, `archive-migration`, `cli`, `core`, `documentation`, `linking`, `list-consumption`, `packaging`, `treeview`, `webapp`, plus `artifacts/README.md` itself (the artifacts-root `FolderNode`). `archive/` is deliberately excluded — superseded content, not worth the churn. The goal is exercising the mechanism, not polishing prose: each file gets one brief, genuinely-considered description (not a mechanical first-sentence copy), authored across the whole batch, then reviewed by the user as a batch at the end rather than file-by-file. Per-file loop, run to completion before moving to the next: (1) read the file, draft a one-line `description:` frontmatter value; (2) prepend `---\\ndescription: <text>\\n---` to the file on disk; (3) `aperas ingest <path> --track --flush`; (4) `aperas project <path> --flush`; (5) round-trip check — `aperas show <ArtifactNode-id>` (or `git diff`) confirms `description` landed as a real prop, any markdown links in it resolved to real `Link`s, and the re-projected file's frontmatter/body matches what was intended (no corruption, no dropped content). `aperas check-links` once at the end of the whole batch, not per file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
