    "title": "00CN4DTJJ0001",
    "text": "**Four concern docs had drifted between their committed `.md` and the graph, predating this session, found only because the frontmatter sweep was the first thing to force a full re-ingest of them in a while.** `design/aperas-skill.md`, `history/aperas-skill.md`, `issues/aperas-skill.md` and `discussion/archive-migration.md` each produced a real (non-phantom) \"would remove\" confirmation on `aperas ingest --track` — confirmed by checking the named candidates directly (`aperas show`), which came back live, non-tombstoned content, unlike the harmless already-dead phantom found earlier on `design/treeview.md`. Resolved the same way for all four: `aperas project <path> --flush` first (resync the on-disk file to the graph's current truth), *then* add frontmatter on top of that accurate base — confirmed via `git diff` afterward that every non-frontmatter line changed was pure blank-line-between-list-items normalization (the file's last commit predates whatever changed how the serializer spaces consecutive top-level list items), no actual text lost. Not investigated further: why these four specific files' on-disk copies had gone stale relative to the graph in the first place — plausibly just ordinary `.md` edits or projections that happened before their last `git commit`, never re-diffed since. Same underlying theme as [the ingestFromDisk scope-mismatch fix](#id/BlockNode:00CN1PKAQG001) and [the packaging slug-path collision](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CN4DGBQ0001) above: the whole-artifact ingest path is exercised rarely enough in ordinary use that unrelated latent issues accumulate invisibly until something forces it to run corpus-wide.",
