    "title": "**`aperas retype`'s automatic title derivation has no slug-path collision guard, unlike every other title-changing write path**",
    "text": "**`aperas retype`'s automatic title derivation has no slug-path collision guard, unlike every other title-changing write path**: confirmed live — `rejectSlugPathCollisions` (`node.ts`, design/linking.md's Full-Path Collisions) is called from `ArtifactNode.ingestFromDisk` (`node.ts`), `kg:insert` (`kgInsert.ts:125`), and `kg:update` for *any* title change, heading retitle or non-heading re-derivation alike (`kgUpdate.ts:207-214`, explicitly scoped to cover exactly this case per its own comment: \"relevant whenever `title` actually changed... heading retitle or non-heading re-derivation alike\"). `kgRetype.ts` has no such call anywhere in the file — its title assignment at `target.title = toTitle` (line 248) is a bare, unguarded write, even though retype's own defining feature is deriving a *fresh* title (folding a heading's words into a lead-in, or cutting a lead-in back out into a heading) exactly the kind of change the other three sites exist to protect. Reproduced live in a scratch artifact: two sibling blocks under one parent heading, one a heading titled \"Existing Sibling\", the other a listItem with the identical bold lead-in \"**Existing Sibling**\" — `aperas retype <listItem> --to h3` succeeded with no error or warning, producing two live sibling headings both titled \"### Existing Sibling\" under the same parent, indistinguishable in `aperas tree`'s own render. Fix direction: call `rejectSlugPathCollisions(store, target.parent.toPath(), [...])` at `kgRetype.ts`'s title-assignment point, the same shape `kgUpdate.ts:207-214` already uses — not yet implemented, found while auditing every title-extraction path after [the packaging slug-path collision](../discussion/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CN4DGBQ0001) raised the question of whether the guard covers every site that mints or changes a title, not just full-document ingest.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDBYV5A8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
