        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Every generation below the current snapshot is unverified, so the provenance layers can be corrupted or destroyed with no signal at all**",
    "text": "**Every generation below the current snapshot is unverified, so the provenance layers can be corrupted or destroyed with no signal at all**: `recorded_roots` takes the latest snapshot plus the deltas above it and nothing else, deliberately — its own docstring reasons that \"older snapshots are history, not a baseline,\" since v1 restructuring v0 wholesale is the point of a major version rather than drift, and comparing against v0 would report the entire rewrite as drops. That is correct for detecting drift against the *current* file, but it means the v0 and v1 generations — six snapshot/delta section roots as of 2026-09-22, holding the reasoning for how most current rules came to be — are never read by any check. Confirmed live and unpleasantly: the `Supersedes:` line on the v1.1 Citation-direction entry was overwritten outright, taking with it the only recorded account of what v1 paragraph that entry replaced, and the very next run still reported `DROPPED, unaccounted — 0`. It was recovered from `git show HEAD:` rather than from anything the instrument said, and only because a reader thought to ask where the line had gone. Same blindness applies to the deltas' own cross-references: a `Supersedes:` target in a superseded generation can rot to a tombstoned or nonexistent id without anything noticing. Fix direction, two candidates rather than one settled choice: either a second, cheaper integrity mode that verifies each older generation against itself — entries still parse, `Supersedes:` targets still resolve to live blocks, no entry silently emptied — or an explicit decision that history layers are write-once and unprotected, recorded as such so nobody later assumes a passing check covers them. The sibling gap in the same instrument, which does affect in-scope entries, is [the containment-direction blind spot](#id/BlockNode:00CN89ERE8000). Not yet implemented.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5KW4G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
