    "title": "## v2.9 additions — delta on the v2 snapshot",
    "text": "Threaded onto [the v2 snapshot](#id/BlockNode:00CGF613VR001). A layout repair rather than a new rule: two Orientation items are promoted to subsections of their own, so each one's scope is stated rather than inferred from adjacency. Both were written when Orientation had no subsections at all, and were silently re-scoped the moment \"Deep read and deep write run along the same three directions\" was introduced above them — in a flat layout a paragraph belongs to whatever heading precedes it, so an item written for the section level is captured by the first subsection appearing before it, with nothing marking which one it was meant for. Neither item lost or gained a word; each bold lead-in simply became the `###` heading it had been acting as. Promotion rather than relocation is what restores the scoping, since once a subsection opens there is no way back to section level except to precede every subsection or to carry a heading of one's own. Surfaced when [v2.8](#id/BlockNode:00CN7YEND0001)'s new subsection landed between \"Dense linking is the precondition for both\" and the sentence supplying that \"both\", making a long-standing mis-scoping visible by breaking a pronoun.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZJR001",
