    "title": "**Resolved: the webapp's 1s poll remounted the entire tree**",
    "text": "**Resolved: the webapp's 1s poll remounted the entire tree**: `<For>` reconciles by object reference, and a plain `createResource` handed it a fresh object graph on every poll — so it tore down and remounted every row each second, dropping any open inline editor mid-edit. Fixed with `reconcile(data, {key: 'id'})` (`solid-js/store`), merging each poll's response into a persistent store by node id. Unblocked by renaming `RenderLinkItem.linkId` to `id` in `core` — an unmotivated naming split with no functional reason, found while auditing for a uniform reconcile key. Verified live in a browser: 45 tagged DOM nodes and a mid-edit, unsaved textarea both survived 4 poll ticks with no remount. Full investigation: [Freeflow](../discussion/webapp.md#id/BlockNode:00CNR2E3D0001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ6V637000F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
