    "title": "### Top matter — Status bumped to v2.10",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v2.9's own status line](#id/BlockNode:00CN8KBK9G002)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW4V5GG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CNW61XZG001",
      "BlockNode:00CP9RSEW0001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNW61XZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v2.10** — four levels, Philosophy through Mechanics, each item explaining a consequence of the one above it. Only current, verified items appear here; superseded material, unverified hypotheses and version-by-version rationale live in `discussion/aperas-skill.md`'s snapshot and deltas. Concern docs: `AperasKG/artifacts/{design,issues,planning,history,discussion}/aperas-skill.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW5Y57G001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0002:props:StringProp:00CNWK39NG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0002:props:StringProp:00CNWK39NG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CNWK33W0002",
    "text": "**Appending at the end is safe when the number is right.** For a list numbered `1, 2, …, n-1`, piping `n. new item` after the last one is accepted. Piping any other number is rejected outright, naming the number it expected instead.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW50VZ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWK33W0003",
    "text": "**A middle-of-the-list insertion still needs the full renumbering route** — the fix above only covers appending at the end, since inserting in the middle genuinely requires renumbering everything after it. The safer route there is to target the list's **parent heading** (`aperas update <heading-id>`) and pipe the heading line plus the *complete* list (every existing item verbatim plus the new one).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW50VZ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0004",
      "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0004:props:StringProp:00CNWK39NG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0004:props:StringProp:00CNWK39NG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CNWK33W0004",
    "text": "Exact-key matching reuses every unchanged item's id, **but only while every item keeps its parent and depth**. A push that changes item depth (e.g. regrouping under sub-headings) recreates everything; use `aperas insert` (moves) for that instead.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWK33W0005",
    "text": "**This only works if the piped content is genuinely complete.** Piping the heading plus *only* the new item reconciles the existing ones away as removed, tombstoning real content.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNWK33W0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0002:props:StringProp:00CNWKAC48000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0002:props:StringProp:00CNWKAC48001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CNWMVMBR001",
    "text": "**For an ordinary text change, pipe bare text with no bullet marker** (e.g. `updated text`, not `- updated text`). This also updates any nested children in the same call, if you include them — see the next point for the cases that need a marker instead.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW58YAG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWKA6Q0003",
    "text": "**A marker is needed only for a checkbox, an ordered item's position, or text that's deliberately blank.** Use whatever you'd normally write: `- [x]`/`- [ ]` for a checkbox, `n.` for an ordered item, or a bare `- ` (nothing after it) if you want the item's own text to end up empty while still giving it children:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW58YAG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWKA6Q0004",
    "text": "```\n  - \n    - child\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0003",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWKA6Q0005",
    "text": "**Updating an item never changes where it sits in the list.** Whether it's ordered or unordered, and its position in the numbering, stays exactly as it was, no matter which marker you use to update it. To actually reorder or renumber, use the parent-plus-complete-list technique above — not a single-item update.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW58YAG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWQMSVG001",
    "text": "**The title always tracks your current text, never the old one.** If your new text has a bold lead-in term (`**Like this**: ...`), the title updates to match it. If it doesn't, the title falls back to the item's own id — the same fallback any untitled node gets — rather than keeping whatever the title used to say about text that's now gone.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW58YAG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKA6Q0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CNWKA6Q0007",
    "text": "**The text itself works differently: leaving it out clears it.** If you only pipe new children (a list, with no text of its own before it), the item's own text becomes empty — unlike the title, nothing here is left alone by default. Restate the existing text if you don't want it wiped.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW58YAG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKKD80001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKKD80001:links:Link:00CNWKKGV0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CH5FJME8002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKKD80001:links:Link:00CNWKKGV0000:props:StringProp:00CNWKKGV8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKKD80001:links:Link:00CNWKKGV8001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CH5FJME8003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CNWKKD80001:links:Link:00CNWKKGV8001:props:StringProp:00CNWKKGV8002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "59"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### Supersedes note — the old input-rule bullets",
    "text": "Supersedes: [The input rule](#id/BlockNode:00CH5FJME8002), [Explanation](#id/BlockNode:00CH5FJME8003)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNW4V5GG001",
