    ],
    "title": "Missing bootstrap for a brand-new graph",
    "text": "Missing bootstrap for a brand-new graph: `rehydrateStore` (`store.ts`) treats a missing `Apeiron/*.jsonld` instance file as `ENOENT`, not an empty graph, so a fresh directory with no store files at all crashed the service on startup — surfacing only as `aperas serve`/`aperas service start`'s generic \"did not become ready in time\", with nothing pointing at the real cause. Found live installing the published `aperas` package into a brand-new project. Fixed with a new `aperas init` command that creates `aperas.config.json`, the four empty instance files, and `artifacts/` — see [history](../history/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00CP9QYPNG000).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CDDVC8N0007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CP9R475R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
