    "title": "**Staging exemption contradicts its own section**",
    "text": "**Staging exemption contradicts its own section**: `aperas/SKILL.md`'s *Stage each verified step* ends \"the orchestrator stages neither, since it writes nothing that is not staged by the grapher's next turn\". The rationale is wrong: each agent stages its own edits for its own recovery, and does not hand that to another role's next turn. Decided (user): remove the exemption; every role stages what it writes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z68000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No guidance when the topic's discussion lacks `## Freeflow`**",
    "text": "**No guidance when the topic's discussion lacks `## Freeflow`**: `discussion/cli.md` has only Dashboard and Settled. The orchestrator stalled, went to `design/documentation.md` to learn the convention, and switched to `discussion/treeview.md` instead. Decided (user): the orchestrator just creates it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z68001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The orchestrator pre-surveyed the corpus itself**",
    "text": "**The orchestrator pre-surveyed the corpus itself**: to find where to record, it chose between `cli.md` and `treeview.md` and read the Freeflow shape in `design/documentation.md`. That is deep read, which belongs to the grapher. The gap above partly forced it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z68002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The first Ask folded the coder's survey turn into the grapher's**",
    "text": "**The first Ask folded the coder's survey turn into the grapher's**: it told the grapher to find `tree`'s source and map its render behavior. `aperas-coder` makes the coder's first turn a no-change code survey that the grapher files; the grapher's own survey is graph-first and touches code only to pinpoint. The orchestrator was also about to send the coder straight to implementation, skipping that survey turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z68003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The orchestrator read `node.ts` itself mid-discussion**",
    "text": "**The orchestrator read `node.ts` itself mid-discussion**: after relaying the grapher's summary wrongly twice, it read the code for ground truth instead of sending a follow-up Ask. The resulting finding — scope and detail are independent axes — lived only in chat until recorded under the task's freeflow entry.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z68004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Freeflow lagged the conversation**",
    "text": "**Freeflow lagged the conversation**: three user corrections and two decisions went unrecorded until after the fact, despite \"record before acting\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z68005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A failed insert left a live orphan**",
    "text": "**A failed insert left a live orphan**: a rejected `aperas insert` (the item itself passed as parent) hydrated `BlockNode:00CR6BD1X0001` before anchor validation, and the retry placed a second copy. This is known tool behavior (base Mechanics, *`--after`/`--before` anchors*); the orchestrator didn't clean up after the failure.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR7N7Z60001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
