    "title": "**Removing a thread subtree leaks its descendants' tombstones into the tracked mirror**",
    "text": "**Removing a thread subtree leaks its descendants' tombstones into the tracked mirror**: this contradicts [Threads persist to `.state/` by membership, not by class](../design/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3WYRG8001), which says pruning a thread is an ordinary `remove`. Found 2026-09-27 when resetting both threads. Promoted to [issues/treeview.md](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1DDF58003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8002",
      "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8003",
      "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8002:props:StringProp:00CR81SJJ0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8002:props:StringProp:00CR81SJJ0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Mechanism**",
    "text": "**Mechanism**: `aperas remove` on a thread heading keeps the removed root's `parent`, so the root stays in `Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld`. Every descendant loses its `parent`, so the ancestor walk to `artifacts/.threads/` no longer reaches it, and it dehydrates into tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld`. Placement has to hold for tombstones too, not only while an ancestor under `.threads` is still reachable.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Repro**",
    "text": "**Repro**: remove `## tree --format flag` in `.threads/grapher.md` (`BlockNode:00CR6BH1PR001`). The heading lands in `.state`; its Task, Turn, Ask, Work and Report nodes (e.g. `BlockNode:00CR6BKSS8001`, `BlockNode:00CR6BRTPG001`) land tracked with `tombstonedAt` and no `parent`. 15 thread tombstones leaked this way, and they are now in `AperasKG`'s git index.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Also needed**",
    "text": "**Also needed**: moving the already-leaked tombstones back into `.state`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81SDX8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
