  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81Y470003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — missing `## Freeflow`**",
    "text": "**Decided — missing `## Freeflow`**: the orchestrator creates it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81Y470001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81Y470004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — the orchestrator's reads use read-and-record**",
    "text": "**Decided — the orchestrator's reads use read-and-record**: the orchestrator may read the graph or code itself, for example to verify or to answer the user, but any finding it relays must first go into freeflow, citing its source. Chosen over routing every question as a follow-up Ask, because a subagent round-trip took about 6.5 minutes and what routing protects for a read is the record.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81Y470001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR81Y470005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — the loop lives in the base skill, and an Ask cites its decisions**",
    "text": "**Decided — the loop lives in the base skill, and an Ask cites its decisions**: user approved 2026-09-27. Move the full loop and its turn types into the base skill's *Three roles* section: grapher survey (graph only), coder survey (no change), grapher files, coder change, orchestrator verifies, grapher files, finish. A hand-off Ask must cite a freeflow node for every decision it relies on, so an unrecorded decision blocks the Ask. The orchestrator makes the skill edit itself, since the skill has not held, then hands it to the grapher to record.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR81Y470001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
