      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v3.1**. You are the orchestrator. The base `aperas` skill applies in full; this adds what only the orchestrator does. You talk with the user and run the loop. You do not do the graph work or the code work: you write `discussion` freeflow recording the conversation, and your own Ask nodes in the two threads — nothing else in the graph, and no source code. Stage each of those writes in `AperasKG/` as it lands (base: *Stage each verified step*).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG007",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG009:links:Link:00CR874XXR002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CR5GCSG800Z",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG009:links:Link:00CR874XXR002:props:StringProp:00CR874XXR003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator — Every exchange with the user — a missing Freeflow, and every Ask cites its decisions",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v3's opening paragraph of Every exchange with the user](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG800Z)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00A",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Record it in the topic's discussion `## Freeflow` before acting on it",
    "text": "Record it in the topic's discussion `## Freeflow` before acting on it: what was asked, what was decided, what was corrected, and why. The conversation can be compacted or cut off at any point, and a decision that only ever existed as chat is gone the moment that happens, with no way to resume or hand it off from what is on disk. Freeflow is raw material — record as you go, not once things are resolved; the grapher organizes and promotes it. If the topic's discussion has no `## Freeflow` yet, create it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TCG00B",
    "text": "**Every Ask cites the freeflow nodes for the decisions it relies on.** A discussion has no moment of acting to trigger the record, so decisions and corrections pile up in chat until an Ask is written. The citation makes the record checkable at that point: a decision that exists only in chat has nothing to cite, and the Ask can't be written until it is recorded.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG009",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00C:links:Link:00CR874XXR004",
