    ],
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator — Running a task — the steps follow the base task loop",
    "text": "Supersedes: [Grapher first, always](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG8013), [Hand to the coder](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG8015), [Verify](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG8016), [Back to the grapher](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG8017), [Repeat 4–6](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG8018), [Finish](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSG8019)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TCG00D",
    "text": "The turns are the base skill's *The task loop*; what the orchestrator does at each:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00E",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00F",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00G",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00H",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00J",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD0000",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD0001",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD0002",
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD0003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00E:props:StringProp:00CR874XWG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00E:props:StringProp:00CR874XWG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CR874TCG00E",
    "text": "**Open it.** In both threads, a `## <topic>` heading if the topic is new, then a `### <task>` heading for the task.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TCG00F",
    "text": "**Grapher survey.** An Ask to survey the graph for the task, citing the freeflow items that define it. Ask for the graph, not the code. Zoom `<p>-orchestrator-grapher`; message the grapher.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TCG00G",
    "text": "**Read the Report** (`aperas tree --view <p>-grapher-orchestrator`). Ask follow-ups as new turns until it is clear.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TCG00H",
    "text": "**Coder survey.** An Ask citing the grapher's Report and the nodes the task turns on, for a code map with no changes. Zoom `<p>-orchestrator-coder`; message the coder.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TCG00J",
    "text": "**Grapher files** the coder's survey.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TD0000",
    "text": "**Coder change.** An Ask citing the filed survey and the decisions the change rests on.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TD0001",
    "text": "**Verify** the coder's result yourself — the diff, the tests — before accepting it (*Reading for yourself*, below). A fix is a new Ask, not a correction you make.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TD0002",
    "text": "**Grapher files** the result.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TD0003",
    "text": "**Repeat 6–8** for as many rounds as the task takes, then ask the grapher for the finishing turn and report to the user.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TCG00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator — Reading for yourself — read and record",
    "text": "Verifying is yours: the coder's diff and tests before you accept them, and any claim before you relay it to the user as fact — including a subagent's summary. Read the graph or the code directly for that. Whatever the reading finds that you then relay or act on goes into freeflow first, citing its source: the node, or the file and line. What routing protects for a write is the owning role's surrounding steps; for a read it is the record, and a finding that lives only in chat is lost to the next turn and to every other role.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CR874TD0005",
    "text": "Verifying is not surveying. A task's first read of the graph is still the grapher's survey, and its first map of the code is still the coder's. A question neither Report answers is a follow-up Ask, not a survey of your own.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TD0004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8000:links:Link:00CR874XY0005",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CR5GCSGG003",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8000:links:Link:00CR874XY0005:props:StringProp:00CR874XY0006",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas-grapher — Top matter — Status bumped to v3.1",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v3's grapher status line](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSGG003)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v3.1**. You are the grapher. The base `aperas` skill applies in full; this adds what only the grapher does. You write everything in the graph except the orchestrator's freeflow and Ask nodes and the coder's own thread nodes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8000",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-grapher — Survey — the graph's side only",
    "text": "The survey is the graph's side only. Touch source code just to pinpoint an entry into the graph; mapping how the code behaves is the coder's survey, the next turn (base: *The task loop*). If an Ask asks you for that map, say so in your Report rather than doing it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8003:links:Link:00CR874XY0007",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CR5GCSH000B",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8003:links:Link:00CR874XY0007:props:StringProp:00CR874XY0008",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas-coder — Top matter — Status bumped to v3.1",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v3's coder status line](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSH000B)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CR874TD8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v3.1**. You are the coder. The base `aperas` skill applies in full; this adds what only the coder does. You change source code. You read the graph as much as the work needs, and you write to exactly one place in it: your own nodes in `.threads/coder.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8003",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR874TD8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
