    "title": "**v3 — the skill split across three roles, with the graph as the medium they hand off through**",
    "text": "**v3 — the skill split across three roles, with the graph as the medium they hand off through**: by 2026-09-27 the loop had outgrown what one agent follows reliably, and the user was routinely reminding agents of the steps they dropped. The skill became a base every role loads plus three role skills: an orchestrator that talks with the user and writes only freeflow and its own Asks, a grapher that owns every other graph write, and a coder that owns source code and writes only its own thread. Roles hand off through per-role threads and through views rooted on the current Ask or Report: the view carries the state of the work, the chat only its progress. Threads sit at the bottom of the citation gradient, so nothing outside one links in. Settled as [Multi-agent working](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3X3N00001) and planned as [Batch 3](../planning/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3XQKNG001). Recorded as [v3 SKILL.md (verbatim, 2026-09-27)](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSEG001), a fresh snapshot and the first to span more than one file, since the base skill's Discipline was rewritten wholesale and the three role files had no baseline to delta against.",
