  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CR92ZRJ8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Gap in the skill**",
    "text": "**Gap in the skill**: *Threads* asks subturns for \"the essence of each tool result a later turn will need\", which reads as task results. Nothing asks for a workaround built, a call that hung or failed, or a tool that fell short, so that friction is invisible after the turn — though the base skill's own premise is that the graph must notice what no one will remember. The orchestrator has the same habit: it looped `aperas show --text` over children twice this session for the same reason.",
