    "title": "**A tombstoned node stays listed in its parent's `children` array**",
    "text": "**A tombstoned node stays listed in its parent's `children` array**: `ArtifactNode:00CR5ANC6G000` (`.threads/coder.md`'s holder) still lists `BlockNode:00CR6BXGTR001` as a child, though it was tombstoned during the September 27 thread reset. `tree`/`unfold` hide it correctly since both filter tombstoned nodes at render time, but `aperas show` on the parent exposes the stale reference, and a bare anchor-less `insert` after it would have needed a live anchor. Found 2026-09-27, not yet investigated further; possibly related to [the `.state` tombstone leak](../discussion/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CR81SDX8001), a different symptom of the same area of the code. Promoted to [issues/treeview.md](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR008).",
