    "text": "Drift check: `skill_drift.py --added` → 0 (nothing unrecorded). The plain `skill_drift.py` also shows 1 pre-existing \"DROPPED, unaccounted\" entry, `BlockNode:00CR9D1WW0001` (the Report template's Tool-gap line) — unrelated to this edit. It's a drift-script matching weakness: the recorded unit is one line lifted out of a much larger single `code` block in the live file (the whole thread-template example under *Threads*), and the script compares whole code blocks as one unit, so a substring match doesn't register even though the line is present verbatim in the file. Not fixed here — a pre-existing tool gap, not part of this Ask.",
