            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas — Discipline — Threads, threads may link to each other",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v3's thread-tier paragraph in Threads](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSF000N)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRAZ91C8002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZ91C8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRAZ91C8002",
    "text": "Threads are the lowest tier of the gradient (*Citation direction*, below), so a thread cites upward freely, and threads cite each other sideways — an Ask citing the other subagent's Report is the ordinary case. **Nothing above the threads tier links into one**: no formal doc, `concepts.md` entry or discussion node. What a thread finds reaches the rest of the graph by the grapher copying it up, never by citation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZ91C8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZB02G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZB02G001:links:Link:00CRAZB51R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CR5GCSF0011",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZB02G001:links:Link:00CRAZB51R000:props:StringProp:00CRAZB51R001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas — Discipline — Every claim carries its source, the thread clause follows the tier rule",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v3's where-you-check paragraph in Every claim carries its source](#id/BlockNode:00CR5GCSF0011)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRAZB02G002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZB02G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRAZB02G002",
    "text": "Where you check depends on where you wrote it. A thread or freeflow entry cites forward, since nothing above the threads tier links into a thread and freeflow is not itself a citation target (base *Citation direction*, below) — so the check there is simply: does this entry's own text name what it rests on? A formal-doc entry can be checked from the other side, and more strongly: run `aperas backlinks <id> --text` on **what you just wrote**, not only on what you were about to read. A node whose claims rest on nothing returns nothing, and that silence is the entire signal. The mechanics of applying this to a formal-doc promotion — where the link goes when citation direction forbids the obvious direction — belong to the grapher, the only role that writes one (`aperas-grapher`'s *Provenance at the origin*).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZB02G001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZBN0G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZBN0G001:links:Link:00CRAZBRQR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CR9D9NQG002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZBN0G001:links:Link:00CRAZBRQR000:props:StringProp:00CRAZBRQR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas-grapher — Filing — never link into a thread from the graph above it",
    "text": "Supersedes: [the tool-gap Filing entry](#id/BlockNode:00CR9D9NQG002)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRAZBN0G002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZBN0G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRAZBN0G002",
    "text": "Read the coder's latest Report and the Work under it in `.threads/coder.md`. Record what the coder found where it belongs: into the task's `discussion` freeflow first, then promoted into `issues`/`history`/`design` once it has earned a home (*Discussion is where meta-info is born*, below). Copy content up; never link into a thread from the graph above it. Where the coder reports code and design disagreeing, that discrepancy is itself the finding — record it, and fix whichever side is stale. File every tool gap in a Report, the coder's or your own, in the freeflow of the concern that owns the tool.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZBN0G001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator — Before sending an Ask — a new section, the pre-send checklist",
    "text": "Run every Ask against this list before dispatching it. Each item is a rule stated elsewhere that has already been broken while an Ask was being written, because nothing brings it up at that moment:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRAZC840002",
      "BlockNode:00CRAZC840003",
      "BlockNode:00CRAZC840004",
      "BlockNode:00CRAZC840005",
      "BlockNode:00CRAZC840006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840002:props:StringProp:00CRAZCEP0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840002:props:StringProp:00CRAZCEP0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CRAZC840002",
    "text": "**Only the receiver's kind of work.** A grapher Ask asks for the graph, never \"find the source\" or \"map the behavior\"; a coder Ask asks for code, never for a graph write (base: *The task loop*).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRAZC840003",
    "text": "**Every decision cited from freeflow.** A scope call, a resolved Question, a choice between approaches: if it isn't recorded in freeflow yet, record it first, then cite it (*Every exchange with the user*).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRAZC840004",
    "text": "**Cite, don't retype.** Point at the Report, the filed entry or the design block; don't paste its content into the Ask or the chat message (base: *Hand-offs*). The message names the view and at most one argument.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRAZC840005",
    "text": "**One task per dispatch.** A hand-off view has one root; a second task's Ask would be reachable only through chat.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Skipping these costs more than time",
    "text": "Skipping these costs more than time: a code map surveyed twice, an Ask that repeats what it should cite, and a turn built on a decision nobody recorded.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAZC840001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
