  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRB689SR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CRB689SR001",
    "text": "**Decided — subagents get their own personal view, named `${profile}-${topic-or-task}`** (user, 2026-09-27): the grapher's Turn 3 finishing turn needed to browse across a whole task and had nowhere sanctioned to do it — its only two views are the fixed hand-off ones (`claude-orchestrator-grapher`, owned by the orchestrator; `claude-grapher-orchestrator`, re-rooted onto its Report every turn), neither meant for free browsing. It created a bare-named `claude-grapher` view on the spot to work around this. The orchestrator already does this for itself (`kg-cleanup`, `core-redesign`, `webapp-design`, bare topic names, no prefix), but `TreeView` names are globally unique, so a subagent using the same bare-topic convention would collide with the orchestrator's own view on that topic. The profile prefix avoids that. The base skill's *Keep an active view, and keep it current* gets this stated as the convention for any role's personal view, not only the orchestrator's.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAQQ2V0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRBE4WDR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRB6ZTXG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided — Turn 6 follow-ups** (user, 2026-09-27)",
    "text": "**Decided — Turn 6 follow-ups** (user, 2026-09-27): fix the misattributed drift entry now (`BlockNode:00CR9D1WW0001`'s heading, a note about the change rather than skill text, incorrectly flagged as a code-block matching problem); leave the v3.1 history milestone for the actual finishing turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRAQQ2V0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRBE35S8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas — Orientation — Keep an active view, personal-view naming for any role",
    "text": "This is separate from the fixed hand-off views a subagent already owns (*Hand-offs*, below), which are re-rooted onto an Ask or a Report every turn and aren't meant for free browsing. A subagent that needs to look around a whole task — to write a finishing turn, say — sets up one of these for itself the same way. `TreeView` names are globally unique, so name it `${profile}-${topic-or-task}`, not a bare topic name: the orchestrator's own personal views are bare (`kg-cleanup`, `core-redesign`), and a subagent using the same bare name for the same topic would collide with one that already exists.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR874TC8001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
