  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC1S4MR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The orchestrator cleared the grapher's own Turn 8 Report text**",
    "text": "**The orchestrator cleared the grapher's own Turn 8 Report text**: ran `printf '\\n' | aperas update BlockNode:00CRC0M9GG001 --text-only` against the live Report node, as an idle check of whether a thread-size warning still fired after pruning — exactly the trap the base skill's *Updating an existing list item* documents (leaving text out wipes it), hit carelessly against production content instead of a disposable node. Only one child (the pruning note) survived; the Report's substance was in its own top-level text, now empty. `.threads/` and `Apeiron/.state/` are both gitignored, so there was no git-based recovery path. The orchestrator independently reverified the underlying facts (the new v3.1 delta entry, the design promotion, the provenance link, clean drift/check-links) and is routing the restoration to the grapher rather than writing into its own thread content.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC6N7TG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A flushed `update`/`project` can stay in the `.state/` mirror without reaching the tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` file**",
    "text": "**A flushed `update`/`project` can stay in the `.state/` mirror without reaching the tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` file**: found 2026-09-27 while restoring the accidentally-cleared Turn 8 Report (`.threads/grapher.md`). After `aperas update ... --flush` and `aperas project ... --flush`, the new content was live in the service and in `Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld`, but absent from the git-tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` — plain `--flush` didn't sync the tracked file this time. `aperas service restart` forced it. The restart's own `pruneUnreachableTombstones` GC also hard-deleted the already-tombstoned Turn 1–3 \"tree rendering\" thread content still lingering in the tracked mirror at that point — confirmed intended, documented behavior (that content was already tombstoned by an approved prune), not new data loss.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRC9JSGR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC97EM0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolution — `--detail {long|short}`, as already designed, is not implemented**",
    "text": "**Resolution — `--detail {long|short}`, as already designed, is not implemented**: `--detail` appears nowhere in `packages/cli/src/*.ts` and nowhere in `design/treeview.md` as a CLI flag — confirmed 2026-09-27. The coding task itself was cancelled when the first-run test was reset before implementation, and the cap-removal task that ran afterward only fixed the truncation prerequisite, not the flag. `--detail {long|short}` remains the correct answer to this evidence; it just hasn't been built.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CR92W8TR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC9E2SR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-09-27T09:40:11.438Z",
    "title": "**Correction — this was not a sync failure, it was correct, by-design behavior**",
    "text": "**Correction — this was not a sync failure, it was correct, by-design behavior**: verified 2026-09-27 by reading `dehydrate.ts` and `threadScope.ts` directly. A `.threads/`-scoped `BlockNode`/`ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` is unconditionally excluded from `dehydrateToJsonLd` (the tracked mirror) and written only via `dehydrateStateToJsonLd`, into `.state/` — for every such node, not intermittently. Confirmed live against the restored Turn 8 Report: it's in `Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld` (5 occurrences) and correctly absent from tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` (0 occurrences), exactly as design intends. `--flush` did its job the whole time; nothing needed forcing. The `service restart`'s real effect was unrelated: its own `pruneUnreachableTombstones` GC, which happened to run at the same moment. The original entry below is left for the record, corrected rather than deleted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZE18004",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC9JSGR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC9JSGR001:props:StringProp:00CRC9JYKR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRC9JSGR001:props:StringProp:00CRC9JYKR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Correction — this was not a sync failure, it was correct, by-design behavior**",
    "text": "**Correction — this was not a sync failure, it was correct, by-design behavior**: verified 2026-09-27 by reading `dehydrate.ts` and `threadScope.ts` directly. A `.threads/`-scoped `BlockNode`/`ArtifactNode`/`FolderNode` is unconditionally excluded from `dehydrateToJsonLd` (the tracked mirror) and written only via `dehydrateStateToJsonLd`, into `.state/` — for every such node, not intermittently. Confirmed live against the restored Turn 8 Report: it's in `Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld` (5 occurrences) and correctly absent from tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` (0 occurrences), exactly as design intends. `--flush` did its job the whole time; nothing needed forcing. The `service restart`'s real effect was unrelated: its own `pruneUnreachableTombstones` GC, which happened to run at the same moment. Left uncorrected above, since retyping the mistake in place would erase the trail — this is the standing correction.",
