    "title": "**Removing a thread subtree leaks its descendants' tombstones into the tracked mirror**",
    "text": "**Removing a thread subtree leaks its descendants' tombstones into the tracked mirror**: this contradicts [Threads persist to `.state/` by membership, not by class](../design/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3WYRG8001), which says pruning a thread is an ordinary `remove`. Found 2026-09-27 when resetting both threads.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR003",
      "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR004",
      "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR005",
      "BlockNode:00CVNX6YD0001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR003:props:StringProp:00CRCGRNAG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR003:props:StringProp:00CRCGRNAG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Mechanism**",
    "text": "**Mechanism**: `aperas remove` on a thread heading keeps the removed root's `parent`, so the root stays in `Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld`. Every descendant loses its `parent`, so the ancestor walk to `artifacts/.threads/` no longer reaches it, and it dehydrates into tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld`. Placement has to hold for tombstones too, not only while an ancestor under `.threads` is still reachable.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Repro**",
    "text": "**Repro**: remove `## tree --format flag` in `.threads/grapher.md` (`BlockNode:00CR6BH1PR001`). The heading lands in `.state`; its Task, Turn, Ask, Work and Report nodes (e.g. `BlockNode:00CR6BKSS8001`, `BlockNode:00CR6BRTPG001`) land tracked with `tombstonedAt` and no `parent`. 15 thread tombstones leaked this way, and they are now in `AperasKG`'s git index.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Also needed**",
    "text": "**Also needed**: moving the already-leaked tombstones back into `.state`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR006:links:Link:00CRCGRNB8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CE1GW4Y800G",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR006:links:Link:00CRCGRNB8000:props:StringProp:00CRCGRNB8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "427"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`aperas tree --view` doubles a link's `#id/` fragment when the stored href already carries one**",
    "text": "**`aperas tree --view` doubles a link's `#id/` fragment when the stored href already carries one**: `bakeResolvedLinkIds` in `packages/core/src/apeironNgn/node.ts` appends `#id/<target>` to every relative href it has a resolved `Link` for, whether or not the href already has a fragment. The base skill tells agents to write `[title](../x.md#id/BlockNode:<ID>)`, which is exactly that case. This belongs to the preview text of [Rendering](../design/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CE1GW4Y800G). Found 2026-09-27.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW63800A",
    "type": "listItem",
