    "title": "**A tombstoned node stays listed in its parent's `children` array**",
    "text": "**A tombstoned node stays listed in its parent's `children` array**: `ArtifactNode:00CR5ANC6G000` (`.threads/coder.md`'s holder) still lists `BlockNode:00CR6BXGTR001` as a child, though it was tombstoned during the September 27 thread reset. `tree`/`unfold` hide it correctly since both filter tombstoned nodes at render time, but `aperas show` on the parent exposes the stale reference, and a bare anchor-less `insert` after it would have needed a live anchor. Not yet investigated further; possibly related to [the tracked-mirror tombstone leak above](#id/BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002), a different symptom of the same area of the code.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE1GW638002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
