  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CRCH1DBR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`aperas update --text-only` always reports \"overflow prepended, no reconciliation\", even with zero overflow**",
    "text": "**`aperas update --text-only` always reports \"overflow prepended, no reconciliation\", even with zero overflow**: `kgUpdate.ts:444` prints that message unconditionally whenever `--text-only` is passed, not gated on whether any content actually followed the leading paragraph. Confirmed live: a bare single-line `--text-only` update against a disposable throwaway node printed the same message with nothing to prepend. Behavior is correct — nothing gets reconciled away either way — only the message is misleading. Found 2026-09-27.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF2AEAX0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
