  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas/SKILL.md",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG003",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG004",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG005",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG006",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG007",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG008",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00R",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG003",
    "text": "```\n---\nname: aperas\ndescription: >-\n  Before anything else in this project — first turn, every session, whatever the task looks like, including when it looks unrelated, trivial, read-only, or like one quick lookup — check memory for a standing decision on whether Aperas manages this session. Do this without loading this skill, and never ask permission to do it or offer it as an option; just do it. If a decision is recorded, follow it. If none is, ask with AskUserQuestion using exactly these choices — Never / Not now / Yes, this session only / Yes, all sessions — and record only 'all sessions' or 'never' durably, so a session-scoped answer is asked again next session. Load this skill only once the answer is yes, and with it `aperas-orchestrator` if you are the main agent, or the appropriate subagent skill (e.g. `aperas-grapher` or `aperas-coder`) if not. \n  Aperas is this project's external memory: a knowledge graph, worked through the `aperas` CLI, holding what has been decided, tried, found and planned, and the medium the three roles communicate through.\n---\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v4** — Base skill for all Aperas roles.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG005",
    "text": "Aperas is an evidence-based knowledge-graph documentation system. This skill establishes the common mental model, traversal discipline, multi-agent protocol, and CLI mechanics used across all roles (`aperas-orchestrator`, `aperas-grapher`, `aperas-coder`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG006",
    "text": "> **Aperas-repo insiders**: `aperas` is published as a package (`npm install -g aperas`), but this repo develops it from source. Running bare `aperas <verb>` invokes whatever is globally installed, not your local changes. Run commands from `Aperas/monorepo/` as:\n> ```bash\n> npm run aperas -- <verb> ...\n> ```\n> In normal projects using the published tool, run bare `aperas <verb> ...`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG007",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "#### 1. Philosophy",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG009",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00E",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00H",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00M"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### The Apeiron is the source; `.md` files under `artifacts/` are shadows it casts",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG008",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00A",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00B",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00C",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00A:props:StringProp:00CS1597T0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00A:props:StringProp:00CS1597T0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MG00A",
    "text": "Projections can be regenerated from the graph at any time.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG00B",
    "text": "A projected markdown file is never where a change is made, and never where a question is answered.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG00C",
    "text": "Modifying a projection mistakes the shadow for the source. Reading it gives text stripped of links, backlinks, and graph position.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG00D",
    "text": "Projections on disk can be **unprojected or stale**. Graph truth lives only in Apeiron.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### A claim and its provenance are one object",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG008",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00F",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00F:props:StringProp:00CS1597T8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00F:props:StringProp:00CS1597T8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MG00F",
    "text": "A claim without a link to its source/evidence is incomplete.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG00G",
    "text": "Readers must be able to drill down into the supporting evidence subgraph via forward links or backlinks. One of the two must exist before a claim is left in place.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Substance matures",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG008",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00J",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00J:props:StringProp:00CS1597T8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00J:props:StringProp:00CS1597TG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Content Axis**",
    "text": "**Content Axis**: Formless prose hardens from `discussion` Freeflow into typed concerns (`design`, `issues`, `planning`, `history`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Topology Axis**",
    "text": "**Topology Axis**: Relationships begin mediated by discussion nodes citing both ends; as they prove load-bearing, they crystallize into direct citations.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### System memory over human memory",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG008",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00N",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00P",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00Q"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00N:props:StringProp:00CS1597TG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00N:props:StringProp:00CS1597TG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MG00N",
    "text": "Nobody working this graph will remember across weeks or context windows.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MG00P",
    "text": "The graph is not just a passive repository; it actively notices structural gaps and omissions unbidden (via queries, checks, and backlinks).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
