      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00Y",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00Z"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00S:props:StringProp:00CS1597VG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00S:props:StringProp:00CS1597VG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR00S",
    "text": "Views provide structured lenses into the graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Triage active views**",
    "text": "**Triage active views**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00V"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR00V",
    "text": "```bash\n  aperas profile list <profile>   # e.g. antigravity or claude\n  aperas tree --view <view-name>\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00T",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Manage views**",
    "text": "**Manage views**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00X"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR00X",
    "text": "```bash\n  aperas profile create-view <name> --profile <handle>\n  aperas unfold <ref> --view <name> --flush\n  aperas fold <ref> --view <name> --flush\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00W",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR00Y",
    "text": "Keep views scoped per task. A view left pointing at last session's work is worse than no view.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR00Z",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR00R",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "#### 3. Discipline",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR011",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01E",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01P",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01V",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Y",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR023"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Three Roles, One Graph",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR012",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR013"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR012",
    "text": "| Role | Runs As | Writes | Reads |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Orchestrator** | Active session | `discussion` Freeflow, thread `**Ask**` nodes | Graph, threads, **and source code/diffs/tests during Verification** |\n| **Grapher** | Subagent | Everything else in graph (deep read/write, promotions, thread lifecycle) | Graph, thread reports |\n| **Coder** | Subagent | Source code, `.threads/coder.md` | Source code, graph context |",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR011",
    "type": "table",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR013",
    "text": "> [!CRITICAL]\n> **Orchestrator Role Gate**:\n> **NEVER START WITH** surveying or modifying source code when a task begins. Always delegate initial graph and code surveys to the Grapher and Coder subagents.\n> The Orchestrator inspects source code, git diffs, and test outputs **ONLY at the Verification stage** (Step 7 of the task loop).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR011",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### The Task Loop (9 Steps)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR015",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR016",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR017",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR018",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR019",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01A",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01B",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01C",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR015:props:StringProp:00CS1597W0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR015:props:StringProp:00CS1597W0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Open Task**",
    "text": "**Open Task**: Orchestrator creates `## <topic>` and `### <task>` in `.threads/grapher.md` and `.threads/coder.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Grapher Survey**",
    "text": "**Grapher Survey**: Grapher surveys graph context (design, issues, drift), writes Report in `.threads/grapher.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Orchestrator Review**",
    "text": "**Orchestrator Review**: Orchestrator reads Grapher Report (`aperas tree --view <p>-grapher-orchestrator`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Coder Survey**",
    "text": "**Coder Survey**: Orchestrator asks Coder to map code behavior (no code edits). Coder reports in `.threads/coder.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Grapher Files Survey**",
    "text": "**Grapher Files Survey**: Grapher records Coder findings into graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Coder Change**",
    "text": "**Coder Change**: Coder applies fix and runs tests, reporting diff and results.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Orchestrator Verification**",
    "text": "**Orchestrator Verification**: Orchestrator verifies diff and test output directly (`npm run verify`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Grapher Files Result**",
    "text": "**Grapher Files Result**: Grapher promotes findings, marks issues resolved.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finishing Turn**",
    "text": "**Finishing Turn**: Repeat steps 6–8 as needed, then Grapher executes the finishing turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Thread Structure (`.threads/{grapher,coder}.md`)",
    "text": "Threads are stored under `.threads/` and are **Git-ignored**. Nothing above the thread tier links into a thread.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01F",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01G",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01F",
    "text": "A thread represents the complete working memory of a subagent across turns. When starting a fresh thread or continuing an existing one, use this tree structure:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01E",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01G",
    "text": "```markdown\n# Grapher thread                              ← H1: role thread root (in fresh thread)\n## <topic>                                   ← H2: named by the user\n### <task>                                   ← H3: set by the orchestrator\n#### Turn <n>                                ← H4: one exchange with the orchestrator\n- **Ask**: <what is wanted, in a sentence>   ← orchestrator; root of <p>-orchestrator-grapher\n  - [<argument>](../design/x.md#id/BlockNode:…) — why it matters here\n- **Work**: <the approach, in a line>        ← subagent; subturns nested under it\n  - <subturn 1: batch progress and exact tool results>\n  - <subturn 2: files inspected, lines, failure output>\n- **Report**: <the outcome, in a sentence>   ← subagent; root of <p>-grapher-orchestrator\n  - [<changed or found node>](…) — what changed, or what it shows\n  - **Question**: <whatever the Ask left unsettled>\n  - **Tool gap — <what>**: <a workaround built, a call that failed or hung>\n  - **Tool gap — <what else>**: <a second one, if the turn hit more than one>\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01E",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "###### Core Thread Disciplines",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01J",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01K",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01M",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01N"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01J:props:StringProp:00CS1597WG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01J:props:StringProp:00CS1597WG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**A follow-up is a new turn, not an edit to an old one**",
    "text": "**A follow-up is a new turn, not an edit to an old one**: Never mutate prior turns to add follow-up work.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Every turn has subturns**",
    "text": "**Every turn has subturns**: At least one per batch of tool calls. Record the essence of each tool result (failing line numbers, node IDs, counts, filenames) — not just \"ran tests\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Record friction**",
    "text": "**Record friction**: Record workarounds, retries, and tool failures under distinct `**Tool gap — <topic>**` lead-ins (identical lead-ins collide on slug generation).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Ask back instead of guessing**",
    "text": "**Ask back instead of guessing**: Not only against the Ask, but for **anything unsure during execution** — unexpected code behaviors, conflicting requirements or evidence, missing schemas/dependencies, architectural trade-offs, or unexpected tool failures — the subagent **must stop and ask back** via a `**Question**` in its Report rather than making speculative assumptions. Guessing wastes full round trips and creates technical debt.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Hand-Off Views & Zooming",
    "text": "The view carries the graph state (`this`); the chat message carries only control and pointers.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Q",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01R",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01S",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01T"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01Q",
    "text": "| View Name | Owner | Faces | Rooted On |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `<p>-<topic>` | Orchestrator | User | `discussion/<topic>.md` `## Dashboard` |\n| `<p>-orchestrator-grapher` | Orchestrator | Grapher | Current Ask in `.threads/grapher.md` |\n| `<p>-orchestrator-coder` | Orchestrator | Coder | Current Ask in `.threads/coder.md` |\n| `<p>-grapher-orchestrator` | Grapher | Orchestrator | Current Report in `.threads/grapher.md` |\n| `<p>-coder-orchestrator` | Coder | Orchestrator | Current Report in `.threads/coder.md` |",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01P",
    "type": "table",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Zooming Rule**",
    "text": "**Zooming Rule**: On every hand-off, zoom the view onto the current turn's root (`**Ask**` or `**Report**`):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01S",
    "text": "```bash\naperas zoom <turn-node-id> --view <view-name> --flush\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01P",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01T",
    "text": "The receiver always reads `aperas tree --view <sender-view>` before doing any work.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01P",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Every Claim Carries Its Source",
    "text": "Before leaving a claim in place (a freeflow finding, thread report, or formal doc entry), confirm its provenance:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01W",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01X"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01W:props:StringProp:00CS1597WR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01W:props:StringProp:00CS1597WR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR01W",
    "text": "Threads and freeflow cite forward to what they rest on.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01X",
    "text": "Formal doc entries are checked via `aperas backlinks <id> --text` to confirm supporting links exist.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Citation Direction & Gradients",
    "text": "The concern taxonomy forms a strict abstraction gradient:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Z",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR020",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR021",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR022"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR01Z",
    "text": "```\ndesign (most abstract)\n  ↑\nissues / planning / history\n  ↑\nconcepts.md\n  ↑\ndiscussion\n  ↑\nthreads (least abstract — Git-ignored)\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Y",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR020:props:StringProp:00CS1597X0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR020:props:StringProp:00CS1597X0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR020",
    "text": "Citations may point **UP** or **SIDEWAYS**.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR021",
    "text": "Citations must **NEVER point DOWN** (except normative singular references, such as a doc's `# Context` section).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR022",
    "text": "Nothing above the thread tier may link into `.threads/`. Content reaches the graph from threads by the Grapher copying it up, never by citation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR01Y",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Stage Each Verified Step",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR010",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR024",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR027",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR028",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR029"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR024",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR024:props:StringProp:00CS1597X0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR024:props:StringProp:00CS1597X8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "After each verified mutation, stage changes immediately with `git add`",
    "text": "After each verified mutation, stage changes immediately with `git add`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR023",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR025",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR026"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR025",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR025:props:StringProp:00CS1597X8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR025:props:StringProp:00CS1597X8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR025",
    "text": "Code changes in the code repo.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR024",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR026",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR026",
    "text": "Graph mutations in `AperasKG/`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR024",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR027",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Important Rationale**",
    "text": "**Important Rationale**: Staging creates a running checkpoint for **your own recovery when an operation goes wrong (usually!)**. If a subsequent command misreconciles or corrupts state, `git restore` / `git diff` against the staged index recovers cleanly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR023",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR028",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR028",
    "text": "**Staging only, never commit** (`git commit` is reserved for the user).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR023",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR029",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR029",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR023",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "#### 4. Mechanics",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02B",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02D",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02F",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02J",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02S",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02W",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR030",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR033",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0003",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0008",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000C",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000H",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000M",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000S",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000W",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Z",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0012",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0015",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0017",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Quick Syntax & Command Reference",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR02C",
    "text": "| Operation | Command Pattern | Key Rule / Note |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Peek Node** | `aperas unfold <ref>` | Read-only peek; does not mutate view |\n| **Unfold into View** | `aperas unfold <ref> --view <name> --flush` | Adds `<ref>` to view's unfolds set |\n| **Inspect Backlinks** | `aperas backlinks <id> --text` | Inspects dependents and provenance |\n| **Render View Tree** | `aperas tree --view <name>` | Renders structured lens of the view |\n| **Raw Stored Text** | `aperas show <ref> --text` | Exact stored text undecorated (safe for editing) |\n| **Full Node State** | `aperas show <ref>` | Inspects props, tombstonedAt, links, parent, children |\n| **Insert Turn Node** | `cat ask.md \\| aperas insert <turn-id> --flush` | Appends Ask/Report node to turn heading |\n| **Zoom View** | `aperas zoom <node-id> --view <name> --flush` | Re-roots view onto current Ask or Report |\n| **Retitle Heading** | `echo \"## Title\" \\| aperas update <id> --text-only --flush` | **Must use `--text-only`** to preserve child blocks |\n| **Update List Item** | `echo \"text\" \\| aperas update <id> --flush` | Bare text replaces text and children |\n| **Clear Checkbox** | `echo \"- text\" \\| aperas update <id> --flush` | Bare bullet `- ` removes checkbox entirely |\n| **Insert List Item** | `echo \"- text\" \\| aperas insert <parent> --after <sibling> --flush` | Unordered items **must include bullet `- `** |\n| **Reposition Node** | `aperas insert <node-id> --after <anchor-id> --flush` | **No stdin piped** moves node without reminting ID |\n| **Retype Block** | `aperas retype <ref> --to <type>` | In-place kind change (`h1`..`h6`, `listItem`, etc.) |\n| **Sweep Links** | `aperas check-links` (or `--repair`) | Verifies internal wikilink integrity |\n| **Restart Service** | `aperas service restart` | Flushes and restarts daemon from disk |\n| **Reload Disk State** | `aperas reload -- --discard` | Clears memory orphans after failed insert |",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02B",
    "type": "table",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Common Command Patterns",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR02E",
    "text": "```bash\n# 1. Traversal & Inspection\naperas unfold <ref>                           # Read-only peek\naperas unfold <ref> --view <name> --flush     # Unfold into view\naperas backlinks <id> --text                  # Inspect backlinks and provenance\naperas tree --view <name>                     # Render view tree\naperas show <ref> --text                      # Stored text only (undecorated)\n\n# 2. Turns & Hand-Off Zooming\ncat ask.md | aperas insert <turn-id> --flush  # Insert Ask/Report node\naperas zoom <node-id> --view <name> --flush   # Re-root view onto node\n\n# 3. Safe Edits\necho \"## New Title\" | aperas update <heading-id> --text-only --flush   # Heading update\necho \"Updated content\" | aperas update <item-id> --flush               # List item update\necho \"- New child\" | aperas insert <parent-id> --after <sibling-id> --flush # List item insert\n\n# 4. Service & Integrity\naperas check-links                            # Sweep internal link integrity\naperas check-links --repair                   # Re-resolve and persist repairs\naperas service restart                        # Flush and restart service daemon\naperas reload -- --discard                    # Discard memory state and re-read disk\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02D",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Path Resolution",
    "text": "Paths passed to `aperas` CLI resolve relative to the graph's `artifacts` root defined in `aperas.config.json` (e.g. `discussion/foo.md` relative to `AperasKG/artifacts/`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02G",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02G:props:StringProp:00CS1597XR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02G:props:StringProp:00CS1597XR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**CORRECT**",
    "text": "**CORRECT**: `aperas project discussion/foo.md`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**INCORRECT**",
    "text": "**INCORRECT**: `aperas project AperasKG/artifacts/discussion/foo.md` (fails with \"No ingested ArtifactNode or FolderNode found\").",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Wikilink & Link Syntax",
    "text": "The link resolver recognizes:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02K",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02M",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02Q",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02R"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02K:props:StringProp:00CS1597XR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02K:props:StringProp:00CS1597XR003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Bare relative paths** (`./file.md` or `../folder/file.md`)",
    "text": "**Bare relative paths** (`./file.md` or `../folder/file.md`): Resolve directly to the whole target `ArtifactNode` or `FolderNode`. No fragment needed when citing an entire document or folder.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Fragment links** (`path#id/BlockNode:<ID>` or `path#anchor`)",
    "text": "**Fragment links** (`path#id/BlockNode:<ID>` or `path#anchor`): Required when linking to a specific block or heading *within* an artifact.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02N",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02N:props:StringProp:00CS1597XR004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02N:props:StringProp:00CS1597XR005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Direct node ID",
    "text": "Direct node ID: `[Title](../folder/file.md#id/BlockNode:<ID>)` (unambiguous, preferred).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Anchor match",
    "text": "Anchor match: `[Title](../folder/file.md#heading-title)` (matches `name='...' class='aperas-anchor'`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Scheme prefixes**",
    "text": "**Scheme prefixes**: `[[code]]`, `aperas://tree/<path>`, or `aperas://id/<ID>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "*Note*",
    "text": "*Note*: An internal block link without `#id/...` or `#anchor` resolves to the whole document, not the specific block. Always verify block-level links with `aperas backlinks BlockNode:<ID> --text` on the target block.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02J",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Anchor Placement — The Bold-Colon Rule",
    "text": "In list items, the lead-in colon must sit **outside** the bold span:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02T",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02V"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02T:props:StringProp:00CS1597Y0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02T:props:StringProp:00CS1597Y0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR02T",
    "text": "`**Term**: text` (CORRECT)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR02V",
    "text": "`**Term:** text` (INCORRECT — rejected by lead-in detector; anchor gets spliced into random text).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Sketching a Structure",
    "text": "Build new headings or subtrees directly in the graph with zero disk-first authoring:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02X",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02Z"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02X:props:StringProp:00CS1597Y8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02X:props:StringProp:00CS1597Y8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Create placeholder node",
    "text": "Create placeholder node:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR02Y",
    "text": "```bash\n   aperas resolve --create-holder <path> --titles \"<Heading Title>\"\n   ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02X",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR02Z",
    "text": "Populate content using `aperas update` and `aperas insert`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR030",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### `--after` and `--before` Anchors",
    "text": "The anchor node must be a **direct child** of `<path>`, not a descendant:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR031",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR032"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR031",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR031:props:StringProp:00CS1597Y8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR031:props:StringProp:00CS1597Y8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR031",
    "text": "Check tree structure first via `aperas tree` or `aperas show <path>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR030",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR032",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR032",
    "text": "If an anchor is invalid, the insert fails after hydrating nodes into memory, leaving live orphans. Recover by running `aperas reload -- --discard`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR030",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR033",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Inserting into Lists",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR034",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR038"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR034",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR034:props:StringProp:00CS1597YG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR034:props:StringProp:00CS1597YG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Unordered Lists**",
    "text": "**Unordered Lists**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR033",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR035",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR037"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR035",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR035:props:StringProp:00CS1597YG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR035:props:StringProp:00CS1597YG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Pipe bare text **with its bullet marker**",
    "text": "Pipe bare text **with its bullet marker**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR034",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR036"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR036",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR036",
    "text": "```bash\n    echo \"- new item\" | aperas insert <parent-id> --after <sibling-id> --flush\n    ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR035",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR037",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Never pipe plain text without a bullet**",
    "text": "**Never pipe plain text without a bullet**: it parses as a paragraph, breaking the list run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR034",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR038",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Ordered Lists**",
    "text": "**Ordered Lists**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR033",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR039",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR039",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR039:props:StringProp:00CS1597YG004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR039:props:StringProp:00CS1597YG005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR039",
    "text": "Appending at the end is safe when the numbering continues (`n. new item`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR038",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR03A",
    "text": "Inserting in the middle requires renumbering everything after it. Target the **parent heading** (`aperas update <heading-id>`) and pipe the heading line plus the *complete* list verbatim with the new item included.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR038",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Updating an Existing List Item (`aperas update <item-id>`)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03C",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03F",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03J",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0000",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0001",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03C:props:StringProp:00CS1597YR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03C:props:StringProp:00CS1597YR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Ordinary text change**",
    "text": "**Ordinary text change**: Pipe bare text with **no bullet marker**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03D",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR03D",
    "text": "```bash\n  echo \"updated text\" | aperas update <item-id> --flush\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03C",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "*Note*",
    "text": "*Note*: This replaces the item's text **and its children**. Restate children if you want to keep them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03C",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Checkboxes**",
    "text": "**Checkboxes**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03G",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03G:props:StringProp:00CS1597YR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03G:props:StringProp:00CS1597YR003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR03G",
    "text": "Marker `- [x]` or `- [ ]` sets checkbox state.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR03H",
    "text": "Bare `- ` with text (marker-less bullet) **removes an existing checkbox entirely**.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Ordered List Items**",
    "text": "**Ordered List Items**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03K",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03M"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03K:props:StringProp:00CS1597Z0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03K:props:StringProp:00CS1597Z0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593MR03K",
    "text": "Use `n.` marker when updating an ordered item (e.g. `echo \"1. updated text\" | aperas update <item-id> --flush`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593MR03M",
    "text": "Updating an item never changes its position in the list (ordered or unordered, its sequence position is preserved). To reorder or renumber, update the parent heading with the complete list.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Deliberately blank text**",
    "text": "**Deliberately blank text**: A bare `- ` (bullet with nothing after it) clears the item's text while allowing children to be attached.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Title Tracking**",
    "text": "**Title Tracking**: The title updates if text has a bold lead-in (`**Term**: ...`). Without one, title falls back to the item's ID.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Symmetry Rule**",
    "text": "**Symmetry Rule**: Whichever piece you do not restate is wiped. If you pipe only text with no children, existing children are tombstoned. Restate whichever side you are not modifying.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR03B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Updating a Heading (`--text-only`)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0004",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0004:props:StringProp:00CS1597Z8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0004:props:StringProp:00CS1597Z8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N0004",
    "text": "Calling `aperas update <heading-id>` without `--text-only` reconciles children against piped input. Piping just `## Title` tombstones all existing child blocks!",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Always use `--text-only`** when retitling headings",
    "text": "**Always use `--text-only`** when retitling headings:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0006",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0006",
    "text": "```bash\n  echo \"## Corrected Heading\" | aperas update <heading-id> --text-only --flush\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0005",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0007",
    "text": "`--text-only` updates `.title` and `.text` while leaving child blocks completely untouched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0005",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Changing Block Types (`aperas retype`)",
    "text": "Convert a block's type in place while preserving ID, links, parent, and position:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0009",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000A",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0009",
    "text": "```bash\naperas retype <ref> --to <type>   # h1..h6, paragraph, listItem, code, blockquote, table\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0008",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000A:props:StringProp:00CS1597Z8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000A:props:StringProp:00CS1597Z8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N000A",
    "text": "Heading → non-heading folds title into text as `**Title**: <body>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N000B",
    "text": "Non-heading → heading cuts lead-in term back into the heading line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Renaming Artifacts",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000D",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000D:props:StringProp:00CS1597ZG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000D:props:StringProp:00CS1597ZG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Single Artifact**",
    "text": "**Single Artifact**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000E",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N000E",
    "text": "```bash\n  git mv old.md new.md\n  aperas ingest <new-path> --track --flush\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000D",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N000F",
    "text": "Rename detection matches by abstract-text equality against tracked nodes whose old path vanished.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000D",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Cross-Referencing Docs**",
    "text": "**Cross-Referencing Docs**: Complete all internal content/heading/path updates first while files remain at old names; verify with `check-links`, then execute `git mv`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Shell Quoting Gotcha",
    "text": "A piped `echo \"...\"` silently drops nested double quotes in bash (`\"foo \"bar\" baz\"` becomes `foo bar baz`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000J"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000J:props:StringProp:00CS1597ZG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000J:props:StringProp:00CS1597ZG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N000J",
    "text": "For content with quotes, write to a temporary file first and pipe via `cat`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N000K",
    "text": "```bash\n  cat /tmp/content.md | aperas update <id> --flush\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000J",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Service State & Recovery",
