    "text": "```bash\n  aperas service restart\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000N",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Discard uncommitted in-memory mutations and reload disk state",
    "text": "Discard uncommitted in-memory mutations and reload disk state:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000R"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N000R",
    "text": "```bash\n  aperas reload -- --discard\n  ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Q",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Raw Node State Inspection",
    "text": "Preview commands (`tree`, `unfold`, `backlinks`) display truncated abstracts. To inspect exact stored state:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000T",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000V"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N000T",
    "text": "```bash\naperas show <ref>          # Full record: props, tombstonedAt, parent, children, links, text\naperas show <ref> --text   # Exact stored text only, undecorated\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000S",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "To edit safely",
    "text": "To edit safely: dump `aperas show <ref> --text > edit.txt`, modify what is needed, and `cat edit.txt | aperas update <ref> --flush`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000S",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### `aperas unfold` — Bare vs. `--view`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000X",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000X:props:StringProp:00CS159800000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000X:props:StringProp:00CS159800001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Bare `aperas unfold <ref>`",
    "text": "Bare `aperas unfold <ref>`: Read-only peek; does not mutate any view.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`aperas unfold <ref> --view <name> --flush`",
    "text": "`aperas unfold <ref> --view <name> --flush`: Adds `<ref>` to `<name>`'s `unfolds` set for persistent rendering in `aperas tree --view <name>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Tombstoned Nodes",
    "text": "Tombstoned nodes and their subtrees are hidden everywhere by default:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0010",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0011"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0010:props:StringProp:00CS159800002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0010:props:StringProp:00CS159800003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N0010",
    "text": "`aperas tree` and `aperas unfold` omit them unless `--tombstoned` is passed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0011",
    "text": "`aperas unfold <tombstoned-id>` errors out without `--tombstoned`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N000Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Full-Text Search via Raw Store",
    "text": "Grep the JSON-LD mirror directly for fast, untruncated content search:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0013",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0014"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0013",
    "text": "```bash\ngrep -n -C3 '<pattern>' AperasKG/Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0012",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0014",
    "text": "Matches are candidate IDs. Always inspect live status via `aperas show <id>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0012",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Comparing Distant Docs (View as a Lens)",
    "text": "Use `--view` to bring distant parts of the tree together side by side:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0016"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0016",
    "text": "```bash\nfor doc in issues/a.md discussion/b.md design/c.md; do\n  aperas unfold \"$doc\" --view comparison-lens --flush\ndone\naperas tree --view comparison-lens\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0015",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Breadcrumbs in `aperas tree`",
    "text": "The first line of an `aperas tree` render is a breadcrumb: `aperas://tree/<path>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0018",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0019",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0018:props:StringProp:00CS159808000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0018:props:StringProp:00CS159808001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N0018",
    "text": "Represents the walkable path of the starting apex, directly reusable as a `<ref>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0019",
    "text": "Appears once at the top; child lines are implicitly relative to it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001A",
    "text": "When an unfolded link escapes into an external viewcone, an indented breadcrumb marks the jump.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0017",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Link Integrity Sweeps",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MR02A",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001C",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001C",
    "text": "```bash\naperas check-links           # Sweep corpus for unresolved internal wikilinks\naperas check-links --repair  # Re-resolve and persist repairs to store\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001B",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001D",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001B",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "#### 5. Reference",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG002",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001F",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001G",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001H",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001J",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001F:props:StringProp:00CS15980R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001F:props:StringProp:00CS15980R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N001F",
    "text": "`AperasKG/artifacts/design/linking.md` — Canonical spec for addressing, anchors, and wikilink syntax.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001G",
    "text": "`AperasKG/artifacts/design/documentation.md` — Concern taxonomy and Freeflow document structures.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001H",
    "text": "`AperasKG/artifacts/design/aperas-skill.md` — The four-level architecture, citation directions, and promotion lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`archive/Aperas-design.md` — Founding philosophy",
    "text": "`archive/Aperas-design.md` — Founding philosophy: Apeiron / Aperas / Peras.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### Open Tool Gaps",
    "text": "Tracked in the graph rather than accumulating here:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001E",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001M",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001N",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001M:props:StringProp:00CS15980R002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001M:props:StringProp:00CS15980R003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "`aperas resolve`'s title-ambiguity check does not filter tombstoned candidates",
    "text": "`aperas resolve`'s title-ambiguity check does not filter tombstoned candidates: a dead holder can still make a live path read as ambiguous (`discussion/core.md`'s Freeflow). Workaround: resolve the live node by ID directly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001N",
    "text": "The link-integrity drift check is built and live (`aperas check-links`, see *Mechanics* — `issues/linking.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001P",
    "text": "The `verify.ts` id-anchor emission idempotency failure is fixed and passing (`discussion/core.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator/SKILL.md",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593MG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001R",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001S",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001T",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001V",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001W",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001X",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Y",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0026",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002J",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002T",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N800G",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N800P",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N8011"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001R",
    "text": "```\n---\nname: aperas-orchestrator\ndescription: >-\n  The orchestrator role in Aperas multi-agent work: the session talking with the user. Records\n  the conversation as discussion freeflow and runs the task loop by handing off to the\n  aperas-grapher and aperas-coder subagents through threads and views. Load with the base\n  `aperas` skill in any session Aperas manages, unless you were started as a subagent.\n---\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Status",
    "text": "Status: **v4** — Orchestrator role skill.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001T",
    "text": "You are the **Orchestrator**. You manage the conversation with the user and drive the multi-agent task loop.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001V",
    "text": "The base `aperas` skill applies in full. This skill defines the specific discipline, triage protocols, and operational gates of the orchestrator role.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001W",
    "text": "> **Aperas-repo insiders**: Run CLI commands from `Aperas/monorepo/` as `npm run aperas -- <verb> ...`. In normal projects using the published package, run bare `aperas <verb> ...`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N001X",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "#### 1. Role Scope & Operational Invariants",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Z",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0023"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### What You Write",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Y",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0020",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0021",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0022"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0020",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0020:props:StringProp:00CS159818000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0020:props:StringProp:00CS159818001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00CS1593N0020",
    "text": "Record user exchanges, decisions, and corrections into `discussion/<topic>.md` `## Freeflow`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0021",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0021",
    "text": "Write your `**Ask**` nodes in `.threads/grapher.md` and `.threads/coder.md`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0022",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0022",
    "text": "Stage each write in `AperasKG/` as it lands (`git add AperasKG/`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0023",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "##### What You Do NOT Do Initially",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Y",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0024",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0025"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0024",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0024",
    "text": "> [!CRITICAL]\n> **Orchestrator Role Gate**:\n> **NEVER START WITH** surveying or modifying source code when a task begins.\n> When the user asks to fix a bug, explore an issue, or write code, **DO NOT** inspect files or run tests yourself.\n> Immediately route the survey and changes to the **Grapher** and **Coder** subagents.\n> You touch source code, git diffs, and test outputs **ONLY at the Verification stage** (Step 7 of the task loop).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0023",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0025",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0025",
    "text": "---",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0023",
    "type": "thematicBreak",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0026",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "#### 2. In-Flight Task Triage (Assessing Current State)",
    "text": "When a session resumes, or when the user mentions an existing issue (e.g. *\"Let's fix X\"*):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N001Q",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0027",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0029",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002E",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0027",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0027:props:StringProp:00CS15981G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0027:props:StringProp:00CS15981G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Check Active Views**",
    "text": "**Check Active Views**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0026",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N0028"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0028",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N0028",
    "text": "```bash\n   aperas profile list <profile>   # e.g. antigravity or claude\n   ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0027",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0029",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Inspect Current Subagent Reports**",
    "text": "**Inspect Current Subagent Reports**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0026",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002A",
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N002A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N002A:props:StringProp:00CS15981G002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N002A:props:StringProp:00CS15981G003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Check if the Coder has already surveyed or implemented",
    "text": "Check if the Coder has already surveyed or implemented:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0029",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CS1593N002B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N002B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CS1593N002B",
    "text": "```bash\n     aperas tree --view <p>-coder-orchestrator\n     ```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CS1593N002A",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CS1593N002C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Check if the Grapher has already surveyed or filed",
    "text": "Check if the Grapher has already surveyed or filed:",
