  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTT270YR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Skill v4.1 refinements — dual memory/rules, positive behavioral bridges, native harness artifact scope, and orientation reordering (2026-10-01)**",
    "text": "**Skill v4.1 refinements — dual memory/rules, positive behavioral bridges, native harness artifact scope, and orientation reordering (2026-10-01)**: analysis and user agreement on resolving operational gating failures. (1) Antigravity has no native \"memory\" tool or store; standing decisions must use dual \"memory/rules\" terminology, persisting to `.agents/rules/aperas.md` in Antigravity or harness memory in Claude, retiring legacy `.agents/aperas_memory.json`. (2) Native harness artifacts (e.g. Antigravity artifacts) are strictly restricted to user communication (proposals, discussion, visual alignment) and must never be used for implementation plans or execution tracking; all implementation and technical state tracking belong solely in Apeiron. (3) Meta-tasks: check if `.agents/` customizations are tracked by git or symlinked into the codebase; if tracked, they are code work owned exclusively by the Coder role. (4) Positive behavioral bridge: restructure Section 2 (Orientation) in `aperas/SKILL.md` to place View Triage & Management first, replacing passive negative paper gates with an imperative positive command to start with View Triage.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTTFHT2G001"
    ]
  },
