    "title": "### aperas — Frontmatter — description, dual memory/rules",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v4 SKILL.md frontmatter](#id/BlockNode:00CS1593MG003)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTTFFW08001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CTTFFW08003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTTFFW08003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CTTFFW08003",
    "text": "```\n---\nname: aperas\ndescription: >-\n  Before anything else in this project — first turn, every session, whatever the task looks like, including when it looks unrelated, trivial, read-only, or like one quick lookup — check memory/rules for a standing decision on whether Aperas manages this session (`.agents/rules/aperas.md` or harness memory). Do this without loading this skill, and never ask permission to do it or offer it as an option; just do it. If a decision is recorded, follow it. If none is, ask with AskUserQuestion using exactly these choices — Never / Not now / Yes, this session only / Yes, all sessions — and record only 'all sessions' or 'never' durably (into `.agents/rules/aperas.md` or harness memory), so a session-scoped answer is asked again next session. Load this skill only once the answer is yes, and with it `aperas-orchestrator` if you are the main agent, or the appropriate subagent skill (e.g. `aperas-grapher` or `aperas-coder`) if not. \n  Aperas is this project's external memory: a knowledge graph, worked through the `aperas` CLI, holding what has been decided, tried, found and planned, and the medium the three roles communicate through.\n---\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CTTFFW08002",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CTTFFW0G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
