    "title": "**Defect — citation direction violations in resolved issue BlockNode:00CTVZR8P0001 (2026-10-01)**",
    "text": "**Defect — citation direction violations in resolved issue BlockNode:00CTVZR8P0001 (2026-10-01)**: During issue resolution, [BlockNode:00CTVZR8P0001](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CTVZR8P0001) in `issues/aperas-skill.md` was written with two illegal downward citations: (1) `Provenance: [BlockNode:00CTTBGC00002](#id/BlockNode:00CTTBGC00002)` (down-citation to `discussion/`), and (2) `Verified by ... [Coder Report]` (down-citation to `.threads/coder.md`). Both violate the abstraction gradient (`design` > `issues`/`history` > `concepts` > `discussion` > `.threads`), which permits citations only upwards or sideways, never downwards. Provenance from discussion must live strictly at the origin pointing up per *Provenance at the Origin*, and threads are ephemeral working memory into which formal docs must never link. Caused by Orchestrator asking for thread citation and Grapher executing without applying the citation direction gate. Formal graph fix deferred for a later pass while subagent roles stabilize.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
