        "@id": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000B:props:StringProp:00CV2CG2FG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Open Task**",
    "text": "**Open Task**: Orchestrator creates `## <topic>` and `### <task>` in `.threads/grapher.md` and `.threads/coder.md` via graph CLI recipes (see [Step 1 Thread Initialization CLI Recipes](#step-1-thread-initialization-cli-recipes)). Never inspect or touch `.threads/` with filesystem tools.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Orchestrator Verification**",
    "text": "**Orchestrator Verification**: Orchestrator verifies diff and test output directly (`npm run verify` for code/engine changes; for skill-only tasks, strictly run `python3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py` and `npm run aperas -- check-links` — never run `npm run verify` on skill tasks).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CV2CFX7000D",
    "text": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **`.threads/` is a graph path, not a local directory**:\n> `.threads/` is a graph node path rooted under `artifacts/.threads/` in `AperasKG/`. Projections under `artifacts/.threads/` are Git-ignored in `AperasKG`.\n> There is no `.threads/` directory in the `Aperas/` code repository. Never run `ls .threads/` or `cat .threads/...`. Access threads strictly through graph commands (`npm run aperas -- tree .threads/grapher.md`, `npm run aperas -- show .threads/grapher.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000A",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CV2CFX7000E",
    "text": "When opening a task in Step 1 of the task loop, use these graph CLI commands without touching the disk:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000A",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CV2CFX7000F",
    "text": "```bash\n# 1. Inspect existing thread tree to locate the topic or root ID:\nnpm run aperas -- tree .threads/grapher.md\n# (To resolve the ArtifactNode ID if starting fresh: npm run aperas -- show .threads/grapher.md)\n\n# 2. Insert ## <topic> heading if it does not yet exist:\necho \"## <topic-name>\" | npm run aperas -- insert <thread-root-id> --flush\n\n# 3. Insert ### <task> heading under the topic:\necho \"### <task-name>\" | npm run aperas -- insert <topic-heading-id> --flush\n\n# 4. Insert #### Turn 1 heading under the task:\necho \"#### Turn 1\" | npm run aperas -- insert <task-heading-id> --flush\n\n# 5. Insert initial **Ask** with Freeflow citation under the turn heading:\ncat << 'EOF' | npm run aperas -- insert <turn-heading-id> --flush\n- **Ask**: Survey graph context for <task-name>\n  - [<Freeflow decision>](../discussion/<topic>.md#id/BlockNode:<ID>) — why it matters here\nEOF\n\n# 6. Repeat for .threads/coder.md when opening coder turns.\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CV2CFX7000A",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
  {
