  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVH4Y5GR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — Claude subagents do not reproduce the failure**",
    "text": "**Finding — Claude subagents do not reproduce the failure**: Of 18 `aperas-grapher`/`aperas-coder` subagent transcripts across 2 Claude Code sessions, none hit the `package.json` ENOENT failure. 13 started at the workspace root (`/home/will/source/Aperas`), the same starting point as Antigravity, and each prefixed its first call with `cd /home/will/source/Aperas/monorepo &&`, so it succeeded on the first try; the other 5 inherited `monorepo/` as their starting directory. Which source led Claude subagents to the `cd` — the \"Aperas-repo insiders\" callout or the orchestrator's Ask — is not determinable from the transcripts. The one transcript containing \"ENOENT\" is a coder reading source code (`serviceLock.ts`), not a failed command.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CV3WG2C0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
