    "title": "**Finding — the service has dropped repeatedly during one task**",
    "text": "**Finding — the service has dropped repeatedly during one task**: In the skill-edit task at least six commands failed because the service was unreachable: the orchestrator's `aperas project`, two of the orchestrator's `insert` calls (the coder's Turn 1 Ask and the grapher's Turn 3 Ask), one in the grapher's Turn 2, and two in the grapher's Turn 3 (an `update`, then a `project`, `tree` and `check-links` sequence). The messages were \"No ApeironNgn service running. Start one with: aperas service start\", and once \"ApeironNgn service did not become ready in time\". Earlier friction entry: [Friction — ApeironNgn service dropped between commands](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVJPV978001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVN8QN08001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK46RQ8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Observation — the process was alive during at least one drop**",
    "text": "**Observation — the process was alive during at least one drop**: After the orchestrator's Turn 1 Ask failed with \"not running\", `aperas service start` answered \"Already running (pid 209499)\". That pid had started at 15:42 local and was the one the commands had been using. So at least some failures are the client not finding or reaching a live service (lock, socket or token), not the process dying. The current service is a different process (pid 220722, started 16:16 local, after the grapher's restart).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVK46RQ8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Observation — what the log shows and doesn't**",
    "text": "**Observation — what the log shows and doesn't**: `service.log` today records only startups (rehydrates at 05:25, 06:13, 08:42 and 09:16 UTC) and no shutdown or reconnect lines, so it does not say why a client could not reach the service. Cause not established; concurrent clients (the orchestrator and a subagent running at the same time) is a hypothesis, not tested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
