    "title": "**Finding — hand-back length follows the harness, not the skill**",
    "text": "**Finding — hand-back length follows the harness, not the skill**: The grapher and coder skills say to reply in chat in 1–2 lines. The harness tells every subagent to deliver its whole report through one `SubagentHandback` call and says plain text at the end is not delivered. All five subagent runs (grapher Turns 1–3, coder Turns 1–2) ended with a one-line plain message (82 chars at most) and put a full report of 11–37 lines into the hand-back. That is obedience to the later, more specific harness instruction, not a violation. Decision (user): do not fight the harness; a long hand-back is fine as long as its content is recorded fully in the Report. No skill change needed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — grapher Turn 1 kept friction out of the graph**",
    "text": "**Finding — grapher Turn 1 kept friction out of the graph**: Its slug collision on two identical `**Question**` lead-ins and its `check-links --repair` appear only in its chat hand-back; its Report has no `Tool gap` node. Grapher Turns 2 and 3 recorded theirs (the service drop; the drift checker's `---` folding). The likely reading is that the subagent took the trouble for its own mistake or a tool-use issue, not a gap in the tool itself.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — collect any trouble, not only tool gaps**",
    "text": "**Decision — collect any trouble, not only tool gaps**: (user) The skills' entry for friction should be reworded so a turn records any trouble it meets — its own mistakes, tool-use problems, and tool gaps alike. Not yet written into the skills.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — the Report template collides on two Questions**",
    "text": "**Finding — the Report template collides on two Questions**: The template shows a bare `**Question**`, and the distinct-lead-in rule names only `Tool gap`. Two Questions in one Report collided in grapher Turn 1; later grapher turns wrote `**Question — <topic>**` on their own.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — projections read for answers**",
    "text": "**Finding — projections read for answers**: Grapher Turn 3 grepped projected `artifacts/*.md` files, and Turn 1 projected with `--dry-run` into scratch files and read those with `sed`/`awk`. The base skill treats projections as shadows that never answer a question. No turn recorded why `unfold` was not enough. Greps of the raw store are the sanctioned bottom-up entry and are not counted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Observation — the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` workaround was repeated by every subagent**",
    "text": "**Observation — the `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` workaround was repeated by every subagent**: 6–29 calls per run carried `env -u`, `unset` or `export LD_LIBRARY_PATH=` boilerplate. The subagents' context includes the auto-memory note about Opcode, which is the likely source. The global `aperas` shim makes it unnecessary for bare `aperas`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Observation — the orchestrator's \"do not stage\" Ask overrode the coder skill, and defeated its purpose**",
    "text": "**Observation — the orchestrator's \"do not stage\" Ask overrode the coder skill, and defeated its purpose**: The coder skill says to stage verified changes, and the base skill's stated reason is that staging is a running checkpoint for the writer's own recovery when an operation goes wrong, not a gate for the orchestrator's final verification. The orchestrator misread \"verified\" as meaning the orchestrator's verification and told the coder not to stage. The subagent followed the latest instruction, as expected, so no change in the coder was needed. The skill text is not ambiguous (user, who read it as clear); the fix is the orchestrator's practice: let each writer stage its own verified work.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — widen the orchestrator's source-reading gate**",
    "text": "**Decision — widen the orchestrator's source-reading gate**: (user) Reviewing a report is part of verification, so the gate's wording should cover any checking, assessment or review, not only a verification step. The orchestrator did read source lines while checking the coder's survey report (`aperas_gate.py`, `kg-doc-ingest`), and that fits the wider wording. One read does not: before any report existed, the orchestrator ran a repo-wide `grep -c` and `ls .claude/skills` to size the request. Not yet written into the skills.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKEM3C8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — the orchestrator's other misses**",
    "text": "**Finding — the orchestrator's other misses**: A filesystem `ls` on `AperasKG/artifacts/*/packaging.md`; Freeflow edits not projected (twice); the shim decision not recorded until asked; a coder Ask citing a block id that did not exist; a grapher Ask drafted with placeholder text; edit lists retyped into an Ask instead of cited; service friction recorded only after several drops. Held up: a fresh subagent per turn, one task per dispatch, decisions in Freeflow before the Asks that cited them, the correct skill-only checks, no edits to code by the orchestrator.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKEK84G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
