    ],
    "title": "**Finding — the design calls the drift check mechanical, but nothing gates on it**",
    "text": "**Finding — the design calls the drift check mechanical, but nothing gates on it**: [Versioning — snapshot, delta, thread](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CF595QQR001) says drift between the file and this record \"is then mechanically checkable, which is the point\" and that `skill_drift.py` \"reports\" the two defects. The code only prints and always exits 0, and the only chains that mention it are text, so a clean-looking run proves nothing about a stale delta or Status line. The design has no statement about the exit status; the decision to exit nonzero on every finding ([Decision — `skill_drift.py` exits nonzero on every finding](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVKV9DPG002)) is the new content, to be recorded in the design when the edit lands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVKY8V6R008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
