    "title": "**Finding — the design is silent on the `Status:` lines, and the record disagreed with them**",
    "text": "**Finding — the design is silent on the `Status:` lines, and the record disagreed with them**: The design says nothing about the `Status:` lines or what keeps them equal to the recorded version; the only `Status` it names is the History concern's Current Status. The graph already held `## v4.3 additions — delta on the v4 snapshot` for the bare-`aperas` edit while all four `Status:` lines read v4.2, which the guard would have caught on its first run. That mismatch is settled by [Decision — bump the skills to v4.3 in this update](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVKQEDTG002) and [Decision — the wording edit rides on the existing v4.3 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVKWW9FG002), and the design wording for the guard follows the edit.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM0R5A0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM0R5A0001:props:StringProp:00CVM0RCT8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM0R5A0001:props:StringProp:00CVM0RCT8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Verification — the v4.3 skill edit inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the v4.3 skill edit inspected and confirmed**: The orchestrator read the `skill_drift.py` change and the wording in the four skills. The Status guard sits after `recorded_roots`, anchored to line start, reading only the four skill files, comparing versions with trailing zeros trimmed, and counting a `Status:` line ahead of the graph as a finding too. The exit is 1 on a Status mismatch, an unrecorded addition or an unaccounted drop, and the accounted-for list stays out of it. No `Tool gap —` lead-in, bare `**Question**`, \"only at Verification\" or v4.2 `Status:` line is left in the four skills; they use `Friction — <topic>`, `Question — <topic>`, the widened gate wording and v4.3. The grapher skill carries the one-sentence delta and guard rule and the split filing rule. The orchestrator ran `skill_drift.py` bare, with `--added` and with `--dropped`: all exit 1, with 0 Status findings, 24 ADDED but unrecorded, 13 DROPPED unaccounted and 171 superseded and accounted for, which is the expected drift until the v4.3 delta is updated. `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. `npm run verify` was not run, as this is a skill-only change. The coder staged its own changes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM0R5A0002",
