            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas — Orchestrator Role Gate",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v4 Base Orchestrator Role Gate](#id/BlockNode:00CS1593MR013)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVM2MEX800C",
    "text": "> [!CRITICAL]\n> **Orchestrator Role Gate**:\n> **NEVER START WITH** surveying or modifying source code when a task begins. Always delegate initial graph and code surveys to the Grapher and Coder subagents.\n> The Orchestrator may read source code, git diffs, and test outputs to check, assess or review a result or claim (a report, a diff, a change's scope), as in Step 7 of the task loop. Mapping code behaviour stays with the Coder.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800B",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
