    ],
    "title": "### aperas — Thread Structure template, Question and Friction lead-ins",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v4 Thread Structure template](#id/BlockNode:00CS1593MR01G)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVM2MEX800E",
    "text": "```markdown\n# Grapher thread                              ← H1: role thread root (in fresh thread)\n## <topic>                                   ← H2: named by the user\n### <task>                                   ← H3: set by the orchestrator\n#### Turn <n>                                ← H4: one exchange with the orchestrator\n- **Ask**: <what is wanted, in a sentence>   ← orchestrator; root of <p>-orchestrator-grapher\n  - [<argument>](../design/x.md#id/BlockNode:…) — why it matters here\n- **Work**: <the approach, in a line>        ← subagent; subturns nested under it\n  - <subturn 1: batch progress and exact tool results>\n  - <subturn 2: files inspected, lines, failure output>\n- **Report**: <the outcome, in a sentence>   ← subagent; root of <p>-grapher-orchestrator\n  - [<changed or found node>](…) — what changed, or what it shows\n  - **Question — <topic>**: <whatever the Ask left unsettled>\n  - **Question — <other topic>**: <a second one, if the Ask left more than one open>\n  - **Friction — <topic>**: <a mistake of your own, a tool-use problem, or a tool gap: a workaround built, a call that failed or hung>\n  - **Friction — <other topic>**: <a second one, if the turn hit more than one>\n```",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800D",
    "type": "code",
    "children": []
  },
