    "title": "### aperas — Core Thread Disciplines, Record friction and Ask back",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v4 Record friction](#id/BlockNode:00CS1593MR01M) [v4 Ask back instead of guessing](#id/BlockNode:00CS1593MR01N)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800G",
      "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800G:props:StringProp:00CVM2MPA0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800G:props:StringProp:00CVM2MPA8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Record friction**",
    "text": "**Record friction**: Record any trouble the turn meets (your own mistakes, tool-use problems, tool gaps, workarounds, retries, failed calls) under `**Friction — <topic>**` lead-ins. A Report with more than one Question or Friction entry gives each its own topic, because identical lead-ins collide on slug generation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Ask back instead of guessing**",
    "text": "**Ask back instead of guessing**: Not only against the Ask, but for **anything unsure during execution** — unexpected code behaviors, conflicting requirements or evidence, missing schemas/dependencies, architectural trade-offs, or unexpected tool failures — the subagent **must stop and ask back** via a `**Question — <topic>**` in its Report rather than making speculative assumptions. Guessing wastes full round trips and creates technical debt.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800J:links:Link:00CVM2MPB0006",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CS1593N0024",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800J:links:Link:00CVM2MPB0006:props:StringProp:00CVM2MPB0007",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator — Orchestrator Role Gate",
    "text": "Supersedes: [v4 Orchestrator Role Gate](#id/BlockNode:00CS1593N0024)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVM2MEX800K",
    "text": "> [!CRITICAL]\n> **Orchestrator Role Gate**:\n> **NEVER START WITH** surveying or modifying source code when a task begins.\n> When the user asks to fix a bug, explore an issue, or write code, **DO NOT** inspect files or run tests yourself.\n> Immediately route the survey and changes to the **Grapher** and **Coder** subagents.\n> You may read source code, git diffs, and test outputs to check, assess or review a result or claim (a report, a diff, a change's scope), as in Step 7 of the task loop. Mapping code behaviour stays with the Coder.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVM2MEX800J",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
