  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM9MMM8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — a coder was told the drift check would fail, and the skills do not say so**",
    "text": "**Finding — a coder was told the drift check would fail, and the skills do not say so**: (user: \"This should be an item in Coder skill and also in Orchestrator skill, not to confuse the Coder when doing skill work\") With the new nonzero exit, `skill_drift.py` fails after every skill edit until the grapher records the delta, which is the expected sequence. Only the orchestrator's Ask told the coder so. The Coder and Orchestrator skills should say it themselves, so no Ask has to.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM9MMM8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Consequence — the one-line verification chain no longer works for skill tasks**",
    "text": "**Consequence — the one-line verification chain no longer works for skill tasks**: (orchestrator) `skill_drift.py && aperas check-links` stops at the expected drift failure and never runs `check-links`. The chain appears in the base skill (Task Loop step 7 and Verification Scope) and in the orchestrator's section 7. The two commands need to be separate, with the note that drift is expected to fail at step 7 and to pass after step 8.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVM9MMM8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Proposal — fold both into v4.3**",
    "text": "**Proposal — fold both into v4.3**: (user asked whether it can be; not yet confirmed to proceed) v4.3 is still unreleased, so the edit updates the existing v4.3 delta entries in place and the `Status:` lines stay at v4.3.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
