    "title": "**Finding — how the drift checker reads a skill delta**",
    "text": "**Finding — how the drift checker reads a skill delta**: (read from `skill_drift.py` by the orchestrator, to elaborate the rest of the Grapher skill item) An entry is a block whose text holds the new skill text in full; the checker looks for each skill unit as a substring of the concatenated recorded text, and the delta root's own text is commentary that is never compared. A replaced unit is named by a `Supersedes: [title](#id/BlockNode:…)` line in the entry, which the checker strips before comparing and reads for `#id/` ids; one entry may name several ids, and a block made only of `Supersedes:` lines removes a unit with no replacement. The version label is the first `vN.N` in the delta's title. Skill units of 40 characters or fewer are skipped, so they can be neither recorded nor checked; the Status guard covers the `Status:` lines separately. The order of work is: the coder edits the file, drift fails and lists the added and dropped units (truncated to 100 and 80 characters), the grapher matches each added unit to the dropped unit it replaces, records the delta and re-runs until it exits 0 with 0 Status, 0 added and 0 dropped. Entries in an unreleased delta are updated in place; entries in a released delta are superseded.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMGWF48000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — the `---` gotcha, from the paragraph splitting**",
    "text": "**Finding — the `---` gotcha, from the paragraph splitting**: (read from `file_units`) Paragraphs split on blank lines and then on list-item starts, so a `---` on the line right after a bullet, with no blank line, stays in that bullet's unit and the unit matches nothing recorded. The grapher worked around it with a `---` child on the entry. A blank line before `---` should avoid it; not tested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMGWF48001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — fold the drift-expectation item and the verification-chain split into v4.3**",
    "text": "**Decision — fold the drift-expectation item and the verification-chain split into v4.3**: (user, answer to a direct question) The Coder and Orchestrator skills each say that `skill_drift.py` fails after a skill edit until the Grapher records the delta, which is expected. The one-line `skill_drift.py && aperas check-links` chain in the base and orchestrator skills becomes two commands with the note that drift is expected to fail at step 7 and pass after step 8. The existing v4.3 delta entries are updated in place and the `Status:` lines stay at v4.3.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMGWF48002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — fix the checker for the `---` gotcha**",
    "text": "**Decision — fix the checker for the `---` gotcha**: (user, answer to a direct question) `file_units` in `skill_drift.py` treats a lone `---` line as a separator, so a `---` after a list item no longer folds into that item's unit.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMGWF48003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — write the Grapher skill's \"Recording a skill delta\" subsection and file the `aperas.ts` mismatch**",
    "text": "**Decision — write the Grapher skill's \"Recording a skill delta\" subsection and file the `aperas.ts` mismatch**: (user, answer to a direct question) The Grapher skill's drift section gains a short subsection covering the delta shape, the order of work and the 40-character limit. The grapher files the `aperas.ts` skill-count mismatch (line 53 lists two skills, `kgSkill.ts` lists five) as an issue in its next turn, together with the History milestones.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMH0MB0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — issue promotion belongs to the Filing Turn, other promotions to the Finishing Turn**",
    "text": "**Decision — issue promotion belongs to the Filing Turn, other promotions to the Finishing Turn**: (user: \"The issue promotion should be done at Filing Turn, and other promotions at Finishing Turn. Let's fold this into the skill v4.3\") A finding that is a defect or a gap is promoted to an `issues/` entry in the Filing Turn that records it; promotions of recurring patterns to `concepts.md` and of settled outcomes to design and history stay in the Finishing Turn. This corrects the orchestrator's earlier statement that promoting a finding to an issue is a finishing-turn step. The Grapher skill's Filing Turn currently says to \"promote to `issues/`/`history/`/`design/` as earned\", which does not draw that line; the orchestrator's Ask had also told the grapher to record findings only.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMJDSX0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification — the second v4.3 skill edit inspected; one wording fix remains**",
    "text": "**Verification — the second v4.3 skill edit inspected; one wording fix remains**: The orchestrator read the new Grapher subsection \"Recording a skill delta\" (six items), the Filing and Finishing Turn wording (defects and gaps to `issues/` in the Filing Turn; recurring patterns and settled outcomes in the Finishing Turn), the new Coder-skill item, the two-command verification lines in the orchestrator and base skills (no `&&` chain of the two commands is left), and the `file_units` change (a lone `---` line now ends a paragraph, with the reason in the docstring). `skill_drift.py` exits 1 as expected: 0 Status, 18 ADDED unrecorded, 9 DROPPED unaccounted, 183 accounted for. `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. Remaining: orchestrator section 7, item 3, still says to document that \"the diff and tests/drift checks were inspected and confirmed clean\", which contradicts the expected drift failure at Step 7. The coder's question about frontmatter units needs no action unless drift lists them as ADDED, and it does not.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
