    "title": "**The CLI throws an unhandled `EPIPE` when its output pipe closes early**",
    "text": "**The CLI throws an unhandled `EPIPE` when its output pipe closes early**: `aperas tree discussion/aperas-skill.md | head -1` and `aperas unfold BlockNode:00CVMKAP28001 | head -1` both exit 1 with Node's \"Unhandled 'error' event … write EPIPE\" stack trace on stderr, after the reader has already taken what it wanted. Reproduced 2026-10-02; `aperas show`, `aperas backlinks` and `aperas check-links` did not fail the same way on the same pipe (their output is small, which is not confirmed as the reason). The throw comes from the plain `console.log` at `packages/cli/src/kgTree.ts:114`, which writes the whole result in one call; no `EPIPE` handler exists anywhere in `monorepo/packages`, and the CLI has about 270 `console.log` sites, so a per-call-site guard would not hold. Fix: handle the `error` event on `process.stdout` once, in the dispatcher `aperas.ts`, exiting quietly on `EPIPE` for every verb. Found by the coder piping `aperas tree` into `head` and `grep`, reproduced by the grapher.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF2AEAX0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMP9N5G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMP9N5G000:links:Link:00CVMP9X20000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CR3X3N08007",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMP9N5G000:links:Link:00CVMP9X20000:props:StringProp:00CVMP9X20001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "508"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**`aperas --help` lists two bundled skills where `aperas skill install` installs five**",
    "text": "**`aperas --help` lists two bundled skills where `aperas skill install` installs five**: `packages/cli/src/aperas.ts:53` describes `skill` as installing \"this package's bundled skills (aperas, kg-doc-ingest)\", while `packages/cli/src/kgSkill.ts:25` lists `aperas`, `aperas-orchestrator`, `aperas-grapher`, `aperas-coder` and `kg-doc-ingest` in `SKILLS`, and that file's own description at line 70 names all five. The top-level help is the one a first-time user reads, and it hides the three role skills that [Skill packaging](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3X3N08007) says ship together. Fix: reword the `aperas.ts` description to the five names, or build it from `SKILLS` so the two cannot disagree. Found by the coder during the v4.3 skill edit; filed 2026-10-02.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF2AEAX0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A command can fail with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" while the service is up, and an unchanged retry works**",
    "text": "**A command can fail with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" while the service is up, and an unchanged retry works**: recorded in two separate grapher Reports. Filed 2026-10-02.",
