    "title": "**v4.3 — one command form, trouble recorded under its own topic, a source-reading gate that allows checking, a drift check that gates, and one minute as every role's limit on a stuck thing**",
    "text": "**v4.3 — one command form, trouble recorded under its own topic, a source-reading gate that allows checking, a drift check that gates, and one minute as every role's limit on a stuck thing**: recorded as [the v4.3 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001). All four skills now write the bare `aperas <verb>` and the \"Aperas-repo insiders\" callouts are gone. The thread template and Core Thread Disciplines take any trouble under `**Friction — <topic>**` and give each Question its own topic lead-in, and the Grapher files only real tool gaps under a tool issue. The Orchestrator's source-reading gate holds at task start and lets it read code, diffs and tests afterwards to check, assess or review a result. A defect or a gap is promoted to `issues/` in the Filing Turn, and other promotions wait for the Finishing Turn. Skill-only verification runs `skill_drift.py` and `aperas check-links` as two commands and expects drift to fail at Step 7 until the Grapher records the delta, which the Grapher skill's new \"Recording a skill delta\" subsection explains. `skill_drift.py` itself now exits nonzero on a `Status:` mismatch, an unrecorded addition or an unaccounted drop, and requires the four `Status:` lines to equal the newest delta's version; the design's [Versioning](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CF595QQR001) states that check. Last, one minute is the limit on anything that does not answer, for every role: after it an agent stops trying harder and reports to its upline, a subagent with a `Friction` entry and a `Question` to the orchestrator and the orchestrator to the user, who is also the one to approve a restart or kill of the service; the base skill carries the rule, the Coder and Grapher skills restate it for their turns, and the Orchestrator skill adds the callout \"Stuck Things Go to the User\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
