    "title": "**Resolved — the delta records the second v4.3 edit, and the drift check passes**",
    "text": "**Resolved — the delta records the second v4.3 edit, and the drift check passes**: [`## v4.3 additions`](#id/BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001) now covers the 19 units the drift check reported as unrecorded and the 10 it reported as dropped. Seven new entries carry the new text: the base task loop's steps 5, 8 and 9 (superseding `00CS1593MR019`, `00CS1593MR01C`, `00CS1593MR01D`), the Coder's drift-expectation invariant, the Grapher's Filing Turn item (superseding `00CS1593NG025`) and Promote item (superseding `00CS1593NR001`), the Grapher's six-item \"Recording a skill delta\" subsection, the Orchestrator's task-loop steps 5, 8 and 9 (superseding `00CS1593N8001`, `00CS1593N8009`, `00CS1593N800D`) and its \"Record Verification Findings\" item (superseding `00CV2CFX78011`). Four nodes written earlier in this delta were updated in place, as [Default — the v4.3 delta entries already recorded are updated in place](#id/BlockNode:00CVKV9DPG005) set out: the base step 7 \"Orchestrator Verification\" line, the base \"Skill-only changes\" line (which gained its code block), and the Orchestrator's section 7 code block (dropped `00CVJXQWNR00X`) and the paragraph under it. No `Supersedes:`-only entry was needed, because every dropped unit has a replacement. The delta's intro now also names the drift-expectation wording and the promotion wording. `skill_drift.py` exits 0 with 0 Status, 0 ADDED unrecorded and 0 DROPPED unaccounted, and 192 superseded and accounted for, against the 19 and 10 that [the orchestrator's verification](#id/BlockNode:00CVMK6KF8001) counted.",
