    "title": "**Decision — the rest of the reported trouble is not a tool gap and stays here**",
    "text": "**Decision — the rest of the reported trouble is not a tool gap and stays here**: by the Grapher skill's Filing Turn rule, own mistakes and tool-use problems stay in Freeflow. (1) Unfold truncating long paragraphs does not reproduce: `kgUnfold.ts` documents that unfold prints the target's full, uncapped text and each child's, and `aperas unfold` on a node whose child holds 4,094 characters printed all of it with no truncation hint, so only `backlinks`'s own preview line still caps. The grapher's earlier read of the design through a projection rested on a truncation that cannot now be shown, and I did not try `aperas show --text` first, so it stays here as a tool-use problem and is not filed. (2) Raw-store scripts not seeing thread nodes is by design: the thread tier persists to the gitignored `Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld` ([Threads](../design/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00CR3X3N08004)), and those scripts read the tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld`. (3) The filesystem read under `artifacts/`, the coder's dangling skill-file links in its first Report insert and the grapher's thread-size-cap warnings are own mistakes, a tool-use problem and a working warning. (4) `skill_drift.py` exiting 0 on drift and folding a `---` into the bullet above it were real gaps that the coder's guard and separator rule already fixed. (5) Units of 40 characters or fewer slipping past the ADDED pass is the documented limit that the Grapher skill's \"40-character limit\" item now states, with the `Status:` guard covering the one short unit that mattered.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVMS4YMR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
