    "title": "**Finding — a bold lead-in followed by a parenthetical qualifier loses its title**",
    "text": "**Finding — a bold lead-in followed by a parenthetical qualifier loses its title**: the orchestrator saw that several bullets inserted with `aperas insert` showed their block id in `aperas tree` instead of their bold lead-in, for example the \"Decision\" bullets under this heading. Reproduced 2026-10-02 on the parser alone, so `aperas insert` is not the cause: a bullet that starts with a bold lead-in, then a parenthetical such as `(orchestrator, not yet confirmed by the user)`, then the colon, gets its block id as its title once the lead-in and the qualifier pass 10 visible words, and the same bullet without the parenthetical gets its bold lead-in. Under this task's five Freeflow headings, 40 of the 87 bold-led bullets are titled by their id, every one with that shape, and 4 more have a title cut at a colon inside the parenthetical. The 10-word cap is the rule `design/linking.md`'s Lead-In Term Detection states, so this is a gap between that rule and the Freeflow convention, not a regression.",
