    "title": "**A thread-task `aperas remove` can leave the service CPU-bound for many minutes, during which every command fails and a graceful stop does not complete**",
    "text": "**A thread-task `aperas remove` can leave the service CPU-bound for many minutes, during which every command fails and a graceful stop does not complete**: found 2026-10-02 pruning finished tasks in the v4.3 skill task; the stalls were observed and the suspected causes below fit them, but no run attributed a stall to any of them before the fix. Filed 2026-10-02. **Resolved 2026-10-11** for the cause the Root cause section names, the scan of the whole store for every embedded node removed: the object-bound `removeDanglingUnfolds` landed in commit `0a7a226` and ran in the live service, where one `aperas remove --flush` of a task of 164 live blocks and 101 embedded `Link` nodes took 3.7 s with exit 0 and no stall, the thread tree then showed every other task intact, and `aperas check-links` scanned 6,549 live blocks with 0 discrepancies. That is about 36 ms per embedded node, against about 14,000 ms for 34 nodes at the old cost per scan, and the old service stalled 5.4 and 12 minutes on removals of 42 and 31 blocks. It covers every field that exists: `removeDanglingUnfolds` sweeps `unfolds`, and `unfoldsCollapsed` and `unfoldsNoPreview` do not exist in code (`shape.ts` defines only `unfolds` and `root` on a `TreeView`). One removal is one sample; the other suspected causes below (the link-integrity sweeps, the tombstone hard-deletes at shutdown and startup, a process-lifetime slowdown) were not separated from the scans by any run, and the scans' wrappers remain in [the scan entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
