    ],
    "title": "**Reproduced 2026-10-02**",
    "text": "**Reproduced 2026-10-02**: pruning 15 task and topic roots across `.threads/grapher.md` and `.threads/coder.md` in the v4.3 skill task leaked about 320 descendant tombstones into the tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` (3,314 nodes with 167 tombstoned before the removals, 3,637 with 490 after), and from there into the staged index. They left the tracked mirror only by accident: the service was killed before it flushed `.state/` (see [the persistence issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001)), and on the next start the leaked tombstones merged with the stale `.state/` copies of the same ids, which made them thread-scoped again and dropped them from the tracked mirror at the next flush. Three removals repeated on that fresh service leaked 22 more, which a `reload --discard` merged away in the same manner; the tracked mirror is back to 167 tombstones. So the leak is real and its only cleanup so far has been a lost-write recovery, not the sweep this entry asks for.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVNYDD18001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
