        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Observation — the service wedged for over 25 minutes during the grapher's prune, and was killed**",
    "text": "**Observation — the service wedged for over 25 minutes during the grapher's prune, and was killed**: While pruning finished thread tasks with `aperas remove`, the grapher saw the service freeze for 5.4 and about 12 minutes after removing tasks of 42 and 31 live blocks. It then ran `aperas service restart`, which never completed. The old process (pid 220722, about 3.4 hours up) climbed from 4.7 to 5.8 GB resident at roughly 40–50 MB a minute, ran two threads at 100% CPU, wrote nothing, and answered no command, while its lock file said \"ready\" and system memory was down to a few hundred MB free. Its own swapped memory was 26 MB, so it was not swapping. A normal stop (`aperas service stop`) failed after 10 s, and at the user's instruction (\"Just stop it -- clearly stuck!\") the process was killed with SIGKILL at 19:42 after copying the store directory to the scratchpad. A fresh service needed about 60 seconds to answer, was already at 1.5 GB after two minutes, and still dropped commands intermittently while it started.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVNYDD18002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Observation — what the kill lost and kept**",
    "text": "**Observation — what the kill lost and kept**: Kept: every Freeflow entry and Ask recorded before about 19:00 and the Turn 5 Ask. Lost: the grapher's thread prune tombstones (six checked, all live again with no `tombstonedAt`), the grapher's stall-issue text, and the orchestrator's note on service memory (written again here). The thread store file still showed a write time of 18:26 although it held newer nodes, so what reached disk and when is not clear.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVNYDD1G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Observation — the service reports 323 duplicate ids on start**",
    "text": "**Observation — the service reports 323 duplicate ids on start**: The start-up log says \"323 duplicate @id(s) in the mirror — quads from every occurrence merged onto one subject, so at most one document per id survives the next dehydrate\". A scan of every `.jsonld` file in the store found only two ids in more than one place (`BlockNode:00CR9MFS68001` and `BlockNode:00CRBH4RHR001`, in both the main and the thread store). The 323 is not explained.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
