    ],
    "title": "**Hypothesis — the stall is the same mechanism as the earlier process-lifetime slowdown**",
    "text": "**Hypothesis — the stall is the same mechanism as the earlier process-lifetime slowdown**: (user: \"This sweep, I think, links to the issue of the very long run of `verify` which forced us to split it to `verify:slow`\") The issue [verify slowdown](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001) recorded a process-lifetime slowdown that only a fresh process reset (oxigraph's WASM footprint at about 1 GB and V8 heap size were ruled out), and [why isolation helps](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000) says to profile with `--prof` or `--trace-deopt` if it recurs where a process split is not viable. The service is a long-lived process where a split is not viable. Differences: the earlier slowdown was slower steps, not multi-minute stalls, and the footprint is now about 5 GB. Not tested. A test that separates the two causes: time one large `remove` on a fresh service and the same `remove` after a long uptime.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVK45ZQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A write to a thread node never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty, so it exists only in memory until a view change or a shutdown sweep, and a killed service loses it**",
    "text": "**A write to a thread node never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty, so it exists only in memory until a view change or a shutdown sweep, and a killed service loses it**: found 2026-10-02 when the service stuck after the pruning removals (see the removal-stall entry above) was killed. Filed 2026-10-02.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
