    "title": "**Decision — wait for the fixes before pruning the 12 verified-promoted thread tasks**",
    "text": "**Decision — wait for the fixes before pruning the 12 verified-promoted thread tasks**: (user, answer to a direct question) Re-running `aperas remove` on thread tasks stalled the service again on a fresh process, and thread writes reach `.state/` only through a view operation or shutdown, so the threads stay over the cap until the stall and thread-flush issues are fixed. The grapher's Turn 5 Report holds the list: grapher `memory-rules-and-orientation-restructure`, `promote-and-fix-subagent-tool-gap`, `fold-bottlenecks-dispatch-and-pathing-into-skills`, `v4.2-progressive-disclosure-refactor`, `ApeironNgn service reliability` and `Promote tool gaps to issues`; coder `tree rendering`, the same four v4.x tasks and the `Promote tool gaps to issues` shell.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVP855D8002",
