    "title": "**Decision — Freeflow lead-ins keep the qualifier out of the title position**",
    "text": "**Decision — Freeflow lead-ins keep the qualifier out of the title position**: (user: \"That's the wrong shape. You should put the parenthetical after the colon or into the bold.\") A Freeflow bullet is written `**Decision — <what>**: (<who>, <how>) <body>`, or with the qualifier inside the bold span, never `**Decision — <what>** (<who>, <how>): <body>`. The parser's rule works as written, so the convention changes and the engine does not; the filed issue [lead-in titles](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMYB5W0001) lists both options and records this choice. The grapher rewrote the 53 old-shape entries under the five Freeflow headings of the v4.3 task in its Turn 6, and none of them now carries an id as its title.",
