    "title": "**Finding — the 10-second timer does not persist thread writes**",
    "text": "**Finding — the 10-second timer does not persist thread writes**: (user: \"That means the 10s flush has no effect on threads, doesn't it?\") Confirmed by reading `service.ts` and `dehydrate.ts`. Thread-scoped `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` records are excluded from the content mirror that the 10-second `flushIfDirty` writes, and are written only by `flushStateIfDirty` into `.state/`. That runs on a 3-second timer but does nothing unless `stateDirty` is set, and `insert`, `update`, `remove` and `retype` set only `dirty`. So a thread write makes the 10-second timer rewrite a mirror that does not contain it, and nothing the 3-second timer does touches it, until a view operation (`unfold`, `fold`, `zoom`), the garbage-collection sweeps or shutdown sets `stateDirty`. Filed as [thread flush](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001), with the fix of setting `stateDirty` on any write to a thread-scoped node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPG6108001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
