        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Finding — every `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` runs a whole-artifact link-integrity check before and after**",
    "text": "**Finding — every `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` runs a whole-artifact link-integrity check before and after**: (read from `service.ts`, not tested) The handlers call `checkArtifactLinkIntegrity(store, artifactId)` before the operation and again in `withLinkCheck` after it, over the whole artifact, so one `remove` of a task inside a 600-block thread file costs two full sweeps on top of the removal itself. The earlier verify-slowdown issue ([verify slowdown](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001)) named the same kind of operation, `checkLinkIntegrity`'s corpus sweep, as the one that went from low hundreds of milliseconds fresh to 12–55 seconds late in a long process. That makes the sweep a candidate for the removal stall; a lead for the investigation, not a finding.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQ1EPRR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPG6108002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — a `remove` of a main artifact sets only `dirty`, which is correct for it**",
    "text": "**Finding — a `remove` of a main artifact sets only `dirty`, which is correct for it**: (user: \"a `remove` of a main artifact also sets only `dirty`, doesn't it?\") `remove` sets `dirty` and flushes with `--flush`, whatever the node, and the content mirror it feeds is the right one for a main artifact, so main removals persist within 10 seconds. Only thread-scoped nodes need the `.state/` mirror, which is why the thread-flush gap affects threads alone. One loose end: a removed main node can leave stale `unfolds` entries in the `.state/` TreeView mirror until the next reload sweep.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPK8PA8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPK8PA8000:props:StringProp:00CVPK8Y5R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPK8PA8000:props:StringProp:00CVPK8Y60000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Finding — the thread-flush gap is a routing mismatch, not a timer-cadence one**",
    "text": "**Finding — the thread-flush gap is a routing mismatch, not a timer-cadence one**: (user: \"the gap is the behavior mismatch between the 3s flush to `.state` and the main 10s flush, isn't it?\") Both timers work as designed and their cadences (3 s and 10 s) are not the defect. The mismatch is that a thread-scoped node is routed to the `.state/` mirror when the store is dehydrated (`THREAD_PARTITIONED_CLASSES`, `isThreadScopedId`), but the dirty flag is chosen without that partition: `insert`, `update`, `remove` and `retype` set `dirty`, which feeds the content flush that excludes thread nodes, and never `stateDirty`, which feeds the `.state/` flush that includes them. The fix keeps one rule in both places, setting `stateDirty` when a write touches a thread-scoped node. Possibly related, not checked: the `.state/` divergence check stamps only `STATE_CLASSES` (`TreeView`), so an external change to the thread `BlockNode` file there would not be noticed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQ1GWQ8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPK8PA8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPK8PA8001:links:Link:00CVQ72CRR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPK8PA8001:links:Link:00CVQ72CRR000:props:StringProp:00CVQ72CS0000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "253"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Decision — record the link-sweep lead on the removal-stall issue**",
    "text": "**Decision — record the link-sweep lead on the removal-stall issue**: (user: \"worth recording to the workflow\") The grapher adds the whole-artifact link-integrity sweeps before and after each `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` to the stall issue [removal stall](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) as a suspected cause, labelled untested, with the link to the earlier verify-slowdown issue. It joins the next grapher Filing turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
