        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Never wait on a silent command beyond one minute**",
    "text": "**Never wait on a silent command beyond one minute**: If a command, the service or a test run does not answer, wait, poll or retry no more than one minute in total, then record a `**Friction — <topic>**` entry and end the turn with a `**Question — <topic>**`. If the service is down, end the turn and do not restart it; the orchestrator owns the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90G003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-grapher — Every Invocation, Never wait on a silent command",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVPXK90R001",
    "text": "> **Rule**: Never wait on a silent command beyond one minute. If a graph command, the service or a projection does not answer, wait, poll or retry no more than one minute in total, then record a `**Friction — <topic>**` entry and end the turn with a `**Question — <topic>**`. If the service is down, end the turn and do not restart it; the orchestrator owns the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVPXK90R000",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVPZKPN8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — the one-minute rule applies to every agent, including the orchestrator, and the orientation is to bubble up**",
    "text": "**Decision — the one-minute rule applies to every agent, including the orchestrator, and the orientation is to bubble up**: (user: \"The 1min rules applies to all agents, if the Orchestrator waits longer, it must report to user. The general orientation is: don't try hard on a thing seemingly stuck, just bubble up to the upline.\") After one minute of waiting, polling or retrying something that is not answering, an agent reports to its upline instead of trying harder: a subagent ends its turn with a `**Question — <topic>**` to the orchestrator, and the orchestrator reports to the user, and may keep waiting only after telling the user. This replaces the orchestrator's earlier plan of a longer limit for service start and supersedes the unconfirmed note that the orchestrator restarts the service on its own. The wording of the base skill, which now says \"to the orchestrator\", and a line in the orchestrator skill need updating; queued as a coder edit after the grapher's current turn, so the delta is updated once.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ0PVS0001",
