    ],
    "title": "**Verification — the widened one-minute rule inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the widened one-minute rule inspected and confirmed**: (orchestrator) The base bullet now reads \"One minute is the limit on anything that does not answer, for every role\": after a minute an agent stops trying harder and reports to its upline, a subagent with a `Friction` entry and a `Question` to the orchestrator and the orchestrator to the user, which may keep waiting only after telling the user; it carries the orientation sentence and says a restart or kill of the service is for the user to approve. The orchestrator skill has a callout, \"Stuck Things Go to the User\", with the user as its upline. The Coder and Grapher skills are unchanged and agree. `skill_drift.py` exits 1 with 2 ADDED (the base bullet and the orchestrator callout) and 1 DROPPED (the old base bullet, [base one-minute entry](#id/BlockNode:00CVPXK90G002)), 0 Status; `aperas check-links` is a clean pass. The coder stayed inside the one-minute rule and did nothing to the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ4MKH0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### aperas-orchestrator — What You Do NOT Do Initially, Stuck Things Go to the User",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVJXQWNG001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQ4MKH0002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQ4MKH0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00CVQ4MKH0002",
    "text": "> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **Stuck Things Go to the User**:\n> Your upline is the user. When a subagent hand-off, command, service or test run has not answered after one minute, stop trying harder and report it to the user. You may keep waiting only after telling the user, and a restart or kill of the service is for the user to approve.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQ4MKH0001",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "children": []
  },
