    "title": "**Resolved — the orchestrator's bare ids are converted to wikilinks**",
    "text": "**Resolved — the orchestrator's bare ids are converted to wikilinks**: (orchestrator) Nine entries under the five Freeflow headings now cite [verify slowdown](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001), [thread flush](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001), [removal stall](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000), [lead-in titles](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMYB5W0001) and the delta entry by link, and `aperas check-links` is clean. Five mentions stay as code on purpose: three ids of thread nodes, which the graph above the thread tier must not link into; one id that does not exist, which the `check-links` finding documents; and one verbatim quotation of the user's question.",
