    "title": "**Finding — the coder's code survey gives mechanisms for the spurious \"not running\" and the removal stall**",
    "text": "**Finding — the coder's code survey gives mechanisms for the spurious \"not running\" and the removal stall**: (orchestrator, from the coder's Turn 1 Report in `.threads/coder.md`, a thread node and so not linked; code-derived points tagged read, numbers tagged measured in a scratch process) Every request, `ping` included, goes through the single `enqueue` chain and `handle` has no `await`, while the client's ping gives up after 300 ms, so any operation over about 0.3 s, or two or three queued, makes the next command say \"No ApeironNgn service running\" with nothing stalled (read; the orchestrator checked `PING_TIMEOUT_MS`, `handle`'s `ping` case and the `enqueue` call). This is a mechanism for [the spurious \"not running\"](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001). Each `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` re-parses every live block of the artifact with remark before and after the operation, about 1.7 to 2.5 ms a block (measured), so about 1.3 to 1.9 s each time on a 767-block thread file. A removal tombstones every embedded `Link` and `StringProp`, and each calls `removeDanglingUnfolds`, which scans every quad in the store, about 140 ms at 39.6k quads (measured); the cost therefore follows the number of embedded nodes under the removed task, not the block count, which fits [the recorded removal stall](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) pattern of 39 and 50 blocks fast and 42 and 31 slow. The 5.4 and 12 minute stalls would need about 2,300 and 5,000 such scans; whether those tasks held that many embedded nodes is not known, and the coder's run of an in-memory removal did not finish in 100 seconds, consistent but not attributed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQJTMJR001",
      "BlockNode:00CVQJVSJG001",
      "BlockNode:00CVQJWW3G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQFC3SR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — boot and shutdown cost grows with the tombstones, and sit close to the client's timeouts**",
    "text": "**Finding — boot and shutdown cost grows with the tombstones, and sit close to the client's timeouts**: (orchestrator, from the same Report) Boot is all synchronous before the socket exists: rehydrate about 1.06 s, `tombstoneVacuousContainers` about 1.2 s and `pruneUnreachableTombstones` about 2.3 s even with nothing to prune (measured), against a client `waitForReady` of 5 s. The next reload, startup or shutdown prunes each tombstoned block with the same per-node scan, so every removal also adds roughly 140 ms per node to later starts and stops. SIGTERM runs in JavaScript, so it cannot fire mid-operation, and shutdown re-runs the sweeps (about 3.5 s idle) while `stopIfRunning` waits only 10 s, which fits \"didn't stop within 10s\". `unfold`, `fold` and `zoom` set both dirty flags, so each costs a full content dehydrate and a state dehydrate within seconds.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQJXXNG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQFC3SR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Finding — nothing measures the service and nothing tests it under load**",
    "text": "**Finding — nothing measures the service and nothing tests it under load**: (orchestrator, from the same Report) The service has no timing or memory logging, `APERAS_DEBUG_TIMING` output is lost because the service spawns with `stdio: 'ignore'`, `logService` is the only durable channel, and `verify.ts` and `verifyExtended.ts` never run the service process or call `runRemove`. The sampler as written cannot tell the 300 ms ping failure from a request error or a timeout, because it discards the failure text, and it probes only once a minute through a full client. The coder also left `/tmp/coder-survey/probe.mts` on disk outside both repos.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQJYZ0G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQFC3SR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Open — where the instrumentation goes, and what the investigation may run**",
    "text": "**Open — where the instrumentation goes, and what the investigation may run**: (the coder's three questions, with the orchestrator's recommendations; none decided) Instrumentation in a new `apeironNgn/serviceDiagnostics.ts` behind one environment switch read by `spawnService`, which already copies `process.env`; event-loop delay histogram, `process.memoryUsage()` and heap statistics every 30 to 60 seconds, per-operation timings split into queue wait, pre-check, operation, flush and post-check for operations over about 250 ms, and one timestamped line per boot phase, all through `logService`. The sampler stays Python in `monorepo/packages/cli/diagnostics/` with a `svc:sample` script, adds a raw-socket ping each second that keeps the failure text, and drops the one-minute client probe. A scratch run that times the removal path step by step in a separate `/tmp` process (rehydrates the store read-only and never writes, 60 second limit) was refused by the permission classifier; it needs the user's explicit approval, and the orchestrator does not retry it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVKQDJ2G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00CVQK01JR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Every `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` re-parses the whole artifact with remark before and after the operation, about 1.7 to 2.5 ms a block, so a write to a large thread file costs seconds before its own work**",
    "text": "**Every `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` re-parses the whole artifact with remark before and after the operation, about 1.7 to 2.5 ms a block, so a write to a large thread file costs seconds before its own work**: found 2026-10-02 in the slow-service investigation's code survey of the service. Filed 2026-10-02.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
