    "title": "**Handoff — the state for the next session**",
    "text": "**Handoff — the state for the next session**: (orchestrator) The v4.3 skill work is committed by the user in the code repo, with the sampler files restaged apart from it, and `AperasKG` is staged and not committed. The service is a fresh process (pid 290034, up since 19:42) and the repo sampler is `monorepo/packages/cli/diagnostics/svc_sampler.py`. Open for the user: whether to make the removal fix first, `removeDanglingUnfolds` (`node.ts:251`) using one object-bound `store.match(null, unfolds, id, null)`, verified on a scratch copy and then a separate approval for the repo edit; and whether [the written design for `serviceDiagnostics.ts`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001) stands. The queue behind them: [the canonical-address authoring gap](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQHG5JR001), then [the `check-links` miss on an id link to a node that does not exist](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00CVKFWNB8001). Still waiting: the thread prune, until the stall and thread-flush issues are fixed, and the Status-lines issue, which stays open for the skill wording that says who moves `Status:`. Defaults the user has not confirmed are marked as such in the entries above.",
