  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00CVRVYV00001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification — the Harness Tool Mappings patch inspected and confirmed**",
    "text": "**Verification — the Harness Tool Mappings patch inspected and confirmed**: (orchestrator) The orchestrator skill's two lines now say that `SendMessage` in Claude Code, like `send_message` in Antigravity, is how a session gets reused, and that the Claude Code line is to call `Agent` (formerly `Task`) every turn and never `SendMessage` across distinct turns, with a note to a running subagent within a turn allowed. The diff is 2 insertions and 2 deletions in one file, the `.claude/skills` and `.agents/skills` paths being symlinks to it, and `Status:` stays v4.3. `skill_drift.py` exits 1 as expected with 2 ADDED (the Preventing Transcript Bloat bullet and the Claude Code mapping bullet) and 2 DROPPED (their old versions), 0 Status; `aperas check-links` is a clean pass.",
