  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38001:props:StringProp:00D0V8DYYG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38001:props:StringProp:00D0V8DYYG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0V8DQ38001",
    "text": "**Request — find why a 4 MB mirror becomes a store of up to 1 GB, and why rehydration takes close to a minute** (2026-10-10, user, the first request of the session after the v4.3 patch was handed over): \"How can a mirror of only 4MB be loaded to a store up to 1GB!? Both that monstrous size and the near 1-minute rehydration time are clearly problematic.\" The user ranks this as the serious problem of the core and takes it before the removal stall.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002",
      "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ3G000",
      "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ3G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002:links:Link:00D0V8DYZ0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002:links:Link:00D0V8DYZ0000:props:StringProp:00D0V8DYZ0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "29"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002:links:Link:00D0V8DYZ0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002:links:Link:00D0V8DYZ0002:props:StringProp:00D0V8DYZ0003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "172"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002:props:StringProp:00D0V8DYYG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38002:props:StringProp:00D0V8DYYR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Earlier records it rests on",
    "text": "Earlier records it rests on: [the service memory issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) (fresh service about 1.3 GB for 3.66 MB of data, about 350 times) and [the boot and shutdown issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001) (rehydrate about 1.06 s and startup collection about 3.5 s measured on a scratch copy).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ3G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Open — the one-minute figure**",
    "text": "**Open — the one-minute figure**: the earlier scratch measurement of `rehydrateStore` was about 1 s, and the whole synchronous boot about 4.5 s; the user's \"near 1 minute\" is not yet matched by a measurement. The first job is to find which wall-clock the user sees (a `service restart` end to end, a `--reload`, a cold start after a kill) and time its phases.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ3G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Scope — investigation first**",
    "text": "**Scope — investigation first**: the project rule is that an investigation is not approval for a fix. The Coder surveys and measures on scratch copies in `/tmp` without editing source; the findings and the candidate fixes come back to the user, who decides the shape of the fix before any code changes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V8DQ38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VB37T0001",
    "text": "**Review — the Grapher's survey inspected, and what the Coder is asked to measure** (2026-10-10, orchestrator): read the Grapher's Turn 1 Report through its view. What it establishes, and what it does not:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0003",
      "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8000",
      "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8001",
      "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8002",
      "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0002:props:StringProp:00D0VB3F20000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0002:props:StringProp:00D0VB3F20001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0VB37T0002",
    "text": "The mirror is 3.10 MB of content plus 1.13 MB of `.state/`, 4.24 MB in all, which is the user's \"4 MB\". From the data shape the Grapher derives about 36,000 quads in the content mirror and about 14,600 in `.state/`, so about 50,600 together; the recorded 37,000 and 39,600 match the content mirror alone, and no record says how they were counted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VB37T0003",
    "text": "Against that, a fresh service idling at about 1.3 GB is about 26 KB resident per quad (derived by the orchestrator: 1.3 GB over 50,600), which is not the scale an embedded RDF store is expected to need for that many quads. The expectation is a hypothesis, not a measurement: no sourced per-quad figure for Oxigraph's WASM store is in the graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VB37T8000",
    "text": "No record shows a rehydrate or a start near a minute. The nearest are post-removal flushes of 19 to 29 s and state flushes of 16 to 20 s, a start that missed its 5 s ready wait and succeeded about 20 s later, and a restart-recovery loop of about 1 m 15 s with no phase timing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VB37T8001",
    "text": "`design/` has no document on the store, hydration or the service lifecycle; the only specification is the archived, untracked ApeironNgn design, which chose an in-memory store \"until GB-level\". That is now the situation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Drift the Grapher found",
    "text": "Drift the Grapher found: the coder's removal measurement lives only in this Freeflow, and neither the removal-stall issue nor the memory issue links to it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — the Coder measures, in this order, on scratch copies and in scratch processes only**",
    "text": "**Decision — the Coder measures, in this order, on scratch copies and in scratch processes only**: (1) the live store's quad count split by what loaded from the content mirror and from `.state/` (answers the Grapher's \"which count\"), and `process.memoryUsage()` plus RSS at each boot phase; (2) a bare Oxigraph store loaded with synthetic quads of the same shape at several sizes, to find what a healthy per-quad cost is on this machine, apart from Aperas code; (3) the Aperas rehydrate path repeated several times in one process, to see whether memory grows per reload; (4) timings of every wall-clock the user might have seen. Why: the three steps separate the engine's own cost, the load path's cost and the lifetime growth, which the earlier records mixed. How to apply: no source edit and no run against the live service; the live service may be read through `/proc` only. Because the user did not say which minute, the Coder times all of them (the Grapher's \"which minute\" question, answered by covering all).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VB37T0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VEY44R001",
    "text": "**Clarification — the \"minute\" is a `service restart`, as measured by the orchestrator when the one-minute cap was set** (2026-10-10, user): the user's figure comes from the last time the orchestrator timed the service, \"maybe a restart\"; at that time the user set the one-minute cap for all agents including the orchestrator, and the orchestrator said the restart \"barely passes\". This answers the Grapher's open \"which minute\": the candidate is a `service restart` end to end (stop, then start to ready), which the earlier records time at no better than about 1 m 15 s in a recovery loop and never by phase.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R002",
      "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R002:props:StringProp:00D0VEYK88000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R002:props:StringProp:00D0VEYK88001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0VEY44R002",
    "text": "The orchestrator could not find that measurement again, in this session's transcript or in the graph, so the figure is the user's recollection plus the orchestrator's remembered remark, and its phases are unknown. That is a gap in the record, not a finding.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decision — measurement (4) puts the restart first**",
    "text": "**Decision — measurement (4) puts the restart first**: the Coder times a stop (SIGTERM to exit, with the three sweeps and both flushes) and a start (to the ready lock) in phases, against the client's 10 s stop wait and 5 s ready wait, and states which phase carries the minute. How to apply: a note to the running Coder reaches it between its tool calls; the Ask stands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VEY44R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001:props:StringProp:00D0VYDFMG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001:props:StringProp:00D0VYDFMG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0VYD6R0001",
    "text": "**Finding — measured: the 1 GB is not the engine, it is wasm-bound JavaScript objects from full-store scans that are never released inside a long synchronous run; the \"minute\" is a restart that errors out twice and then refuses commands for about 20 s** (2026-10-10, orchestrator, from the Coder's Turn 1 Report, inspected): the Coder measured on copies in `/tmp/aperas-scratch/`, including a scratch service with its own run directory and port. Source untouched, the scratch service stopped, the live lock still pid 33127 and ready (checked by the orchestrator after the hand-back). Figures are single runs unless a count is given, at a machine load of 2 to 3.5.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8000",
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8001",
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8002",
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8003",
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8004",
      "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8005",
      "BlockNode:00D0W14D2G001",
      "BlockNode:00D0W14D2R000",
      "BlockNode:00D0W14D2R001",
      "BlockNode:00D0W14D2R002",
      "BlockNode:00D0W14D2R003",
      "BlockNode:00D0W14D2R004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0002:props:StringProp:00D0VYDFMG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0002:props:StringProp:00D0VYDFMG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Quad count**",
    "text": "**Quad count**: 41,752 quads, 29,537 from the content mirror and 12,216 from `.state/`, counted with `store.size`, which equals the length of a full match. The live service logged 41,246 at its boot, so the live store does hold the thread partition. The Grapher's derived 50,610 overshoots because every `parent` quad is written twice and deduplicated; the earlier 37,000 and 39,600 had no recorded method.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The engine is not the cost**",
    "text": "**The engine is not the cost**: bare Oxigraph 0.5.11 (Node CJS build, wasm, in memory) costs about 0.5 KB resident per quad when bulk-loaded, 20 to 55 MB for 41.7k quads. The idle 1.3 GB is about 26 to 36 KB per quad, so the earlier hypothesis that the store itself is that big does not hold.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Where the memory goes**",
    "text": "**Where the memory goes**: after `rehydrateStore` alone, rss 273 MB over a 119 MB baseline (heapUsed 60, external 81), about 3.7 KB per quad including parse garbage. After the boot sweeps and the link sweep, rss 572 MB with external 282 MB, and external memory never shrinks. Memory is allocated per JavaScript wrapper object and per full scan, not per quad: `allIdsOfKind` does a full `store.match(null, null, null, null)` and is called at least 8 times in boot and 4 times per flush; `wrap`, `readField` and `childrenOf` each issue further matches; the second pass of `rehydrateStore` scans the whole store; JSON parsing is 28 ms.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VYD6R8002",
    "text": "**A reload leaves the old store alive** until an event-loop turn runs: each synchronous rehydrate adds one store (about 75 MB external), a forced `gc()` frees nothing of it, and the run time climbs from 1.2 s to 8 to 23 s. A reload-style cycle reached rss 1.73 GB by run 4 (26 s, 64 s, 98 s, 225 s a run); with a turn between runs, external plateaus at 104 MB and a run takes about 1 s. The live service's high-water mark is 1.66 GB.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Where the time goes**",
    "text": "**Where the time goes**: the same code costs 8 s as separate event-loop turns and 88 s as one synchronous request (dirty reload: rehydrate 0.9 s against 29.6 s, link sweep 1.8 s against 38.5 s, flushes 2.6 s against 18.8 s). The garbage-collection count grows with the number of live wasm-bound objects. A `reload` after a mutation took 74 s and 119 s wall time on two fresh scratch services; a clean reload takes 4.4 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The restart**",
    "text": "**The restart**: stop takes 0.6 s when the service is settled, but 12.5 s (2 of 2) after any `unfold`, `fold` or `zoom --view`, which is the usual state in agent use, and 21 s when issued during the startup link sweep; the client waits 10 s, so `restart` errors with \"didn't stop within 10s\" and starts nothing. Start: the lock turns ready at 5.3 to 5.8 s in 6 of 6 runs, and the CLI prints \"did not become ready in time\" at 5.4 to 5.8 s every time, although the service is up within 60 ms of that. After ready, every command is refused with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" for 19.5 to 23 s, because the startup link sweep holds the event loop and the 300 ms ping times out. A restart, its error at 10 s, a start, its error at 5.5 s and retrying until commands work adds up to about 40 to 50 s, which fits the user's recollection of a restart that barely passed one minute.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Not measured or in doubt**",
    "text": "**Not measured or in doubt**: the live service's own phases (they would need the user's approval to stop it); one read right after a clean reload exited 1 with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" and its message was not captured; run 5 of the reload cycle was killed with `kill -9` after 647 s (a tight synchronous loop ignores `kill`), so only four runs are reported.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0VYD6R8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0VYD6R8006",
    "text": "**Friction — the orchestrator's Ask let a long run sit behind an uncapped poll loop** (2026-10-10, orchestrator): the Ask told the Coder that its own measurement runs could outlast the one-minute rule, run in the background and be polled. The Coder polled with two `until [ -f …/m3-cycle.done ]` loops inside blocking tool calls, which have no cap of their own; they ran 6 m 49 s and 6 m 11 s, and while the Coder sat in them a message to it, including the orchestrator's note that the minute was a restart, could not be delivered, because messages reach a subagent only between tool calls. The user caught it. How to apply in later Asks: a long measurement is a background process with its own `timeout`, polled with short bounded calls (each under about 20 s), and the Ask names the number of minutes after which the Coder reports.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0W00YCR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A reload leaves the old store alive until an event-loop turn runs, and a reload after a mutation takes 74 to 119 s**",
    "text": "**A reload leaves the old store alive until an event-loop turn runs, and a reload after a mutation takes 74 to 119 s**: measured 2026-10-10 by the Coder in the store-size investigation. Filed 2026-10-10.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8XR90001",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8XR90005",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8XR90009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8XR9R00D",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8XR9R00G",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8XR9R00J"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Full-store scans materialize every quad as a JavaScript object, and the service's memory and time follow the scans and the wrappers they leave, not the 41.7k quads**",
