    "title": "Corrected in place from this finding",
    "text": "Corrected in place from this finding: [**The ApeironNgn service's resident memory climbs to about 5.8 GB over hours under heavy use, and a fresh service idles at about 1.3 GB for 3.66 MB of data**](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) (quad count, engine cost, hypotheses), [**Boot and shutdown cost grows with the tombstones and sits close to the client's 5 s ready wait and 10 s stop wait**](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001) (measured phases), [**A thread-task `aperas remove` can leave the service CPU-bound for many minutes, during which every command fails and a graceful stop does not complete**](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) and [**A command can fail with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" while the service is up, and an unchanged retry works**](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001) (the refusal window after ready)",
