  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0W1WT7G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0W1WT7G001",
    "text": "**Verification — the Grapher's filing of the store measurements inspected** (2026-10-10, orchestrator): `aperas check-links` scanned 4,635 live blocks and found 0 discrepancies. The five new entries in `issues/core.md` exist and open with the claims the Grapher reported (reload leaves the old store alive; full-store scans materialize every quad; `service restart` errors at 10 s after a view op; the CLI's 5 s ready wait against a lock ready at 5.3 to 5.8 s; no `design/` document for the store and the service lifecycle). The memory issue now carries the \"overturned\" mark. `AperasKG` is staged (`Apeiron/*.jsonld`, `artifacts/discussion/aperas-skill.md`, `artifacts/issues/core.md`) and the code repo holds only the staged diagnostics files. No fix has been chosen: the user has not yet answered the choice between fixing the cause (yield between phases and stop materializing every quad) and raising the client waits only.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0W6Q9DR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0W6Q9DR001",
    "text": "**Request — focus on the core issue and explain it from root causes down to the measurements** (2026-10-10, user): after the orchestrator's long summary of the filing, \"Too much info! Let's put all other issues aside to focus on the core issue. Explain me from the root causes to the rationale of the causes and then measurements supporting them.\" The three open choices (the fix, the live-service repeat, the stale README) wait until the explanation is settled. Nothing is dispatched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WMVJ78001",
    "text": "**Request — rewrite the walls of text in `issues/core.md` as subtrees, in the clear shape of the root-cause report** (2026-10-10, user): after the explanation \"from the root causes to the rationale of the causes and then measurements supporting them\", the user understood and asked: \"Let's rewrite the 'walls of text' in issues/core.md with a format as clear as this. An issue with complicated content must be broken down into a subtree instead of a single item with endless text.\" The orchestrator measured the file first: of 38 items, 10 run 2.6 to 8.8 KB (the service-performance cluster, filed 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-10, plus one resolved entry), and about 20 more run 1 to 2.4 KB.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78002",
      "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78003",
      "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78004",
      "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ7G000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78002:props:StringProp:00D0WMVV30000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78002:props:StringProp:00D0WMVV30001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WMVJ78002",
    "text": "**Decision — scope is the service cluster only** (user, answering a direct question): the 9 open service issues of 2.6 KB or more: the removal stall, boot and shutdown, memory, no coverage, spurious \"not running\", full-store scans, reload, thread flush, whole-artifact re-parse, and the `service restart` error. The rest of the file stays as it is.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WMVJ78003",
    "text": "**Decision — a pilot first, on the removal-stall issue** (user, answering a direct question): the longest entry (8.8 KB). The user reviews the result; the same shape is then applied to the rest, so a wrong shape costs one issue.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WMVJ78004",
    "text": "**Shape proposed by the orchestrator, put to the user as part of the question and accepted with the pilot** (the pilot is where the user can still change it): the issue keeps its block id, so every backlink holds, and its own text shrinks to a bold title and one sentence of claim. Its children are **Symptom**, **Root cause** (the rationale as sub-items under each cause), **Measurements** (one bullet per figure, with its caveat), **Not proven**, **Workaround** and **Related**. Nothing is dropped and nothing new is claimed: every number, date and link target of the old text must be found in the new subtree.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ7G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Open — the issues are not merged**",
    "text": "**Open — the issues are not merged**: several service issues overlap (the scans, the reload, the removal stall). Merging them is a separate decision that the user has not asked for; each keeps its id and its own subtree, and cross-links stay as they are.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WMVJ78001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDYR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDYR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK570001",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578000",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578001",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578002",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578003",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578004",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578005",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578006",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK578007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDYR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZ0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK578000",
    "text": "Found 2026-10-02 pruning finished tasks from `.threads/grapher.md` and `.threads/coder.md` in the v4.3 skill task. Of 15 removals, most returned in 2 to 10 seconds.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578001",
    "text": "After removing `memory-rules-and-orientation-restructure` (42 live blocks) the service answered nothing for about 5.4 minutes (tombstone at 11:37:44Z, next success at 11:43:07Z).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578002",
    "text": "After removing `promote-and-fix-subagent-tool-gap` (31 live blocks) it stayed unreachable for about 12 minutes (tombstone at 11:44:10Z, first answer at about 11:56:40Z).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578003",
    "text": "Tasks of 39 and 50 blocks returned quickly, so size alone does not predict it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578004",
    "text": "Throughout, the process was alive at 100 to 290 percent CPU and 3.4 to 4.6 GB resident, and `service.log` recorded nothing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578005:links:Link:00D0WPKE20000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578005:links:Link:00D0WPKE20000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE20001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "108"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK578005",
    "text": "Every command, `aperas show` included, failed with \"No ApeironNgn service running\", which is the symptom of [the service-ping issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578006",
    "text": "A later `aperas service restart` sent SIGTERM and failed with \"didn't stop within 10s of SIGTERM\"; the old process was still alive more than 40 minutes later, when it was killed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578007",
    "text": "On the fresh service started afterwards (about 1 GB resident), three further removals took 2, 2 and 45 seconds and the next command could not reach the service for minutes, so age and heap size alone do not explain the stall.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK570001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK578008",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR001",
      "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK578009",
    "text": "**A scan of the whole store for every embedded node under the removed task** (read from `service.ts` and the store code in the investigation's code survey of 2026-10-02; the cost of one scan measured in a scratch process)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800A",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800B",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800C",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800D",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800E",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800A:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800A:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57800A",
    "text": "One `aperas remove --flush` of a task `T` in artifact `A` runs, synchronously and in this order, `artifactForRef`, the pre-check sweep of `A`, `runRemove`, the content flush, and the post-check sweep of `A`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800B",
    "text": "`runRemove` calls `tombstoneLiveSubtree`, which for each block depth-first sets `children = []`, `links = undefined`, `props = undefined` and `tombstonedAt`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800C",
    "text": "The `links` and `props` assignments go through `writeField`'s embed branch, which calls `hardDeleteNode` on every embedded `Link` and `StringProp`, recursing into each `Link`'s position props.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800D",
    "text": "Each `hardDeleteNode` begins with `removeDanglingUnfolds`, which calls `allIdsOfKind(store, 'TreeView')`, a `store.match` over every quad in the store.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800E",
    "text": "The cost of a removal therefore follows the number of embedded nodes under the removed task, about that count times 140 ms, and not its block count.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800F",
    "text": "This fits the pattern in Symptom (39 and 50 blocks fast, 42 and 31 slow): a task whose blocks carry many wikilinks has many `Link` nodes and position props, while a plain list has few.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK578009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800G",
    "text": "**The tombstones that each removal leaves are hard-deleted one at a time at shutdown and startup** (read, with the per-node cost measured; the likely cost; not tested)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800H",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800J",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800H:links:Link:00D0WZWWTR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800H:links:Link:00D0WZWWTR000:props:StringProp:00D0WZWWTR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "102"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800H:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800H:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57800H",
    "text": "Each removal also leaked its descendants' tombstones into the tracked `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld` (see [the leak issue](../issues/treeview.md#id/BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR002) in `issues/treeview.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800J",
    "text": "`pruneUnreachableTombstones` hard-deletes each unreachable tombstone one at a time at shutdown and startup.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800K:links:Link:00D0WPKE20002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800K:links:Link:00D0WPKE20002:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE20003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "232"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57800K",
    "text": "At the next reload, shutdown or startup it finds the removed blocks unreachable and calls `hardDeleteNode` on each, another full scan each: about 6 s for 42 blocks (derived) on top of its fixed 2.3 s, which is the cost described in [the boot and shutdown issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800M",
    "text": "**Each scan leaves a JavaScript `Quad` wrapper per store quad, which raises garbage-collector pressure and external memory** (read, untested; the effect is measured in the Coder's runs and in the store-size investigation)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800N",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800N:links:Link:00D0WPKE28000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800N:links:Link:00D0WPKE28000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE28001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "193"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800N:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800N:props:StringProp:00D0WPKDZR003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57800N",
    "text": "The scan allocates a JavaScript `Quad` per store quad on every call (about 40k objects, 140 ms), which is a candidate source of the garbage-collector pressure and the external-memory growth in [the memory issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) (read, untested).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57800P",
    "text": "The retained external memory in the Coder's removal runs (see Measurements) is the same effect that the memory issue records.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57800M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G000:links:Link:00D0WPKE28002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G000:links:Link:00D0WPKE28002:props:StringProp:00D0X08P5R000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "163"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G000:links:Link:00D0WPKE28004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D0W00YCR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G000:links:Link:00D0WPKE28004:props:StringProp:00D0X08QKR000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "210"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57G000",
    "text": "The scans create a wrapper per quad that is released only after a garbage collection and an event-loop turn, and a reload leaves the old store alive until a turn ([the scan entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001), [the reload entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W00YCR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G001",
    "text": "**Two whole-artifact link-integrity sweeps around every write** (second suspected cause; untested; a lead, not a finding)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G002",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G003",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G004",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G002:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE00000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G002:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE00001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57G002",
    "text": "Every `remove`, `insert`, `update` and `retype` runs `checkArtifactLinkIntegrity(store, artifactId)` before the operation and again in `withLinkCheck` after it, over the whole artifact (read from `service.ts`), so one `remove` of a task inside a 600-block thread file costs two full link-integrity sweeps on top of the removal itself.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G003:links:Link:00D0WPKE28006",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G003:links:Link:00D0WPKE28006:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2G000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "28"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G003:links:Link:00D0WPKE2G001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G003:links:Link:00D0WPKE2G001:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2G002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "90"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57G003",
    "text": "The verify-slowdown issues, [the `npm run verify` entry](#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001) and [its resolved \"why\" entry](#id/BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000), name the same kind of operation, `checkLinkIntegrity`'s corpus sweep, as the one that went from low hundreds of milliseconds fresh to 12 to 55 seconds late in a long process, so the sweeps are a candidate for the removal stall.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G004",
    "text": "No test has separated the sweeps from the tombstone hard-deletes above.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G005:links:Link:00D0WPKE2G003",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G005:links:Link:00D0WPKE2G003:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2G004",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "119"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57G005",
    "text": "The sweeps are real and are measured (see Measurements), but two of them cost seconds (derived), not the minutes seen; [their own issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001) carries them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G006",
    "text": "**A process-lifetime slowdown, the same mechanism as the verify slowdown** (hypothesis, not a finding)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WZYWFR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G008",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G009",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00A",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007:links:Link:00D0WPKE2G005",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007:links:Link:00D0WPKE2G005:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2G006",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "62"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2R001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "124"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE00002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G007:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE00003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57G007",
    "text": "It would be the process-lifetime slowdown already recorded in [the `npm run verify` entry](#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001) and [its resolved \"why\" entry](#id/BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000): a long-lived node process that degrades, here the service at about 5 GB resident after about three hours, where a process split is not an option because the service is the shared store.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G008",
    "text": "The earlier slowdown showed up as steps running 12 to 55 seconds instead of hundreds of milliseconds, with oxigraph at roughly 1 GB, not as multi-minute stalls with no answer at all.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G009",
    "text": "The repeat on a fresh process fits poorly with a slowdown that builds up over a process's lifetime, though degradation within a few minutes of heavy work would still match.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G00A",
    "text": "The earlier entry's leading guess was a JIT-level degradation, which this entry does not test.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G00B",
    "text": "If it is the same mechanism, the profiling that entry proposes (`--prof` or `--trace-deopt`) is the next step, run against the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G00C",
    "text": "**Measurements**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00D",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00F",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R001",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R002",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R006",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R007",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R009",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00A",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00B",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00D:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE08000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00D:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE08001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57G00D",
    "text": "**One full-store scan costs 136 to 144 ms at 39.6k quads** (measured, in a scratch process)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00E:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE0G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00E:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE0G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Caveat",
    "text": "Caveat: the 39.6k count had no recorded method. The store holds 41,752 quads by `store.size`, measured 2026-10-10.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57G00F",
    "text": "**A whole-artifact link-integrity sweep costs 1.7 to 2.5 ms a live block, so about 0.6 to 0.9 s on a 367-block thread file** (measured per block)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R000:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R000:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R002:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2R003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "35"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE0G002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE0G003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R000",
    "text": "Two sweeps cost seconds (derived); [their own issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001) carries them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R001",
    "text": "**Pruning the removed blocks costs about 6 s for 42 blocks on top of a fixed 2.3 s** (derived from the per-scan cost; read)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R002",
    "text": "**Removing one `#### Turn` of a thread (34 embedded nodes) took 30 to 40 s with the event loop blocked, and the state flush added 16 to 20 s** (measured by the Coder 2026-10-02 and recorded here 2026-10-10)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R003",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R004",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R003:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE0R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R003:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE0R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Conditions",
    "text": "Conditions: seven bounded runs of the removal path on `/tmp` copies of the store, nothing written to the real graph or the live service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R004",
    "text": "The pre-sweep cost about 0.6 s, `runRemove` 9 to 10.6 s, the content flush 19 to 29 s and the post-sweep 0.2 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R005",
    "text": "`runRemove` did exactly 34 full-store scans, one per embedded node, at 208 to 352 ms each.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R006",
    "text": "**The heaviest task (122 embedded nodes) was still inside `runRemove` when the 60-second limit hit, after 60 scans, and the average cost per scan rose from 130 ms to 3,013 ms across them** (measured by the Coder, same runs)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R007",
    "text": "**Under `--trace-gc`, Mark-Compact time per ten scans rose from 1.0 s to 28.3 s of that window's 29.2 s** (measured by the Coder, same runs)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R008:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE10000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R008:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE10001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "It was triggered by external memory pressure",
    "text": "It was triggered by external memory pressure: each scan retained about 9 MB of heap and 21 MB of external memory until the event loop turned, and resident size reached 2.0 GB after 60 scans.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R009",
    "text": "**Repeated scans alone slowed down; 160 deletions did not, and a fresh `Store` did not restore the speed** (measured by the Coder, same runs)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00A",
    "text": "**Content and state flushes cost 3 to 4 times as much after a removal** (measured by the Coder, same runs)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00B",
    "text": "**An in-memory removal of the heaviest coder tasks in a fresh process did not finish in 100 s** (measured by the Coder)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00C:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE10002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00C:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE10003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Caveat",
    "text": "Caveat: consistent with the mechanism but not attributed to a step.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00D:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D0W044DG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00D:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R004:props:StringProp:00D0WZV820000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "137"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00D",
    "text": "**A settled scratch service marked dirty by a view op took 12.5 s to stop, so it misses the client's 10 s stop wait** (measured, 2 of 2, [the restart entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W044DG001))",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00E:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE10004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00E:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE18000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00E",
    "text": "Consistent with the \"didn't stop within 10s of SIGTERM\" in Symptom, not an explanation of it: that process was stuck CPU-bound for more than 40 minutes, and this figure comes from a settled scratch service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00F",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00G",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00H",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00J",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00K",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00M",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00N",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00G:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE18001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00G:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE18002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00G",
    "text": "The 5.4 and 12 minute stalls would need about 2,300 and 5,000 such scans at 140 ms, and whether those tasks held that many embedded nodes is not known.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00H",
    "text": "A task of about 120 embedded nodes plausibly takes minutes, which fits the 5.4 and 12 minute stalls; it is not proven, because no run finished a removal of that size and `.threads/grapher.md` was not measured.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00J:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R006",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00J:links:Link:00D0WPKE2R006:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE2R007",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "118"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00J",
    "text": "The whole mechanism against a stall is untested; it needs the per-operation timings and a profile during a stall that [the no-coverage issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001) lists.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00K",
    "text": "Whether the sweeps or the tombstone hard-deletes cost more is untested: no test has separated them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00M",
    "text": "That the tombstone hard-deletes at shutdown and startup are the likely cost is not tested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00N",
    "text": "That the scans' wrappers are the source of the garbage-collector pressure and the external-memory growth is read, not tested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00P",
    "text": "That this is the verify slowdown again is a hypothesis, not a finding.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00Q",
    "text": "**Workaround**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00R",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00S"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00R:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE1G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00R:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE1G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00R",
    "text": "Wait, retry the command unchanged, and do not kill the process.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00S:links:Link:00D0WPKE30000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00S:links:Link:00D0WPKE30000:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE30001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "140"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00S",
    "text": "Killing the service lost every removal, because the thread tier's `.state/` mirror had not been flushed since before the removals, which is [its own issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WPK57R00T",
    "text": "**Related**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00V",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00W",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00X",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00Y",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK580000",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK580001",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK580002",
      "BlockNode:00D0Y9KNP8001",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK580003",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK580004",
      "BlockNode:00D0WPK580005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00V:links:Link:00D0WPKE30002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00V:links:Link:00D0WPKE30002:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE30003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00V:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE1G002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00V:props:StringProp:00D0WPKE1G003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "[The service-ping issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001)",
    "text": "[The service-ping issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001): a command can fail with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" while the service is up.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WPK57R00W:links:Link:00D0WPKE30004",
