  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WQXNW8001",
    "text": "**Verification — the pilot subtree of the removal-stall issue read in full, with two corrections and one shape change proposed** (2026-10-10, orchestrator): `aperas check-links` is clean. The issue keeps its id and now has six children (Symptom, Root cause, Measurements, Not proven, Workaround, Related) in 78 blocks, none over about 370 characters; every status label (\"measured\", \"read\", \"derived\", \"untested\", \"hypothesis, not a finding\") sits on its own bullet, and the Grapher's comparison of numbers, dates, code spans and link targets found nothing lost after three fixes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8002",
      "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8003",
      "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8004",
      "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8002:props:StringProp:00D0WQXYP8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8002:props:StringProp:00D0WQXYP8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Correction 1 — an over-claim**",
    "text": "**Correction 1 — an over-claim**: under Measurements the line \"A service marked dirty by a view op takes 12.5 s to stop\" ends \"This explains the 'didn't stop within 10s of SIGTERM' in Symptom\". The 12.5 s was measured on a settled scratch service; the stop in Symptom failed on a process that stayed CPU-bound for more than 40 minutes. The measurement shows a dirty service also misses the 10 s wait, so a failed stop does not by itself show a stall; it does not explain that one. The old text said only \"consistent with\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Correction 2 — the added link**",
    "text": "**Correction 2 — the added link**: the Grapher linked \"the service-ping issue above\" to the issue about the same \"No ApeironNgn service running\" message. That is the right target and stays. The \"leak issue in `issues/treeview.md`\" is still unlinked and should be found and linked.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Shape change proposed**",
    "text": "**Shape change proposed**: the established cause is buried. The measured mechanism (scans create wrappers that are released only after a garbage collection and an event-loop turn) sits as the third bullet under the third suspected cause, while Root cause opens with \"five suspected causes; no run has attributed a stall to any of them\". The user's pattern is root cause, then rationale, then measurements, so the established cause belongs first, and the suspected ones follow under their own heading. For single-cause issues the cause goes directly under Root cause, without a cause level (the Grapher's own question, answered yes).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WQXNW8005",
    "text": "Waiting on the user's review of the pilot before the other eight are touched, as decided.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0WQXNW8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0WYXHXG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0WYXHXG001",
    "text": "**Decision — apply the pilot's two corrections and the shape change, then restructure the other service issues the same way** (2026-10-10, user, answering the direct question): \"apply those fixes to the pilot and then restructure the other eight service issues in the same shape.\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0WYXHXG002",
      "BlockNode:00D0WYXHXR000",
