      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00E:props:StringProp:00D0X1T848003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ3R00E",
    "text": "**The store is Oxigraph's WASM store, whose linear memory grows and never shrinks, and each reload builds a new store, so a leak in reload or removal could keep old stores alive** (hypothesis, written 2026-10-02 as untested; measured in part since: the reload keeps the old store alive until an event-loop turn (2026-10-10), and external memory added by the boot sweeps was seen never to shrink; no leak in reload or removal was shown. After [the `free()` landing](../history/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG003) of 2026-10-12 the old `Store` is still left to the garbage collector at reload, because the whole-store `free()` on reload was left out. The growth that followed the unfreed wrappers of the scans stopped in a scratch process, where eight scans stay flat at about 265 MB, and a fresh service answered at 379 MB resident where a fresh service had idled at 1.05 to 1.5 GB, one sample; the removal scan is replaced by the object-bound form of commit `0a7a226`. Whether resident memory still grows over a longer run is not shown)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00F:links:Link:00D0X1T860002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00F:links:Link:00D0X1T860002:props:StringProp:00D0X1T860003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "87"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00F:props:StringProp:00D0X1T848004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00F:props:StringProp:00D0X1T848005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ3R00F",
    "text": "A reload also builds a new `Store` and leaves the old one to the garbage collector, as [the boot and shutdown issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001) describes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ3R00G",
    "text": "**Each full-store scan allocates a JavaScript `Quad` per store quad, a candidate source of garbage-collector pressure and of the external-memory growth recorded here** (read, untested; from the investigation's code survey)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00H:links:Link:00D0X1T860004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00H:links:Link:00D0X1T860004:props:StringProp:00D0X1T868000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "30"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00H:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00H:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ3R00H",
    "text": "`allIdsOfKind`, the scan that [the removal-stall issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) charges per embedded node, allocates a JavaScript `Quad` for every store quad on each call (about 40k objects, about 140 ms).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ3R00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40000",
    "text": "**Measurements**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40001",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000B",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000E",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000H",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000J"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40001:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84G002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40001:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84G003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Conditions** (by the Coder in the store-size investigation, 2026-10-10)",
    "text": "**Conditions** (by the Coder in the store-size investigation, 2026-10-10): scratch processes and scratch services on copies under `/tmp`, single runs unless a count is given, machine load average 2 to 3.5, the live service not stopped or touched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40002",
    "text": "**The store holds 41,752 quads by `store.size`** (measured)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40005",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40006",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40007",
      "BlockNode:00D217Y2N8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40003:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84G004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40003:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84G005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40003",
    "text": "29,537 come from the content mirror and 12,216 from `.state/`, one shared; 10,622 nodes, 0 dangling, 0 duplicate ids.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40004",
    "text": "The count equals the length of a full `store.match`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40005",
    "text": "The live service logged 41,246 at its boot, so the live store does hold the thread partition.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40006",
    "text": "The earlier 37,000 and 39,600 had no recorded method.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40007",
    "text": "A count of about 50,610 derived from the mirror overshoots, because `add()` was called 46,519 times and 4,767 of those were duplicates (every `parent` quad is emitted twice, from the child's `parent` field and from the parent's `children` array, `store.ts` lines 95 and 112).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40008",
    "text": "**The engine is not the cost** (measured)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40009:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40009:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ40009",
    "text": "Bare Oxigraph 0.5.11 (Node CJS build, wasm, in memory) costs about 0.47 KB resident and 0.59 KB external per quad when bulk-loaded and about 1.3 KB external per quad with per-quad `add` (rssAnon 59 to 196 MB for 10k to 100k quads), so 41.7k quads are 20 to 55 MB.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000A",
    "text": "The idle 1.3 GB is about 26 to 36 KB per quad, so the hypothesis that the store itself is that large does not hold.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000B",
    "text": "**Where the memory goes** (measured)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000C",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000C:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84R002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000C:props:StringProp:00D0X1T84R003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000C",
    "text": "After `rehydrateStore` alone rss was 273 MB over a 119 MB baseline (heapUsed 60 MB, external 81 MB), about 3.7 KB per quad including parse garbage, and the JSON parse took 28 ms.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000D",
    "text": "After the boot sweeps and the link sweep rss was 572 MB with external 282 MB, the V8 heap back to about 54 MB after a `gc()` and an event-loop turn, and external never shrinking.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000E:links:Link:00D0X1T868001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D0W00YCR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000E:links:Link:00D0X1T868001:props:StringProp:00D0X1T868002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "76"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000E",
    "text": "**A reload leaves the old store alive until an event-loop turn** (measured, [the reload entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W00YCR001))",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000F",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000F:props:StringProp:00D0X1T850000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000F:props:StringProp:00D0X1T850001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000F",
    "text": "Each synchronous rehydrate adds a store of about 75 MB external, and a reload-style cycle reached rss 1.73 GB by its fourth run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000G",
    "text": "A dirty reload on a scratch service reached 1.26 GB.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000E",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000H",
    "text": "**The live service's high-water mark is 1.66 GB** (VmHWM, read from `/proc`)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000J:links:Link:00D0X1T868003",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000J:links:Link:00D0X1T868003:props:StringProp:00D0X1T868004",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "340"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000J",
    "text": "**Each full-store scan retained about 9 MB of heap and 21 MB of external memory until the event loop turned, with resident size at 2.0 GB after 60 scans of the heaviest task** (the removal measurement of 2026-10-02: seven bounded runs on `/tmp` copies by the Coder, nothing written to the real graph or the live service; its figures are in [the removal-stall issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000))",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000K",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000M",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000N",
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000M:props:StringProp:00D0X1T858000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000M:props:StringProp:00D0X1T858001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000M",
    "text": "Not known whether the climb and the stall share a cause.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000N",
    "text": "The live service's own phases are not measured (they would need the user's approval to stop it).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000P",
    "text": "The climb to 5.8 GB under heavy use is not measured: no scratch run reproduced it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Measurements still to take",
    "text": "Measurements still to take: have the service report `process.memoryUsage()` (heap used, external, array buffers) and the store's own size, and start it with `--heapsnapshot-signal=SIGUSR2` so a snapshot can be taken when the process is large, since the external sampler cannot see inside it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X59G5R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000R:links:Link:00D0X1T868005",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000R:links:Link:00D0X1T868005:props:StringProp:00D0X1T868006",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "70"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000R",
    "text": "The measurements that would tell these hypotheses apart are listed in [the no-coverage issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X59G5R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000S",
    "text": "**Workaround**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000T"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000T:props:StringProp:00D0X1T858002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000T:props:StringProp:00D0X1T858003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000T",
    "text": "A restarted service returns to about 1.3 GB, but a restart is for the user to approve.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ4000V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X1SZ4000V",
    "text": "**Related**",
