  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X3TH58001",
    "text": "**Verification — batch 1 of the issue restructuring read, and two shape decisions for the remaining batches** (2026-10-10, orchestrator): `aperas check-links` is clean. Read from the graph: the removal-stall issue now has Root cause = **Established mechanism** then **Suspected causes** (\"five; no run has attributed a stall to any of them\"), its 12.5 s stop line says the settled scratch service \"misses the client's 10 s stop wait\", the only \"explain\" left is the old text's own \"age and heap size alone do not explain the stall\", and the leak issue is linked (`issues/treeview.md`, found by the Grapher). The boot-and-shutdown issue and the memory issue keep their ids and have the pilot's children; the memory issue's \"roughly 350 times the data size\" is kept with a \"Corrected 2026-10-10\" child and \"overturned\" under Measurements.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58002:props:StringProp:00D0X3TTJG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58002:props:StringProp:00D0X3TTJG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X3TH58002",
    "text": "**Decision — a seventh child, Fix directions, where the old text had them** (orchestrator, answering the Grapher's question; open to the user's veto): the old text of several issues ends with \"Fix directions: none decided. Candidates, none tried: …\" and \"Measurements still to take\", which sit wrongly under **Not proven** in batch 1. A separate **Fix directions** child (saying \"none decided\" where that is so) keeps them from reading as unproven claims, and adds no content. Batch 1's two issues are moved to it in the next batch.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X3TH58003",
    "text": "**Decision — keep the per-item date and status tag** such as \"(measured 2026-10-10)\" on a bullet (orchestrator, answering the Grapher's question): the findings come from two dates, 2026-10-02 and 2026-10-10, and the date tells the reader which conditions apply.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X3TH58001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X59G5R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X59G5R001",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
