        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQER002",
    "text": "**In the service** (read)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER003:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0G0004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER003:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0G0005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQER003",
    "text": "There is no timing or memory logging.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER004",
    "text": "`APERAS_DEBUG_TIMING` output is lost because `spawnService` starts the service with `stdio: 'ignore'`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER005",
    "text": "`logService` (`service.log`) is the only durable channel and holds startup lines only, so a stall of 5.4 or 12 minutes left no line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER006",
    "text": "**In the tests and scripts** (read)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER007",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00A",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER007:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0G8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER007:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0G8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQER007",
    "text": "`verify.ts` (749 lines) and `verifyExtended.ts` (757 lines) run in-process against a `rehydrateStore()` copy, never import `service.ts` or `serviceClient.ts`, never spawn the service, and never call `runRemove` or `withLinkCheck`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER008:links:Link:00D0X5K0HR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER008:links:Link:00D0X5K0HR000:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0HR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "157"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQER008",
    "text": "`verifySupport.ts#instrumentStepTiming`, a `console.log` wrapper that times each \"N. Testing...\" step, is the only timing harness and produced the record in [the `npm run verify` entry](#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER009",
    "text": "`apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts` checks rehydrate and field access only.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00A",
    "text": "`packages/web/devApiServer.ts` is one more concurrent client that calls `request()` with no timeout but is not a load test.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00B",
    "text": "There are no concurrent-client, latency or long-uptime scripts, and no test of the timers, `reloadStore`, `shutdown` or the SIGTERM path.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00C",
    "text": "**The external sampler**, a Python script in a session scratch area outside the repo, has these gaps (read from the script and its CSV)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00D",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00E",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00F",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00T"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00D:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0GG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00D:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0GG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00D",
    "text": "The lock path (`/run/user/1000/aperas/apeironngn.lock`), the probe node (`BlockNode:00CE8XWZK0000`, which a future prune or another graph can remove, turning every probe into a false failure) and `aperas` on `PATH` are hard-coded.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00E",
    "text": "The probe is a full `aperas show` client, so each probe time includes a `tsx` client start (541 ms on the first row) and a 60 s cadence cannot resolve a stall of seconds.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00F",
    "text": "`probe()` keeps only whether `\"@id\"` appears in stdout and discards stderr and the exit code, so the 300 ms ping failure, a request error and the 20 s timeout all read as a failed probe, which is exactly what the 11 failed probes need to be told apart by.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**It has no**",
    "text": "**It has no**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00H",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00J",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00K",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00M",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00N",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00P",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00Q",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00R",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00S"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00H:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0GG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00H:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0GG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00H",
    "text": "raw ping over the unix socket at 1 s cadence,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00J",
    "text": "separate main-thread and garbage-collector-thread columns,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00K",
    "text": "`VmHWM`,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00M",
    "text": "`/proc/<pid>/io` write bytes,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00N",
    "text": "mirror-file size or modification time (flush cadence would be visible for free),",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00P",
    "text": "join with `service.log` by time,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00Q",
    "text": "stall durations or memory slope in its report,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00R",
    "text": "metadata row,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00S",
    "text": "test.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQER00T",
    "text": "It records only a client count and not the verbs of the running `aperas` commands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQER00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Fix directions**",
    "text": "**Fix directions**: none decided; from the investigation's Freeflow and the orchestrator's recommendations.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0006",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000B",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0001",
    "text": "**Instrumentation** in a new `apeironNgn/serviceDiagnostics.ts` behind one environment switch read by `spawnService` (which already copies `process.env`), all through `logService`:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0002:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0002:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0002",
    "text": "an event-loop delay histogram,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0003",
    "text": "`process.memoryUsage()` and heap statistics every 30 to 60 s,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0004",
    "text": "one timestamped line per boot phase,",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0005",
    "text": "per-operation timings split into queue wait, pre-check, operation, flush and post-check, for operations over about 250 ms.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0006",
    "text": "**Limits** (read, unverified where marked)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0007",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0007:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H0004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0007:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H0005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0007",
    "text": "The histogram records only when the loop turns, so a 5-minute stall appears as one sample after it ends, and a worker-thread watchdog on a `SharedArrayBuffer` heartbeat would see it live (not built or tried).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0008",
    "text": "`--heapsnapshot-signal=SIGUSR2` can reach the service through `NODE_OPTIONS` with no code change but blocks the loop on a large process, needs about that much memory again, and misses the WASM memory (the V8 heap is about 2.1 GB against up to 5.8 GB resident).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF0009",
    "text": "`--cpu-prof` writes only at exit and cannot capture a stuck or killed process.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000A",
    "text": "For a live stall an inspector or `perf` is the candidate (unverified).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000B",
    "text": "**The sampler** moves into the repo as Python under `monorepo/packages/cli/diagnostics/` with a `svc:sample` script, adds a raw-socket ping each second that keeps the failure text, and drops the one-minute client probe.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The first measurements, in order**",
    "text": "**The first measurements, in order**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000D",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000E",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000F",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000G",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000H",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000J",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000K",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000M"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000D:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "true"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000D:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0H8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000D",
    "text": "Event-loop lag and `process.memoryUsage()` logged by the service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000E",
    "text": "Per-operation timing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000F",
    "text": "One controlled `remove` on a fresh service against the same after a long uptime, with the link sweep timed alone.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000G",
    "text": "A CPU profile during a stall.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000H",
    "text": "A heap snapshot at idle and when large.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000J",
    "text": "A timestamped boot log and ping timing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000K",
    "text": "Sweep cost against tombstone count.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000M",
    "text": "Dehydrate time at current node counts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000N",
    "text": "**Related**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000P",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000Q"
    ]
  },
  {
