          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000P:links:Link:00D0X5K0J0000:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0J0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "149"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000P:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0HG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000P:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0HG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5JQF000P",
    "text": "This is the missing ground for [the spurious \"not running\" issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001), [the removal stall](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) and [the memory issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001), whose mechanisms rest on code reading and one reproduction each.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000Q:links:Link:00D0X5K0J0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000Q:links:Link:00D0X5K0J0002:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0J0003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000Q:links:Link:00D0X5K0J0004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000Q:links:Link:00D0X5K0J0004:props:StringProp:00D0X5K0J0005",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "69"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "[The whole-artifact re-parse issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001) and [the boot and shutdown issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001)",
    "text": "[The whole-artifact re-parse issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001) and [the boot and shutdown issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001): the two cost centres other than the removal scan whose figures are measured only in a scratch process.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5JQF000N",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXX8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXX8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G001",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G005",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G006",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G002:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXX8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G002:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXX8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G002",
    "text": "The first `aperas insert` of one turn failed with that message while `aperas service start` immediately reported the service already running (pid 220722).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G003",
    "text": "The same message came back later in that turn on `aperas project issues/linking.md`, and in a second turn on an `aperas update` between otherwise working commands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G004",
    "text": "Every unchanged retry succeeded with no restart.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G005:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CRBJ0VYG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G005:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ0000:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXZ0001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "7"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G005",
    "text": "Unlike [the silent death below](#id/BlockNode:00CRBJ0VYG001), the service never went down.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G006",
    "text": "**Reproduced by load later the same day**, in the v4.3 filing sweep: while the service was busy after an `aperas remove --flush` of a finished thread task (the process was alive at 100 to 290 percent CPU for minutes), every command, `aperas show` included, failed with that message.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G007:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXX8004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G007:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G007",
    "text": "The same commands worked once the service was idle again, which fits a 300 ms ping reading a busy service as down.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Two earlier observations point the same way**",
    "text": "**Two earlier observations point the same way**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G009:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G009:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G009",
    "text": "`aperas service start` answered \"Already running\" with the old pid right after a command failed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00A",
    "text": "`service.log` holds only startup lines, with no shutdown, flush or connect-failure line, so it cannot say why a client could not reach a live service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00B",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXG004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00C",
    "text": "**A likely cause**, read from the code and consistent with the load observations under Symptom and Measurements:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00D",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00E",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00D:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXG005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00D:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00D",
    "text": "`ensureServiceRunning` (`packages/cli/src/apeironNgn/serviceClient.ts:149`) throws that message whenever `ping()` returns false.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00E",
    "text": "`ping()` (line 83) turns every error, a timeout included, into `false` after `PING_TIMEOUT_MS = 300`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00F",
    "text": "A service busy with a flush or an ingest and slow to answer within 300 ms therefore reads as not running.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "text": "**The mechanism**, from the investigation's code survey of 2026-10-02 (read from `service.ts`, `serviceClient.ts` and `kgService.ts`; the failures are consistent with it, and no direct test has isolated it):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00H",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00J",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00K",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00M",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00N",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00P"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00H:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00H:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXXR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00H",
    "text": "Every request, `ping` included, enters `handleConnection`, is chained onto the single promise `queue` by `enqueue`, and runs `handle`, which has no `await`, so each operation is one uninterrupted synchronous run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00J",
    "text": "A `ping` therefore waits behind the operation in flight and every request already queued ahead of it, and the client's `ping()` gives up after `PING_TIMEOUT_MS = 300`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00K",
    "text": "The 300 ms bound covers queue wait plus the ping's own handling, not whether the loop is stuck.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00M",
    "text": "Any operation over about 0.3 s, or a queue of two or three, makes the next command say \"No ApeironNgn service running\" with nothing stalled.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00N",
    "text": "Every other command first calls `ensureServiceRunning`, which is that one 300 ms ping, and `request()` itself sends with no timeout, so a command that passes the ping waits as long as the service takes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the queue takes depends on what the queue holds**",
    "text": "**What the queue takes depends on what the queue holds**:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Q",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00R",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00S"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Q:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Q:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ0002:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXZ0003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Q:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Q:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00Q",
    "text": "[Every write re-parses its whole artifact twice](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00R:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ0004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00R:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ0004:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXZ0005",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00R",
    "text": "[A task removal runs a full-store scan per embedded node](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00S:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00S:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ8000:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXZ8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00S",
    "text": "[Boot does seconds of synchronous work before the socket exists](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00T",
    "text": "**Measurements**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00V",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00V:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00V:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00V",
    "text": "**After the lock turned ready, every `aperas` command failed with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" for 19.5 to 23.0 s in 6 of 6 starts** (measured 2026-10-10 by the Coder in the store-size investigation; scratch service, 6 cold starts, load average 2 to 3.5)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00W",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00X"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00W:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00W:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00W",
    "text": "They failed because the startup link sweep is enqueued on the event loop right after `markReady` (`service.ts` lines 818 to 826) and the 300 ms `ping` times out.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00X:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ8002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D0W05P08001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00X:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ8002:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXZ8003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "101"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00X",
    "text": "This is the mechanism above shown on a service that is not stalled, only busy; the measurement is in [the start entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W05P08001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00Y",
    "text": "**A settled service answers a `profile list` in 0.55 s wall** (measured 2026-10-10, same runs)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G00Z",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G010",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G011",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G012",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G013"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G010:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXY8004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G010:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXYG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G010",
    "text": "How much of a failed ping's 300 ms is queue wait against the in-flight operation is untested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G011",
    "text": "The fix to try, under Fix directions, is untested against a counted run of the same load.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G012",
    "text": "A concurrent second client as the cause of the earlier drops is not tested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G013",
    "text": "**The sampler's recorded failures fit it without a stall** (read, not proven):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G014",
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G015"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G014:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXYG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G014:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXYG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G014",
    "text": "Of its 11 failed probes, three are at 5, 12 and 19 percent CPU with 2 to 4 `aperas` clients running (21:11:24, 21:14:24, 21:15:24), where another client's operation or flush was probably queued ahead of the probe.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G013",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G015:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ8004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G015:links:Link:00D0X5TXZ8004:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXZ8005",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "160"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G015",
    "text": "The sampler keeps only whether the answer held `\"@id\"` and discards the failure text, so it cannot tell the ping failure from a request error or a timeout (see [the no-coverage issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G013",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X5TK4G016",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G017"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G017:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXYR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G017:props:StringProp:00D0X5TXYR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Fix to try**",
    "text": "**Fix to try**: retry the ping once or twice, or raise the timeout, before throwing, and say in the message when a socket exists but did not answer.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X5TK4G016",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0001:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0001:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RA0001",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RA0002",
    "text": "**The scans** (read from the source)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA000A",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA000B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0003:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0003:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RA0003",
    "text": "`allIdsOfKind` (`dehydrate.ts` lines 49 to 58) does `store.match(null, null, null, null)` and reads `q.subject` on each of the 41.7k quads.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "It is called by",
    "text": "It is called by:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0005",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0006",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0007",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0008"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0005:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G006",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0005:props:StringProp:00D0X6630G007",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RA0005",
    "text": "`tombstoneVacuousContainers` (`node.ts` lines 2230 to 2248, once per fixed-point loop, so at least once).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`pruneUnreachableTombstones` (lines 2183 to 2214",
    "text": "`pruneUnreachableTombstones` (lines 2183 to 2214: 2 calls for the mark roots and 3 for the sweep).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RA0007",
    "text": "`pruneStaleUnfolds` (line 2087, 1 call).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RA0008",
    "text": "`checkLinkIntegrity` (`linkIntegrity.ts` lines 85 and 86, 1 call).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RA0009",
    "text": "Together that is at least 8 scans in boot, and 4 scans per flush (`dehydrate.ts` lines 111 to 116 and 149 to 168).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RA000A",
    "text": "Further matches are made by `wrap` (`node.ts` line 2144, a new object plus `Object.seal` per node), `readField` (lines 156 to 162, one `store.match` per field read) and `childrenOf` (lines 73 to 84, one match plus one more per child).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RA000B",
    "text": "The second pass of `rehydrateStore` (`store.ts` lines 154 to 158) scans the whole store for dangling references (97 ms).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RB0000",
    "text": "**The wrappers the scans leave** (read from the source)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RA0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0001",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0001:props:StringProp:00D0X6630R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0001:props:StringProp:00D0X6630R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RB0001",
    "text": "`store.match` returns an array of `Quad` wrappers (`oxigraph/node.js` lines 611 to 620, then `.slice()`), so each scan creates 41.7k quad wrappers plus the term wrappers.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RB0002",
    "text": "The wrappers are released only after a garbage collection and a macro-task turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RB0003",
    "text": "WASM linear memory, once grown, is never returned (the comments at `node.ts` lines 2166 to 2169 say \"WASM's grow-only memory\").",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RB0004",
    "text": "**Measurements**",
