            "key": "position",
            "value": "47"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RB8007",
    "text": "The engine alone is not slow at this size (see [the memory issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) for its per-quad cost).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X65RB8008",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8009",
      "BlockNode:00D1DP5GG0001",
      "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8000",
      "BlockNode:00D0Y9HG30001",
      "BlockNode:00D0Y9HG30005",
      "BlockNode:00D0Y9HG30009",
      "BlockNode:00D0Y9HG3000D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8009:props:StringProp:00D0X6631R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8009:props:StringProp:00D0X6631R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X65RB8009",
    "text": "The object-bound `removeDanglingUnfolds` landed in commit `0a7a226` and ran in the live service: it replaces the scan of every quad, made once per embedded node removed, with one `store.match` on the predicate `unfolds` and the deleted id as object. Result (2026-10-11, one removal in the live service): a task of 164 live blocks and 101 embedded `Link` nodes was removed in 3.7 s with no stall, the tree then showed every other task intact, and `aperas check-links` scanned 6,549 live blocks with 0 discrepancies. Before it, removals of 42 and 31 blocks stalled the service for 5.4 and 12 minutes, and a scratch removal of 34 embedded nodes took 21 s with 34 full scans. On a copy of the real store the old form took 512.8 ms per deleted id and the object-bound form 0.015 ms. It covers every field of a `TreeView` that holds an unfolded id and exists in code, which is `unfolds` alone. The `free()` item below landed as commit `d794060` on branch `oxigraph`, with its measurements and its live check recorded in that item; Layers 1 to 3 and the pause are not decided and not tried, and are parked until the comparison with a JavaScript engine.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB8008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
