    "title": "[The memory issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) and [the removal-stall issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000)",
    "text": "[The memory issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001) and [the removal-stall issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000): the scan point already in them (a candidate source of garbage-collector pressure, read, untested) is extended and linked to this entry; this one is filed separately because it covers boot, flush and read paths and not only removal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X65RB800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X6PVC0001",
    "text": "**Question — what defines a \"turn\", and why does one op not wait for the last op's turn when all ops are synchronous?** (2026-10-10, user, while the Grapher restructures the issues; answered by the orchestrator, no dispatch): the answer, read by the orchestrator from `service.ts` (lines 215 to 220, `enqueue`, and 698 to 727, `handleConnection`) and not yet confirmed by the Coder:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0002:props:StringProp:00D0X6Q5TR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0002:props:StringProp:00D0X6Q5TR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**A turn is one pass of the Node event loop**",
    "text": "**A turn is one pass of the Node event loop**: it runs one task (a socket read, a timer, an `setImmediate`, a garbage-collector finalization callback), then drains the promise (microtask) queue, then picks the next task. Synchronous code of any length, however many calls deep, is inside one task. Finishing an op returns to its caller and is not a turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`enqueue` serializes, and serializing is not turn-separating**",
    "text": "**`enqueue` serializes, and serializing is not turn-separating**: `queue.then(fn, fn)` starts the next op as a microtask when the previous op's promise settles. Microtasks drain before the loop moves to the next task, so when ops are waiting in the queue, they run back to back with no turn between them. When the queue is idle, each request starts in the turn of its own socket read and the loop turns before the next request arrives. A backlog (the 300 ms `ping`, the timed flushes and every client's retries all go through `enqueue`) is therefore the case with no turns.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Inside one op there is never a turn**",
    "text": "**Inside one op there is never a turn**: a reload, the boot sweeps, or a removal of 34 embedded nodes is one synchronous run, so its garbage cannot be finalized until it ends. That is the 88 s against 8 s measurement.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Untested**",
    "text": "**Untested**: the Coder's runs used a 300 ms pause between phases. Whether a zero-delay `setImmediate` yield is enough, or the finalizer also needs a garbage collection that V8 schedules by itself, has not been measured.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X6PVC0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X7HV3G001",
    "text": "**Verification — batch 2 of the issue restructuring read, and answers to the Grapher's two questions** (2026-10-10, orchestrator): `aperas check-links` is clean. The three issues keep their ids and carry the shape: the no-coverage issue has **Root cause** (the gap itself, in the service and in the tests and scripts), **Fix directions** (\"none decided\", the numbered list of measurements to take kept as a list because the boot issue cites \"measurements 6, 7 and 8\") and **Related**; the spurious \"not running\" issue has **Symptom**, **Root cause**, **Measurements**, **Not proven** and **Fix directions**; the full-store-scans issue has **Root cause**, **Measurements**, **Fix directions** (\"No fix has been tried.\") and **Related**. The fix-direction bullets of the boot and memory issues moved into **Fix directions**.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G002:props:StringProp:00D0X7J4X0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G002:props:StringProp:00D0X7J4X0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X7HV3G002",
    "text": "**Decision — the \"97 ms\" figure stays where the old text had it** (orchestrator): it sits under the \"read\" group in the full-store-scans issue and looks measured with no recorded method. Without a record of how it was taken, moving it to Measurements would raise its strength; it stays as \"read\", and the missing method is the point to note if the figure is ever used.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X7HV3G003",
    "text": "**Decision — the memory issue's pointer bullet stays under Fix directions** (orchestrator): it points to the measurements that would tell the hypotheses apart, which are measurements to take, so the Grapher's move is right.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X7HV3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8FR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8FR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0001",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0004",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0002:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8FR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0002:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0002",
    "text": "`.state/BlockNode.jsonld` was last written at 18:26:20 while 15 `aperas remove --flush` calls, each reporting success, ran after it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0003",
    "text": "Every earlier turn's thread writes persisted only because the turn ended with `aperas zoom`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0004",
    "text": "After the kill, the fresh service rehydrated the stale `.state/` records of the removed tasks beside their tombstoned copies that had leaked into the tracked mirror (see the leak entry in `issues/treeview.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0005",
    "text": "It logged \"323 duplicate @id(s) in the mirror\", merged them, and listed the removed task roots as live again with their descendants tombstoned.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0006",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0007",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000A",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0007:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0007:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0007",
    "text": "In `packages/cli/src/apeironNgn/service.ts`, `insert`, `update`, `remove` and `retype` set only `dirty`, whose `flushIfDirty` writes the tracked content mirror, and that mirror excludes every `.threads/`-scoped node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0008",
    "text": "The thread-scoped `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` records are written only by `flushStateIfDirty` into `.state/`, which does nothing unless `stateDirty` is set.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0009"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0009:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0009:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G0004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK0009",
    "text": "Only the `unfold`, `fold`, `zoom` and profile ops, the garbage-collection sweeps and `shutdown`'s own sweep set `stateDirty`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK000A",
    "text": "The gap is a routing mismatch, not a timer-cadence one, and both timers (3 s and 10 s) work as designed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000B",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000C"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000B:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000B:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK000B",
    "text": "A thread-scoped node is routed to the `.state/` mirror when the store is dehydrated (`THREAD_PARTITIONED_CLASSES`, `isThreadScopedId`), but the dirty flag is chosen without that partition.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK000C",
    "text": "So the four handlers set `dirty`, which feeds the content flush that excludes thread nodes, and never `stateDirty`, which feeds the `.state/` flush that includes them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK000A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8000",
    "text": "**History, from git**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8001",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8001:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8001:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8G8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8001",
    "text": "The `.state/` mirror and `dehydrateStateToJsonLd` arrived on 2026-09-03 with the TreeView refactor (`e4cc806`), for views only, so no node record needed it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8002",
    "text": "`stateDirty` followed in the 09-15 and 09-17 commits (`96ed8f9`, `0624b7d`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8003",
    "text": "The thread partition arrived on 2026-09-27 with the multi-agent v3.0 commit (`b58dc5d`), which added the `zoom` op with `stateDirty = true` and one `dirty = true` and did not touch the four handlers, so the thread tier inherited a flush path built for views.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8004",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8005:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8GG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8005:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8GG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8005",
    "text": "That an external change to the thread `BlockNode` file in `.state/` goes unnoticed today (not checked).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8006",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8GG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8GG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8007",
    "text": "**Fix, agreed 2026-10-02 as three parts that fold all node-related persistence into `.state/`**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK800A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8008:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8GG004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8008:props:StringProp:00D0X8T8GG005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8008",
    "text": "(1) any write to a thread-scoped node sets `stateDirty` (`isThreadScopedId` is already imported in the same file), so the 3-second timer and every `--flush` persist it;",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK8009",
    "text": "(2) the `.state/` divergence stamps cover the thread-partitioned node classes and not only `STATE_CLASSES` (`TreeView`), so an external change to the thread `BlockNode` file there is noticed (not checked: that an external change goes unnoticed today);",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8SYK800A",
    "text": "(3) every flush path writes both mirrors from one rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8SYK8007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG001:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG001:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8TTAG001",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG002:links:Link:00D0X8V4Z8001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG002:links:Link:00D0X8V4Z8001:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z8002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "161"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG002:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG002:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8TTAG002",
    "text": "Because the service runs one operation at a time, every second a write spends in the sweeps is also queue wait for every other client, which is the mechanism in [the spurious \"not running\" issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR000",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR001",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR001:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YG004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR001:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YG005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Read from `service.ts`",
    "text": "Read from `service.ts`: each of the four handlers calls `checkArtifactLinkIntegrity(store, artifactId)` before the operation (`artifactForRef`, then the pre-check, then the `runX` call) and `withLinkCheck` calls it again after, over the whole owning artifact and not only the blocks the operation touched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR002",
    "text": "Each sweep (`collectAllBlockNodes`, then `sweepBlocks`) walks every live block, reads its `text`, parses the whole text with the remark processor (`collectLinkCodesFromText`, no cache).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR003",
    "text": "For each block that has link text it reads `.links`, computes `toPath()` and calls `resolveOneCode` per link.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR004",
    "text": "**Measurements**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR005",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR005:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR005:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Measured in a scratch process",
    "text": "Measured in a scratch process: 638 to 932 ms for `.threads/coder.md` (367 live blocks, 65 links), which is about 1.7 to 2.5 ms per live block, so about 1.3 to 1.9 s for the two sweeps.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR006",
    "text": "For `.threads/grapher.md` (767 blocks, 487 links) the same rate gives about 1.3 to 1.9 s a sweep, derived and not measured, because the in-memory run on that file did not finish in 100 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR007",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR009"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR008:links:Link:00D0X8V4Z8003",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR008:links:Link:00D0X8V4Z8003:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z8004",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "97"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR008:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR008:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4YR003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Derived, not measured",
    "text": "Derived, not measured: the sweeps cost seconds, so on their own they do not reach the minutes of [the removal stall](#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000); they are one of three cost centres of a `remove` there.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR009",
    "text": "Whether the per-write sweep slows the same way in the long-lived service as the corpus sweep did in a long process (see the earlier record under Related) is untested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00A",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00B",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00C",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00B:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00B:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Fix directions",
    "text": "Fix directions: none decided.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Candidates, the grapher's reading and none tried",
    "text": "Candidates, the grapher's reading and none tried:",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00D",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00E",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00D:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00D:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00D",
    "text": "Parse a block's text once and cache the result by that text, so unchanged blocks are not re-parsed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00E",
    "text": "Check after the operation only the blocks it touched and the links that point at them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00F",
    "text": "Keep the pre-check only where it tells something the post-check cannot.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00G",
    "text": "The first measurement is to time the sweep alone on a thread artifact and against block count (item 3 of the investigation's first measurements, which needs per-operation timing the service does not yet have).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00H",
    "text": "**Related**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVQHBP0R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00J",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00K",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00M"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00J:links:Link:00D0X8V4ZG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00J:links:Link:00D0X8V4ZG000:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4ZG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "16"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00J:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z0004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00J:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4Z8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Earlier record",
    "text": "Earlier record: [the `npm run verify` entry](#id/BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001) names the same kind of operation, `checkLinkIntegrity`'s corpus sweep, as the one that went from low hundreds of milliseconds fresh to 12 to 55 seconds late in a long process.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00K:links:Link:00D0X8V4ZG002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00K:links:Link:00D0X8V4ZG002:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4ZG003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00K",
    "text": "[The boot and shutdown issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHCEW8001), whose startup and shutdown sweeps share the full-store scan cost.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00M:links:Link:00D0X8V4ZR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00M:links:Link:00D0X8V4ZR000:props:StringProp:00D0X8V4ZR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8TTAR00M",
    "text": "[The no-coverage issue](#id/BlockNode:00CVQHD7CR001), which lists the measurements that would time the sweep.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8TTAR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG001:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1QR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG001:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1QR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZG001",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W044DG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG003",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG002:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1QR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG002:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1QR003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZG002",
    "text": "After one `unfold ... --view <view>`, the CLI gave up at 10.45 and 10.42 s with \"Service (pid N) didn't stop within 10s of SIGTERM\" and, for `restart`, started no new service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZG003",
    "text": "After the failed stop the old process did exit, so the next `service start` costs about 5.5 s plus about 20 s in which commands are refused (see the start entry below).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR000",
    "text": "A restart, its error at 10 s, a start, its error at 5.5 s and retrying commands until they work adds up to about 40 to 50 s of waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR001",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W044DG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR002",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR002:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR002:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR002",
    "text": "The client's stop wait is shorter than the flushes that the stop runs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR003:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR003:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR003",
    "text": "The SIGTERM handler runs in JavaScript and queues behind the work in flight.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR004",
    "text": "The dirty state is the usual state in agent use.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR005",
    "text": "**Measurements**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W044DG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR006",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR007",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR008",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00B",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00F"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR006:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R0004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR006:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R0005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Conditions** (by the Coder in the store-size investigation, 2026-10-10)",
    "text": "**Conditions** (by the Coder in the store-size investigation, 2026-10-10): a scratch service with its own run directory (`XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, `APERAS_HTTP_PORT=2790`; `getRunDir()` reads `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, `serviceLock.ts` lines 49 to 52), single runs unless a count is given, load average 2 to 3.5; the live lock stayed on pid 33127 throughout.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**An idle `service stop` of a settled service**",
    "text": "**An idle `service stop` of a settled service**: the old pid was gone 1.96 s after the command started (about 1 s of that is CLI startup).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR008",
    "text": "**A restart of an idle settled service**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR009",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR009:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR009:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR009",
    "text": "The pid was gone at 1.64 and 1.60 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00A",
    "text": "The CLI exited 1 at 6.76 and 6.65 s with \"did not become ready in time\", and the new lock turned ready at 6.79 and 6.70 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00B",
    "text": "**After one `unfold ... --view <view>`**, which sets `dirty` and `stateDirty` (`service.ts` lines 520 to 534; an `unfold` without `--view` is a peek and sets nothing)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00C",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00D",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00C:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00C:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1R8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00C",
    "text": "`service stop` and `service restart` took the old pid 12.49 s to exit in 2 of 2 runs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00D",
    "text": "The mirror files show the content flush at 20:51:55 to 56 and the state flush finishing at 20:52:05.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00E",
    "text": "Of the 12.5 s the shutdown sweeps are about 1.6 s and the two flushes the rest.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00B",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00F",
    "text": "**A `restart` issued about 6 s after a start, while the startup link sweep still runs**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00G",
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00H"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00G:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1RG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00G:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1RG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00G",
    "text": "It took 21.08 s for the old pid to go; the CLI gave up at 10.69 s and started nothing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00H",
    "text": "A first attempt failed the same way.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D0X8VQZR00J",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W044DG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00K"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D0X8VQZR00K:props:StringProp:00D0X8W1RG002",
