    "text": "**Replaces**: the unbounded `store.match(null, null, null, null)` in `allIdsOfKind` (`dehydrate.ts` lines 49 to 58) with a match for a kind's type quads only; the scan in `removeDanglingUnfolds` with one object-bound `store.match(null, unfolds, deletedIri, null)`; the reads in `wrap` (`node.ts` line 2144) and `readField` (lines 156 to 162) with one subject-bound match per node. **Corrected 2026-10-11**: the store has no type quads, because `encodeDoc` skips `@type` (`store.ts` line 86), and `urn:aperas:pred:type` is the `type` field of a `BlockNode` (paragraph, heading, listItem), so the `allIdsOfKind` part has no form to be bound on. The `removeDanglingUnfolds` part is done (see the fix status above). What a bound `allIdsOfKind` could use instead: a kind quad written by `encodeDoc` and every creation path (exact, touches many files); a predicate that every instance of the kind carries, which gave identical id sets on a copy of the real store for `ArtifactNode` (54, on `path`), `FolderNode` (17, `path`), `TreeView` (17, `name`) and `Profile` (9, `handle`) and 5,556 against 5,557 for `BlockNode`, the missing one being a stray block with no title, `type`, parent or children, so `BlockNode`, the big kind, stays on the scan; or Layer 2.",
