    "title": "**Scope as the orchestrator reads it, and puts to the user to veto**",
    "text": "**Scope as the orchestrator reads it, and puts to the user to veto**: layer 1 has three forms. The two that are small and local are changed: `allIdsOfKind` (a kind's type quads in place of every quad) and `removeDanglingUnfolds` (one object-bound match in place of the view scan). The third, a subject-bound match for `wrap` and `readField`, is only measured, not changed, because it restructures how every field is read; its numbers decide whether it is tried next.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0YAEKZ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0YAEKZG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Order, with a stop**",
    "text": "**Order, with a stop**: first the equivalence on a copy of the real store (for every kind that callers pass, the ids from the full scan against the ids from the type-quad match); if they differ anywhere, the Coder changes nothing and reports the differences and the cause. Then the cost of each form against the full scan, in time, resident and external memory, and the number of `Quad` objects made. Then the change, with a test that keeps the old scan as a reference. Then the removal of the tasks that took 30 to 40 s and did not finish in 60 s, before and after.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0YAEKZ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D0YAEKZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the change cannot show**",
    "text": "**What the change cannot show**: the live service runs the old code and is restarted only with the user's approval, so every measurement is in scratch processes and the live service is untouched.",
