    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`pruneUnreachableTombstones` with 10 unreachable tombstones",
    "text": "`pruneUnreachableTombstones` with 10 unreachable tombstones: 16.8 s → 3.3 s. Whole boot with them: 160 s → 70 s; rehydrate to ready on a scratch service 81.5 s → 34.4 s (part of the drop is the startup flush, 51.6 → 25.5 s, and the link sweep, 87.4 → 37.5 s, running in a process that no longer retains 20 extra scans of external memory).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Unchanged as expected",
    "text": "Unchanged as expected: boot on a clean store 28.9 s → 29.0 s; dirty reload 94.1 s → 92.3 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What is left in `allIdsOfKind`'s scans**",
    "text": "**What is left in `allIdsOfKind`'s scans**: on a clean store boot has 8 full scans, 1.9 s, 6.6% of 29.0 s, and a flush has 8, 3.7 s, 12.7% of 29.4 s. The rest of boot and flush time is elsewhere: the flushes (14 s and 12 s unyielded) and the link sweep (2 to 18 s), both known to depend on the event loop turning.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D19BJTWR00A",
    "text": "**Routes for `allIdsOfKind`, measured** (BlockNode 5,586 ids, ArtifactNode 54, FolderNode 17, TreeView 17, Profile 9): a bound predicate per kind (`path`, `name`, `handle`) takes 0.05 to 0.24 ms against a 120 to 940 ms scan with identical sets, and `BlockNode` stays on the scan (a `title` or `type` predicate loses the stray block); a kind quad in `encodeDoc` adds 12,155 quads (+25%), about 1.2 s to a 1.5 s rehydrate and 7 MB, with identical sets, and must be written wherever `wrap` first creates a node; a kind index from `seenIds` builds in 12 ms and 7 MB, identical sets, microsecond lookups, and must be kept in step at creation, `hardDeleteNode` and reload (that part not measured).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Subject-bound match against `wrap` and `readField`** (1,000 `BlockNode`s)",
    "text": "**Subject-bound match against `wrap` and `readField`** (1,000 `BlockNode`s): one accessor read 89 to 111 µs, 418 µs for seven fields; one subject-bound match 93 µs, 188 µs with the four literal fields decoded against 229 µs through accessors, about 18% less; layer 3 is not where the time is.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`free()`** (ten scans in one tick, baseline external 90.7 MB)",
    "text": "**`free()`** (ten scans in one tick, baseline external 90.7 MB): left to the finalizer 223 ms a scan and 253.9 MB external; `q.free()` only 162 ms and 115.8 MB; `q.free()` plus the subject term freed 109 ms and 101.3 MB with no growth after the first scan. Each `q.subject` read allocates a new wasm term and `allIdsOfKind` reads it twice per quad.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`npm run verify`**",
    "text": "**`npm run verify`**: on the real mirror it fails at step 7 after 811 s on 4 dangling references, `Link.target` values of the form `BlockNode:X#id/BlockNode:X` in `AperasKG/Apeiron/.state/BlockNode.jsonld` (ids 00CVQ4Z968001, 00CVQHCEW8001, 00D0VAPWBG008, 00D0W02KPG001); step 7 runs before the new step 9c, so the change is not the cause. On a scratch copy with those targets rewritten to the plain id it passes: exit 0 in 1,434 s, steps 7, 9c, 10 and 11 costing 649, 203, 188 and 202 s. These are the doubled anchors the tree view showed on the orchestrator's own Ask citations: a compat link `…#id/BlockNode:X` written from a thread into another artifact is stored with the anchor appended to the target.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The service**",
    "text": "**The service**: it exited on its 30-minute idle timeout while the Coder worked about 86 minutes, so the Coder could not write its thread. The user chose \"Start it with the change\" and the orchestrator started it; `aperas service start` reported \"did not become ready in time\" at 5.4 s, and commands were refused for about 2 minutes while the startup link sweep and the Coder's insert ran, then answered. It runs the changed `node.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19BJTWR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D19KXRP8001",
    "text": "**Question — why are the four link targets malformed, and why is the stray block not removed at restart?** (2026-10-11, user; answered by the orchestrator from the stored records and `node.ts` lines 2196 to 2252, read and not yet checked by the Coder):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8002",
      "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8003",
      "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8002:props:StringProp:00D19KY2PG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8002:props:StringProp:00D19KY2PG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The malformed targets, what is verified**",
    "text": "**The malformed targets, what is verified**: five `Link` records in three nodes of the Coder's Reports (`BlockNode:00D0VY04SG00B`, `BlockNode:00D0VY04SG00F`, `BlockNode:00D0YDBAM0009`) hold targets of the form `BlockNode:X#id/BlockNode:X`. The stored text of those same nodes contains the doubled anchor, `…md#id/BlockNode:X#id/BlockNode:X`, so the doubling is in what was written, and the parser then takes everything after the first `#id/` as the id. The orchestrator's own Ask citations are stored with a single anchor (checked with `aperas show --text`), yet `aperas tree` displays them with the anchor doubled, and a link in the Coder's Report showed it four times. Nothing flags the result: the insert reports \"0 dangling\" and `aperas check-links` is clean, because a target that names no node is not checked (the filed `check-links` gap).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What is likely and not shown**",
    "text": "**What is likely and not shown**: that the Coder copied the doubled form from the tree view, the only place it appears for correctly written links. The code that doubles the anchor in the tree rendering has not been read.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The stray block, what is read**",
    "text": "**The stray block, what is read**: `BlockNode:00CJ2TCV40000` has no `type`, so it is neither a `list` nor a text-less `listItem`, and `tombstoneVacuousContainers` never marks it vacuous; `pruneUnreachableTombstones` skips any block that is not tombstoned (\"never tombstoned — not a GC candidate regardless of reachability\"). So an unreachable block that was never tombstoned is collected by neither sweep, by design. How it came to be a block with only a link is not known. Its link targets `BlockNode:00CJ6TGSX8001`, which exists.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19KXRP8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19Q0C40001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D19Q0C40001",
    "text": "**Correction — the tree view's doubled anchor is already filed, and was already misread once; what is not filed is its consequence** (2026-10-11, orchestrator, answering the user's \"Has the malformed link issue filed?\"): searching the graph found `issues/treeview.md`'s \"`aperas tree --view` doubles a link's `#id/` fragment when the stored href already carries one\" (filed 2026-09-27, Repro `BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR007`, still open, no backlinks) and a Freeflow entry in which the orchestrator had blamed the grapher for the same doubled fragment before checking the stored text with `aperas show`. The orchestrator's previous message said the code that doubles the anchor \"has not been read\" and did not look for the issue first; it is the same defect, not a new one. Filed: the render bug; the `check-links` gap for targets that name no node (`issues/linking.md`, 00CVKFWNB8001). Not filed: that a reader copies the doubled form into new text, the parser then stores a target `X#id/X` that names no node (five Links in three of the Coder's Report nodes), and `npm run verify` therefore fails at step 7 on the real mirror. The repair of those five targets is also not done.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D19SYHZR001",
    "text": "**Decision — file the consequence and the collector's blind spot, then debug the cause of the anchor duplication** (2026-10-11, user, answering the orchestrator's question: \"File them then debug the cause of the anchor dupe.\"):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR002",
      "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR003",
      "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR004",
      "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR002:props:StringProp:00D19SYWSG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR002:props:StringProp:00D19SYWSG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**File**",
    "text": "**File**: two issues by the Grapher. (1) In `issues/linking.md`: a doubled `#id/` anchor copied from `tree --view` is stored in new text, the parser takes it to a target that names no node, and `npm run verify` fails at step 7 on the real mirror; with a pointer from the existing tree-view issue (`issues/treeview.md`, filed 2026-09-27) to it. (2) In `issues/core.md`: garbage collection never collects an unreachable block that was never tombstoned, so the stray block `BlockNode:00CJ2TCV40000` survives every restart.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Not covered by \"file them\", so not done**",
    "text": "**Not covered by \"file them\", so not done**: the repair of the five malformed `Link` targets in the stored text. It is graph content and the user has not said to repair it; the orchestrator asks separately. The stray block is not touched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Debug, as the orchestrator reads it**",
    "text": "**Debug, as the orchestrator reads it**: find and explain the cause of the duplicated anchor in the code, with lines, by reading and by a scratch reproduction, and bring back the root cause and the candidate fixes with their trade-offs. It is not a go to change source: a fix has more than one available shape (the renderer, the parser, both), so the user chooses the shape first, as the project rule on investigations asks.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D19SYHZR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
