      }
    ],
    "title": "[The full-store-scans issue](#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001)",
    "text": "[The full-store-scans issue](#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001): a bound `allIdsOfKind` on `title` or `type` gives 5,556 `BlockNode` ids against 5,557 from the scan, and the one missing is this block, so it would drop from the next flush (measured by the Coder in the store-size investigation).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A2AY6800F",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2D1Q8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2D1Q8001:links:Link:00D1A2DD6R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D1A28XNG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2D1Q8001:links:Link:00D1A2DD6R000:props:StringProp:00D1A2DD6R001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "13"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Related**",
    "text": "**Related**: [A doubled anchor copied from the tree view is stored and breaks `npm run verify`](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00D1A28XNG001) is the consequence of this rendering.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1A2FPSG001",
    "text": "**Finding — the anchor is doubled by the preview renderer's `bakeResolvedLinkIds`, not by the stored text; verified by reading, with the candidate fixes** (2026-10-11, orchestrator, from the Coder's Turn 1 of `debug-doubled-anchor`; the orchestrator read `node.ts` lines 1700 to 1732):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG002",
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG003",
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG004",
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG005",
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG006",
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG007",
      "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG008",
      "BlockNode:00D21GE798001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG002:props:StringProp:00D1A2G5M0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG002:props:StringProp:00D1A2G5M0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Root cause**",
    "text": "**Root cause**: `bakeResolvedLinkIds` (`monorepo/packages/core/src/apeironNgn/node.ts` lines 1711 to 1732) appends `#id/<target>` to any href that starts with `./` or `../` (gate at line 1722, insertion at line 1724). Its doc comment says it bakes only where the href has \"no existing fragment\", but the code never checks for a `#`, and every `path#id/X` link also starts with `../`, so each gets the anchor a second time. It was written for bare-path links; called from `buildNodeItem` (line 1809) and `buildLinkItem` (line 1872); it came in with commit `0f710e4` in this form, and no test covers it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**How the doubled form becomes stored data**",
    "text": "**How the doubled form becomes stored data**: only when a reader pastes the rendered link back. Then `astParser.ts` 475 to 482, `artifacts.ts` 160 to 166 (`fragment.slice(3)`) and `resolveCreate.ts` 237 (also `resolve.ts` 139) make a `Link` whose target is `X#id/X`, with no existence check and no `#` check; the next preview appends the two-id target after the two stored ids, which is the four-times display.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Where it shows**",
    "text": "**Where it shows**: `aperas tree --view` and `--format render-tree` (which the webapp consumes). It does not show in `tree` without `--view`, `unfold`, `show` or `backlinks --text`, which print raw text; the projection does not call the function (by reading). Nothing else was found that writes it into stored text.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Scratch evidence**",
    "text": "**Scratch evidence**: a single-anchor link renders with two ids; a doubled link stores target `X#id/X` and renders four; a link with three or more ids throws an uncaught `URIError: Invalid IRI code point '#'` (`artifacts.ts` 475, `node.ts` 396, `vocab.ts` 59); `aperas check-links` reports 0 discrepancies with a doubled link present.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A2FPSG001",
    "type": "listItem",
