    "text": "**The user's rule on forward references (answers the orchestrator's second open point)**: a link to a non-existing target in deep path form places a holder, as it does today and as it keeps doing; a link to a non-existing id does not, and is refused. This makes the Coder's candidate B3 part of C, limited to the direct-id spellings. Risk to check before it lands: existing content that links to ids not yet existing (ingest of legacy documents); the Coder surveys it and reports before anything breaks `npm run verify`.",
