    "title": "**After the code**",
    "text": "**After the code**: the orchestrator reads the diff and has the tests run; then the user-approved stop of the service (a graceful `service stop`, no kill; the stop takes about 12.5 s on a dirty service against the client's 10 s wait, so the orchestrator expects its error and checks the pid); then an offline sweep of the mirror files for malformed links (the five known `Link` targets and the doubled anchors in the stored text of the Coder's three Report nodes, plus anything D finds), dry-run on a copy first and the diff shown before it is applied to the real mirror, with a backup because `.state/` is not under git; the stray block `BlockNode:00CJ2TCV40000` is removed in the same offline pass; then the service is started on the new code, `aperas check-links` must be clean and `npm run verify` is run on the real mirror.",
