  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1AVZH7G001",
    "text": "**Verification — A, C and D read, with answers to the Coder's four questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; the full `npm run verify` was not run, per the user's rule): the Coder's staged diff (+453 −19 over seven files, plus the earlier `removeDanglingUnfolds` change) matches the Ask: A skips an href containing `#` in `bakeResolvedLinkIds`; C is `classifyLinkCode`, `findRefusedLinks` and `assertLinksAcceptable` in `artifacts.ts`, run in `resolveBlockLinks` before any `.links` is rewritten, refusing a repeated `#id/` and a direct-id spelling whose id names no node while a non-existing deep path still places a holder, with ingest and `--repair` setting a bad link aside with a warning; D adds `unresolvedTargets` to the link-integrity report, printed by `check-links` and never touched by `--repair`. Reported checks: `tsc` clean, the new standalone script passes in 1.7 s and fails when the A line is toggled off, and on a copy of the real mirror 2036 direct-id codes include none that names a missing id and exactly five repeat an anchor (the known five, all in `.threads/coder.md`), so C refuses no existing content.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G002",
      "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7R000",
      "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7R001",
      "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7R002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G002:props:StringProp:00D1AVZXE0000",
