        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G002:props:StringProp:00D1AVZXE0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D1AVZH7G002",
    "text": "**Q1 — decision: yes, one `assertLinksAcceptable` call before the first mutation in `kgUpdate.ts` and `kgInsert.ts`** (orchestrator, inside the user's go for C): without it a refused write has already changed the text and hydrated the new nodes, and the half-written state stays in memory until the next flush; making the refusal safe is part of C. Those two files are added to the allowed list for that one call and its test, nothing else.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1AVZH7R000",
    "text": "**Q2 — decision: a block keeps a bad link it already stores until the sweep** (orchestrator): only new bad links are refused, so unchanged content stays writable and ingestable, and the five are visible to D until the offline sweep removes them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1AVZH7R001",
    "text": "**Q3 — decision: A skips only an href that contains `#id/`** (orchestrator): the defect is the second `#id/`; a `path#slug` link that resolves to a `Link` was baked to `path#slug#id/X` so the webapp, which recognises a `#…id/<Kind>:<id>` fragment, could navigate it, and skipping every `#` would take that away. Narrowing is a one-condition change to the Coder's line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1AVZH7R002",
    "text": "**Q4 — decision: `folders.ts` gets the skip policy for description links (one word); `service.ts` is not edited** (orchestrator): a bad link in a folder README description would otherwise fail `ingestFolderTree` and strand the folder; the service's startup and write-time warnings reading `unresolvedTargets` is a `service.ts` edit that the user has not cleared, so it is noted for the user, not done.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1AVZH7G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1AYPMDG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1AYPMDG001",
    "text": "**Verification — the follow-up turn read and run by the orchestrator; the plan for the offline sweep** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; the full `npm run verify` was not run): `tsc --noEmit` on `core` and `cli` is clean (4.3 s) and `verifyLinkRefusals.ts` passes when run by the orchestrator (all checks in 136 ms, about 1 s wall), including the refused writes leaving the store unchanged, the folder description set aside with a warning, `check-links` reporting both planted targets, and the render line with `path#id/` kept, a bare path and `path#slug` baked and none doubled. The small diffs match the Ask: `assertLinksAcceptable` before the first mutation in `kgInsert.ts` and `kgUpdate.ts` (the Coder also put it in `runFolderUpdate`, which is in `kgUpdate.ts`; accepted), `bakeResolvedLinkIds` skipping only `#id/`, and `resolveBlockLinks(..., 'skip')` in `folders.ts`. The Coder's note that a link to a block created by the same piped markdown would now be refused is accepted: ids are minted by the parse, so nobody can write one, and the corpus survey found none.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1AYPMDG002",
      "BlockNode:00D1AYPMDG003",
