  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BAYMDR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1BAYMDR001",
    "text": "Seven prose blocks quote the doubled shape in backticks and are not links (reported by the sweep, 2026-10-11).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A28XNR00Q",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: fixed on 2026-10-11 by the changes A, C and D and an offline sweep of the mirror; the code is carried by commit `0a7a226` on branch `oxigraph`, and the full `npm run verify` was not run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1A28XNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG002",
      "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG003",
      "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG004",
      "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG005",
      "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG006",
      "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG002:props:StringProp:00D1BB6MMG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG002:props:StringProp:00D1BB6MMG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**A, the preview**",
    "text": "**A, the preview**: `bakeResolvedLinkIds` skips an href that contains `#id/`, so the preview no longer doubles the anchor. A `path#slug` href is still baked, so the webapp can navigate it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**C, the writer**",
    "text": "**C, the writer**: `resolveBlockLinks` refuses a repeated `#id/` and a direct-id link whose id names no node, before any `.links` is rewritten. `kgInsert.ts` and `kgUpdate.ts` assert before their first mutation, so a refused write changes nothing. A deep path that names nothing still places a holder.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**D, the check**",
    "text": "**D, the check**: `check-links` lists `unresolvedTargets`, a `Link` whose target names no node, and never repairs them. Ingest and `--repair` set a bad link aside with a warning. A block keeps a bad link it already stored until the sweep.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The sweep** (offline, service stopped, backup taken, dry-run shown first)",
    "text": "**The sweep** (offline, service stopped, backup taken, dry-run shown first): the five stored targets went from `X#id/X` to `X`, the text of the three blocks lost its repeated anchors, and the stray block was removed; records went from 5,972 to 5,971.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Checked**",
    "text": "**Checked**: on the new code `check-links` scanned 5,674 live blocks and reported a clean pass with no unresolved targets. The Coder reported `tsc` clean and a new standalone script passing in 1.7 s and failing with the A line toggled off. On a copy of the mirror, 2,036 direct-id codes held none naming a missing id and exactly five repeated an anchor, the known five.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG007:links:Link:00D22ZYCAG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D1EGQDN8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG007:links:Link:00D22ZYCAG000:props:StringProp:00D22ZYCAG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "94"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Not done**",
    "text": "**Not done**: the full `npm run verify` on the new code. The verify emergency it waited on is [resolved](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D1EGQDN8001): `npm run verify` now runs the `commit` suite, so the run is no longer blocked. The service's startup and write-time warnings on `unresolvedTargets` would be a `service.ts` edit, which the user has not cleared.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB69AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8001:links:Link:00D1BBA5PR001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D1A28XNG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8001:links:Link:00D1BBA5PR001:props:StringProp:00D1BBA5PR002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "53"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: fixed on 2026-10-11 by the change A of [the doubled-anchor issue](../issues/linking.md#id/BlockNode:00D1A28XNG001); the code is carried by commit `0a7a226` on branch `oxigraph`, and the full `npm run verify` was not run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CRCGRGJR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8002",
      "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8002:props:StringProp:00D1BBA5PG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8002:props:StringProp:00D1BBA5PR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Cause**",
    "text": "**Cause**: the gate in `bakeResolvedLinkIds` (`node.ts` lines 1711 to 1732 as they were) checked only the `./` or `../` prefix, so a `path#id/X` href got a second anchor. Its doc comment said it bakes only where the href has no existing fragment, and the code never checked.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Fix**",
    "text": "**Fix**: the function now skips an href that contains `#id/`. A `path#slug` href is still baked, so the webapp can navigate it. The Coder reported a new standalone script that passes and fails when the line is toggled off; commit `0a7a226` carries a check of the single-anchor rendering, `checkSingleAnchorRendering` in `verifyLinkRefusals.ts` (step 13 of `verify.ts`, also run by `tests/links/refusals.test.ts`); the rendering is not otherwise checked in this record.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BB9VE8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G001:links:Link:00D1BBAZKG001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D1A28XNG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G001:links:Link:00D1BBAZKG001:props:StringProp:00D1BBAZKG002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
