        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The write**",
    "text": "**The write**: `resolveBlockLinks` refuses a direct-id link whose id names no node, before any `.links` is rewritten, so the write-time summary no longer counts it as resolved. The refusal sits in `resolveBlockLinks`, not in `resolveDeepPathDetail`. A deep path that names nothing still places a holder, by the user's rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The check**",
    "text": "**The check**: `check-links` lists `unresolvedTargets`, a `Link` whose target names no node, and never repairs them. On the new code it reports a clean pass.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Not covered in this record**",
    "text": "**Not covered in this record**: a target that exists but is tombstoned, which the sources do not state. The fixture for a link to a nonexistent id is carried by commit `0a7a226`: step 5g of `verify.ts` runs `checkLinkRefusals` (`verifyLinkRefusals.ts`, also run by `tests/links/refusals.test.ts`), whose cases include the `path#id/`, `[[id]]` and `aperas://id/` spellings naming no node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BBAN3G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BBPCKG001",
