        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**(a) no yield**",
    "text": "**(a) no yield**: step 2 1,812; step 3 9,974; step 4 0; step 5 17,029; total 28,847; wall 30.1 s; user CPU 62.0 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**(b) `setImmediate` at each step header**",
    "text": "**(b) `setImmediate` at each step header**: 1,781; 8,456; 10; 23,113; total 33,392; wall 34.5 s; user CPU 71.5 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**(c) a 50 ms timer at each step header**",
    "text": "**(c) a 50 ms timer at each step header**: 1,763; 10,890; 127; 1,649; total 14,762; wall 15.4 s; user CPU 29.9 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Reading**",
    "text": "**Reading**: step 5's cost is not intrinsic to step 5: the same code takes 1.6 s after a 50 ms timer and 17 to 23 s after `setImmediate` or nothing, so it comes from state that builds up over the process and that a stretch of wall-clock time clears and a bare pass of the loop does not. This answers the point left untested in the earlier turn discussion: a zero-delay `setImmediate` was not enough here. Step 3's 10 s is untouched by either yield, so it is its own work or garbage that 50 ms does not clear. User CPU was about 2.1 times wall in (a) and (b) and 1.9 times in (c), which fits V8's parallel collector threads and a cost that is garbage collection; not proven, because no `--trace-gc` was run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**How far it is shown**",
    "text": "**How far it is shown**: one sample per variant, machine load not controlled, steps 2 to 5 only; step 7, where the 649 s sit, was not run. The Coder asks whether to run (d) the prefix to step 7 as it is and (e) the same with the 50 ms timer, each capped at 180 s, and a repeat of (c). These were conditional on the three runs not separating, and they did separate, so they are not authorised by the earlier go; the orchestrator puts the question to the user.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BQN1HG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1BXAQH0001",
    "text": "**Decision — three tiers of tests, and two more capped runs** (2026-10-11, user, answering the orchestrator's account of the measurement and of the industry practice: \"What's the diff between registry & standalone script? 3 tiers sound good: per change (should be in seconds) > per commit (under a minute) > on demand (large sets or full suite). run two more capped runs: OK.\"):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0002",
      "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0003",
      "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH8000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0002:props:StringProp:00D1BXB3P8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0002:props:StringProp:00D1BXB3P8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Tiers, the user's shape**",
    "text": "**Tiers, the user's shape**: (1) per change, in seconds; (2) per commit, under a minute; (3) on demand, for large sets or the full suite. How the tiers map onto the `verify` command's arguments (`--case`, a fast set, the full suite and `verify:slow`) and onto the skills is not yet designed; the Coder's command design and the v4.4 skill text follow the tiers.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The two runs, and no more**",
    "text": "**The two runs, and no more**: (d) the prefix of `verify.ts` up to and including step 7 as it is, and (e) the same prefix with the 50 ms timer at each step header, each capped at 180 s, one after the other. The orchestrator adds that both are run with `--trace-gc`, summarised per step as Mark-Compact count and total time, because that tests the garbage-collection reading without a further run. The repeat of (c) is not run: the user said two runs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1BXAQH8000",
    "text": "**The question on registry and standalone scripts** was answered in the chat, not in a decision: a registry makes each case a function that declares what it needs and builds its own fixtures, all inside the one runner; a standalone script is a separate file per case that sets up its own tiny store and runs on its own (the form already used by `verifyLinkRefusals.ts` and `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BXAQH0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1C1W5CG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1C1W5CG001",
    "text": "**Result — runs (d) and (e): neither reached step 7 in 180 s; the slow steps are back-to-back full garbage collections that free almost nothing, which a 50 ms pause stops in some steps and not in others** (2026-10-11, orchestrator, from the Coder's Turn 3 of `verify-command-survey`; one sample per run, each cut by its cap; no repository or graph change; `trace-gc` and `stdbuf` add cost, so (d) and (e) are compared with each other and not with Turn 2's times):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1C1W5CG002",
