    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D5F64800V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-10-11T10:27:30.645Z",
    "title": "00D1D5F64800V",
    "text": "How the corpus checks reach the real mirror, given that the fixture helper refuses its root.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D5F64800P",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D5PV78001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D5PV78001:links:Link:00D1D5QAFR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D5PV78001:links:Link:00D1D5QAFR000:props:StringProp:00D1D5QAFR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "44"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D1D5PV78001",
    "text": "**The test design is settled** and lives in [Testing — Design](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001): standalone scripts in groups, suites as compound scripts, the `essential`, `commit` and `demand` tiers, a runner on `node --import tsx --test` with concurrency 2 and a per-file timeout, and the legacy suite moved under `src/tests/legacy/`. The design marks each claim measured, read or designed, not built; the build is not done, and the core slowdown remedy for the service is not part of it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BAT6Q8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1D5PV78002",
      "BlockNode:00D1D5PV78003"
    ]
  },
