    ],
    "title": "Written",
    "text": "Written: [Testing — Design](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001) holds the settled design with each claim marked measured, read or designed, not built; [the \"Verify emergency\" issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D1BAT6Q0001) points at it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D2MKVR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D6SVZG001",
    "text": "**Verification — `design/testing.md` read in outline, with answers to the Grapher's three questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator): `aperas check-links` is clean. The new document (`ArtifactNode:00D1D5F2SR000`) has Context (an Issues line), a note on the three claim marks (measured, read, designed and not built), the problem (the 1,434 s run, the cost coming from the process and not the steps, the collection numbers, the 50 ms result, the external-memory trigger as a reading, what is not shown), the architecture (scripts and groups, suites and tiers, runner, fixtures, the rule that no run saturates the machine), the workflows (after an edit `--group` plus `essential`; before a commit `npm run verify`; on demand the `demand` suite; the legacy suite; the migration order; the emergency as the open issue), and the open points. The \"Verify emergency\" issue's Fix directions now link up to it. The Grapher also rewrote three older Fix-directions items that stated as open what the design settles; accepted. The service printed a stale-code warning on every call because the Coder's source edits are on disk and the running service predates them; expected, and it is restarted only with the user's approval after the work is verified.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG002",
      "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG003",
      "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG002:props:StringProp:00D1D6T92R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG002:props:StringProp:00D1D6T92R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D1D6SVZG002",
    "text": "**Q1 — decision: add a Discussion line to the Context** (orchestrator): the repository's rule allows a design's Context to cite its discussion as a normative singular reference, and other design documents carry that line; it goes in the next Grapher turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D6SVZG003",
    "text": "**Q2 — decision: the corpus checks use a copy of the mirror** (orchestrator): the fixture helper keeps refusing the real roots, and a separate helper (for example `makeCorpusCopy()`) copies the real `Apeiron/` into scratch roots for the on-demand corpus checks, so no test ever reads or writes the real mirror in place.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D6SVZG004",
    "text": "**Q3 — decision: the `all` suite and the `essential` member list are settled after the build** (orchestrator): the Coder builds the `all` comparison now and measures each file; the document is updated with the built `all` suite, the `essential` members and the timeout value when the Coder reports and the orchestrator has read it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D6SVZG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D7DCY0001",
    "text": "**Verification — phase 1 of the test redesign built, read and run by the orchestrator; answers to the Coder's three questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; no legacy step was run by anyone):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0002",
      "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0003",
      "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0004",
      "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0005",
      "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0006",
      "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0002:props:StringProp:00D1D7DRXR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0002:props:StringProp:00D1D7DRXR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Run by the orchestrator**",
    "text": "**Run by the orchestrator**: `npm run verify -- --suite essential` passes 8 cases in 3 files in 1.6 s wall (the Coder reported 2.3 s); `npm run verify` (the `commit` suite) passes 20 cases in 5 files in 5.6 s wall (the Coder 6.6 s), of which the runner's own tests take 4.2 s of the 5.1 s the runner counts; `--list` shows the 5 files; `--case zzz` exits 1. The staged change is 19 files, +727 −37: the runner `run.mjs`, `suites/` (`essential`, `commit`, `demand`), `support/` (`fixture.ts`, `reporter.mjs`, `suite.mjs`, `sampleMarkdown.ts`), the test files `links/refusals.test.ts`, `store/dangling-unfolds.test.ts`, `store/fixture.test.ts`, `parse/ast.test.ts` (the pure steps 1 to 1e, which `essential` now holds) and `runner/runner.test.ts` (10 cases), the legacy suite moved under `legacy/` with steps 5g, 9c and 13 taken out, and `package.json` with `verify`, `verify:legacy` and `verify:legacy:slow` (`verify:slow` is gone). A suite is `suites/<name>.suite.mjs` with `export default defineSuite(import.meta.url, [paths])`; a test is `<name>.test.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Reported by the Coder, not re-run**",
    "text": "**Reported by the Coder, not re-run**: `tsc --noEmit` clean on core and cli (the cli run includes the moved legacy files); a syntax-error file and a hung file each give a FAIL line and exit 1; the run of the runner from inside a `node:test` file needs `NODE_TEST_CONTEXT` cleared, which only the runner's own tests do; each extra file in `essential` costs about 0.3 to 0.5 s, mostly process and `tsx` start-up. One assertion was not carried over: \"ids unique\" in `parse/ast.test.ts`, because the old step only printed it and the sample's ids are not unique.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D7DCY0004",
    "text": "**Q1 — decision: the unlisted-file warning compares the disk with the union of the suites, and there is no literal `all.suite.mjs`** (orchestrator): the union needs no list of its own to keep in step; `design/testing.md`, which says \"an `all` suite\", is corrected in the next Grapher turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D7DCY0005",
    "text": "**Q2 — decision: phase 2 removes steps 1 to 1e from the legacy file** (orchestrator): they live in `parse/ast.test.ts` now and a copy in the legacy file only runs twice and drifts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D7DCY0006",
    "text": "**Q3 — decision: the type check and a search are enough to confirm the removal of 5g, 9c and 13 from the legacy suite** (orchestrator): no run of `verify:legacy`, which the standing rule excludes and which is to be retired.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Next**",
    "text": "**Next**: the skills' v4.4 text (a Coder edit) describing the built runner; then the Grapher records the delta and settles the design document's open points that the build answered (the `essential` members, the timings, the union, the corpus copy, the Discussion line).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D7DCY0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1DBW9DR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1D8WCV0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1D8WCV0001",
    "text": "**Verification — the skills' v4.4 edit read and checked by the orchestrator** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; skill-only checks, `npm run verify` not run): the staged diff (4 files, +17 −8) matches the Ask: `Status:` is v4.4 in all four role skills; the base skill's Step 7 says `npm run verify` runs the `commit` suite, and its Verification Scope has the after-an-edit commands (`--group <area>`, `--suite essential`), the `commit` run before handing back and at Step 7 (under a minute, warning past it), \"stop and report to the user\" when it passes a minute, never `verify:legacy` or `verify:legacy:slow` unless asked (about 24 minutes), and the new-test rule; the orchestrator's section 7 and the Coder's step 2 and two Operational Invariants say the same in their own places; the Grapher's skill and `kg-doc-ingest` name no test command and only the Grapher's `Status:` moved. There is no emergency flag or mode in the text. `python3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py` exits 1 as expected before the delta: all four `Status:` lines ahead of v4.3, 13 added units, and 7 dropped units that the Grapher must account for (the four v4.3 `Status:` lines and the replaced Step 7 and Verification Scope units); `aperas check-links` is clean. The Coder's open question, that the dropped list has no unit reading like the old base Step 7 text, is the Grapher's to match by the `Supersedes:` rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
