      }
    ],
    "title": "**Orchestrator Verification**",
    "text": "**Orchestrator Verification**: Orchestrator checks the diff and test output directly, reading source, diffs and tests as needed to assess the result (`npm run verify` for code/engine changes, which runs the `commit` suite; for skill-only tasks, strictly run `python3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py` and `aperas check-links` as two separate commands, expecting drift to fail here naming the edited units until the Grapher records the delta at Step 8 — never run `npm run verify` on skill tasks).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DA0Q1800A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DBCA98001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1DBCA98001",
    "text": "**built** — exists in the source tree under `monorepo/packages/cli/src/tests/` and was read there. A built claim that also gives a number from a run carries *built, measured*, and the numbers keep the one-sample rule above.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D5F640000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DBEMC0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1DBEMC0001",
    "text": "A test file in no suite is a warning, not a failure: on every run the runner compares the test files on disk (outside `support/` and `suites/`) with the union of the files every suite resolves to, and prints one `warning:` line naming the files in no suite. There is no `all` suite file to keep in step. *(built)*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D5F64000H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
