    "title": "**v4.4 — verification text that follows the new test structure: the `commit` suite, the per-change commands, and no legacy suite unless asked**",
    "text": "**v4.4 — verification text that follows the new test structure: the `commit` suite, the per-change commands, and no legacy suite unless asked**: recorded as [the v4.4 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D1DA0Q18001). A code task now runs `npm run verify -- --group <area>` and `npm run verify -- --suite essential` after an edit, and `npm run verify`, which runs the `commit` suite, before handing a change back and at Step 7; the suite is expected to finish in under a minute, and if it passes a minute the agent stops and reports to the user. `verify:legacy` and `verify:legacy:slow` run only when the user asks. The base skill states this in Step 7 and in Verification Scope, the Orchestrator's Verification Protocol and the Coder's step 2 restate it, and the Coder gains two Operational Invariants: verify before handing back, and a new test is a standalone `<name>.test.ts` file in a group directory under `src/tests/`, named in a suite, never added to the legacy files. Skill-only tasks still never run `npm run verify`. The four `Status:` lines move to v4.4. The text follows [Testing — Design](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001) and the [Verify emergency](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D1BAT6Q0001) issue, which stays open.",
