      }
    ],
    "title": "00D1DDSWYG002",
    "text": "**Decision — the Current Status sentence names v4.4** (orchestrator, answering the second Grapher's first question): the sentence listing \"the v4, v4.1, v4.2 and v4.3 milestones below\" gets v4.4; a small Grapher edit in the next turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DDSWYG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DDSWYR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1DDSWYR000",
    "text": "**Decision — no thread pruning yet** (orchestrator, answering its second question): the threads are at about 1,190 and 550 live blocks against the cap of 200; the prune was deferred until the removal stall and the thread-flush gap are fixed, and only the removal stall is (`removeDanglingUnfolds`, running in the service since its start at 07:57 UTC, not tested on a real removal yet); the thread-flush gap is not; the prune stays deferred.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DDSWYG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DDSWYR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Answers to the design Grapher's questions**",
    "text": "**Answers to the design Grapher's questions**: the Discussion line cites the decision node only; the fourth claim mark \"built\" is kept and must be defined in the note on the marks (to check when the document is read in full).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DDSWYG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1DF2BF0001",
    "text": "**Decision — migrate the remaining steps of the legacy suite into groups (phase 2)** (2026-10-11, user, choosing from the orchestrator's list of what is pending: \"Let's migrates the remaining steps from the legacy suite into groups.\"):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0002",
      "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0003",
      "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0002:props:StringProp:00D1DF2S88000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0002:props:StringProp:00D1DF2S88001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**How the orchestrator runs it**",
    "text": "**How the orchestrator runs it**: in batches, one Coder turn each, read by the orchestrator before the next, in the order of the Coder's inventory (its Turn 1 Report of `test-runner-design`): batch 1 the parse, ingest and folder groups with the demo-artifact chain (steps 3 to 5f) and step 6; batch 2 the store and gc groups with the chains 7 to 11 and step 12; batch 3 the extended steps and the three corpus checks, which need the corpus-copy helper (`makeCorpusCopy()`, designed, not built) and go to the on-demand tier. Each batch may change the boundaries if the code shows a better split and says so.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Rules for every batch**",
    "text": "**Rules for every batch**: every assertion of a migrated step is carried over or its omission is stated (the previous batch dropped one: \"ids unique\", because the old step only printed it); a mapping table from each old step to its new file and case, with assertion counts, is part of the Report; the migrated steps are removed from the legacy files so nothing runs twice; each migrated group has at least one negative control (break the code in a scratch copy and see the test fail) since the legacy suite is not run to compare; each file is placed in a suite by its measured time, and the `commit` suite stays under a minute at concurrency 2 (the running total is reported after each batch), a file that does not fit goes to `demand`; steps whose cost turns out to come from their own work, not from the store size, are reported with their measured time; no change to production code, and a step that needs one is a Question; the legacy suite is not run by anyone.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The end state**",
    "text": "**The end state**: the legacy suite is retired when its last step has moved; then the graph's \"Verify emergency\" issue is resolved, the legacy files and the `verify:legacy` scripts are deleted, and the skills' mentions of the legacy suite are removed (a v4.5 edit, to be decided then).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1DF2BF0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1DJHTX8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1DJHTX8001",
    "text": "**Verification — migration batch 1 read and run by the orchestrator; answers to the Coder's three questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; the legacy suite was not run by anyone): run by the orchestrator, `npm run verify -- --suite essential` passes 18 cases in 5 files in 2.7 s wall and `npm run verify` (the `commit` suite) passes 30 cases in 7 files in 6.9 s wall (the Coder reported 2.41 to 2.68 s and 6.60 to 6.65 s). The staged change moves steps 3 to 5f into `ingest/chain.test.ts` (8 ordered cases, 370 ms), steps 6 and 6b into `folder/folders.test.ts` (2 cases, 78 ms), adds `support/tree.ts`, and removes the copy of steps 1 to 1e from the legacy file; step 2 stays there as the set-up of steps 7 to 12, with a prelude of about 25 lines and no assertions that rebuilds the state those steps read. All three new files are in `essential` (0.5 to 0.77 s each alone). The Coder reports 7 negative controls in a scratch copy, all failing the new tests as intended (parse 2, ingest 3, folder 2), and one break of `extractAbstract`'s recursion that left `6b` green because the fixture README is not deep enough, the same blind spot as the old step. A check in the old step 1d was always false (it looked for a `list` among children already filtered to `listItem`) and was dropped; \"ids unique\" was never a check (parsed blocks have null ids, so the old line printed `false`) and is now checked after ingestion, in case 4.",
