    "title": "00D1EDH18R002",
    "text": "After an edit, run the tests of what you changed with `npm run verify -- --group <area>` and `npm run verify -- --suite essential` (a budget of 5 seconds).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EDH18R003",
    "text": "Before handing a code change back, and at Step 7, run `npm run verify`, which runs the `commit` suite (a budget of 60 seconds); the reporter prints a warning once a run is past its suite's budget.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EDH18R004",
    "text": "If the `commit` suite passes its budget, stop and report to the user: the suite has outgrown its budget and needs a split. Do not keep waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EDH18R005",
    "text": "`npm run verify -- --suite demand` runs the corpus checks on a copy of the real mirror; it takes more than a minute, has no budget and prints no warning, so run it only when the user asks for it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EDH18R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
