    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: the legacy suite is retired and deleted, and `npm run verify` runs the `commit` suite in 8 to 20 s, with the corpus checks in the `demand` suite on a copy of the real mirror. The emergency was closed by making the suite independent of the core's slowness, not by fixing the core: the core's cost stays open in [the full-store-scans issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001), [the reload issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W00YCR001), [the memory issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001), [the issue of commands refused while the service is up](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001) and [the issue of commands refused after a start](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W05P08001). The flag is therefore off. The built suites are in [Testing — Design](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1BAT6Q0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EGVZR8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EGVZR8001",
    "text": "**Decision — add `--help`, a run header and the suite name in the summary to the runner** (2026-10-11, user, on the orchestrator's proposal: \"Yep, update it like that.\"): `--help` prints the usage, the options with their defaults, the suites found in `suites/` with their budgets, file counts and the first comment line of each, and the groups with their file counts; every run starts with a header line naming the suite (or the group), its budget, the number of files, the concurrency and the per-file timeout; the summary line carries the suite's name. `--list` keeps printing only the files. A Coder change to `run.mjs` and the runner tests; the design document and the skills are updated after, if they name the output.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EJSXQ8001",
    "text": "**Verification — the v4.5 delta, the design update and the closing of the emergency read and run by the orchestrator; answers to the Grapher's three questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator): `python3 skills/aperas/scripts/skill_drift.py` exits 0 bare, with `--added` and with `--dropped` (three separate commands, exit codes read): STATUS vs the newest recorded v4.5 0, ADDED 0, DROPPED 0, 210 superseded and accounted for; `aperas check-links` is clean. The delta `## v4.5 additions` (`BlockNode:00D1EDH18G001`) has 8 entries, each dropped v4.4 unit matched to its replacement, with four more `Supersedes:` ids for v4.4 blocks that the drift script does not list as dropped because it compares only the first 120 characters; History has the v4.5 milestone and \"revised through v4.5\"; `design/testing.md` was updated in 20 nodes (suites, budgets, timeouts, the nine built groups, `makeCorpusCopy()`, the legacy suite deleted, the 2.9 s against 37.8 s fact), its marks now *(built)* or *(built, measured)*; the \"Verify emergency\" issue is under `## Resolved` with a Resolved child; Layer 1's wording is corrected. The Grapher's orphan milestone node, created by an insert with the wrong parent, was tombstoned.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8002",
      "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8003",
      "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQG000",
      "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8002:props:StringProp:00D1EJTBB0000",
