        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D1EJSXQ8002",
    "text": "**Q1 — decision: keep the \"designed, not built\" mark in the legend** (orchestrator): the note on the marks defines the vocabulary the document uses, and the mark will be used again when a design item is next added before its code.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EJSXQ8003",
    "text": "**Q2 — correction: the refused-commands issue is `BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001`** (\"A command can fail with 'No ApeironNgn service running' while the service is up, and an unchanged retry works\"), not the `service start` entry `00D0W05P08001` that the Grapher linked; the Resolved child of the \"Verify emergency\" issue links the right one (and may keep the other as a second link) in the next Grapher turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Q3 — decision: no thread pruning yet** (orchestrator)",
    "text": "**Q3 — decision: no thread pruning yet** (orchestrator): the grapher thread is at 1,252 live blocks and the coder thread over 1,000, against the cap of 200; the prune waits for the thread-flush fix, as decided earlier; the Grapher's finding that a loop of 20 `update --text-only` calls left seven not applied, with no cause found, is a reason to prune one task at a time and read each back.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EJSXQG001",
    "text": "**The Grapher's loop of updates that did not apply** is noted: it is one more case of a write that returns without an effect while the service is busy, to be filed with the service-side issues if it recurs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EJSXQ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EK5S98001",
    "text": "**Verification — `--help`, the header and the suite name read and run by the orchestrator; two follow-ups** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; `demand` not run): run by the orchestrator, `tsc --noEmit` clean on cli; `npm run verify -- --help` prints the usage, each option with its default, the three suites with budget, file count and a description, the nine groups with their file counts and three examples; a `commit` run starts with `suite commit (budget 60 s) - 15 files, concurrency 2, timeout 120 s a file` and ends with `SUMMARY suite=commit ran=51 passed=51 failed=0 cancelled=0 skipped=0; 19157 ms` (51 cases: the Coder added three runner tests); the Coder reports `essential` 27/27 in 3.6 s and `commit` 51/51 in 20.4 s, no warning. `commit` has grown from 8 s to 19 s as the runner tests, which start the runner as a child process, were added; it is a third of its 60 s budget, and the runner tests are the largest share, worth watching.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98002",
      "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98003",
      "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98002:props:StringProp:00D1EK66F8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98002:props:StringProp:00D1EK66F8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D1EK5S98002",
    "text": "**Decision — the header forms the Coder chose are accepted** (orchestrator): `suite <name> (<budget>) group <dirs> - ...` for `--suite` with `--group`; `, case \"<name>\"` appended for `--case`; `no timeout` for `--timeout 0`; `suite=group:<dirs>` in the summary of a bare `--group` run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EK5S98003",
    "text": "**Decision — the help description of a suite is its first sentence** (orchestrator, answering the Coder's second question): `--help` takes the first `//` line of each suite file, which for `demand` and `essential` is cut where the comment wraps, so the description reads as truncated; the fix is to join the leading comment lines and cut at the first sentence end, in `run.mjs`, with a test, and not to reword the suite comments. A small Coder turn.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1EK5S98004",
    "text": "**Decision — the Resolved child of the \"Verify emergency\" issue links `BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001`** and the design document names `--help`, the header and the 51-case `commit`: a small Grapher turn (see the previous verification entry for the first).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1EK5S98001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
