    "title": "**What remains, as the orchestrator lists it**",
    "text": "**What remains, as the orchestrator lists it**: (1) the `--help` description of each suite is its first comment line, cut where the comment wraps: join the leading comment lines and cut at the first sentence end (Coder, `run.mjs`, with a test); (2) the skills say the `demand` tier \"takes minutes\", which 74 s no longer is: the wording becomes \"takes more than a minute, with no budget and no warning\" in the base, orchestrator and Coder skills (Coder, the unreleased v4.5, so the delta entries are updated in place and not superseded); (3) the graph: the Resolved child of the \"Verify emergency\" issue links `BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001` (the refused-commands issue), the design document names `--help`, the run header, the 51-case `commit` (about 19 s) and the two measurements of `demand` (73 and 74 s), and the v4.5 delta entries for the edited skill units are updated in place (Grapher); (4) the orchestrator's final checks: `tsc`, `essential`, `commit`, the drift script in three modes, `check-links`, and the state of both staging areas, and a message line for the commit. The service still runs the code of 07:57 UTC and is restarted only with the user's approval.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1ERQFRR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1ET3G88001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1ET3G88001",
    "text": "**Verification — the two small fixes read and run by the orchestrator; the `essential` description** (2026-10-11, orchestrator; `demand` not run): the Coder reports `suiteDescription` in `run.mjs` (the leading `//` lines joined, cut at the first sentence end, shortened to 110 characters with an ellipsis only if still longer), the `--help` test checking that the three descriptions end in a period or an ellipsis, \"takes minutes\" changed to \"takes more than a minute\" in the three skills (the only hits for \"minutes\" in all skill folders, `kg-doc-ingest` included), no `Status:` moved, `tsc` clean, `essential` 27/27 in 3.4 s and `commit` 51/51 in 19.7 s without a warning, the drift script exit 1 with 4 findings (the three edited units added, one old `demand` bullet dropped) and `check-links` clean. The orchestrator runs the final checks after the graph work.",
