          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: the slowdown was measured further on 2026-10-11 and the suite this entry describes no longer exists. What was found: in every slow step the full garbage collections (Mark-Compact) took 70 to 87% of the step's time, and fast steps had 0 or 1 of them; 849 of 895 collections in one run and 1,041 of 1,088 in the other freed 5 MB or less from a heap of about 230 to 450 MB, each pause about 150 to 290 ms, so the cost is repeated full collections that find almost nothing to free (two runs, each cut at 180 s, one sample each). A 50 ms timer between steps cut the collection time in some steps (step 5 from 24,985 ms to 0, step 5d from 47,103 ms to 3 ms, steps 5c and 5f less) and not in others (step 3, step 5g); a bare `setImmediate` yield and no yield did not. A fresh process takes 2.9 s to rehydrate the corpus directory, against 37.8 s in a process that has already rehydrated and dehydrated it (one run, 55,968 quads), so the slowness is state built up in the process and not the data. The old suite's steps 7, 10 and 11 cost 649, 188 and 202 s on the real-size store and milliseconds on a tiny fixture, so the cost came from the size of the store and not from the steps' own work. What replaced it: the monolithic suite (26 steps, about 1,430 s (1,431 s in the run's own table, 1,434 s wall) in one measured run) is retired and deleted, its checks are standalone files in groups under `monorepo/packages/cli/src/tests/`, `npm run verify` runs the `commit` suite in 8 to 20 s, and `npm run verify -- --suite demand` runs 56 cases on a copy of the real mirror in 73 s and 74 s (two occasions); the built suites are in [Testing — Design](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001). What is still a reading and not shown: that the trigger is V8 starting full collections when external (wasm) memory has grown past its limit, which the collection cannot lower because the wasm side is released by a later callback, was not tested; the earlier guess of a JIT-level degradation is replaced by the collection reading and was not tested either. The core's own cost is not fixed, only the suite made independent of it, and stays open in [the full-store-scans issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001) and [the removal-stall issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1EZSCH8001",
