        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Resolved**",
    "text": "**Resolved**: explained, in part measured, not proved (2026-10-11). Measured: the slow steps are repeated full garbage collections (Mark-Compact), 70 to 87% of the time of every slow step, that free 5 MB or less each from a heap of about 230 to 450 MB; a 50 ms timer between steps cut them in some steps (step 5 from 24,985 ms to 0, step 5d from 47,103 ms to 3 ms) and not in others (step 3, step 5g), and a `setImmediate` yield or none did not; a fresh process rehydrates the same directory in 2.9 s against 37.8 s in a process that has already rehydrated and dehydrated, about thirteen times (one run); the old suite's steps 7, 10 and 11 cost 649, 188 and 202 s on the real-size store and milliseconds on a tiny one. This replaces the leading guess of inline-cache megamorphism or another JIT-level degradation in a long process, which the collection measurements replace as the reading and which was itself not tested; the V8 profiling (`--prof`, `--trace-deopt`) proposed here was not run. Still a reading and not shown: that the trigger is V8 starting a full collection when external (wasm) memory has grown past its limit, which the collection cannot lower because the wasm side is released by a later callback, so that a pause lets the callbacks run and stops the collections. Whether `free()` on the quads would remove the growth, which was not tested when this was written, was tested by [the `free()` landing](../history/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG003) of 2026-10-12: in a scratch process on a copy of the mirror (59,275 quads, 3 samples per case, a fresh process each), eight scans of all ids stayed flat at about 265 MB where they had grown 40 MB a call, a dehydrate of both mirrors fell from 33 to 38 s to 2.5 to 3.8 s and a rehydrate from 3.3 to 3.5 s to 2.0 to 2.9 s. That agrees with the reading and does not prove it, because the recorded measurements do not count collections. Two runs, each cut at 180 s, one sample per variant, for the earlier measurements. The suite no longer depends on it: the monolithic suite is retired and replaced by standalone files, `npm run verify` runs the `commit` suite in 8 to 20 s and `npm run verify -- --suite demand` runs 56 cases on a copy of the real mirror in 73 s and 74 s, as recorded in [Testing — Design](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001); the core's cost itself stays open in [the full-store-scans issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
