        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Since measured (2026-10-11), not resolved**",
    "text": "**Since measured (2026-10-11), not resolved**: the 40-minute stall during a corpus-wide re-ingestion is consistent with the mechanism measured since for the slow `verify` steps, a long synchronous burst over wasm-bound wrappers that never yields, with repeated full garbage collections taking 70 to 87% of the time of the slow steps and a fresh process rehydrating the same directory in 2.9 s against 37.8 s after a rehydrate and a dehydrate; it is not shown to be the same cause, since the migration was neither profiled nor traced for collections. The related service-side costs are in [the removal-stall issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) and [the full-store-scans issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001). This entry stays open: the service-level stall it records is not closed, and the `verify` suite's independence of the core's cost (see the resolved entries on the `verify` slowdown and on why isolation helps) does not touch it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CKSAK04R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1F10W9G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1F10W9G001",
    "text": "**Verification — the older verify issues updated; answers to the Grapher's two questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator): `aperas check-links` is clean (6,629 live blocks). The Grapher resolved \"`npm run verify` costs ~5 minutes\" (`BlockNode:00CJ0202MG001`, child \"Practical problem resolved, root cause still not\" kept) and \"Why isolation helps is still unexplained\" (`BlockNode:00CJ0HX2Y0000`, resolved as \"explained, in part measured, not proved\") under `## Resolved`, after \"Verify emergency\", with their children and ids; \"Confirmed at real production scale, 2026-09-20\" (`BlockNode:00CKSAK04R001`) stays open with a child \"Since measured (2026-10-11), not resolved\"; the History line says \"takes more than a minute\" and the Resolved child of \"Verify emergency\" says \"in 8 to 20 s\". The Grapher softened one sentence it had overstated (\"do not support\" the JIT guess became \"replace it as the reading; the guess was untested\").",
