  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1F5X55R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1F5X55R000",
    "text": "**Done — the user committed and restarted the service; the new code is live** (2026-10-11, user: \"I committed and restarted the service.\"): the orchestrator checked: the lock shows pid 300846 `ready`, started at 12:33:08Z (07:33 local); `service.log` records \"Rehydrated 58376 quad(s)\" at 12:32:59Z (the store was 41,246 quads on 2026-10-10 and 50,055 at the previous start: the threads, the issues and the discussion have grown it); no stale-code banner; `aperas check-links` scanned 6,687 live blocks (1,471 with internal link text) and reports a clean pass with no unresolved targets, on the code with the link refusals, the unresolved-target report and the object-bound `removeDanglingUnfolds` running for the first time in the live service. Not yet exercised live: a real removal (the 34-node and 122-node cases that stalled the service for 5 to 12 minutes) and the refusal of a repeated `#id/` by `insert` and `update`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FB15WR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1FB15WR001",
    "text": "**Decision — try the live removal: the Grapher removes one finished task from its thread, timed** (2026-10-11, user, answering whether to test the fix with a real removal: \"Yeah, try it.\"): the removal is the test of `removeDanglingUnfolds` as one object-bound match in the live service, which was restarted on the new code at 07:33 local. The old service stalled for 5.4 and 12 minutes on two such removals (42 and 31 blocks) and took 2 to 45 s on others; the scratch measurement was 21 s with 34 full scans before and 12 ms after. The first step of the thread prune. Rules for it: one task, a finished one whose content has been promoted (the Grapher checks and names where), counted first (blocks and embedded `Link` nodes), removed with one `aperas remove --flush`, timed, the service's CPU and resident memory read before and after from `/proc`, a view operation straight after so that the thread's `.state/` mirror is written (the thread-flush gap is not fixed), the removal read back, `aperas check-links` run; the one-minute rule applies to the command: if it does not answer in a minute, stop, report, and do not kill or restart anything.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1FCX9E8001",
    "text": "**Result — the live removal: 164 blocks and 101 embedded links removed in 3.7 s with no stall; the removal fix works in the live service** (2026-10-11, orchestrator, from the Grapher's Turn 1 of `live-removal-test`; one removal): the task `### Record the v3.1 skill edit` (`BlockNode:00CR8567ZR001`, the oldest under `## aperas skill`; its content is held by the v3.1 delta `00CR874TC8001`, the v3.1 History milestone `00CR8MWVYG000` and the Threads design block `00CR3X3N08004`, all live) had 164 live blocks and 101 embedded `Link` nodes (counted in the `.state` mirror). One `aperas remove --flush` took 3.711 s and exited 0; `aperas tree .threads/grapher.md` then shows 34 headings, down from 35, every other task intact; `aperas check-links` scanned 6,549 live blocks, 0 discrepancies. For comparison, the old service stalled for 5.4 and 12 minutes on removals of 42 and 31 blocks, and the scratch measurement of a 34-embedded-node removal was 21 s with 34 full scans before the fix; here 101 embedded nodes took 3.7 s, about 36 ms per embedded node against about 14,000 ms for 34 at the old cost per scan.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8002",
      "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8003",
      "BlockNode:00D1FCX9EG000",
      "BlockNode:00D1GD50SG001",
      "BlockNode:00D21GJMT8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8002:props:StringProp:00D1FCXNC8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8002:props:StringProp:00D1FCXNC8001",
