        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Service cost**",
    "text": "**Service cost**: the service (pid 300846) went from 952,640 kB resident and 435.32 s of total CPU to 1,075,560 kB and +4.89 s CPU after the removal, and to 1,375,420 kB after the view operation that wrote the mirror; the peak stayed at 2,007,656 kB. So the removal and the flush after it cost about 420 MB of resident memory that the process keeps, which fits wasm memory that grows and is not returned.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The thread-flush gap is confirmed live**",
    "text": "**The thread-flush gap is confirmed live**: the removal did not write `.state/BlockNode.jsonld` (modification time still 19:47:08); the next view operation did, at 19:48:32, from 2,161,489 to 2,010,375 bytes. A removal followed by a kill would have been lost.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9EG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The question on the root**",
    "text": "**The question on the root**: 163 of the 164 blocks are gone from the mirror but the task's root remains as a tombstoned record (`tombstonedAt`, no children), and the `## aperas skill` heading's `children` list still names it; seven other removed tasks are the same. That is the soft delete: a tombstoned block stays until the garbage collection prunes it, and a tombstone still named by its live parent may count as reachable and stay. Whether this is by design is not settled; `issues/treeview.md` records a removal leaking tombstones into the tracked mirror and the design says a pruned thread is an ordinary remove. To check: whether the next restart's collection removes the root, and whether the parent's children list should drop a tombstoned child.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1FCX9E8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FFV2FR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1FFV2FR001",
    "text": "**Decision — raise the thread size cap to 1,000 blocks instead of pruning, and have subagents record their transcript path in their thread** (2026-10-11, user, declining the proposed prune: \"No, let's increase the threshold to 1000 blocks instead :D And let's update the skill to ask subagents to record their transcript path into their thread, so that the later agents can trace details when needed.\"):",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1FFV2FR002",
      "BlockNode:00D1FFV2FR003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FFV2FR002",
