    "title": "## v4.6 additions — delta on the v4 snapshot",
    "text": "Records the v4.6 edits to the skills: the rule that every Work begins with a subturn recording the path of the agent's own transcript, decided in [the user's decision to raise the thread cap and record the transcript path](#id/BlockNode:00D1FFV2FR001) and checked in [the verification of the thread cap and the transcript-path rule](#id/BlockNode:00D1FHX5MG001). The base skill states the rule in the thread-structure template and in Core Thread Disciplines, with the Claude Code method (an `echo` of a unique marker in one call, then a `grep -lF` for it in the next) and an Antigravity line that says no method is recorded yet; the Coder and Grapher skills add one `**Transcript**` line to their turn templates. The `Status:` lines of all four skills (the base, Orchestrator, Coder and Grapher skills) move to v4.6, with four `Status` entries, one per skill; the Orchestrator skill's `Status:` line moved with no other change in its text, because the base rule covers how a later agent reads a transcript. Each entry that rewrites text recorded in an earlier delta carries a `Supersedes:` line naming the blocks it replaces.",
