    "title": "00D1FK5CM0001",
    "text": "**Decision — the thread size cap is 10,000, and no prune now** (2026-10-11, user, on learning that both threads exceed 1,000: \"How, both has exceeded 1k.... They're growing so fast! I still don't want a pruning now because it requires more skill to learn from the threads, but the concepts.md has not been even designed yet. So, maybe bump the cap to 10k :D I see it's still far ahead, and no practical pressure on pruning.\"): the field in `AperasKG/aperas.config.json` becomes `\"threadSizeCap\": 10000`; pruning waits until there is a skill for learning from threads and a designed `concepts.md` to promote recurring patterns into. The running Grapher turn for the v4.6 delta was told by message to write 10,000, not 1,000, where its Ask said so. The service reads the cap once at start, so the new value applies after a restart, which is the user's.",
