    "title": "**The orchestrator's note, not an objection**",
    "text": "**The orchestrator's note, not an objection**: the cap is only a warning; the practical pressure is the data, not the warning. The store went from 41,246 quads (2026-10-10) to 50,055 and 58,376 over the last two starts, mostly thread blocks and their links; the startup sweep, the boot and the resident memory all grow with the store (the service idles above 1 GB and the start answers about a minute after launch). Pruning is cheap now that removal takes seconds (3.7 s for 164 blocks and 101 links), so the choice to wait is safe to revisit when the store passes a size the user chooses; a figure such as 100,000 quads or 2 GB resident would be a measurable trigger for it. The user may decide that later.",
