        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Record your transcript first**",
    "text": "**Record your transcript first**: The first subturn of every Work is `**Transcript**: <harness>: <path>`, the path of your own transcript file, so a later agent can look up a detail your Report left out. If you cannot find the path, record `**Transcript**: <harness>: not found` with what you tried, once, so nobody searches again. A later agent that needs a detail searches that file with `grep` or `jq` for the detail and never reads the whole file: a transcript is large and can overflow the context.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0003",
      "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0003:props:StringProp:00D1FM91SR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0003:props:StringProp:00D1FM91SR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Claude Code**",
    "text": "**Claude Code**: Run `echo \"TRANSCRIPT_$(date +%s%N)\"` in one tool call, then in the next call run `grep -lF <the printed marker> ~/.claude/projects/*/\"$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID\"/subagents/*.jsonl`; the one file it names is yours, because only your transcript holds your marker. `CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID` names the session that dispatched you, not you, and the file name `agent-<id>.jsonl` is not in any environment variable, so the marker is how you find it. The newest file by modification time is not reliable with several subagents running. The main session's transcript is `~/.claude/projects/*/\"$CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID\".jsonl`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FM8NJ0004",
