    "title": "**v4.6 — every Work begins with a subturn that records the path of the agent's own transcript**",
    "text": "**v4.6 — every Work begins with a subturn that records the path of the agent's own transcript**: recorded as [the v4.6 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D1FJW728001). The thread-structure template in the base skill gains a `**Transcript**: <harness>: <path>` line as the first subturn of a Work, and Core Thread Disciplines gains \"Record your transcript first\": a later agent that needs a detail the Report left out searches that file with `grep` or `jq` and never reads the whole file. The Claude Code method is an `echo` of a unique marker in one tool call and a `grep -lF` for it over the session's `subagents/*.jsonl` in the next, because only the agent's own transcript holds its marker; for Antigravity no method is recorded yet. The Coder and Grapher turn templates gain one `**Transcript**` line, and the `Status:` lines of the base, Coder and Grapher skills move to v4.6. The rule came with the decision to raise the thread size cap instead of pruning; the cap is now configurable (`threadSizeCap` in `aperas.config.json`, or `APERAS_THREAD_SIZE_CAP`), with a default of 200; this graph sets it to 10,000, and the service reads it once at start.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CEA5MHD8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1FP4FGR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1FP4FGR001",
    "text": "**Verification — the v4.6 delta read; the orchestrator's `Status:` moves too; answers to the Grapher's two questions** (2026-10-11, orchestrator): the Grapher recorded `## v4.6 additions` (`BlockNode:00D1FJW728001`) with seven entries (three `Status`, the thread-structure template superseding the v4.3 block `00CVM2MEX800E`, \"Record your transcript first\", and the Coder and Grapher Work and Report blocks superseding `00CVJXQWNR009` and `00CVJXQWNR00J`), every dropped unit matched, one more unit superseded that the checker misses because it compares only the first 120 characters; the History has the v4.6 milestone (`00D1FMR19G001`) and \"revised through v4.6\", and says the cap is configurable, 200 by default, 10,000 here, read once at start; no design, issue or planning text names 200. The drift script exits 1 on one finding only: the orchestrator skill's `Status:` is v4.5, behind the newest recorded v4.6; `aperas check-links` is clean.",
