    ],
    "title": "**Order**",
    "text": "**Order**: (1) the `free()` helper over the store reads (the item above, with the map of the sites under it), with its scratch measurement on a copy of the real store; (2) no further hacks on Oxigraph; (3) a pure JavaScript ApeironNgn engine, the dedicated engine the name suggested, as a separate task, compared with the `free()` version. The user's words: \"I think we should applied the `free()` patch as our best effort on Oxigraph, but no more hack on Oxigraph. After that, we'll try the pure JS ApeironNgn (as the name originally suggested, a dedicated engine) to compare with the `free()`-patched version.\"",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Why the store may change**",
    "text": "**Why the store may change**: the store is only an in-memory reflection of the mirror, and the mirror (the JSON-LD under `Apeiron/`) is the source of truth, which has stayed stable from TerminusDB to now, so a replacement store (Oxigraph, or plain JavaScript) does not hold the truth.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**In the `free()` change**",
    "text": "**In the `free()` change**: the whole read helper of the map (reads as plain values, write helpers that take strings, `predIri` cached per field name), taken from the Coder's recommendation because \"best effort\" points that way. **Out of it**: the whole-store `free()` on reload (measured to change nothing), the plain JavaScript engine, and new fields for `removeDanglingUnfolds` (none exist in code).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The comparison of the `free()` version with the pure JavaScript engine**",
    "text": "**The comparison of the `free()` version with the pure JavaScript engine**: not decided, not tried. What a replacement has to offer is small: the code calls only `match`, `add` and `delete` on a store, plus the term and quad constructors `quad`, `namedNode` and `literal`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GC79B8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR001",
