    ],
    "title": "**Full scans** (`match(null, null, null, null)`)",
    "text": "**Full scans** (`match(null, null, null, null)`): `allIdsOfKind`, `core/.../dehydrate.ts:49-59`, makes per quad the `Quad` and `q.subject` read twice (`termType` at 52, `value` at 53), 3 wasm objects, about 176k per call here, last used at 53, returns `string[]`. Callers, each paying the whole scan: `folders.ts:21`, `artifacts.ts:200`, `dehydrate.ts:136,161,168` (once per kind per flush), `kgTrack.ts:82,92,104`, `kgProfile.ts:65,111`, `linkIntegrity.ts:112`, `node.ts:985,2094,2201,2209,2247` (`tombstoneVacuousContainers` repeats it in a loop until nothing changes), `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts:24`. The second pass of `rehydrateStore`, `store.ts:154-159`, is a full scan too: the `Quad` and `q.object` at 155 and 157, 3 objects, output a `Set<string>`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Field reads**",
    "text": "**Field reads**: `readField` and `decodeTerm`, `node.ts:149-162`, reached by every field read through `defineAccessors` (`node.ts:1329-1337`); bound subject and predicate; per quad the `Quad`, `m.object` at 150 and, for a literal, `decodeLiteral` (`vocab.ts:99-104`) takes `term.datatype`, one more `NamedNode`. The hottest site in the program. `decodeField`, `dehydrate.ts:75-95`, is the same read plus recursion into `serializeDoc` for `embed` (82); `serializeDoc` calls it for every field of every node on every flush.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Child reads**",
    "text": "**Child reads**: `childrenOf`, `node.ts:73-83`, a match bound on the object (`PARENT_PRED`, `nodeIri(id)`), then per child a bound match with `nodeIri(childId)`, reading `m.subject.value` and `idxMatches[0].object` twice; the same shape in `insertOrderedChild` (`node.ts:119-125`) and `orderedChildIds` (`dehydrate.ts:63-73`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Other bound reads**",
    "text": "**Other bound reads**: `nodeExists` (`vocab.ts:65-67`, only `.length`, 20 call sites); `ownerOfLink` (`node.ts:1423-1424`); `findProfileByHandle` and `findTreeViewByName` (`node.ts:2040,2050`); `backlinks` (`node.ts:2161`; callers `kgBacklinks.ts:32`, `kgProfile.ts:59,69`, `node.ts:1789,2266`, `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts:103`); `findByExactPath` (`tree.ts:19-22`), `findLiveByKindAndPath` (`artifacts.ts:187-193`), `pathOf` (`threadScope.ts:18-23`) and `owningArtifactOrFolderId` (`threadScope.ts:32-44`, one match per level up the parent chain, per id, called by `isThreadScopedId` from `dehydrate.ts:137` and `168`). One flush, `dehydrate.ts:128-146` and `dehydrateStateToJsonLd` (`dehydrate.ts:160-170`), costs about 3 full scans, about 7000 x (1 + parent depth) path matches and every field of every node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Delete and add paths**",
    "text": "**Delete and add paths**: `node.ts:100,101,136-141,178,231,237,256,265-269,294,301` (`appendOrderedChild`, `insertOrderedChild`, `clearField`, `hardDeleteNode`, `writeField`): each quad is passed to `store.delete(m)` and dropped; line 237 deletes every quad of a node; `insertOrderedChild` does 2 matches and 2 deletes per sibling. `hardDeleteNode` recurses (`node.ts:231-233`, `294-298`) while its own quad array is being iterated. `removeDanglingUnfolds` (`node.ts:251-259`) is bound on `predIri('unfolds')` and the deleted id, and passes each quad only to `store.delete(m)`. The adds (`node.ts:103-104,144-145,201,203,274-275,313,318,327` and `store.ts:95,96,107,112,116` in rehydrate) make a fresh `Quad` plus 2-3 args per call and drop them; `store.add` does not consume them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No match of their own**",
    "text": "**No match of their own**: `checkLinkIntegrity` (`linkIntegrity.ts:110-122`) calls `allIdsOfKind` and `wrap` (`node.ts:2149-2154`, a node is `{store, id}`) and reads through the accessors; `service.ts` calls the boot `rehydrateStore` at 162, the sweeps `tombstoneVacuousContainers`, `pruneUnreachableTombstones` and `pruneStaleUnfolds` at 202-204, 365-373, 418-420 and 474-477 (each runs `allIdsOfKind` several times), and the dehydrate at 237, 328, 421 and 425; at reload (378-379) `store = result.store` drops the old `Store` without `store.free()`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Test only**",
    "text": "**Test only**: `cli/src/verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts:25` returns the `Quad[]` and `store.add(q)` at 60 re-adds them (`referenceDanglingUnfoldQuads`, retained on purpose), 48 and 56 (`.length` only), 70-73 `unfoldedIds`; `cli/src/verifyLinkRefusals.ts:60` spreads the whole store.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1GCR1XR00A",
    "text": "**What can be freed, and what must be kept**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00B",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00C",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00D",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00E"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00B:props:StringProp:00D1GCRX80000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00B:props:StringProp:00D1GCRX80001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Free at the root as soon as the value is read**",
    "text": "**Free at the root as soon as the value is read**: every quad and term in `allIdsOfKind`, the rehydrate second pass, `readField`/`decodeTerm`, `childrenOf`, `orderedChildIds`, `decodeField`, `pathOf`, `owningArtifactOrFolderId`, `findByExactPath`, `findLiveByKindAndPath`, `ownerOfLink`, `backlinks`, `find*ByName/Handle`, `nodeExists`, `unfoldedIds`. Their results are strings, numbers, booleans, or `wrap`ped nodes holding `store` and `id`, so no wasm object outlives its call in production code; nothing is stored in a Map or a closure.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Free after the call that uses them**",
    "text": "**Free after the call that uses them**: the `Quad` in every delete loop (after `store.delete(m)`), every fresh quad and arg in every `store.add(...)`, every `nodeIri`/`predIri`/`encodeLiteral` arg after its `match` call.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Keep**",
    "text": "**Keep**: `PARENT_PRED`, `SIBLING_INDEX_PRED` (`vocab.ts:139-140`) and `XSD_INTEGER`, `XSD_BOOLEAN` (`vocab.ts:11-12`), module constants used by every call, so freeing one makes every later use throw; `subject` in `encodeDoc` (83) and `childSubject` in `appendOrderedChild` (99) until the last line that uses them; `deletedIri` in `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts:21`; the quads in `referenceDanglingUnfoldQuads` until the comparison ends.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Care points**",
    "text": "**Care points**: free the `Quad` after the term read from it is turned into a string, not before; with `matches[0]` and `matches.map(...)` the array is freed after the last use of any element; `hardDeleteNode` recurses while its quad array is iterated, so each quad is freed per element and after `store.delete`; free an arg only after the `match` that took it, and only if it was created for that call. Measured in a scratch process: a term taken from `q.subject` stays valid after `q.free()`, but `q.subject` after `q.free()` throws \"null pointer passed to rust\"; the results of `match(arg, ...)` stay readable after `arg.free()`, but `match(freedArg, ...)` throws; `store.add(quad)` does not consume the quad; `store.delete(freedQuad)` throws; a freed module constant used later as an argument throws.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The other fields of `removeDanglingUnfolds`**",
    "text": "**The other fields of `removeDanglingUnfolds`**: it covers only `unfolds` (`node.ts:256`, `predIri('unfolds')`); `shape.ts:146` defines only `unfolds` and `root` on a `TreeView`. `unfoldsCollapsed` and `unfoldsNoPreview` exist nowhere in `packages/`, only as a proposal in the graph (4 blocks in `Apeiron/BlockNode.jsonld`). If they are added as set fields of `TreeView`, `removeDanglingUnfolds` must sweep their predicates too, or match on the object alone and filter on the predicate set.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "text": "**Shapes for one helper that frees at the root** (a measured fact for all of them: `match` builds the whole array first, so no shape lowers the peak, only what stays alive after the call)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00H",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00J",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00K",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00M",
      "BlockNode:00D1GCR1Y0000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00H:props:StringProp:00D1GCRX8G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00H:props:StringProp:00D1GCRX8G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**A. Eager plain rows**",
    "text": "**A. Eager plain rows**: `readQuads(store, subjectId|null, field|null, object)` returns `{subject: string, predicate: string, object: {termType, value, datatype?}}[]`; the helper builds its own args from strings and frees args, quads and terms before returning. It changes the read sites listed above and turns `nodeExists` into `countMatches`. Safe by construction (no wasm object leaves the helper); the cost is one plain object per quad.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**B. Callback**",
    "text": "**B. Callback**: `forEachMatch(store, s, p, o, (q) => ...)` frees each quad after the callback; fits the delete loops. Hazard: a callback that keeps `q` or a term gets a null-pointer throw later.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**C. Generator yielding plain values**",
    "text": "**C. Generator yielding plain values**: no gain over A, because the array is already built; a generator that stops early would need a `finally`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**D. Specific helpers**",
    "text": "**D. Specific helpers**: `deleteMatches(store,s,p,o): number` for the delete loops, `countMatches` for `nodeExists`, `addQuad(store,s,p,o)` for all the `store.add(quad(...))` sites.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1Y0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The Coder's recommendation**",
    "text": "**The Coder's recommendation**: A for reads, D for writes, B not used; helpers take ids and field names as strings so they own the lifetime of every arg, with `predIri` cached per field name in a Map (a bounded set from `SHAPE_BY_KIND`, never freed) to remove the second kind of per-call allocation. `using`/`Symbol.dispose` exists on the classes (node 22) but the packages' `tsconfig` targets es2023 with `lib: [\"ES2023\"]`, so it needs a config change; not recommended here.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR00G",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1Y0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D1GCR1Y0001",
    "text": "**Measurement** (on a copy under `/tmp` of 58,780 quads, a fresh process per variant, `node --expose-gc`, `gc()` between calls): the unchanged `allIdsOfKind` grows about 42 MB per call and takes 570 to 1,140 ms; the variant that frees the subject term and the quad stays flat at 349 MB after a first-call rise of 32 MB, at about 150 ms per call. Caveats: one site, one corpus size, and resident set size is the only gauge (`process.memoryUsage().arrayBuffers` reads 0 and oxigraph exports no wasm memory size); without `gc()` between calls the freed variant looked as if it grew 17 MB per call, which was collectable string garbage.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1Y0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the production-bound measurement must show**",
    "text": "**What the production-bound measurement must show**: memory with `gc()` before every reading, the signal being a plateau (flat after call 1 with the change, linear without); the service shape, not one function: a cycle of `dehydrateToJsonLd`, `dehydrateStateToJsonLd`, the three sweeps and `checkLinkIntegrity`, at least 10 cycles, then a `rehydrateStore` reload loop with and without `store.free()` on the old store; time per call and per cycle; identical output, meaning the dehydrated `*.jsonld` byte-for-byte equal to the unchanged code's output on the same copy, and the `commit` suite green, plus a test that a helper never returns or leaves a freed object (any \"null pointer passed to rust\" is a miss); a split of the gain by site (`allIdsOfKind`, `readField`, add-args), because the gauge is rss.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1GCR1XR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
