    "text": "**Still unknown** when the survey was made (2026-10-11): the same plateau for the other sites (only `allIdsOfKind` was measured, with one corpus size), and whether `new Store()` freed on reload is a gain or a hazard for a request in flight (requests go through `enqueue()`, `service.ts:5`, but the swap at 378-379 was not traced against held references). Since the landing, [the Landed entry](#id/BlockNode:00D216W8Z0001) records the plateau on production code for `allIdsOfKind`, the dehydrate and the rehydrate, on one corpus size (59,275 quads); the gain split by site is not shown, and whether releasing the old `Store` on reload is a gain or a hazard stays unknown, because the whole-store `free()` on reload was left out of the change.",
