  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D217Y2N8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D217Y2N8001",
    "text": "**The other counts in the record are other moments, or other quantities, not corrections of this one** (reconciled 2026-10-12 against the entries themselves): the store grows with every write, mostly thread blocks and their links, so each figure belongs to its date. On 2026-10-02 the memory entry's 37,000 and 39,600 had no recorded method. On 2026-10-10 the store held 41,752 by `store.size`, and the live service logged 41,246 at its boot; the scans entry's 41.7k is this count. On 2026-10-11 a fresh copy of the real store held 47,836 (the Coder's comparison of the id sets by kind with the full scan; the testing design's \"about 48,000\" agrees with it), and the service had logged 50,055 at its previous start; two corpus copies of that day held 55,714 and 55,968 (the round-trip measurements, and the testing design's 55,968); the service logged 58,376 at its start that day (12:32 UTC); the Coder's copies for the `free()` item held 58,780 and, for its patch, 59,275. The 46,519 and the 50,610 are not store sizes: 46,519 is the number of `add()` calls of one rehydrate, 4,767 of them duplicates (46,519 less 4,767 is the 41,752), and 50,610 is a count derived from the mirror that overshoots for the same reason. Whether a count includes `.state/` is stated only where it is split (29,537 and 12,216 on 2026-10-10); the others are counts of a full store.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0X1SZ40002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D217Y2N8002"
    ]
  },
