    "title": "00D21860Y8001",
    "text": "**The early design's trigger for revisiting the store was met by wrapper overhead, not by data size** (2026-10-12): the archived ApeironNgn design chose Oxigraph's in-memory store as \"not a from-scratch build\" (its section 3) and decided to revisit it only \"once the KG's actual size makes in-memory rehydration or working-set size a real problem (GB-level)\" (its section 4, in the rollout step on the store; its section 5 repeats the wait). The trigger is a data size. In practice the service idled at 1.05 to 1.5 GB for 3.66 MB of JSON-LD on disk (about 6.3 MB now, see the counts in [the memory entry](#id/BlockNode:00CVQ4Z968001)), and the measured mechanism is the wrappers that full-store scans leave alive, not the data ([the scan entry](#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001)); the recorded trigger names no wrapper overhead.",
