  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21A7P0R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D21A7P0R001",
    "text": "**Verification and performance of the Grapher's correction turn (Turn 2 of `js-apeironngn-survey`, Report `BlockNode:00D2197KV8009`; Coder census Report `BlockNode:00D214DTAR007`)** (2026-10-12, orchestrator): I read the \"Landed\" entry (`00D216W8Z0001`; it names `d794060` on branch `oxigraph` and keeps the out-of-scope items out) and `aperas check-links` is clean over 7,107 live blocks (1,526 with link text); `AperasKG` has five files staged (`ArtifactNode.jsonld`, `BlockNode.jsonld`, `design/testing.md`, `discussion/aperas-skill.md`, `issues/core.md`). Not done by the Grapher: the `history/` milestone (no history document records the store's performance work), and four more statements that predate the landing (`00D0X1SZ3R00E`, `00D1EZSCH8001`, `00D0Y9HG3000B`, `00D1GCR1Y0003`). Performance, from outside the agents (one run, 12.6 minutes, 77 tool calls by the Grapher, the Coder's census finishing at the start): the service (pid 374326) went from 390 MB to 424 MB resident over 63 samples (09:31:18 to 09:41:39 UTC), 5-minute averages 398, 409 and 422 MB, about 3 MB per minute with no plateau seen; load average 0.94 to 3.39. The Grapher's own timings: each write 3.5 to 3.8 s wall with 0.8 s user CPU, inserts of a bullet with a link 4.9 to 5.1 s, `check-links` 2.9 s, projections 2.0 to 2.9 s, one command refused once with \"No ApeironNgn service running\" and answered on the next call. Not known: where the 2.7 s between the 0.8 s of CPU and the 3.5 s wall goes (the service queue, the `--flush`, or the CLI start), because it was not decomposed; and whether the memory rise is garbage the collector would free or retained data, because resident size is the only gauge. Flush hot spots from the census (items 3 and 6): a flush pair runs 8 `allIdsOfKind` scans, each one pass over all 60,810 quads, and one more at rehydrate; the flush reads every shape field of every node with its own match (`holder`: 7,276 reads, 7,274 empty; `links`: 7,276 reads, 5,769 empty); and the thread-scope filter climbs the parent chain (`pathOf` called 14,368 times in one flush); the Coder also reports that this climb makes 46% of about 170k matches at a flush, which I could not find in the filed entries and did not verify.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D21GQN8R001"
    ]
  },
