    ],
    "title": "00D21FP4Z8000",
    "text": "The removal that stalled the service for minutes (a full-store scan for every embedded node removed) is replaced by one object-bound match; one removal in the live service of a task of 164 blocks and 101 embedded `Link` nodes took 3.7 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The `free()` patch is committed as `d794060` on branch `oxigraph`",
    "text": "The `free()` patch is committed as `d794060` on branch `oxigraph`: the reads and writes of the Oxigraph store go through one helper that frees every wasm object at the root; in a scratch process on a copy of the mirror, eight scans of all ids by kind stay flat in memory, and the dehydrate of both mirrors falls from 33 to 38 s to 2.5 to 3.8 s. A fresh service answered 17 s after its process started at 379 MB resident, where a fresh service had idled at 1.05 to 1.5 GB (one sample).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Not shown",
    "text": "Not shown: the trend of resident memory over a long run (it still rose with writes in the two short runs recorded, with no plateau seen), the gain split by site, and whether releasing the old `Store` at reload is a gain or a hazard.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
