    "title": "00D21FP4Z8004",
    "text": "Oxigraph patching is paused. The plain JavaScript engine is begun on `js-apeironngn`: the contract the code asks of the store is surveyed, [the cost of a write](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001) is profiled, the engine is designed and planned in [Core — Planning](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF23FB1G001), [Batch 15](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBFKAG001) moved the current code to `core/src/shell/` on 2026-10-16, [Batch 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG001) built the engine's module in the freed `core/src/apeironNgn/` the same day (the schema and its closing check, the interface as types, the oracle and the `engine` test group), [Batch 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR006) built the records, the literal fields of cardinality `one`, `optional` and `set`, the ids, the collections and the orders, [Batch 5](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H) built the reference and embed fields, the reverse side, the removal of a node and the build of Persistence, [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V) built the ordered fields, the partitioning mark, containment with the parent derived from the reverse of `children`, and the tree of the records, [Batch 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014) built the tombstone, the tombstone of a subtree and the sweep, [Batch 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D) built several graphs (the name grammar, `createGraph`, `dropGraph`, the reads filtered to their graph, `graphOf` unconfirmed by the user, and the refusal of an embedded id in a containment field), [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) built the mirror in the shell (the format and the dump of the records, the load into the three graphs, the exact round trip, the table of settings and the mapping from a graph and a kind to a file, the rule that gives a new node its graph) and `danglingRefs` in the engine, and [Batch 10](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0004) built in the shell the lookups by a literal value (the three maps of a profile by its handle, a view by its name and an artifact or a folder by its stored path, one update function for each write that changes a map, `liveAtPath` for the live node at a path, and the rule for a key held by two live nodes), all committed by the user on `js-apeironngn` (Batches 3 to 10 as `1b58fab`, Batch 15 as `eae00f1`). The engine has behaviour for the literal, reference, embed and ordered fields, for tombstones and for several graphs: it creates a node, writes and reads a field, lists the ids of a kind, orders ids and keys, answers the reverse of a field, refuses a second container and a cycle, derives the parent, removes a node, tombstones a node or a subtree, sweeps the tombstones that no live node reaches, builds a graph from a plan, creates and drops a graph, reads a node's relations in the graph it names, and lists the ids referenced and never defined, tested against the oracle; the shell dumps and loads the mirror on it, and returns the migrated copy of the real mirror byte for byte; the existence and size of a store and the ports are not built, and each of those operations throws. Since the flip (piece 6 of Batch 11, 2026-10-21, committed by the user in `Aperas.dev` as `074670f`) the shell of `Aperas.dev` runs on the engine, and [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) is built (pieces 7 to 10 staged, not committed): the cli commands and the service boot, reload, flush, sweep and stop on it through the handle and the write layer; the reads call the lookups in place of the first-match readers and sort by the rules of the design; ingest, track, project, the writes and the tombstones are on the engine; the service sweeps each graph with the engine's `sweep`, flushes each graph on its own timer (`tree` 10 s, `threads.tree` and `treeviews` 3 s), refuses a mirror the load did not read in full unless started with `--start-anyway` (which copies the skipped documents to a side file first), and frees a replaced handle as far as the engine lets it. The last checks: `commit` 1049 of 1049 in 19.6 s to 21.2 s (budget 60 s), `essential` 74 of 74 in 2.9 s to 3.2 s (budget 5 s), `models` 187 of 187, `tools` 14 of 14, the corpus group 21 of 21. The six old Oxigraph files (`storeAccess.ts`, `shape.ts`, `store.ts`, `dehydrate.ts`, `threadScope.ts` and `vocab.ts`) stay in the tree frozen and guarded by a test until [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes them; the working service and the checkout `Aperas/` still run on the old code until the cutover, and the real mirror is not migrated. It is to be compared with the `free()` version on the same mirror ([Batch 13](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0010)); no comparison has been measured.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
