    "title": "**The sweep**",
    "text": "**The sweep**: `removeDanglingUnfolds` no longer scans every quad once per embedded node removed; it makes one `store.match` on the predicate `unfolds` with the deleted id as object, followed by the deletes. It covers `unfolds`, the only field of a `TreeView` that holds an unfolded id and exists in code. The change rests on [the removal-stall issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) and on [the fix status in the scans issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0X65RB8009).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Equivalence**",
    "text": "**Equivalence**: on a copy of the real store, 59 ids (29 with a hit) gave 43 `unfolds` quads removed and restored with 0 mismatches against the former scan, which stays as a test-only reference in `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Measured on scratch copies** (the old code measured first)",
    "text": "**Measured on scratch copies** (the old code measured first): a removal of 34 embedded nodes went from 21,130 ms with 34 full scans to 12 ms; a removal of a task of 122 nodes, not finished at 600 s (70 scans, 2.6 GB resident), took 24 ms; on a copy of the real store one deleted id cost 512.8 ms before and 0.015 ms after.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG000:links:Link:00D21FPK8R001",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG000:links:Link:00D21FPK8R001:props:StringProp:00D21FPK8R002",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "438"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Live**",
    "text": "**Live**: after the user committed and restarted the service on 2026-10-11, one `aperas remove --flush` of a finished task of 164 live blocks and 101 embedded `Link` nodes took 3.7 s and exited 0 with no stall, the other tasks of the thread were intact, and `aperas check-links` scanned 6,549 live blocks with 0 discrepancies. The old service had stalled for 5.4 and 12 minutes on removals of 42 and 31 blocks. One removal is one sample. [The removal-stall issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNX6A3R000) is recorded resolved for the cause it names, the scan per embedded node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Not shown**",
    "text": "**Not shown**: the other suspected causes of the stall (the link-integrity sweeps, the tombstone hard-deletes at shutdown and startup, a slowdown with the life of the process) were not separated from the scans by any run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
