      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C800A:props:StringProp:00D22ZKJX0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZK7C800A",
    "text": "Which other views show the same reversal, and whether the reversal holds for every block with several links or only for the one tested.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C800B:links:Link:00D22ZQQFG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C800B:links:Link:00D22ZQQFG000:props:StringProp:00D22ZQQFG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "407"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZK7C800B",
    "text": "The user's decision of 2026-10-12 is that the engine keeps JavaScript's natural oldest-first order, and the engine will support a reverse view of a field in general; under that order this display would flip to the text order by accident of the engine and not by a rule of the renderer. Where the order of the display is only cosmetic that may be accepted; where a reader's choice depends on it (the case in [the first-match issue](#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001)) it may not.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZK7C800C",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZK7C800D"
    ]
  },
  {
