    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG003",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG003:props:StringProp:00D22ZN5V8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG003:props:StringProp:00D22ZN5V8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZMTKG003",
    "text": "No wrong result is visible today. The real mirror has exactly one path held twice, `issues/cli.md`: a tombstoned `ArtifactNode:00CF1TZQV8000` and a live, newer `ArtifactNode:00CF2AEA78000`. A removed node keeps its `path`, so `path` is unique only among live nodes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`findByExactPath` (`tree.ts:20`) is `firstSubjectWhere(store, 'path', ...)`",
    "text": "`findByExactPath` (`tree.ts:20`) is `firstSubjectWhere(store, 'path', ...)`: it takes the first match and does not look at `tombstonedAt`. Today the first match is the newer, live artifact because the store returns the newest first; under oldest-first it would be the old removed one, and nothing in the lookup says that the answer depends on the order.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZMTKR001",
    "text": "**Root cause**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR002",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR002:props:StringProp:00D22ZN5V8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR002:props:StringProp:00D22ZN5V8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZMTKR002",
    "text": "The lookup relies on the engine's match order for a choice of node. Its sibling `findLiveByKindAndPath` (`artifacts.ts:188`) filters out the tombstoned and is correct. Callers of the plain one found by `grep`: `resolve.ts:69`, `resolveCreate.ts:98` (both for the root, `.`), `linkIntegrity.ts:323` and `kgProject.ts:46` (an artifact path from the command line), and some verify scripts. Which of them can meet a tombstoned duplicate was not checked for each.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The same first-match lookups exist on other fields",
    "text": "The same first-match lookups exist on other fields: `findProfileByHandle` (`node.ts:2012`), `findTreeViewByName` (`node.ts:2021`) and the owner of a link. `handle` and `name` are unique by design (the code refuses a duplicate view name) and the real mirror has no duplicate (17 views, none repeated; no repeated handle), so they are not a defect today.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZMTKR004",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKR005:props:StringProp:00D22ZN5V8004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
