  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`encodeDoc` and `mintEmbedded` write any key they are given as a predicate, so the closed predicate vocabulary of the store is not enforced at the two paths that take keys from outside the shape**",
    "text": "**`encodeDoc` and `mintEmbedded` write any key they are given as a predicate, so the closed predicate vocabulary of the store is not enforced at the two paths that take keys from outside the shape**: found 2026-10-12 by the Coder in the census of the store's predicates (item 2); latent, as neither produces a foreign predicate with today's data. Filed 2026-10-12.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR002",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR004",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0000",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR002:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB28000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR002:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB28001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZWZMR002",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR003:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB28002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR003:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB28003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZWZMR003",
    "text": "None today. The mirror holds 27 predicates and 60,810 quads, every predicate a shape field or one of the two structural ones (`parent`, `__siblingIndex`), and no predicate outside `SHAPE_BY_KIND` and those two (checked for every subject; 0 foreign IRIs). In production code every field name comes from a shape key or is one of nine literals (`parent`, `__siblingIndex`, `path`, `links`, `handle`, `name`, `unfolds`, `target`, `profile`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZWZMR004",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR005",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR006",
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR005:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB28004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR005:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB28005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZWZMR005",
    "text": "`encodeDoc` (`store.ts:70`) writes every key of a mirror document except `@id` and `@type` as a quad, whether or not the shape has it. A key outside the shape lives in memory, and the dehydrate would later drop it, since `serializeDoc` (`dehydrate.ts:73`) walks only the shape's fields: it would survive until the next flush and then vanish from the mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZWZMR006",
    "text": "`mintEmbedded` (`node.ts:165`) writes every string, number or boolean key of an embedded entry, apart from `@type`, `@id` and `id`, with no check against the shape of the embedded kind.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZWZMR007",
    "text": "In the tests, `storeAccess.test.ts` writes made-up predicates `count` and `flag` on scratch stores, and one quad with a foreign subject IRI to prove that `subjectsWhere` throws and `deleteMatches` still works, on purpose; no test or fixture writes any other predicate outside the shape.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D22ZWZN0000",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0001:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB2G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0001:props:StringProp:00D22ZXB2G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D22ZWZN0001",
    "text": "That any real input reaches either path with an unknown key; the census found none and did not try to build one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22ZWZN0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
