    "title": "## Status",
    "text": "A draft, written with the user from 2026-10-12 to 2026-10-16 and fact-checked against the code and against the mirror on 2026-10-12. The statements are rules the engine must satisfy, not a description of today's code, and where the code differs from a rule the difference is filed as an issue: [tombstoning leaves content on the node](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001), [sibling indexes are not kept dense](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252Y7WR001), [a child can end with two `parent` pairs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2532JJR001), [the kind of an id and an id-like string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2534RSG001), [the store is read outside the helpers](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2536E1R001), [the loader writes `parent` from its own pair](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2538VKR001), [the scans behind every list of the ids of a kind](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001), [artifacts ingested without a `type`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D253D680001), [the first-match lookup of a path](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001), [the order of a block's links](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001), [`danglingRefs` computed and not read by the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001), [the thread-scope test inside the engine's directory](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2590B2R001), [the code differs from the boundary](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBNCF8001), [the first-match `ownerOfLink`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2593220001) and [a repeated `@id` that is logged and merged](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2595QAG001). What is not decided is listed under [Open points](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000J), and the Open points are the work that remains.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "## Purpose and scope",
    "text": "The engine is the graph the service holds in memory, between the mirror on disk and the commands that read and change the graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
