            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "180"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**One schema, handed in at construction**",
    "text": "**One schema, handed in at construction**: the fields a node can have are declared once for each kind, in the schema that the shell passes to the engine when it constructs it (see [The meta-model](#id/BlockNode:00D4MYZ6Q0000)), and that declaration is the only schema. There is no schema language beside it and no query surface that shapes the data differently from it; the accessors of a field, in the shell's classes, go through the schema, which knows the field's cardinality and storage kind. Whether the two paths that take keys from outside the schema (the load of a mirror document and the minting of an embedded node) are held to it as well is an Open point (see [Enforcement](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Versioning is git**",
    "text": "**Versioning is git**: a write to the mirror followed by an ordinary commit is the version control. The engine has no commit layer, and merging work from another copy is git's merge on the mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No concurrent access**",
    "text": "**No concurrent access**: one process owns the engine and handles one request at a time. The engine has no locks, no transactions and no isolation of its own.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00B",
