    "title": "**Closed vocabulary**",
    "text": "**Closed vocabulary**: every field of a record is one that the schema declares for its subject's kind. Nothing else is stored. Containment is the field to which the schema assigns that role, and the parent is its reverse (see [Containment](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z)). That the vocabulary is closed is a property of the data and of the shell; whether the engine enforces it is open (see [Open points](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000J)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A field is a relation**",
    "text": "**A field is a relation**: a reference or embed field relates subjects to the nodes that are their values, and has a forward side (the values of field F of subject S) and a reverse side (the subjects whose field F holds node V). The reverse side exists for every such field; which reverse sides the shell uses is the shell's choice, and the engine keeps no list of the fields that have one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00G:links:Link:00D3EKKM3R000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D255WVK0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00G:links:Link:00D3EKKM3R000:props:StringProp:00D3EKKM3R001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "142"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Cardinalities**",
    "text": "**Cardinalities**: `one` (exactly one value), `optional` (at most one), `set` (any number, unordered) and `ordered` (a set with an order, see [Ordered fields](#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001)). A cardinality is declared in the schema for each field of each kind and is never inferred from the data: a set field that holds one value must stay distinguishable from an optional field that happens to be set, which counting the values cannot tell.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Storage kinds**",
    "text": "**Storage kinds**: `literal` (a plain value), `reference` (the id of another node, which the field does not own) and `embed` (a node the field owns: it has an id of its own, is written inside its owner's document in the mirror and is removed with its owner).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Literal types**",
    "text": "**Literal types**: string, integer and boolean, kept as their JavaScript types, so the string \"1\" and the number 1 are different values. A string that looks like a date stays a plain string, because typing it as a date would let a store rewrite its text.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-10-14T15:07:34.495Z",
    "title": "**Set fields in use**",
    "text": "**Set fields in use**: the set fields that really hold several values are the links and props of a block, the props of a link and the unfolded ids of a view; every other set field holds none or one in practice.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
