    "title": "`ArtifactNode`, extending `TreeNode`",
    "text": "`ArtifactNode`, extending `TreeNode`: it is its own root document and adds `path` (one) and five optional fields, `fileHash`, `lastTrackedAt`, `ingestedHash`, `lastIngestedAt` and `projectedHash`, which are set when the document is tracked, ingested or projected and are absent before. It has no `type`. Its `title` is the name of its file, extension included (the artifact `design/core.md` is titled `core.md`), the identity that the path is built from (see [The title of an artifact or a folder is its name](#id/BlockNode:00D4RSAZ3G001)). The stored `path` is transitional: the shell is to derive the path (see [The path is derived from the parent chain](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01S)), and the field goes with the batch that removes it (see [Deriving the path](#id/BlockNode:00D25698B0001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
