    "title": "**Containment**",
    "text": "**Containment**: containment is the field to which the schema assigns that role (`children` in the Aperas schema, declared on `TreeNode`, so that a block, an artifact and a folder all hold children), declared ordered and partitioning (see [Ordered fields](#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001) and [Partitioning fields](#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)). The list of a container holds its children in order; a node is in at most one container's list, and containment has no cycle. The reverse of the containment field at a node is its port in its container's list, which gives the node's parent and its place; the parent is read from that reverse, under the name the schema gives the reverse side (`parent` in the Aperas schema), and the engine keeps it consistent with the lists on every write. A node has at most one parent. Containment is written through the containment field. Containment is not ownership: taking a node out of its container's list detaches it and does not delete it. A node is owned or contained, never both: an id of the embedded shape (`owner:field:Kind:snowflake`, see [Ids](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01N)) cannot be listed in a containment field, so the node that an owner embeds has no place in any container's list and a node has one place in the tree. A tombstone is in no container's list (see [Tombstones](#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8000)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The artifact is its own root document**",
    "text": "**The artifact is its own root document**: no synthetic root block exists. The top-level blocks of a document (its top-level headings, and any block before the first heading) are ordinary children of its `ArtifactNode`; how the blocks below nest is the mapping of markdown, outside this document. The abstract of an artifact or a folder is its frontmatter `description`, which is also its `text`, the value the rename check compares; an artifact or a folder without a `description` has no basis for a rename, and no rename of it is detected.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Links are outgoing ports**",
    "text": "**Links are outgoing ports**: an outgoing reference of a node is a `Link` in its `links`, which has a `target` and no predicate. A block has one wikilink `Link` for each distinct target, whose `props` hold one `position` for each occurrence of the target in the block's text, as a start offset relative to the block's own text. A block that cites one target through more than one `Link` has a `Link` subject for each, every one with its own `target` pair, so the multiplicity is of subjects and never of a repeated pair. The types of links are to be given by a linking design of their own, through containment and not through a predicate, and the metadata of a link sits in the content of the block that holds it. A claim that links two nodes is content, a block in prose holding a link, and there is no edge class with a justification field of its own. The backlinks of a node are the `Link`s whose `target` is the node, each reported with its owner.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-10-14T14:39:18.430Z",
    "title": "**The key is derived**",
    "text": "**The key is derived**: the part of an id after its kind is the node's `key`. It is derived on read and never stored, so it cannot drift from the id.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR013",
