          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright**",
    "text": "**Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright**: an embedded node (a `Link` or a `StringProp` in the Aperas schema) has an id of its own and can be addressed, but it has no tombstone. Removing a pair of an embed field (`removePair`) removes, recursively, the embedded node the pair names (the embedded nodes of a removed one go with it, as the props of a `Link` do), so no orphan stays in the store. A write of an embed field that keeps some of its embedded nodes is `removePair` for each value it drops and `addPair` for each value it adds, so the nodes it keeps keep their ids (see [Writes](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000C)). Removing any node also drops it from every reference field to which the schema assigns the role of a value dropped with its target (`unfolds` in the Aperas schema). Other incoming references (a link's target, a parent, a profile) are not removed by deleting the node; keeping none of them dangling is the work of the sweeps of the service, and the engine answers the ids that are referenced and never defined, which the shell asks once it has built a graph (see [Persistence](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001)); what is done with them belongs to the service lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No edge class beyond `Link`**",
    "text": "**No edge class beyond `Link`**: the engine has no `Assertion` or `BaseEdge` class.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### The index",
    "text": "Every lookup the shell makes binds either the subject or the field and the value, so the engine answers them from the forward and reverse sides of its records, iterates the collection of a kind when all the nodes of that kind are asked for, and traverses the whole store only for the check the shell asks at load, the ids that are referenced and never defined.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHJXK0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24N87SR016",
      "BlockNode:00D24N87SR017",
      "BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001",
