      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR017:links:Link:00D3EM33F0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR017:links:Link:00D3EM33F0002:props:StringProp:00D3EM33F0003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "543"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Reverse, for each field, built on first use**",
    "text": "**Reverse, for each field, built on first use**: the reverse of a field is built the first time the field is asked in reverse and kept up to date by every write afterwards, so the engine supports reversal for every reference and embed field without paying for the fields nobody reverses. It is held on the record of each object (see [Records follow containment](#id/BlockNode:00D2T5P9Y8001)), not in a table of its own: the bucket of an object for a field, the subjects whose field holds that object, is a leaf or a split record of ports (see [Ports](#id/BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001)). A leaf is a set, for the cost of removal and of membership: a bucket can hold thousands of subjects, and taking one out or asking whether one is present must not scan the rest.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR018:links:Link:00D3EK48DG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01G",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR018:links:Link:00D3EK48DG000:props:StringProp:00D5B402R8002",
