        "target": "BlockNode:00D39EJSZ8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01B:links:Link:00D3WN1YDG000:props:StringProp:00D3WN1YDG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "115"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Layout**",
    "text": "**Layout**: the forward side is a record for each subject and not a table for each field, for the reasons given in [Why a node-based engine](#id/BlockNode:00D39EJSZ8001); the engine aims to keep each record as close as possible to its document in the mirror, without guaranteeing it, the shell bridging the gap, and the records are arranged in the containment tree (see [Records follow containment](#id/BlockNode:00D2T5P9Y8001)). It is chosen for modularity, because the engine serves several graphs (see [Several graphs](#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8002)). The reverse stays built on first use and is held on the records of the objects, and the layout does not change what the shell sees.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Ordering",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHJXK0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01D",
