    "title": "**Orders in the mirror**",
    "text": "**Orders in the mirror**: the children of a container are in the order of its list, which the engine keeps as an ordered field (see [Ordered fields](#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001)); documents within a file, the embedded entries of a set field and the values of a reference set field, such as `unfolds`, are in id order, by plain code-point comparison, and the shell sorts them at a dump (see [A flush is a dump](#id/BlockNode:00D39EAKW0001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01H",
