    "title": "**A path names one live node**",
    "text": "**A path names one live node**: the `path` of an `ArtifactNode` or `FolderNode` identifies exactly one live node. A tombstoned node keeps its path, as it keeps its literal properties (see [Tombstones](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8000)), so two nodes may hold one path and only one of them is live; every lookup by path therefore asks for the live node, through one primitive, \"the live node at this path\" (proposal, not agreed). Whether a node is live is known to the engine, which manages tombstones. What remains open about the path of a removed node is listed under Open points (see [How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
