    "title": "**Written by graph and kind**",
    "text": "**Written by graph and kind**: the write-back is by graph and by kind. The shell has three graphs: `tree`, which holds the tracked kinds (`ArtifactNode`, `FolderNode`, `BlockNode` and `Profile`); `threads.tree`, which holds the thread-scoped nodes of the three tree kinds, since the threads are a graph of their own and the scope test of a node is the graph it belongs to; and `treeviews`, which holds the `TreeView` nodes (see [Addressing](#id/BlockNode:00D5AYBPWR001) for the names and their order). The file of a graph and a kind is a function of the graph alone, through the table of settings: the directory that the graph's entry names, with the name of the kind and the `.jsonld` ending. The shell reads out the records of each kind in each graph through the engine's [persistence API](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001). A document in the mirror has no `graph` field: the graph of a record is given by the file that holds it, the file for its graph and kind, so the load gives each record the graph of the file it reads and the dump writes each record to the file of its graph and kind; in memory the record carries its `graph` as a field (see [Records by kind and by graph](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR018), which states the two folds side by side).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Format**",
    "text": "**Format**: documents are sorted by `@id`, indented by two spaces and end with a newline. A document lists `@id` and `@type` and then its fields in the order the class shape declares. A field that is unset or an empty set is left out, except `children`, which is always written, as an empty array when empty. The field order is:",
