    "title": "**The round trip is exact**",
    "text": "**The round trip is exact**: loading the mirror and writing it back returns the files byte for byte, so a flush with nothing changed leaves git clean. Every ordering above exists to keep this true, and a value must be written as it was read: strings unchanged, integers in their canonical text. The round trip is covered by [the tests](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F63R001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87T0002",
