    "title": "00D24N87T000A",
    "text": "The ids that are referenced and never defined, which the shell asks once it has built a graph: the ids that a pair of the graph references and that no graph defines, an id defined in any graph counting as defined (see [A reference across graphs](#id/BlockNode:00D4KD44M8001)). A `parent` that a build supplies is not a pair, so this read does not see an id that a `parent` names with no document: the load returns that id in a list of its own (see [A file whose `parent` and `children` disagree](#id/BlockNode:00D2PV8GC0001)).",
