  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D24N87T000E",
    "text": "Clear a field of a subject, which a write of a `one` or `optional` field does before it adds the new value: those cardinalities refuse a second value, so changing the value means clearing the field first, and a clear is the plain operation for a caller that holds the new value and not the old. The reverse side is not the reason, since every pair the engine adds or removes keeps it in step.",
