    "title": "**Existence**",
    "text": "**Existence**: whether a node exists by being in a registry or by having at least one pair. One case is undecided under either answer and stays so: a node that has incoming pairs and no record of its own, which arises when a build accepts a reference to a node not yet built ([Build](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG002)) and when a removal leaves the references to the node removed ([Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013)); whether such a node exists is not decided, and the reverse side it has ([Reverse, for each field, built on first use](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR017)) is not to be read as its existence until it is. The shell never asks that case: its `nodeExists` is `graphOf(id) !== undefined` (see [A node exists when a document stands for it](#id/BlockNode:00D76AAE8G001)), and the engine's answer for it stays open.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
