    "title": "**Enforcement**",
    "text": "**Enforcement**: whether the engine enforces the cardinalities and the closed vocabulary from the schema, or the shell does. Enforcement in the engine changes the behaviour of the two paths that take keys from outside the schema and of the tests that write made-up predicates on scratch stores ([the issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR001), [the stale smoke test](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZV0FG001)). For a field marked partitioning it is decided: the engine ensures the mark and refuses the writes that would break it (see [Partitioning fields](#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)); the question stands for every other field.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-10-13T10:45:47.557Z",
    "title": "**Layout**",
    "text": "**Layout**: a record for each subject or a table for each field. Most probes of an optional field find nothing, so the choice depends on whether the cost of a probe of one field or the cost of reading all fields of one subject is the one to cut.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
