    ],
    "title": "**An invalid id and a non-canonical integer**",
    "text": "**An invalid id and a non-canonical integer**: the engine refuses an id that fails the grammar (see [Ids](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01N)), which settles the first half; whether it rewrites a non-canonical integer into its canonical form is not decided.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Size**",
    "text": "**Size**: what happens when the mirror outgrows memory, since the engine holds it all and loads it all at start. The answer is deferred until the size is a problem.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
