    "title": "00D24P9GPG001",
    "text": "Promoted to [Reverse, for each field, built on first use](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR017); the whole draft is [Core — Design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV228001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV228001:props:StringProp:00D24PVGTG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV228001:props:StringProp:00D24PVGTG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Until 2026-09-02, TerminusDB, the first substrate",
    "text": "Until 2026-09-02, TerminusDB, the first substrate: the graph lived in a TerminusDB database that the JSON-LD mirror in git reflected. The reasons and the design are recorded in the archived `Aperas-design.md` (\"Stack Selection Rationales\" and \"Phase 0.1: Substrate Evolution\"); the TerminusDB designs themselves are under `tdb-era/` in the archive.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV228002",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G000",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV228002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV228002:props:StringProp:00D24PVGTG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV228002:props:StringProp:00D24PVGTG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Why it was chosen**",
    "text": "**Why it was chosen**: immutable delta layers with Git-like branches, time travel, diffs and merge requests; JSON-LD document classes that map onto block trees and nested subdocuments; WOQL and generated GraphQL as the two query surfaces.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV228001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What kept the move cheap**",
    "text": "**What kept the move cheap**: the mirror already round-tripped as plain JSON-LD, so \"nothing about the substrate's actual content depends on TerminusDB being the engine\", and every TerminusDB call sat behind named modules (`client.ts`, `crud.ts`, `woql.ts`, `graphql.ts`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV228001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Superseded by**",
    "text": "**Superseded by**: ApeironNgn (next entry). The roadmap named the successor \"a minimal Rust graph engine scoped to exactly what Aperas exercises\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV228001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-02, ApeironNgn designed, and the reasons for leaving TerminusDB",
    "text": "2026-09-02, ApeironNgn designed, and the reasons for leaving TerminusDB: from the commits of the archived `Aperas-apeironngn-design.md` (sections 1 and 2); the findings were read from that file and not re-run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G003",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G004",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G005"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G003:props:StringProp:00D24PVGTR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G003:props:StringProp:00D24PVGTR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Dates**",
    "text": "**Dates**: the archived file does not date its steps; the dates in these entries are those of the commits that changed it, from 2026-09-02 to 2026-09-07, and a step's date is the range in which it landed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The stated reason**",
    "text": "**The stated reason**: architectural fit, \"not a response to a measured bottleneck\" (a bulk tree fetch took 18 ms for 91 nodes). TerminusDB made the projection happen twice, once into its own JSON-LD schema and again into the differently shaped results of WOQL, GraphQL and the Document API; ApeironNgn's promise was one projection, in which the class is the schema and the traversal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What was found against the live TerminusDB**",
    "text": "**What was found against the live TerminusDB**: `List` fields give plain `triple()` no shortcut in either direction (no reverse lookup, and the forward lookup binds to the internal `Cons` cell and needs an `rdf:first` and `rdf:rest` walk); `@abstract` classes do not become GraphQL interfaces; rebuilding a tree node by node lost to the bulk fetch by 47 to 240 times because no API can ask for \"whatever fields this type has\" without knowing the type; two upstream bugs filed, `terminusdb/terminusdb#2509` (bundle and unbundle across stores) and `terminusdb/terminusdb#2512` (`@unfold` on a `List` field); a server panic from a string truncated inside a multi-byte UTF-8 character, reproduced twice.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-02, ApeironNgn on Oxigraph, in memory",
    "text": "2026-09-02, ApeironNgn on Oxigraph, in memory: the design and its first build, from the archived design (section 3 and section 4, step 1), checked then node for node against the raw JSON-LD of the real mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G007",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G008",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G009",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00A",
      "BlockNode:00D3F6J4JG001",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00B"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G007:props:StringProp:00D24PVGV0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G007:props:StringProp:00D24PVGV0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The engine**",
    "text": "**The engine**: Oxigraph, an off-the-shelf embeddable RDF store with SPO, POS and OSP indexes, used synchronously from Node, chosen over a build from scratch.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Containment**",
    "text": "**Containment**: reified `parent` and `siblingIndex` triples instead of `rdf:List`, so both directions are cheap and the order comes from sorting a fetched set.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The schema is the class**",
    "text": "**The schema is the class**: a per-class table of each field's cardinality (`one`, `optional`, `set`, `orderedContainment`) and storage kind (`reference`, `embed`), written against the classes and deliberately not derived from TerminusDB's `schema.json`, which had already drifted from the live schema. The first reading interface was a `Proxy` for each node, so that `a.b.c` was a literal property access.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Storage and scope**",
    "text": "**Storage and scope**: in memory only, because the Node and WASM build has no on-disk store; \"revisit only once the KG's actual size makes in-memory rehydration or working-set size a real problem (GB-level)\". Versioning is git on the mirror; concurrency is not supported by design, and search needs a secondary index under any engine.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00B:links:Link:00D24PVGWR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00B:links:Link:00D24PVGWR000:props:StringProp:00D24PVGWR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "188"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Superseded by**",
    "text": "**Superseded by**: the `Proxy` (step 3, below), the hierarchy it served, and the revisit trigger, which was met by the overhead of the wrapper objects and not by the size of the data (see [the scans issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-02 to 2026-09-03, the scripts migrated one at a time",
    "text": "2026-09-02 to 2026-09-03, the scripts migrated one at a time: each command was given an ApeironNgn implementation, run on the same real data and diffed against its TerminusDB output before the next (archived design, section 4, step 2).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00D",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00E",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00F",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00G"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00D:props:StringProp:00D24PVGVG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00D:props:StringProp:00D24PVGVG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Read paths**",
    "text": "**Read paths**: `kg:tree`, `kg:path`, `kg:resolve` (both tiers) and `kg:project` were diffed clean, including the error paths, once the diff harness compared standard error and exit status as well as standard output. `kg:project` was clean on 17 of 18 artifacts; the 18th failed on the TerminusDB side with a server error at that document's size.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Write paths**",
    "text": "**Write paths**: from `kg:unfold` on, a write was checked on a scratch copy of the mirror and not by a live diff, because a write-capable script run on the real paths changes the real mirror on success. `kg:title`, `kg:link`, `kg:track` and `kg:ingest` were verified that way.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The write-back**",
    "text": "**The write-back**: `dehydrateToJsonLd` rewrote the real mirror to a scratch directory with zero semantic mismatches over all of its documents. One real bug: Oxigraph canonicalised an `xsd:dateTime` literal on read-back and rewrote `...27.480Z` to `...27.48Z`; date-like strings are no longer typed as dates.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00G",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Not migrated**",
    "text": "**Not migrated**: `kg:export` and `kg:import` were retired, since they only bridged TerminusDB and the mirror; `kg:search` waited for a secondary index; `Assertion` and `kg:assert` were left out.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03, step 3",
    "text": "2026-09-03, step 3: the `Proxy` replaced by classes, and the hierarchy made real: from the archived design (step 3).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00J",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00K",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00M",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00N",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00P",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Q"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00J",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00J:props:StringProp:00D24PVGVG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00J:props:StringProp:00D24PVGVR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Accessors**",
    "text": "**Accessors**: each leaf class got real `get` and `set` accessors on a sealed instance, so an unknown read gives `undefined` and an unknown write throws, with the error a generic `TypeError`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Hierarchy**",
    "text": "**Hierarchy**: the flat classes became `ApeironInstance`, `BaseNode`, `TreeNode` and `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode`, `FolderNode`; `Link` and `StringProp` became leaf subdocuments.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The key**",
    "text": "**The key**: `blockId`, `artifactId` and `folderId` were replaced by one derived `key` (the part of the id after its kind), so the mirror stopped writing them, and the old `kg:import` could no longer read it, which was accepted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00N",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`Link` as an embedded node**",
    "text": "**`Link` as an embedded node**: it shed the base node fields and kept `target` and `predicate`, and the hand-made \"mint an id, then attach\" steps went away. `Assertion` and `BaseEdge` were not migrated in any form: a claim linking two nodes is a block of prose with a wikilink, and the real `Assertion` file was empty.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Functions folded into methods by a rule**",
    "text": "**Functions folded into methods by a rule**: a function folds onto a class when one identified node is a natural `this`; a store-wide search or sweep stays free.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Bugs found and fixed**",
    "text": "**Bugs found and fixed**: an embed carry-forward that destroyed a link by treating a bare id string as an object; `props` and `frontmatter` receiving new ids on every ingest (now matched by key and value); the order of a set field not stable across a rehydrate and dehydrate; a test of liveness written as `tombstonedAt !== true`, which is true for every node (the field holds a date string); the projection lacking a final newline.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00R",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03, step 4",
    "text": "2026-09-03, step 4: the real corpus validated and the TerminusDB code archived: from the archived design (step 4).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00S",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00T",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00V"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00S",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00S:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00S:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**First run on the real corpus**",
    "text": "**First run on the real corpus**: 13 artifacts with no real change came back byte-identical, which the TerminusDB path did not achieve on the same corpus; the 5 that changed reconciled sanely.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The tests**",
    "text": "**The tests**: `verifyPhase0.ts` was replaced by a suite that runs on an in-memory store and never writes back to the real mirror. On its first run it found that a freshly minted `Link.target` was stored as a literal and not as a reference.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00V",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The hooks and the archive**",
    "text": "**The hooks and the archive**: the git hooks were moved from the TerminusDB `kg:track` to the ApeironNgn one, and the TerminusDB scripts were renamed with a `Tdb` suffix and archived under `web/.archive`, with the shared modules they need copied beside them as a frozen snapshot.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00R",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03, step 5",
    "text": "2026-09-03, step 5: the shared service process: from the archived design (step 5); the mechanics of the service remain recorded only there, since no design document describes the service yet.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00X",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Y"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00X:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00X:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**What replaced what**",
    "text": "**What replaced what**: every command used to start a process that rehydrated and dehydrated the whole mirror; one long-running service now holds one store, and every command is a thin client.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**How it behaves**",
    "text": "**How it behaves**: a Unix socket, a lock file claimed atomically, a queue that handles requests strictly one at a time, a flush of the mirror every 10 seconds when dirty or at once on `flush`, `reload` to read the mirror again, a hash stamp per file so that a flush refuses to overwrite a file that changed on disk, `reload --discard` and `flush --clobber` as the two explicit ways to resolve a conflict, and an exit after 30 idle minutes or on a signal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00W",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 6 and 7",
    "text": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 6 and 7: ingest ordering, and the root block retired: from the archived design (steps 6 and 7).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G010",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G011"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G010:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G010:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Step 6**",
    "text": "**Step 6**: `ingest --track`; the folder tree rebuilt before any content is parsed or any link resolved, so that a wikilink to a not-yet-attached path does not mint a duplicate holder; folder and file path segments matched the way headings are; a synthetic root block per artifact made invisible to addressing by four patches.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G011",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Step 7 (supersedes the four patches)**",
    "text": "**Step 7 (supersedes the four patches)**: `ArtifactNode` became a `BlockNode` and its own root document, the synthetic root block was removed from storage, and `text` of an artifact and a folder became a copied abstract for both. `FolderNode` stayed on `TreeNode`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G00Z",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G012",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 8 and 9",
    "text": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 8 and 9: link positions, embedded-node cleanup and tombstone consistency: from the archived design (steps 8 and 9).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G013",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G014"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G013:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G013:props:StringProp:00D24PVGW8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Step 8**",
    "text": "**Step 8**: `Link` gained `props`; a block keeps one `Link` for each distinct target, carrying one `position` prop for each occurrence, as a start offset relative to the block's own text; the title of a heading is no longer scanned for links. Two bugs: the kind of a nested embedded id was read from its first segment and not its last, and reassigning an embed field detached the old node but never deleted it (now removed recursively).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G014",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Step 9**",
    "text": "**Step 9**: all three tombstone sites clear `children`, `links` and `props`, and removing an artifact tombstones its whole subtree. A wikilink `Link` keeps its id while its target stays; a first version that also required the positions to match was corrected, because a position moves with any earlier edit.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G012",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G015",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 10 and 11",
    "text": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 10 and 11: visible tombstones, the garbage collection and the merge of `parent`: from the archived design (steps 10 and 11).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G016",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G017"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G016",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G016:props:StringProp:00D24PVGWG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G016:props:StringProp:00D24PVGWG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Step 10**",
    "text": "**Step 10**: a tombstoned node is printed with a `(tombstoned)` tag, and deleting an embedded node removes the `unfolds` entries that name it; the sweep was made object-bound in the first commit of the performance work (`0a7a226`, below). Its answer to \"when is a tombstone ever removed\" (\"never\") is superseded by the next step.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G017",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Step 11**",
    "text": "**Step 11**: a tombstoned node is deleted once nothing live reaches it, by a mark and sweep from the live artifacts and folders (a first design that counted any incoming reference was rejected, because a dead cluster would keep itself alive); the stored `parent` field and the private containment predicate, which recorded the same fact twice, were merged into one, a workaround for the `List` limitation of TerminusDB that had outlived its reason; `kg:unlink` was added, the removal counterpart of `kg:link`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G018",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 12 and 13",
    "text": "2026-09-03 to 2026-09-07, steps 12 and 13: the id scheme and the backlinks: from the archived design (steps 12 and 13).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4Z8005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G019",
      "BlockNode:00D24PV22G01A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G019",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G019:props:StringProp:00D24PVGWG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G019:props:StringProp:00D24PVGWG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Step 12**",
    "text": "**Step 12**: ids were `/`-separated compound ids under the base `urn:aperas:node:`; they became `:`-separated under `aperas://id/`, and `aperas://tree/` was added as a resolution-time address that is never stored; the test for a full id now requires a valid snowflake after the kind, which closes the hole of a folder named after a kind.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G018",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PV22G01A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Step 13**",
