    "title": "**Moved to the design**",
    "text": "**Moved to the design**: the closed vocabulary with its cardinalities and storage kinds, the fields of each class, containment as `parent` and a sibling index, the artifact as its own root document, the embedded `Link`, the derived key, ownership of embedded nodes, the id scheme, tombstones and their garbage collection, and the mirror's format and exact round trip. The index, the ordering rules, the uniqueness of a path and the engine's interface are new to the design: they come from the decisions and the census, not from the archive.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ48000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Moved to this history**",
    "text": "**Moved to this history**: the TerminusDB era and the reasons for leaving it, the choice of Oxigraph and its in-memory limit, the `Proxy`, the flat class hierarchy, the synthetic root block and its four patches, the `/`-separated ids, and the rollout steps with the bugs each one found.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ48001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Left in the archive, not placed**",
    "text": "**Left in the archive, not placed**: the mechanics of the service (the wire protocol, the lock and the race on start, the divergence guard, the shutdown and the kill target, the `npm` and `tsx` notes), the order of ingest and the reconciliation details, the grammar of the wikilink code with its `<...>` rule, and the list of which function folded onto which class. They stand but are not about the engine; they wait for a service design and an ingest design.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24PYZ40001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
