    "title": "00D250TTE0001",
    "text": "**The user agrees: the design states the rule the engine guarantees; today's gaps are filed as issues; Status notes the fact-check** (2026-10-12, user, answering [the recommendation](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D24ZD0QR001)): \"Yes.\" Orchestrator's reading of what follows: (1) the false and partly true statements of `design/core.md` are corrected so that each says what the engine guarantees, and only where the design or the user's decisions already settle the rule; where the right rule is a choice (whether sibling indexes are dense, whether a tombstoned node stays in its container's `children` or is emptied, what an id-like title does at load, whether `parent` is the lister's fact or a pair of its own) it goes to Open points with the options; (2) every gap between that rule and today's code is filed as an issue with the Coder's evidence, nothing fixed; (3) Status says the draft was fact-checked against the code and the mirror on 2026-10-12 and points to those issues; (4) the path rule stays as drafted (option (a), the live node at a path) with option (b) added to Open points as the alternative, because the user has not chosen between them; (5) the seven live artifacts that have no `parent` (six `README.md` files and `concepts.md`) are an open point of the planned derivation of the path from the parent chain, since for them the chain does not exist today; (6) Context lists its Discussion (`discussion/core.md`); (7) the issue `00D0W07DRR000` stays open until the user has read the document.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
