    ],
    "title": "00D252W7VG007",
    "text": "`applyTombstone` (`node.ts` line 850), `tombstoneLiveSubtree` (line 870, used by `aperas remove` and by the artifact removal at `artifacts.ts` line 278) and the folder removal (`folders.ts` lines 163 to 165) clear `children`, `links` and `props`. The files are `core/src/apeironNgn/` in the `Aperas/` checkout, where the reproductions below were run, and `core/src/shell/` in `Aperas.dev`, at the same lines.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D252W7VG006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D252W7VG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D252W7VG008",
    "text": "`tombstoneVacuousContainers` (`node.ts` line 2206, run at service start, at reload, at clobber and at shutdown) sets `tombstonedAt` alone, so the 40 nodes above keep their `props`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D252W7VG006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D252W7VG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Tested by the Coder on a scratch store (`/tmp/tomb.mts`)",
    "text": "Tested by the Coder on a scratch store (`/tmp/tomb.mts`): `tombstoneLiveSubtree` leaves `children`, `links` and `props` of the removed nodes empty and also removes the `parent` of every descendant, so a subtree removed by `aperas remove` leaves the removed root in its container's `children` and detaches the rest. The script is gone; the Coder wrote this reproduction and the one of the other site again on 2026-10-17, and both are now tests of the engine.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D252W7VG006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
