    "title": "Decided 2026-10-15 for the tombstones the mirror already holds",
    "text": "Decided 2026-10-15 for the tombstones the mirror already holds: the one-time migration strips them from the tree (each loses `children`, `links` and `props`, its `parent` and its entry in the `children` of its container, and keeps its literal properties), in [Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001). For the code that tombstones, the engine does it in [Batch 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014), done 2026-10-17 (see the entry at the end of this issue), and the callers in [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), where whether `tree --tombstoned` still shows a removed child is an open point.",
