    "title": "**Question — a moved child with no sibling index**",
    "text": "**Question — a moved child with no sibling index**: reading `writeField` (`node.ts` lines 242 to 250) suggests that when a reconcile moves a block from an old parent to a new one, and the new parent's `children` is written first, the old parent's later `children` write deletes the child's sibling index (line 244 deletes the indexes of every child it detaches, by subject), and the child stays under the new parent with no index, sorted as 0. The Coder did not run a reconcile with a move. What would decide: a scratch ingest of a document in which a block moves between two headings, then reading the indexes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D252Y7WR009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
