    "title": "**The kind of an embedded id**",
    "text": "**The kind of an embedded id**: `nodeKindFromId` (`vocab.ts` lines 47 to 52) matches only the fields `props` and `links`, so an id such as `Profile:x:preferences:StringProp:y` (the form `mintEmbedded` builds, `node.ts` line 167) is read as `Profile`. The design reads the kind from the last `field:Kind:` segment.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What counts as an id in a value**",
    "text": "**What counts as an id in a value**: `encodeDoc` (`store.ts` lines 100 to 104) with `isNodeRef` (`vocab.ts` lines 38 to 40) tests only the prefix `BlockNode:`, `ArtifactNode:`, `FolderNode:`, `Profile:` or `TreeView:` on every string value of every field. The two resolvers (`resolve.ts` lines 35 to 41 and `resolveCreate.ts` lines 45 to 49) are stricter: a valid snowflake must follow `Kind:`, and only for BlockNode, ArtifactNode and FolderNode.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2534RSR003",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2534RSG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2534RSR004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR004:props:StringProp:00D25354X0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR004:props:StringProp:00D25354X0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2534RSR004",
    "text": "Whether a real title or text can reach the load with such a prefix; the mirror has none today. The `text` of a block is a field of the same kind and goes through the same test, which the Coder did not try.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2534RSR005",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2534RSG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2534RSR006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR006:props:StringProp:00D25354X0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR006:props:StringProp:00D25354X0003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2534RSR006",
    "text": "None decided. What an id-like string does at load is an Open point of the design.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2534RSR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
