  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The store is read directly in places outside the helpers: `nodeExists`, the size, and the dev tools and tests**",
    "text": "**The store is read directly in places outside the helpers: `nodeExists`, the size, and the dev tools and tests**:  found 2026-10-12 by the Coder in the fact-check of the draft `design/core.md`. Filed 2026-10-12.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2536E1R002",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20000",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20005",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20007",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20009",
      "BlockNode:00D3YFA80R001",
      "BlockNode:00D4QJF658001",
      "BlockNode:00D7T5SAYG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R002:props:StringProp:00D2536SX0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R002:props:StringProp:00D2536SX0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2536E1R002",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2536E1R003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R003:props:StringProp:00D2536SX8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R003:props:StringProp:00D2536SX8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2536E1R003",
    "text": "The design's interface section says callers ask for a fixed list of reads and writes and nothing else; the code departs from it in three places, none of which gives a wrong result today.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2536E20000",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20001",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20002",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20003",
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20001:props:StringProp:00D2536SX8002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20001:props:StringProp:00D2536SX8003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2536E20001",
    "text": "`nodeExists` is in `vocab.ts` (lines 65 to 77) and calls `store.match` itself, not a helper of `storeAccess.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E20000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2536E20002",
    "text": "The quad count is read as `store.size` in `store.ts` (line 147).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E20000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2536E20003",
    "text": "The dev tools `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts`, `verifyLinkRefusals.ts` and `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts`, and the tests, call `store.match`, `add` and `delete` directly. The production code does not otherwise.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E20000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2536E20004",
    "text": "The wasm objects of these direct reads are freed by the helpers of `storeAccess.ts` for the production code; the dev tools and tests hold quads. `vocab.nodeExists` frees its own.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E20000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2536E20005",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20006:props:StringProp:00D2536SX8004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20006:props:StringProp:00D2536SXG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2536E20006",
    "text": "Whether the dev tools and tests should count as callers of the interface, or only the production code; the design does not say.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E20005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2536E20007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2536E20007",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2536E1R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2536E20008"
    ]
  },
  {
