    "title": "**Discussion**",
    "text": "**Discussion**: [Core — Discussion](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZE10001) — the freeflow record of the core engine: its scope and the sequencing of its issues, design and history.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D255WVK0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Ordered fields**",
    "text": "**Ordered fields**: a field can be declared ordered. Its forward side is then a list on its host: a set plus an order, so an item appears in it at most once. The port of an item is `host:item`, keyed by the item's own id, and the reverse of the item points at that port. The order is kept only in the live list: a reader that needs an item's place asks its port, which reads it from the host's list on demand. There is no sibling index and no order key, so an insertion or a move is one splice of the list and no reverse entry changes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D256098G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D256098G001:links:Link:00D3EN22PR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000S",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D256098G001:links:Link:00D3EN22PR000:props:StringProp:00D3F5A9NR000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "407"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**An id-like string at load**",
    "text": "**An id-like string at load**: what the load does with a string value that begins like an id, `Kind:` and more, but is not one, in a title, a text or any other field. The options are (a) the load applies the test of the resolvers, a valid snowflake after `Kind:`, so such a string stays a string and a reference is always a real id; (b) the load refuses the string and names the document and the field (see [An invalid id and a non-canonical integer](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000S)); (c) the mirror marks a reference in the file, so that a reference and a string differ by their format and not by their content, which changes the format of the mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2562RC8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2562RC8001:links:Link:00D2563440000",
