            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "815"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Where a node's parent comes from**",
    "text": "**Where a node's parent comes from**: the order of the children lives in the stored containment list of their container, whose positions are the order, so the list is not derived from the parent. Today's code extracts a sibling index for each child from the stored `children` at load, keeps it with the child's `parent`, and derives `children` from them afterwards; a file whose `parent` and `children` disagree loads as it stands ([the issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2538VKR001)). The engine keeps the order in the list itself and reads an item's place from its port (see [Ordered fields](#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001)). The mirror states containment twice, in the container's `children` and in the child's `parent`, redundantly, for clarity; when the two disagree, the shell's load applies its rule (see [A file whose `parent` and `children` disagree](#id/BlockNode:00D2PV8GC0001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D25686RR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
