    "title": "None in the data",
    "text": "None in the data: the real mirror has 0 dangling references (the Coder's boot measurement of the whole store, 10,622 nodes, gave 0 as well).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D258W098004",
    "text": "Were one to appear, a reference to a node that does not exist, the service would not say so. The Coder's scratch store showed a title \"BlockNode:zzz\" loading as a reference to a node that does not exist and reported as dangling in the result of the load, which is the only place the list reaches.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D258W098005",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D258W098006",
      "BlockNode:00D258W098007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098006:props:StringProp:00D258WCEG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098006:props:StringProp:00D258WCEG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D258W098006",
    "text": "`rehydrateStore` (`store.ts` lines 142 to 147) scans the store for object references (`allObjectRefIds`) and returns `danglingRefs`, sorted, in its result. A search of `monorepo/packages` finds readers of the field only in `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts` (lines 50 to 55), in the corpus support (`tests/support/corpus.ts`, `roundtripChild.ts`) and in the two round-trip tests. `service.ts` reads `duplicateIds` from the same result (lines 162 and 390) and logs it; it names `danglingRefs` nowhere.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D258W098007",
    "text": "The design says the load lists the ids that are referenced and never defined and returns the list to its caller, and that what is done with it belongs to the service lifecycle, which has no design yet.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D258W098008",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D258W098009",
      "BlockNode:00D258W09800A"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098009:props:StringProp:00D258WCEG002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W098009:props:StringProp:00D258WCEG003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D258W098009",
    "text": "What the service should do with the list (log it as it does a repeated id, refuse, or leave it to a check on demand); the design does not say.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D258W09800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D258W09800A",
    "text": "Whether the 97 ms second pass that builds the list is worth keeping if nothing reads it at run time; it is a part of the cost listed under the scans issue.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W098008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
