  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The thread-scope test sits in `core/apeironNgn`, inside the engine's directory, and not in the layer above it that the design says it belongs to**",
    "text": "**The thread-scope test sits in `core/apeironNgn`, inside the engine's directory, and not in the layer above it that the design says it belongs to**: found 2026-10-12 by the Coder in the fact-check of the draft `design/core.md`, among the findings the orchestrator asked to file. Filed 2026-10-12.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2590B2R002",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30001",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30005",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30008",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B3000A",
      "BlockNode:00D6HBTYA8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R002:props:StringProp:00D2590Q58000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R002:props:StringProp:00D2590Q58001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2590B2R002",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2590B2R003",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R003:props:StringProp:00D2590Q58002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R003:props:StringProp:00D2590Q58003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "No wrong result",
    "text": "No wrong result: the split by scope is stable on the real mirror (the Coder's round trip gave 4,818 + 2,988 blocks, 55 + 2 artifacts and 16 + 1 folders, content mirror and `.state/`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2590B30000",
    "text": "The design says the scope test belongs to the layer above the engine and that the engine supplies the ids of each kind. In the code the test is `isThreadScopedId` of `threadScope.ts` in `monorepo/packages/core/src/apeironNgn/`, called by the engine's own write-back (`dehydrate.ts` lines 104 and 136) and by the service (`service.ts` line 313, the thread size cap).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2590B30001",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30002",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30003",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30002:props:StringProp:00D2590Q58004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30002:props:StringProp:00D2590Q58005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "The header of `threadScope.ts` says why the module sits there",
    "text": "The header of `threadScope.ts` says why the module sits there: it is a raw-quad twin of the owner walk of `linkIntegrity.ts`, and it must stay importable from `dehydrate.ts`, which `node.ts` and `linkIntegrity.ts` already import, so that nothing cycles. It depends only on `vocab.ts` and the helpers of `storeAccess.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B30001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The rule it applies",
    "text": "The rule it applies: an artifact or a folder is in scope when its own `path` is `.threads` or begins with `.threads/`; a block is in scope when the artifact or folder found by climbing its `parent` chain is; a block with no `parent` is never in scope; `Profile`, `Link`, `StringProp` and `TreeView` never are.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B30001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2590B30004",
    "text": "`firstLiteralOf` and `firstRefIriOf` of the helpers have no other caller than this module (the Coder's reading of the interface).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B30001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2590B30005",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30006",
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30006:props:StringProp:00D2590Q5G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30006:props:StringProp:00D2590Q5G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "What moving it would touch",
    "text": "What moving it would touch: `dehydrate.ts` would have to receive the test or the two sets of ids from outside, and the design does not say in which form the layer above hands it back.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B30005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2590B30007",
    "text": "Whether the design's sentence is a target for the code or the sentence should say that the test lives with the write-back; neither was tried.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B30005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2590B30008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2590B30008",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2590B2R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2590B30009"
    ]
  },
