      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR002:props:StringProp:00D2PCFSQR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PCFDBR002",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR003",
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR004",
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR005",
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR003:props:StringProp:00D2PCFSQR002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR003:props:StringProp:00D2PCFSR0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PCFDBR003",
    "text": "After the service stops, by the idle shutdown of 30 minutes or by any other stop, every command is refused with \"No ApeironNgn service running. Start one with: aperas service start\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR004:links:Link:00D2PCFSRR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR004:links:Link:00D2PCFSRR000:props:StringProp:00D2PCFSRR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "87"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PCFDBR004",
    "text": "The same refusal is given while the service is up and busy and does not answer a ping ([the entry on a refusal while the service is up](#id/BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001)). An agent cannot tell a stopped service, which it must start, from a busy one, which it must wait for, so it reports a crash or waits for a service that is not there.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The CLI does not start the service by itself",
    "text": "The CLI does not start the service by itself: `aperas service start` is the only place that does.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PCFDBR006",
    "text": "The Coder's turn of 2026-10-12 began at about 14:15Z and its first `aperas` calls worked; its `Edit` of `Apeiron/README.md` then waited on a permission prompt for over 30 minutes with no `aperas` command (the turn lasted about 13.7 hours of wall time), and after the answer every call was refused.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PCFDC0000",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0001",
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0002",
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0001:props:StringProp:00D2PCFSR0001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0001:props:StringProp:00D2PCFSR0002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PCFDC0001",
    "text": "`service.ts` sets an idle timer of 30 minutes (`IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS`, line 99), and `resetIdleTimer` (around line 433) ends the service by a plain `shutdown(0)`, which writes no log line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PCFDC0002",
    "text": "`ensureServiceRunning` (`serviceClient.ts`, line 151) throws the one message whenever `ping()` fails, whatever the reason, and its comment says it never starts a service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "Evidence of the stop",
    "text": "Evidence of the stop: the run directory, where the service removes its socket and lock when it stops, last changed at 14:51Z on 2026-10-12, and the log's last line is 14:13Z, so the stop came about 30 minutes after the last command.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PCFDC0004",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PCFDBR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2PCFDC0005"
    ]
  },
  {
