    ],
    "title": "00D2PVVMWG002",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG003",
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR000",
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG003:props:StringProp:00D2PVW278002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG003:props:StringProp:00D2PVW278003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PVVMWG003",
    "text": "A move run from a harness whose standard input is an open pipe does not finish:  the command ran for 120 seconds and the harness moved it to the background. The same move run again with standard input from `/dev/null` finished at once, and the first process stayed blocked on standard input and was left running.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "No wrong result and no fault of the service",
    "text": "No wrong result and no fault of the service:  the wait is in the client, before the request is sent.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR001",
    "text": "The `aperas` skill's quick reference (\"no stdin moves node\"), the `aperas-grapher` skill (\"with no stdin\") and the mechanics reference say the move takes no standard input, and none says that standard input must be closed when the command is run from a harness that leaves it open.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR002",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR003",
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR003:props:StringProp:00D2PVW27G000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR003:props:StringProp:00D2PVW27G001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR003",
    "text": "`readStdinIfPiped` in `monorepo/packages/cli/src/kgInsert.ts` (line 241) returns at once only when `process.stdin.isTTY` is true; otherwise it reads the stream to its end and takes an empty read as \"nothing was piped\", which selects the move.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR004",
    "text": "Its comment says why a test of `isTTY` alone is not enough:  a harness with no terminal reads `isTTY` as false, and a bare `insert` was then taken for a create with empty content. The read to the end was chosen as the signal, and it needs the stream to end; a stream that stays open never ends.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR005",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR006",
      "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR007"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR006:props:StringProp:00D2PVW27G002",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR006:props:StringProp:00D2PVW27G003",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR006",
    "text": "Whether a harness other than the one that ran the move behaves the same:  a harness that closes standard input for each command would not wait.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D2PVVMWR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D2PVVMWR007",
    "text": "Whether any other command that reads standard input waits the same way; only the move was run.",
