    "title": "00D2PW0S50001",
    "text": "**The user: in active design, do not update the design each turn** (2026-10-13, user, after [the correction on the multi-graph content](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PVH8PR001)): \"Because we're in active design, don't update design each turn like that!\" Orchestrator's reading: from now on a settled decision is recorded in Freeflow and kept in a short list of decisions not yet in the design; `design/core.md` is changed only when the user asks, in one batch; filing of defects as issues stays immediate (it is not a design update). The running Grapher turn (Turn 5) was told to stop editing the design beyond what it had written, to leave the document consistent, to finish the issue for the move that waits on standard input, and to list in its Report the design blocks it changed and the parts of the Ask it left undone. Decisions settled and not yet in the design, for a batch the user approves: the layout is a record per subject (rationale: modularity; the multi-graph design is separate); a repeated add of a present pair changes nothing (property), `children` derived, reverse buckets as sets (already written in Turn 4); the Open point on a file whose `parent` and `children` disagree; the lazy-reverse example (not yet approved); the path rule (a) and the removal rule (not yet confirmed). Saved as a memory (design updates in batches).",
