    ],
    "title": "**A partition hierarchy**",
    "text": "**A partition hierarchy**: a field can serve as the hierarchy of a split only if it is marked partitioning (see [Partitioning fields](#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)), so that every pair falls into exactly one port. The mark is set in the schema (see [Partitioning fields](#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)), and the engine refuses every write that would give a node a second value on the climbed side or close a cycle; the climbed side follows from the field's cardinality, with no direction on the mark. For IS-A, where a tag may have several supertags, the data keeps the many-valued relation for its meaning and adds a single-valued primary-supertag field, which is the tree the partition follows, climbed forward from a tag to its primary supertag by its cardinality; a secondary supertag edge is marked as such when it is written, and the partition ignores it, so nothing is trimmed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
