    "title": "**Captured port views**",
    "text": "**Captured port views**: the engine shows the port tree of a bucket as it currently is, and the shell can capture it as a view, which stays still while the engine's own ports go on changing. A captured port view keeps only the shape, the boundary node of each port; its contents are recomputed from the current pairs whenever it is used, and the engine answers through it by merging its own finer ports or sorting a coarser one on the fly. It is a kind of view of its own, distinct from the shell's views (`TreeView` in the Aperas schema); the shell keeps it on disk (see [Files](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01X)), and it is removed only by hand, as it was captured by hand. What it is called is an Open point (see [The name of a captured port view](#id/BlockNode:00D2T6X3CG001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR015",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
