    "title": "**The edge layout**",
    "text": "**The edge layout**: Oxigraph holds every field of every document as a quad (`encodeDoc`), a node object holds only the store and its id, and every field read is one bound match and a decode; a lookup by value goes through the predicate-object index, and a list of the ids of a kind is a match over the whole store. The store pays a lookup for each property read, and most of them find nothing: at one flush on a copy of the mirror the Coder's census counted 7,276 reads of `holder`, 7,274 of them empty, and 7,276 reads of `links`, 5,769 of them empty (one flush; [the cost of a write](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001)). One insert made about 170 thousand bound lookups at about 9 microseconds each ([the path index](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJG004); 6 inserts in 3 fresh processes for each of two artifacts), and the timed flush after it made four full scans that materialised 334,075 quads ([the timed flush](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJG006); 3 profiles).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D39EQJY0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
