            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "513"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The wasm boundary**",
    "text": "**The wasm boundary**: it is not part of RDF, but it multiplies the cost of the edge layout. Each crossing pays for the wrapper objects of a quad and its terms, their decoding and their release, and the edge layout sets the number of crossings at one for each property read, where a node layout behind the same boundary would cross once for each node. Before `free()`, eight lists of the ids of a kind grew resident memory by 40 MB a call, and a dehydrate of both mirrors took 33 to 38 s; after it, 2.5 to 3.8 s ([the `free()` landing](#id/BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG003); 59,275 quads, 3 samples per case, a fresh process each). A scratch plain JavaScript store of the Coder's with the same triple layout (prototype B) rehydrated a copy of about 60 thousand quads in 174 ms against 2,050 ms for Oxigraph and dehydrated it in 530 ms against 2,500 ms, with about 14 MB of heap against about 107 MB of heap and wasm, and the eight output files byte-identical (one run, 2026-10-12).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
