    "title": "**The algorithms of a write**",
    "text": "**The algorithms of a write**: a small local change recomputes what follows the corpus and not the change, and a faster engine makes each lookup cheaper but not fewer, so these costs are fixed in the code whatever the engine; all are filed in [the cost of a write](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001) and [the full-store scans](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001). The path-collision check rebuilds the slug path of every live block for one inserted paragraph, a median of 1,527 to 1,556 ms on a copy of 7,433 live blocks, and recomputes the path of a shared ancestor once for every block below it; two link sweeps of the target artifact parse the text of every block, 831 and 780 ms on a 5,200-line document and 24 and 18 ms on a 37-line one (6 inserts in 3 fresh processes for each artifact); the timed flush within 10 s of a write rewrites all four content files, a median of 1,401 ms (6 flushes); at each flush the thread-scope test climbs every block to its owner, 14,368 path reads in one flush (the census, one flush) and 847 ms of the flush (3 profiles); and every list of the ids of a kind is a scan of the whole store, paid at each call.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D39EVFH8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D39EVFH8001",
    "text": "**The path check recomputes shared ancestors** (added 2026-10-14, read in the code by the orchestrator): `toPath` climbs from each block to its artifact on its own, so the slug path of an ancestor shared by many blocks is recomputed once for every block below it, within the one rebuild of the index that each write makes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22Z1HJG003",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
