    "title": "**The sweep**",
    "text": "**The sweep**: a tombstone is deleted outright once no reference from a node reachable from the roots points at it: a mark from every live node of the root kinds that the schema marks, through the fields that the schema marks for the sweep to follow (in the Aperas schema, every live `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode`, through `children` and the targets of links), and a sweep of every tombstone left unmarked. A dead island of nodes that point only at each other goes too, which a count of incoming references would keep alive. A sweep deals within one graph: the mark and the sweep read only the graph it names, so a live node of another graph does not keep a tombstone alive (see [Reads and rules across graphs](#id/BlockNode:00D5AYGHJ0001)). When the sweep runs belongs to the service lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
