    "title": "**Dropping a graph**",
    "text": "**Dropping a graph**: a graph can be dropped only if no pair from the remaining graphs points into it, and on dropping it the engine removes its records from the master map and its outgoing pairs from the reverse records of the nodes that remain. The check reads across graphs (see [Reads and rules across graphs](#id/BlockNode:00D5AYGHJ0001)). The graph of the views, `treeviews`, is never refused, since nothing points into it (see [Addressing](#id/BlockNode:00D5AYBPWR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
