    "title": "**Ports, the two ends of a pair**",
    "text": "**Ports, the two ends of a pair**: a port is a sub-address of a node that continues its deep path. A pair joins an outgoing port of its subject, such as an embedded node that holds a reference (a `Link` in the Aperas schema) or an item's place in an ordered list, to an incoming port of its object, the partition of its reverse side where the entry lands (see [Ports](#id/BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001)). \"Port\" is one notion with these two ends.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001:links:Link:00D3EKW7T0000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D2T5XBH0001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001:links:Link:00D3EKW7T0000:props:StringProp:00D5AYYPK8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "839"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Partitioning fields**",
    "text": "**Partitioning fields**: a field can be marked partitioning in the schema, closed at construction and never at run time, and the engine ensures the mark: each node has at most one value on the side that is climbed, and the relation has no cycle. The mark names no direction; the engine derives the climb from the field's cardinality. A single-valued field (`one` or `optional`) is climbed forward, from a node to its value, and its cardinality already bounds each node to at most one value on that side. A many-valued field is climbed on its reverse side, from a node to the subjects whose field holds it, and there the engine checks that a node has one subject at most (containment is such a field: a node is in one container's list). The cycle check follows the climb. The ports use a partitioning field as the hierarchy of a split (see [A partition hierarchy](#id/BlockNode:00D2T5XBH0001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
