    "title": "**The boundary**",
    "text": "**The boundary**: the engine manages, in memory, the records of the nodes and the forward and reverse sides of their reference and embed fields, with their ports, the ordered and partitioning fields, the tombstones and several graphs, under the schema it is given (see [The meta-model](#id/BlockNode:00D4MYZ6Q0000)). The shell is the part that calls the engine ([the shell](#id/BlockNode:00D4M7YEZG001)). Dehydrating the records to disk and rehydrating them are the shell's: the mirror, its format, the load, the flush and the maps for lookups by a literal value make up the shell's persistence, which builds the engine's graphs and reads them out through the engine's [persistence API](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001). The code follows the boundary in its folders: `monorepo/packages/core/src/apeironNgn/` is the engine, in memory, `monorepo/packages/core/src/shell/` is the shell, on disk, and the engine's directory imports only files inside it: no `node:` module and no package at all, so nothing of the shell, no file system and no store library. This document follows the boundary: the engine, in memory, then the shell, on disk.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
