            "@id": "BlockNode:00D3DVKXP8000:links:Link:00D3DVMAJG000:props:StringProp:00D3DVMAJG001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "111"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D3DVKXP8000",
    "text": "**The user asks what the Grapher's four judgment calls are** (2026-10-14, user). Orchestrator listed them from [the Turn 8 verification](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CQ83DG001), in plain terms, for the user to accept or reverse: (1) the statement \"the engine has no notion of live; callers decide it from `tombstonedAt`\" was removed, because the user decided the engine manages tombstones; (2) three blocks still say a node's record follows the shape of its mirror document so a flush is a dump, settled before the boundary moved, kept because the question whether it stays as a contract with the caller was not answered; (3) option (b), tombstoning clears the path, was dropped from the Open point on how a path names one node, because a tombstone keeps its literal properties; (4) two writes were added to the engine's interface, splicing an ordered field and tombstoning a node, restating the user's decisions without being asked.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3DYNPH8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3DYNPH8001:links:Link:00D3DYP398000",
