    ],
    "title": "00D3E2D530001",
    "text": "**The user keeps the path Open point open until it becomes moot, and asks what the sorting statement fix is** (2026-10-14, user, on [the path question](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D3DYNPH8001)): \"Let it open till it'll become moot (`path` removed). Why bothering a thing that will be moot anyway?!\" Settled: the Open point on how a path names one node stays open, with its marked rule (a), until the stored `path` is removed. On the sorting fix, the orchestrator showed the block `BlockNode:00D24N87SR01G` as it reads and a proposed wording carrying the settled rules (orders kept on each write, code-point comparison, the caller bridging any gap).",
