        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The user: apply** (2026-10-14, user",
    "text": "**The user: apply** (2026-10-14, user: \"apply.\"), on [the details](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D3EZWV70001): the 23 defaults of the belonging review and the six proposals for the Grapher's questions, as the orchestrator listed them in the chat, go out as one Grapher turn: keep the four settled statements (Status with its fact-check and issue links, the rationale's evidence links, the wording of where a node's parent comes from, the flush as a dump with partitioning later, and the plan to derive the path); drop from the design the sentences about today's code whose issues are filed, the statements of today's data, the remark on Oxigraph's stores, \"the key of a node is not written\" and \"it has no design of its own yet\"; replace today's function names in the interface's reads and writes with plain descriptions; move to history the agreement of the cardinalities with the mirror, the earlier engine's behaviour and refusal, and the comparison of engines as sets; move to issues the parentless artifacts, the live-id callers and the unchecked canonical-render order; link the four \"(see Tombstones)\" to the heading; state that the caller sorts the values of reference set fields at a dump; add that dropping a graph removes its records from the master map; align the interface's repeated add with the index (a property, not a promise); move Turn 8's go note back beside its origin.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
