    "title": "00D3F7C3EG001",
    "text": "Promoted as the fifth batch into [Core — Design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR001), with the sentences on today's code, today's data and the session dropped, the reads and writes of the interface described without today's function names, [Orders in the mirror](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01G) and [Dropping a graph](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8004) completed and the four \"(see Tombstones)\" linked to [the heading](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8000); into the history as [Checked against the mirror](../history/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3F6FTB0001), [Behaviour it gave without being asked](../history/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3F6J4JG001) and the comparison as sets in [the milestone of 2026-10-12](../history/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D21FP4ZG009); and into the issues as [Seven live artifacts have no `parent`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3F6RJCG001), [the callers of all ids of a kind](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3F6ZYWG001) and [the canonical-render order](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3F741JR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3F8D2W8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3F8D2W8001",
    "text": "**Verification — the belonging review applied (`design-core-draft` Turn 10, Report `BlockNode:00D3F7VHA8009`)** (2026-10-14, orchestrator): `design/core.md` has 127 live blocks, one mark (the path rule (a)), no figure, one \"Today\" left (in where a node's parent comes from, kept as the user asked) and \"Oxigraph\" only in the Context's description of the history; `aperas check-links` is clean; three facts moved to `history/core.md`; a new issue `00D3F6RJCG001` for the seven live artifacts with no `parent`; the live-id callers and the canonical-render order added to filed issues. Trial rule for \"Modify Shared Resources\": no refusal this turn; both block removals passed on the first try (one data point). The Grapher's questions: (1) the Enforcement Open point (`00D24N87T000M`) was in its review but missing from the orchestrator's table, an omission of the orchestrator's; it is an open question whose references to today's paths and tests are links to filed issues, so the orchestrator proposes to keep it; (2) Turn 9's go note sits away from its origin: move it back, as for Turn 8; (3) two pieces of wording point at text dropped this turn: the Open point on how a path names one node still calls a first-match lookup a defect, and an issue's Symptom (`00D253D680005`) quotes the dropped design sentence on the `type` an ingest sets: proposed to drop the first and reword the second to state the fact without quoting the design.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WJRR60001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3WJRR60001",
    "text": "**The user's comments on six design blocks, settled; and whether the Coder missed the obsolete abstract** (2026-10-15, user, reading `design/core.md`). (1) `BlockNode:00D24N87SR010`: \"The text of an artifact or a folder is a copied abstract (the text of its first descendant that has any)\" is obsolete: \"Today's text is from the frontmatter. The Coder missed this gap in its verification, didn't it?\" Orchestrator, from the Coder's fact-check and the code: the Coder marked the block TRUE after comparing stored values (of 74 live artifacts and folders, 50 hold a text equal to their first descendant's); that is still the stored value, but its role changed in the frontmatter redesign of 2026-09-20 (comments in `node.ts` at the ingest and the render): the abstract a reader sees is the frontmatter `description`, and the stored `text` of an artifact or folder is kept only as a fingerprint for detecting a rename; the Coder checked the value and not its role, and the orchestrator's Ask asked only for truth against code and mirror, so the miss is shared, the same pattern as the `key` sentence. Asked of the user: whether the design should mention the fingerprint at all, or only that the abstract is the frontmatter `description`. (2) `BlockNode:00D24N87SR011`: a link's \"predicate\" is a legacy of RDF triples: remove the dummy `[[wikilink]]` predicate and the `references` predicate (no manual links have been created); the various types of links will be given in another linking design using containment instead of a predicate, continuing the retraction of \"edges\" into direct links whose metadata sits in the content of the linking block; move the edge class (`BlockNode:00D24N87SR014`) to history. (3) `BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001`: its \"partitioning field\" should link to `BlockNode:00D2T5XBH0001` or `BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001`. (4) `BlockNode:00D24N87SR019`: \"a write of a field clears the field\" is ambiguous (one node's pairs or the field across all nodes); reword precisely: writing a field of a node updates that node's pairs of that field. (5) `BlockNode:00D24N87SR01B` (Layout): give `BlockNode:00D39EJSZ8001` (Why a node-based engine) as its rationale. (6) `BlockNode:00D24N87SR01R`: the stray \"(proposal, not agreed)\" item: the literal field `path` must be gone soon, so it is not kept in the design: move it to history. Filing, since filing is a must: the code still writes a `predicate` on every link, against the design without one. Riding with this turn, as corrections of the last turn rather than design decisions: Turn 9's go note moved back beside its origin, and the two wordings that point at text dropped in Turn 10 (the path Open point calling a first-match lookup a defect; the Symptom `00D253D680005` quoting the dropped design sentence on the `type` an ingest sets) fixed; the Enforcement Open point stays as it is.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WKN8P0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3WKN8P0001",
    "text": "**The user: the root is set at `aperas.config.json` `graph.artifacts`** (2026-10-15, user, on `BlockNode:00D25698B0001`, the Open point on deriving the path). Orchestrator, after reading the config and the mirror: yes: `graph.artifacts` is `./artifacts`, relative to the graph repo; the root folder (`FolderNode:00CDBYV47G000`, title \"Artifacts\", stored path `.`) stands for that directory, so its place comes from the config and needs no stored path; the Open point's \"the root folder has none by definition\" is then no exception at all. What remains are the seven live artifacts with no `parent` (`README.md` at the root and in `design`, `discussion`, `issues`, `planning` and `history`, and `concepts.md`): none of them is listed in any folder's `children` either, so they hang outside the tree; option (a) of the Open point, giving each the folder that holds it as its parent, would close the point. Not decided; no design change until the user settles it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Every `Link` carries a `predicate`, which the design of a `Link` no longer has**",
    "text": "**Every `Link` carries a `predicate`, which the design of a `Link` no longer has**: found 2026-10-15, when the user removed the predicate of a `Link` from `design/core.md`; counted the same day by the Grapher. Filed 2026-10-15.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG002",
      "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPR001",
