    "title": "00D3WNBPPG003",
    "text": "In the mirror files (the tracked files of `Apeiron/` and `Apeiron/.state/`), counted 2026-10-15 with `jq` on a clone, every embedded `Link` has a `predicate`, and every one of them is `[[wikilink]]`: 2,157 in `Apeiron/` (2,155 owned by a `BlockNode` and 2 by an `ArtifactNode`; 2,152 targets are `BlockNode`s, 5 are `ArtifactNode`s, none is undefined) and 1,510 in `Apeiron/.state/`. None is `references` and none lacks a `predicate`. Every `Link` has `props` holding a `position` and nothing else. The `predicate` of `Link` is the only key outside the declared shapes on any node of the mirror (`ArtifactNode`, `BlockNode`, `FolderNode`, `Profile` and `StringProp` have none). No manual link exists as a record: `aperas link` and `kg:link` occur only as prose, in three blocks of `Apeiron/`. The count is of one moment, since the mirror gains a `Link` with each block that holds a wikilink, and it is of the files as last flushed, not of the store in memory.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The code writes a predicate on every `Link` it makes",
    "text": "The code writes a predicate on every `Link` it makes: `[[wikilink]]` for a wikilink (`WIKILINK_PREDICATE` of `@aperas/core/astParser`) and `references` for a manual link (`addLink('references', ...)` in `kgLink.ts`, whose removal of a manual link also filters on that predicate). Tests in `tests/links/`, `tests/ingest/` and `tests/gc/` write `references` links and filter on both values. Found by a search of the code, not traced.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPR001",
