    ],
    "title": "00D3WNXHQG001",
    "text": "**The user: an artifact's stored `text` as a rename fingerprint is a leftover, not intended; file an issue; the `text` should come from the frontmatter and serve the rename check** (2026-10-15, user, on [the abstract's role](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WJRR60001)): \"I think it was a legacy left over, not intended design. Let's file an issue to fix it. The `text` should be used to check rename but not a left over one, always use the frontmatter.\" Orchestrator's reading, for the user to confirm: the `text` of an artifact or a folder is set from its frontmatter `description`, always, never from its first descendant; the rename check compares that `text`; today's code stores the first descendant's text as `text` and uses it only as a rename fingerprint (`node.ts`, the ingest and the render comments of the 2026-09-20 redesign), which is the gap to file. A question for the issue: an artifact with no `description` then has no `text`, so the rename check needs another basis for it (for example its body), or such an artifact is matched on its path only. Queued: the issue and the design statement, for the next Grapher turn after the running one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WPJK8G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3WPJK8G001",
    "text": "**Verification — six design comments applied (`design-core-draft` Turn 11, Report `BlockNode:00D3WP51E0006`)** (2026-10-15, orchestrator): `design/core.md` has 125 live blocks and no \"(proposal, not agreed)\" mark left; `[[wikilink]]` is gone; \"predicate\" remains only in the RDF terms of the data model, in the links block saying types will not come from a predicate, in an issue title cited by Context, and in the Enforcement point's mention of test predicates; `aperas check-links` clean; staged. The edge class and the path block moved to history with their ids; issue `00D3WNBPPG001` filed for the predicate every link still carries (the mirror's links all carry `[[wikilink]]`, none `references`). Trial rule: no refusal again. The Grapher's questions, with the orchestrator's proposals: (1) add a dated history entry saying the two blocks left the design on 2026-10-15: yes; (2) reword `00D24N87SR01S` and `00D25698B0001`, which still quote \"a path names one live node\": yes; (3) the Open point `00D24N87T000P` speaks of \"a manual link\", and the links block keeps the title \"Links are embedded edges\" although edges went to history: for the user (a proposed title: \"Links are outgoing ports\", after the user's port model); (4) move Turn 10's go note back beside its origin: yes. Queued with them: the issue on an artifact's `text` (from the frontmatter, for the rename check) and its design statement.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WPXX6G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
