        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D3WPXX6G001",
    "text": "**The user: the `README.md` files are the organic part of their `FolderNode`, not artifacts hanging outside the tree; the orchestrator missed that design** (2026-10-15, user, on [the root answer](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WKN8P0001)). The orchestrator's mistake: it counted the six `README.md` among \"parentless artifacts\" to be attached, although `shape.ts` says a folder's README content lives directly in the folder's own children. Checked in the mirror: each folder holds one `BlockNode` child with its README's content, beside its artifacts and subfolders, and the folder's `text` is that README's abstract (`design`: one block and ten artifacts; `issues`: one block and eleven artifacts; the root: one block and seven folders). Besides that, six live `ArtifactNode`s exist for the same files (`README.md`, `design/README.md` and the others), each with one child of its own, outside any folder: duplicates of what the folders already hold; how they were made is not traced (a track of every `.md` on disk would do it). So the corrected picture: the six `README.md` nodes are strays to file as an issue (and to remove after the user's go), not artifacts to attach; `concepts.md` is the only real artifact without a parent, which belongs under the root folder. The Open point on deriving the path changes accordingly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
