    "title": "00D3WS45H0001",
    "text": "**Settled by the user: the links block is titled \"Links are outgoing ports\"** (2026-10-15, user: \"OK.\", on [the Turn 11 verification](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WPJK8G001)). The next Grapher turn carries it with the items already settled or due: the two issues (the six stray `README.md` nodes; an artifact's `text` from the first descendant instead of the frontmatter), the design statement on an artifact's `text`, the corrected Open point on deriving the path (the `README.md` files are the organic part of their folder; the root's place is the config's `graph.artifacts`; `concepts.md` the one artifact without a parent), the matching wording of the \"manual link\" Open point, a dated history entry for the two blocks that left the design, the two blocks still quoting \"a path names one live node\" reworded, and Turn 10's go note moved back beside its origin.",
