    "title": "00D3WV3CZ0003",
    "text": "The stored `text` of an `ArtifactNode` or a `FolderNode` is a copy of the text of its first descendant that has any, and its one remaining use is as a fingerprint for detecting a rename; the abstract a reader sees has been the frontmatter `description` since the redesign of 2026-09-20. The design gives the `text` from the `description`, as the value the rename check compares (see [The artifact is its own root document](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR010)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WV3CZ0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WV3CZ8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "In the mirror files read 2026-10-15",
    "text": "In the mirror files read 2026-10-15: of 54 live `ArtifactNode`s, 53 carry a `description` and none has a `text` equal to it, while 48 have a `text` equal to the text of one of their own blocks; of 16 live `FolderNode`s, 6 carry a `description`, none equal to its `text`. Counted on the mirror files as last flushed, not on the store in memory.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WV3CZ0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WV3CZ8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3WV3CZ8001",
    "text": "Where the code sets the `text` and where the rename check reads it (by the orchestrator's reading, the comments in `node.ts` at the ingest and the render) is not traced.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WV3CZ0002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
