    "title": "Promoted as the seventh batch into [Core — Design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR001)",
    "text": "Promoted as the seventh batch into [Core — Design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR001): [The artifact is its own root document](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR010) (the `text` from the frontmatter `description`, compared by the rename check), [Links are outgoing ports](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR011) (retitled), [The path is derived from the parent chain](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01S), and the Open points [The order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P) and [Deriving the path](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25698B0001); into the history as [the entry of 2026-10-15](../history/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WV5V48001) for the two statements that left the design; into the issues as [the six `README.md` artifacts](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WTZG9G001) and [the stored `text` of an artifact](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WV3CZ0001); and Turn 10's go note moved back beside its origin.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WW90N0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Verification — Turn 12 of `design-core-draft` (Report `BlockNode:00D3WVYKKG008`)** (2026-10-15, orchestrator)",
    "text": "**Verification — Turn 12 of `design-core-draft` (Report `BlockNode:00D3WVYKKG008`)** (2026-10-15, orchestrator): two issues filed (`00D3WTZG9G001`, the six stray `README.md` nodes; `00D3WV3CZ0001`, an artifact's `text` from the first descendant instead of the frontmatter `description`); the design carries the `text` rule, the title \"Links are outgoing ports\", the corrected Open points on deriving the path and on types of links; the dated history entry `00D3WV5V48001`; Turn 10's go note back beside its origin; nothing removed, no issue resolved, no write refused (a third data point for the retry rule), `aperas check-links` clean. The Grapher caught and fixed its own draft that presented the orchestrator's paraphrase as the user's words. Its two questions, with the orchestrator's proposals: reword the third design block still quoting \"a path names one live node\" (`00D24N87T000R`); reword the older issue `00D3F6RJCG001` (\"seven live artifacts have no `parent`\") to the corrected picture (six stray `README.md` nodes, filed separately, and `concepts.md`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WY2QZR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Wrap-up of the design drafting of `design/core.md`** (2026-10-15, user",
    "text": "**Wrap-up of the design drafting of `design/core.md`** (2026-10-15, user: \"No next turn, this is the last turn of the design drafting. Let's wrap everything up.\"). The draft stands in `design/core.md` in four parts (purpose and scope with the boundary and the rationale of a node-based engine; the engine, in memory; the caller, on disk; open points), with no \"(proposal, not agreed)\" mark left, `aperas check-links` clean, and the graph staged on `main` of the graph repo; the code repo (branch `js-apeironngn`) has no change. Left open on purpose, for later work, not lost: the two last corrections the Grapher raised and the user did not order (the design block `00D24N87T000R` still quotes \"a path names one live node\"; the issue `00D3F6RJCG001` still counts the six `README.md` nodes among artifacts needing a parent, now filed separately as `00D3WTZG9G001`); the Open points of the design (among them the stored path, `concepts.md` without a parent, enforcement, existence, the captured view's name); the separate designs the user named (multi-graph modularity, a linking design for types of links through containment, the service lifecycle); the issues filed in this stretch for today's code (the cost of a write and the path check, tombstoning, sibling indexes, the kind of an id, direct store reads, `danglingRefs`, the thread-scope test, `ownerOfLink`, repeated ids, the locale sort, the predicate on links, the stray `README.md` nodes, an artifact's `text`, a stopped service's message, the move waiting on standard input); the build of the JS engine on `js-apeironngn`. Standing rules from this stretch, kept as memories: design updates only for settled decisions, in batches, settled meaning the user's consensus; a stopped service is started by whoever finds it; a \"Modify Shared Resources\" refusal of approved graph work is retried once after a short wait (a trial: no refusal came in the three turns since). Housekeeping: a vim swap file of the config (`.aperas.config.json.swp`) had been staged by a `git add -A` and was taken out of the index.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3WZHJ50001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3WZHJ50001",
    "text": "**The user corrects the wrap-up: the next Grapher turn is the last of the design drafting, and everything remaining goes into it; asks what else should be done** (2026-10-15, user). The orchestrator's list, for the user to confirm: (1) the two corrections left open (`00D24N87T000R`; the issue `00D3F6RJCG001`); (2) the \"Promoted to\" note for the removal of the `key` block, which the orchestrator ran itself; (3) the issue `00D0W07DRR000` (`design/` has no document for the store) marked resolved by `design/core.md`, since the user has read and corrected the document; (4) the design's Status: drafted through 2026-10-15, its Open points listed as the remaining work; (5) a milestone in `history/core.md` for the draft of `design/core.md` (2026-10-12 to 2026-10-15) and its Current Status brought up to date; (6) a pointer from `discussion/core.md`, which the design's Context names as its discussion, to this session's Freeflow heading in `discussion/aperas-skill.md`, where the design was actually discussed; (7) the finishing notes in the threads: the tasks `design-core-draft`, `js-apeironngn-survey`, `write-cost-profile` and `store-access-free` marked done, with what remains; no pruning; (8) projection, `aperas check-links`, staging. Not proposed: `concepts.md` (not designed yet), skill changes (the retry rule is still on trial).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0V83SF8001",
    "type": "paragraph",
    "children": []
  },
