      }
    ],
    "title": "**The boundary between engine and caller**",
    "text": "**The boundary between engine and caller**: the engine manages, in memory, the records, the forward and reverse sides of reference and embed fields with their ports, the ordered and partitioning fields, the tombstones and several graphs; the mirror, its format, the load, the flush and the maps for lookups by a literal value are its caller's (see [The boundary](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJFB7G001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3X4321G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
