    "title": "**Ordered and partitioning fields**",
    "text": "**Ordered and partitioning fields**: an ordered field is a list on its host, with no sibling index, so an insertion or a move is one splice of the list; a partitioning field gives each node at most one value on the climbed side and has no cycle; containment, the field `children`, is both (see [Ordered fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001) and [Partitioning fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3X4321G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
