    "title": "**Lazy reverse with ports**",
    "text": "**Lazy reverse with ports**: the reverse of a field is built the first time the field is asked in reverse and kept up to date by every write afterwards, held on the records of the objects; a bucket over its field's cap is split into ports along a partitioning field (see [Reverse, for each field, built on first use](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR017) and [Ports](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001)).",
