  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XP9A18001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "### Verification of Batch 1 and Batch 2",
    "text": "A fix isn't done until its Open Issues entry can honestly move to Resolved with the actual mechanism named, matching this concern's own citation-direction discipline against guessing. Batch 1 verified live against direct reproductions built for each mechanism (a tombstone-interleaved list push, a same-batch multi-file ingest failure, a scratch holder-promotion chain), every scratch test run against the real service and cleaned up immediately after — twice, a mistake mid-verification was itself caught and recovered via the staged `git` checkpoint before continuing. Batch 2 was held to the same bar: a reproduction on record before any diff, not a fresh test written to fit whatever the fix turned out to be.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XP4XK0001",
    "type": "heading",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQHP28001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Make `Aperas.dev/monorepo` runnable, 2026-10-15**",
    "text": "**Make `Aperas.dev/monorepo` runnable, 2026-10-15**: the user asked for `Aperas.dev/monorepo` to be made runnable so that the new engine can be tested there. Until the new engine lands, what is runnable is the live code the checkout still carries, so the first goal is that its dependencies are installed and `npm run verify` runs.",
