    ],
    "title": "**2. The meta-model and the schemas**",
    "text": "**2. The meta-model and the schemas**: the [meta-model](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MYZ6Q0000) as types: kinds and their inheritance; for each field its [storage kind](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00H) and its [cardinality](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00G); for a literal field no type, its value being a string, a number or a boolean; for an embed field the kind it embeds; the name of the reverse side of a reference or embed field, optional and given only where the engine must expose that side as a field; the ordered and partitioning fields; and the roles (containment, the tombstone marker, a value dropped with its target, the root kinds of the sweep and the fields it follows). The engine is constructed with a schema and closes it. A small test schema, which is not the Aperas schema, is the one the engine's tests use. The Aperas schema is written in the meta-model in `src/shell/` ([The Aperas schema](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001), [Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M), [the roles it assigns](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NB5FSR001)): `children` holds containment, ordered and partitioning, with `parent` as its reverse side, a derived entry of the field order and not a stored field; a `Link` has `target` and `props`, which embeds `StringProp`, as do the `props` of a node and the `preferences` of a `Profile`; an `ArtifactNode` has an optional `type`, and the hash and timestamp fields of the `ArtifactNode` and the `FolderNode` and the `kind` and the `name` of a `Profile` are optional. The `orderedContainment` cardinality and the `__siblingIndex` predicate of the reference copy have no counterpart.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
