            "value": "12"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR009:props:StringProp:00D3XQQHJ0000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**3. Ids**",
    "text": "**3. Ids**: [Ids](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01N) are `Kind:snowflake`, an embedded node's id `owner:field:Kind:snowflake`, nested further for the props of a link. The kind of an id is read from its last `field:Kind:` segment, or from its prefix when it has none, and a string counts as an id only if a valid snowflake follows `Kind:`. Ids are unique across all graphs. The shell mints the ids and passes them in; the engine checks the grammar and the uniqueness of each, and refuses an id that fails the grammar.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
