    "title": "**2. The reverse side, built on first use**",
    "text": "**2. The reverse side, built on first use**: the reverse of a field is built the first time the field is asked in reverse, is held on the record of each object as a set, and every later write keeps it ([Reverse, for each field, built on first use](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR017)). The reads: the subjects whose field F holds node V, their first one and their count.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00M",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**3. Removing a node**",
    "text": "**3. Removing a node**: it removes all its pairs, its record from its collection, and its entries in every reverse side that was built, and drops it from every reference field to which the schema assigns the role of a value dropped with its target (`unfolds` in the Aperas schema). Other incoming references are not removed.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
