    "title": "**4. Embedded nodes**",
    "text": "**4. Embedded nodes**: an embedded node has an id that carries its owner and field, is written in its owner's record, and has no tombstone; `removePair(graph, subject, field, value)` removes the pair and, on an embed field, the embedded node the pair names, recursively, and a write of an embed field is `removePair` for each value it drops and `addPair` for each value it adds, so the embedded nodes it keeps keep their ids ([Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013), [Writes](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000C)); the interface types `removePair` since Batch 3 and this batch builds it. Which ids the embedded nodes keep through an edit is the shell's minting and not the engine's ([Ids are stable](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01Q)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
