    "text": "**Gated by**: [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) gates the part of steps 1 and 4 that makes a write outside the shape fail, and so [`encodeDoc` and `mintEmbedded` write any key as a predicate](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZWZMR001); [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) gates a write to a subject that is absent, which every write of the batch reaches; until each is decided, a write follows the schema as the accessors of the reference copy follow the class shape, through one function where the check will sit (`inShape` for Enforcement, `existence` for Existence), each throwing `Undecided`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00T",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done when**",
    "text": "**Done when**: the model-based test holds the reverse side equal to the inverse of the forward side after every operation in a random sequence, including a reverse asked after writes and one asked before; the dangling-`unfolds` and embedded-removal reproductions of the reference copy's tests pass on the engine; steps 1 to 5 pass in `commit`, with the Enforcement and Existence cases recorded as waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
