    "title": "**1. Ordered fields**",
    "text": "**1. Ordered fields**: a field can be ordered; its forward side is a list on its host, so an item appears in it at most once; the port of an item is `host:item`, the reverse of the item points at that port, and the item's place is read from the host's list on demand. There is no sibling index and no order key; an insertion, a move or a removal is one splice of the list and changes no reverse entry ([Ordered fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001), [Ports, the two ends of a pair](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJCK10001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00X",
