    "title": "**3. Containment**",
    "text": "**3. Containment**: the field to which the schema assigns containment (`children` in the Aperas schema) is ordered and partitioning; a node is in at most one container's list, containment has no cycle, the parent (`parent` in the Aperas schema) is read from the reverse of the containment field, and taking a node out of its container's list detaches it and does not delete it ([Containment](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z), [Where a node's parent comes from](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2562RC8001)). Moving a node to another container is a removal from the first list and an insertion into the second, and the engine refuses the insertion while the node is still in another list.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
