    "title": "**Gated by**",
    "text": "**Gated by**: [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) and [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) reach the batch as they reached Batches 4 and 5, through the two functions already in `engine.ts` (`existence`, `inShape`), each throwing `Undecided`. Existence gates every read and write that names a host with no record (`insertItem`, `moveItem`, `removeItem`, `items`, `placeOf`, and `addPair`, `removePair` and `clearField` on an ordered field); Enforcement gates the shape of every ordered read and write (an undeclared field, a derived entry, an item that is not a string) and the second value of a `one` or `optional` partitioning field, which it checks before the partitioning rule. For a field marked partitioning the rule is decided, so its refusals are `Refused`. The batch builds around both: a list entry that names a node with no record stays, and the bucket of that node waits in the map of the reverse of nodes with no record. Until each is decided, the cases that throw `Undecided` are recorded as waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR013",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done when**",
    "text": "**Done when**: the model-based test of random insertions, moves (inside a list and across containers) and removals holds, after every operation, a single container for each node, no cycle, `parent` equal to the reverse of `children`, and the place of an item equal to its index in the list; the reproductions of the two closed issues are tests written first and failing on the reference copy; steps 1 to 4 pass in `commit`, with the Existence and Enforcement cases recorded as waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
