    "title": "**1. The tombstone**",
    "text": "**1. The tombstone**: tombstoning is the engine's operation: a tombstoned node gets the timestamp that the shell passes in (a string), in the field to which the schema assigns the tombstone marker (`tombstonedAt` in the Aperas schema), and a node is live when that field is unset; a tombstone loses all its references, its parent included, so it leaves its container's list, and it keeps its literal properties (`title`, `text`, `tombstonedAt`, and `path`, `holder` and `type` where the document has them) ([Tombstones](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01V), [A removed node leaves its container](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000R)). The engine tombstones one node, or a subtree over containment; the rule that a removed artifact or folder tombstones its subtree is the shell's, in Batch 11 step 4.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
