    "title": "**Gated by**",
    "text": "**Gated by**: [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) and [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M). Existence gates what a node with no pair left is, after its last pair is removed, and so what a tombstone is, a node that keeps only literals: the batch keeps the record in the master map and in the collection of its kind, never reads `exists` or `size`, and leaves both `Undecided('Existence')`; a tombstone of a node with no record is `Undecided('Existence')` too. Enforcement reaches the batch for what a generic write may do with the marker or on a tombstone, which is allowed for now ([the issue of the writes to a tombstone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001)); the `Refused` for a kind that holds no marker follows the oracle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
