    "title": "**1. Graphs in memory**",
    "text": "**1. Graphs in memory**: the engine holds several graphs in a map keyed by `graph.domain`, and holds no settings of a graph (they are the shell's, a table keyed by graph name in its configuration, Batch 9). `createGraph(graph)` enforces the grammar of the name, which is that of the host of a URL authority (lowercase DNS labels joined by dots, hyphens only inside a label), and is `Refused` for a name that fails it, for the name `id` (reserved by `aperas://id/`) and for a name already taken; no other name has a special case (the shell, not the engine, warns of a table entry keyed `tree`), so the graph that exists at the start and `default` are as any other. A node is created in a graph, the collections are kept for each graph and kind, and the master map serves every graph ([Graphs in memory](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8003)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
