    "title": "**Closes**",
    "text": "**Closes**: [the buckets of a reverse side are read across graphs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRWNPR001), by step 3: the decision is made (reads filtered to the graph they name, the rules of the whole store across graphs, the sweep within one graph), and the batch makes the oracle and the engine say it for each read and rule that touches the bucket of an object (the derived entry and the tree, `subjectsOf`, `firstSubjectOf` and `countSubjectsOf`, the second-container and cycle rule of a partitioning field, the entries dropped with their target, the removal from a container by a tombstone, and the mark of the sweep), and tests it with a subject in each of two graphs; and [`insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001), not by step 5 but by the follow-up of the Coder, which has `insertItem` check the embedded-id rule on an embed field as `addPair` does. It is what the scope test of Batch 9 and the threads graph rest on.",
