  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01K",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done when**",
    "text": "**Done when**: the model-based test adds create-graph and drop-graph to the random operations; a name that fails the grammar, and the name `id`, are refused, and no other name is special; a drop with a pair pointing in from another graph is refused and leaves every graph as it was; each read and rule of step 3 is tested with a subject in each of two graphs and the oracle and the engine agree; an embedded id is refused in a containment field by `addPair`, `insertItem` and `moveItem`; `graphOf` answers the graph of an id (built, not confirmed by the user); `schema.test.ts` (which asserts `NotBuiltError` of Batch 8 for the two operations) and `ids.test.ts` (which says the oracle has the graphs of Batch 8) are rewritten; `commit` passes. The `moveItem` refusal of an embedded id has a case that fails without it (the follow-up of the Coder: the case reads the message, since the class cannot tell the two refusals apart), and `insertItem` into an ordered embed field meets the embedded-id rule, tested over a schema that declares one.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
