    "title": "**Closes**",
    "text": "**Closes**: [`dehydrate` sorts with `localeCompare`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D39EY5B0001), in the dump, which sorts by code point, with a test that fails if the sort goes back to `localeCompare` (no real id differs under a locale, so the reproduction is a simulated collation); [the loader writes `parent` from its own pair](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2538VKR001) and [a repeated `@id` is logged and merged](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2595QAG001), in the load, each with a reproduction that fails on the reference copy's `rehydrateStore` and passes on the load; [the thread-scope test inside the engine's directory](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2590B2R001), for `Aperas.dev` only, where `threadScope.ts` has been in `src/shell/` since Batch 15 and `graphOfPath.ts` replaces its rule (the working checkout `Aperas/` keeps the test in `core/src/apeironNgn/`); the computing half of [`danglingRefs` computed and not read by the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001), whose reading is the service's, so the issue stays open for it. The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` is not changed by the batch (`dehydrate.ts`, `store.ts` and `threadScope.ts` keep their code) until [Batch 11](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) moves the shell onto the engine and [Batch 12](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes what is left.",
