    "title": "**Gated by**",
    "text": "**Gated by**: [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) gates whether the load is held to the class, that is what it does with a key outside the shape; [An id-like string at load](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D256098G001) gates what the load does with a string that begins like an id and is not one, and with it the rest of [the kind of an id and an id-like string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2534RSG001); [An invalid id and a non-canonical integer](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000S) gates the load of an integer that is not canonical (an id that fails the grammar is refused by the engine); [The name of a captured port view](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2T6X3CG001) gates the file of captured port views (Batch 14); [The service lifecycle](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000W) gates what is done with the list of undefined ids, and the guard and timing of a flush. The migration of step 6 is settled in its six parts (the `predicate` of every `Link`, the tombstones stripped from the tree, the six `README.md` artifacts deleted, the `kind: human` of `dinhlx` filled, the `unfolds` entries whose target is not defined stripped, the `type` of every artifact stripped), and it leaves the live blocks and the artifact that have no parent as they stand ([settled](#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8002)). The fields of the shapes that the mirror lacks gate nothing: the design now makes the hash and timestamp fields that projection or ingest sets (`projectedHash`, `fileHash`, `ingestedHash`, `lastIngestedAt` and `lastTrackedAt`) and the `kind` of a `Profile` optional, in [Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M) ([documents of the mirror lack fields that the design declares `one`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YV43Q0001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
