    "title": "**2. One primitive for the live node at a path**",
    "text": "**2. One primitive for the live node at a path**: every lookup by path asks the live node, not the first one found, through one primitive, \"the live node at this path\", with an optional kind and an optional graph, over a map that holds only live nodes' ids ([How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001), [A lookup does not depend on first match](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01H)). Built as `liveAtPath(path, { graph?, kind? })`, one map over all the graphs of the mapping with the graph and the kind as filters, the live holders of a path sorted with `compareIds` and the first answered ([A key held by two live nodes](#id/BlockNode:00D6J3N65R001)); no reader of the old files is changed or called.",
