        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "checked",
        "value": "false"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**2. The node classes**",
    "text": "**2. The node classes**: the classes, `wrap` and the accessors stay in the shell, in `src/shell/`, and read and write their fields through the engine under the Aperas schema of Batch 3, which replaces `shape.ts`. `defineAccessors`, `readField`, `writeField`, `clearField`, the ordered insertion and `hardDeleteNode` of `node.ts` go through the engine; with step 1 it is one change. The engine access of `node.ts` is about 350 lines (`childrenOf`, `appendOrderedChild`, `insertOrderedChild`, `readField`, `writeField`, `clearField`, `mintEmbedded`, `hardDeleteNode`, `removeDanglingUnfolds`, `defineAccessors`, `wrap` and `backlinks`), and `hardDeleteNode` is called from four sites (`writeField`, `removeTreeViewByName`, `pruneUnreachableTombstones` and `removeProfile`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
