    "title": "**4. Writes**",
    "text": "**4. Writes**: insert, update, remove, retype, with the subtree tombstoning of a removed artifact or folder. That tombstoning is one engine operation, the tombstone of a subtree over containment of Batch 7, and the rule that a removed artifact or folder tombstones its subtree stays in the shell; it has five callers: `tombstoneLiveSubtree` (`node.ts` lines 870 to 878, called at `kgRemove.ts:42` and `artifacts.ts:272`) and `applyTombstone` (lines 850 to 859, called at `kgUpdate.ts:332`, `folders.ts:104` and `node.ts:803`). A tombstone leaves its container ([settled](#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0001)), so `tree --tombstoned` loses its source for a removed child and `toPath()` of a tombstone is `null`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
