    "title": "**7. The sweeps** of the working service",
    "text": "**7. The sweeps** of the working service: `tombstoneVacuousContainers`, which the design does not state, is kept as the shell's logic over the engine's operations. `pruneStaleUnfolds` is not kept: the engine drops a removed node from every `unfolds` entry by the role of a value dropped with its target ([Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013)), and the entries that already dangle in the mirror are stripped by part (5) of [the one-time migration](#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001). `pruneUnreachableTombstones` is the mark-and-sweep that [the engine's sweep](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8001) states, so it is replaced by the engine's sweep of Batch 7 and not kept: the step is one sweep and not three. Tombstones leave their container ([settled](#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0001)), so `tombstoneVacuousContainers` keeps only the boot rule over a list or a textless item with no live child, and the removal itself tombstones a container that it empties.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
