    "title": "**Closes**",
    "text": "**Closes**: [the store is read outside the helpers](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2536E1R001) with Batch 12; [the tree view lists a block's links newest first](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001); [no test calls most commands of the CLI or the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC8001) with step 10 and, for the groups that move, steps 3, 4, 5 and 8; [three behaviours of the caller depend on the order of an unordered read](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800D), with the five listings sorted by id ([settled](#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0003)); the `predicate` of a `Link` in the code of the shell, with step 9 (the mirror is Batch 9, step 6); [a move of a node after an anchor inside its own subtree is not refused by the working engine, and it loops the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001), with piece 6, whose ordered insertion (step 2) reaches the engine's `insertItem` and `moveItem`, where the no-cycle rule of the partitioning field `children` refuses it ([Partitioning fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)); its reproduction is a heading moved after one of its own children, which is refused while the service goes on answering; the filed cost of [one `insert`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001) and of [a full-store scan](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001) are judged in Batch 13.",
