    "title": "**3. The differential run**",
    "text": "**3. The differential run**: one script of commands on both engines, the reference on an unmigrated copy of the mirror and the new engine on the migrated copy of it ([Layer 4](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002)), and the dumps compared outside the list of deliberate differences. The harness is described in [the Oxigraph engine as the reference of a differential run](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T) in the map of the callers: the reference is a checkout of `d794060`, since the archive is not runnable alone; the two engines run as two services on two copies, apart by their own environment variables; both copies come from one snapshot; and the harness has yet to normalise minted ids, timestamps, the order of the dumps and the order of listings, and to write the script of commands. The harness copies both mirrors from one snapshot that includes `Apeiron/.state/`, runs every command with `</dev/null` under a timeout, and has a fixture for a `children` entry that names an id with no document (the new engine returns it in the list of ids referenced and never defined, and what the shell does with the list is the service lifecycle; [the ghost folder](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001) is the case in the mirror).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0010",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
