    "title": "**1. Splitting a bucket**",
    "text": "**1. Splitting a bucket**: a reverse bucket over the cap set for its field is split into incoming ports along the partitioning field the shell names, by the ancestors of its sources at the next level, and a port still over the cap is split at the level below; pairs the hierarchy cannot tell apart stay together as the residue, even above the cap ([Ports](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2T5VG08001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0019",
    "type": "listItem",
