    "title": "**Layer 1, group tests**",
    "text": "**Layer 1, group tests**: each batch adds its tests to a group `engine/` (or to the group of the code it moved) as standalone `<name>.test.ts` files named in a suite, per [the tiers](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64000N). After an edit, `npm run verify -- --group <area>` and `npm run verify -- --suite essential` (5 s); before handing a batch back, and at the orchestrator's check, `npm run verify` (the `commit` suite, 60 s). If `commit` passes its budget, the work stops and is reported, for the suite needs a split. The legacy suite is never run, and `demand` ([the demand tier](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F648001)) only when the user asks for it. The tests that [step 10 of Batch 11](#id/BlockNode:00D3Z01YER001) adds for the commands and the service that no test group covers today (`runTree`, `runShow`, `runPath`, `runResolve`, `runUnfold`, `runFold`, `runZoom`, `runProfile*`, `runRemove`, `runProject`, `runTrack`, `runReverseTrack`, `service.ts` and `serviceClient.ts`) are group tests of this layer, one test group for each group of the batch whose commands lack one, and each is written at the batch that requires it, Batch 11, before its group moves and not before the batch; only `runLinkCandidates` is waived, because it goes with its verb ([which of them can be waived](#id/BlockNode:00D3Z01YER006)); the other commands are tested, the differential run being Batch 13.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D76D2W00000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Layer 2, model-based tests**",
    "text": "**Layer 2, model-based tests**: seeded random sequences of operations on the engine and on the oracle of Batch 3, compared after every operation, with the seed printed when one fails. The operations grow with the batches: writes of literal, reference and embed fields, ordered insertions, moves and removals, tombstones, sweeps, creating and dropping a graph. The invariants held after every operation: the reverse side is the inverse of the forward side; a node is in at most one container's list and containment has no cycle; `parent` is the reverse of `children` and the place of an item is its index; a tombstone is in no list and keeps its literals; ids come back in code-point order wherever the design promises an order; no operation leaves an orphan embedded node. From Batch 14, the ports flattened equal the flat bucket.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
