    ],
    "title": "**Layer 3, the round trip**",
    "text": "**Layer 3, the round trip**: a load followed by a dump returns the files byte for byte ([The round trip is exact](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0001)), on a tiny fixture in `essential`, and on a copy of the mirror in `demand`. The mirror in the repository holds data that the design no longer states (a `predicate` on every `Link`, tombstones that still hold `children`, `links` or `props` and keep their `parent` and their place in the `children` of their container, six artifacts for `README.md` files that stand outside any folder, a `type` on every artifact, a view's `unfolds` entry whose target is not defined, and `dinhlx` with no `kind`), so the real mirror is migrated once before this layer is run on it, and the baseline of this layer on the real mirror is the migrated mirror ([the migration, Batch 9 step 6](#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001)). In that migration the `predicate` leaves every `Link`, the tombstones are stripped from the tree, the six `README.md` artifacts are deleted, `dinhlx` is given `kind: human`, the `unfolds` entries whose target is not defined are stripped and the `type` of every artifact is stripped (all settled); the live blocks and the artifact that have no parent are left as they stand ([settled](#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8002)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002",
