    "title": "**Layer 4, the differential run**",
    "text": "**Layer 4, the differential run**: the same script of commands on the reference engine and on the new one, and the dumps compared. The two designs have no mirror in common ([which mirror the differential run starts from](#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0002)): the reference runs on an unmigrated copy of the mirror and the new engine on the migrated copy of it, and the dumps are compared after the differences that the migration and the design make on purpose are normalised. The deliberate differences are listed and few: the migration's own changes ([Batch 9, step 6](#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001): no `predicate` on a `Link`, the tombstones stripped from the tree, the six `README.md` artifacts and their paragraphs deleted, `dinhlx` given `kind: human`, the `unfolds` entries whose target is not defined stripped, the `type` of every artifact stripped), the order of ids by code point where `localeCompare` ordered them, the `children` order and `parent` rule of the load, the rejection of a repeated `@id`, the empty tombstone, the text of a link in `tree` and `unfold` without its predicate, the removal of `aperas link` and `aperas unlink` ([manual links are dropped](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG001)), and whatever the settled open points change. Any other difference is a finding and not a pass. The harness copies both mirrors from one snapshot that includes `Apeiron/.state/`, runs every command with `</dev/null` under a timeout, and has a fixture for a `children` entry that names an id with no document ([the ghost folder](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001)): the new engine returns it in the list of ids referenced and never defined, and what the shell does with the list is the service lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
      "BlockNode:00D7TSPH88001",
