      "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Layer 5, the reproductions**",
    "text": "**Layer 5, the reproductions**: each filed issue a batch closes has a test written from its own reproduction first, failing on the reference copy and passing on the engine, as the archived Batches were held to: a sibling gap after a move to another parent and an append, a second `parent` after a write of `children`, a repeated `@id`, a `parent` and `children` that disagree, a live and a tombstoned node at one path, a tombstone that keeps `children`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Layer 6, the tools**",
    "text": "**Layer 6, the tools**: `aperas check-links` and the other commands run on a copy of the mirror and agree with the reference engine's output, and `npm run build:aperas` builds a bundle that starts.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Layer 7, the measurements**",
    "text": "**Layer 7, the measurements**: Batch 13's protocol. A figure is recorded with its sample size and what it does not show, and a comparison is made only between runs on the same machine and the same copy of the mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF23FB1G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D457HDWG001"
    ]
  },
