    "title": "**6. The one-time migration of the mirror**",
    "text": "**6. The one-time migration of the mirror**: the mirror of the repository is migrated once, before the round trip is run on it, so that the baseline of step 4 and of [Layer 3](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR001) is a mirror that matches the design. The shape is settled, in six parts. (1) The `predicate` leaves every `Link` ([every `Link` carries a `predicate`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG001)), since a `Link` is a wikilink and no manual link exists. (2) The tombstones are stripped from the tree ([tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001)): each one loses the `children`, `links` and `props` it still holds, its `parent` and its entry in the `children` of its container, as [Tombstones](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01V) and [Containment](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z) state, and keeps its literal properties (`title`, `text`, `tombstonedAt`, and `path`, `holder` and `type` where the document has them). (3) The six `README.md` artifacts and their six paragraphs are deleted outright and not tombstoned ([six live `ArtifactNode`s for `README.md` files stand outside any folder](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WTZG9G001)): a tombstone would only wait for the engine to run to be wiped, with the same net result, and each folder already holds its own README content. Nothing points at the six: the only references to them or to their paragraphs in the mirror are each artifact's own `children` entry and its paragraph's `parent`; no `Link` targets any of the twelve nodes, no `FolderNode` lists an artifact as a child, and no `TreeView` unfolds or roots at one. A `track` or `ingest` run after the deletion must not register the six again, which the dry run of the migration on a clone checks. (4) `Profile:00CJC4S69R000` (`dinhlx`) gets `kind: human` ([documents of the mirror lack fields that the design declares `one`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YV43Q0001)); it is the only `Profile` that the migration fills. `Profile:00CA03JXD8000` (`default`) is the auto-generated fallback for everyone and has no `kind`, and none can be given, because it cannot know; `kind` is therefore optional in the `Profile` shape, as [Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M) now states. Whether `default` should have a `name` is not decided, and is [an open point of the batch](#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8001). (5) Every `unfolds` entry whose target is not defined is stripped, since the working service's `pruneStaleUnfolds` is not kept ([Batch 11 step 7](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000K)), and the checker verifies that none is left. (6) The `type` of every artifact (`root`) is stripped, since an `ArtifactNode` has no `type` ([Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M)), and the checker verifies that none is left. The script `migrate-mirror.py` and its checker `verify-migration.py` need the rules of parts (5) and (6), and the dry run is repeated before the cutover, as [already planned](#id/BlockNode:00D4JYSYZ0003). The issues named in the parts are the record of what the migration must fix. It leaves the live blocks and the artifact that have no parent as they stand ([settled](#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8002)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M",
    "type": "listItem",
