    "title": "**In flight**",
    "text": "**In flight**: the plan is carried out in `Aperas.dev` on branch `js-apeironngn`. Done: [Batch 15](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBFKAG001), the current code moved to `src/shell/` ([the go](#id/BlockNode:00D4NT02HR001), [checked](#id/BlockNode:00D4NYBTD0001)), which resolves [the code differs from the boundary](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBNCF8001); [Batch 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG001), the engine's module in the emptied `src/apeironNgn/` with its meta-model, the Aperas and test schemas, the interface as types, the oracle and the `engine` test group, with no behaviour yet ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D4QFMSDG001)); [Batch 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR006), the records, the literal fields of cardinality `one`, `optional` and `set`, the ids, the collections and the orders, tested against the oracle ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D4QW4JXG001)); [Batch 5](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H), the reference and embed fields, the reverse side built on first use, the removal of a node and the build of Persistence, with a model-based test of the reverse against the oracle ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D4RTZKK8001)); and [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V), the ordered fields, the partitioning mark, containment with the parent derived from the reverse of `children`, and the tree of the records, with a model-based test of 20 seeds against the oracle and two reproductions that failed on the reference copy and pass on the engine ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D4SGY6JR001)); [Batch 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014), the tombstone, the tombstone of a subtree, embedded nodes removed with their owner and `sweep(graph): Id[]`, with a model-based test of 20 seeds against the oracle, two reproductions that failed on the old engine and pass on the engine, and four mutations, three caught by the model test or a hand-written case and one by the hand-written cases only ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D4T3JTP8001)); [Batch 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D), several graphs: the grammar of a graph's name, `createGraph`, `dropGraph`, the reads of a node's relations filtered to the graph they name, `graphOf` (built, confirmed by the user on 2026-10-20) and the refusal of an embedded id in a containment field, with a model test of 20 seeds against the oracle and the cross-graph cases written first ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D5BATEM0000)); [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M), the mirror, the shell's first batch: the format and the dump of the engine's records, the load into the three graphs, the exact round trip, the table of settings and the mapping from a graph and a kind to a file, the rule that gives a new node its graph, `danglingRefs`, and rules 5 and 6 of the migration scripts, with the round trip of the migrated copy of the real mirror byte for byte for all 8 files and 31 mutations caught ([steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 checked](#id/BlockNode:00D5C44ZSG001), [step 2 checked](#id/BlockNode:00D6H5V1BR001)); and [Batch 10](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0004), the lookups by a literal value, the shell's second batch: the three maps of a profile by its handle, a view by its name and an artifact or a folder by its stored path, one update function for each write that changes a map, `liveAtPath` for the live node at a path, `pathKeyOf` as the one place that gives the key, and the rule for a key held by two live nodes ([A key held by two live nodes](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6J3N65R001)), with a model test of 20 seeds against the oracle and 16 mutations all caught ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D6HRZD8G001)); all nine are committed by the user on `js-apeironngn` (Batches 3 to 10 as `1b58fab`, Batch 15 as `eae00f1`), and the suites are near their budgets (after Batch 10, `commit` 904 of 904 in 50.0 s of 60 s, 49.5 s on a quiet machine, and `essential` 52 of 52 in 3.8 to 4.6 s of 5 s; after Batch 9, `commit` 862 of 862 in 44 s and `essential` 52 of 52 in 3.6 s; after the follow-up of Batch 8, `essential` 51 of 51 in 4.4 s and 3.9 s, and a run under load took 6.6 s, [checked](#id/BlockNode:00D5BFCTAR001)). Batch 3 closes in part [the store is read outside the helpers](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2536E1R001) and the `type` shape part of [artifacts without a `type`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D253D680001), Batch 4 closes in part [the kind of an id and an id-like string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2534RSG001), [the scans that list the ids of a kind](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001), [`dehydrate`'s `localeCompare`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D39EY5B0001) and [the order of a block's links](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001), and Batch 5 closes in part [`ownerOfLink` takes the first node whose `links` names a link](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2593220001) and the scans again (its reverse reads), all seven issues open for the rest (of the seven, the order of a block's links is resolved by piece 7 of Batch 11). Batch 7 closes in part [tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001) for the nodes the engine tombstones, which stays open for the tombstones the mirror holds (Batch 9) and the callers (Batch 11), and files [a plain write sets or clears the tombstone marker and writes to a tombstone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001), open until Enforcement is decided. Batch 8 resolves [the buckets of a reverse side are read across graphs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRWNPR001) with a dated entry (its reproduction is the test, `graphReads.test.ts`), and a follow-up of the Coder resolves [`insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001) (the embedded-id rule on an ordered embed field, tested over a schema that declares one) and adds a case that fails without the `moveItem` refusal; the refusal of an embedded id in a containment field, Batch 8's step 5, did not close that issue by itself. Batch 9 resolves [`dehydrate`'s `localeCompare`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D39EY5B0001) (a simulated collation is its reproduction), [the loader writes `parent` from its own pair](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2538VKR001) and [a repeated `@id` is logged and merged](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2595QAG001) (each with a reproduction that fails on the reference copy's `rehydrateStore` and passes on the load), each with a dated entry, and [the thread-scope test inside the engine's directory](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2590B2R001) for `Aperas.dev` only; it builds the computing half of [`danglingRefs` computed and not read by the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001), which stays open for the reading (a dated entry); the reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps its own code for all five until Batch 11 and Batch 12. Batch 10 resolves no issue: it builds the fix of [`findByExactPath` takes the first node found at a path](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001) and of the first-match behaviour of [three behaviours of the caller depend on the order of an unordered read](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800D), and the maps for the four scans for a literal value of [full-store scans](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001), each with a dated entry and open until Batch 11 moves the callers (the reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps the first-match readers). Batch 6 resolves [sibling indexes are not kept dense](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252Y7WR001) and [a child can end with two `parent` pairs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2532JJR001), each with a dated entry, in the engine; the reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps both until Batch 11 and Batch 12. Batch 4 recorded as waiting step 6 (`exists` and `size`), which still waits, and the deletion half of step 4, which Batch 5 built with `removeNode`. Batches 4, 5 and 6 record as waiting the cases that throw `Undecided` for [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) and [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K), Existence having been added to Batch 5's Gated by as it was to Batch 4's, and both having been written into Batch 6's Gated by, which said nothing; the Coder notes that Existence also decides nothing yet about a node that has only incoming pairs (it has a bucket in the map of the reverse and no record, and no read counts the bucket as existence). One design point of Batch 3 still waits for the user, in its [open points](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8004): the rules the schema check read in; the other three are settled, one of them, clearing an embed field that keeps some of its nodes (by `removePair` and `addPair`), built by Batch 5, and another, that the sweep is an operation of the engine, built by Batch 7. Three points that Batch 6 found were settled on 2026-10-17 and are stated in the design: a node is owned or contained, never both ([Containment](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z)); the order of the checks on a partitioning field is not a design point; the mark names no direction and the engine derives the climbed side from the cardinality ([Partitioning fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001)). The engine holds no settings of a graph, they are the shell's, graphs are named by a `graph.domain` ([Graphs in memory](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8003)), and the mirror holds no `graph` field in a document ([Records by kind and by graph](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR018)). [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), the layers above moved onto the engine, is done (2026-10-21; the flip committed by the user, pieces 7 to 10 staged and not committed): it was surveyed and split into ten pieces of one coder turn each ([the survey](#id/BlockNode:00D763GYZ0001)), and its four design answers are settled and written into the design and the plan ([the answers](#id/BlockNode:00D766N4RR001)): `graphOf` is confirmed and a node exists when a document stands for it, a tombstone leaves its container, the listings are sorted in the shell and the canonical place is the first in code-point order, and a load that rejects a document is refused with a start-anyway option and a side copy. The split of `commit` into `commit`, `models` and `tools` is built, the preparation the survey asked for before piece 4 ([the split](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D792XEJ8001); staged, not committed): `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.6 s of 5 s, `commit` 888 of 888 in 15.4 s of 60 s, `models` 145 of 145 in 12.0 s of 30 s and `tools` 14 of 14 in 14.0 s of 30 s, and a test that holds each file in exactly one suite. Pieces 1 to 10 are done in `Aperas.dev` (staged, not committed; pieces 1 to 4 on the old code, piece 5 beside it, piece 6 the flip, piece 7 the callers' names and the order rules, piece 8 the lookups of ingest, track and project, piece 9 the tests of the writes and tombstones, piece 10 the sweeps and the service lifecycle): [piece 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2MR003) removed the manual links (`commit` 904 of 904 in 39.5 s), [piece 2](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0000) wrote the group `commands/` for the reads (59 cases, 17 of 17 mutations caught), and [piece 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0001) wrote the tests of the writes, `track` and `project` (79 cases and case `5g` of the ingest chain, 22 of 23 mutations caught) and the reproduction of the move into its own subtree (`commit` 1043 of 1043 in 49.5 s of 60 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.6 s), [piece 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0002) wrote the group `service/` for the service (50 cases in about 3 s on a service of its own in a scratch runtime directory and port, all 26 arms of `handle()` reached, none waived, 9 of 9 mutations caught; `commit` 938 of 938 in 18.2 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.5 s), [piece 5](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0003) built the engine-side handle and the write layer beside the old code, `core/src/shell/db.ts` and `writeLayer.ts`, which nothing imports yet, with the group `shell/` (37 cases in `commit`, 20 seeds in `models`; 23 of 24 mutations caught, the one missed an equivalent mutant; `commit` 975 of 975 in 18.1 s, `models` 165 of 165 in 13.7 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.5 s, no old file changed)., and [piece 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0004), the flip ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D7T09ZXG001)), ran the shell, the cli and the service on the engine through the `Db`, the maps and the write layer, starting from a clean tree with `commit` 991 of 991 in 19.4 s (the service boots, reloads and flushes on it; the six old Oxigraph files stay as the frozen set with no diff, held by `shell/oldEngine.test.ts`; `Lookups.subtreeTombstoned` is removed; [the move into its own subtree](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) is refused by the engine's no-cycle rule and its issue is resolved; twelve deliberate differences are recorded in [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002), the main one being that a tombstone leaves its list and a removed node is pruned at the next sweep; 12 of 12 mutations caught; `commit` 999 of 999 in 19.8 s by the coder and 25.6 s by the orchestrator, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.9 to 4.0 s, `models` 165 of 165, `tools` 14 of 14, the corpus group 17 of 17 on a migrated scratch copy). [Piece 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0005), the reads, link integrity, profiles and views ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D7TP74X0001); [done](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001)), moved the callers of the old path lookup onto `liveAtPath` and deleted `findByExactPath`, built the order rules (a block's links by `position`, then id, a link with none last; the canonical place the first link by id within a cone, whatever the order of the unfolds and of building; the other listings sorted by id; `compareByKey` no longer throws on a mixed pair, which settles [the order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P) in the code), gave `runPath` of a node without a path a refusal of its own, and turned the set assertions of pieces 2, 3 and 6 into exact orders, with `commands/order.test.ts` (18 cases) and 21 of 21 mutations caught (`commit` 1018 of 1018 in 17.7 s by the Coder and 18.9 s by the orchestrator, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.0 s and 3.1 s, `models` 165 of 165, `tools` 14 of 14, the corpus group 17 of 17; seven deliberate differences are recorded in [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7TSPH88001)); [the newest-first issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001), [`runPath` of a `Link` id](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76KJ728001) and [`findByExactPath`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001) are resolved and moved to Resolved (the working service and `Aperas/` run the old code until the cutover), and [the canonical place with a nested cone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7TSC16G001) is filed for the user to decide later. [Piece 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0006), ingest, track and project ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D7V14M08001); [done](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7V463CR001)), moved the lookups of `artifacts.ts` and `folders.ts` onto the one path map, the write layer telling it after each accepted write, deleted `findLiveByKindAndPath`, `findLiveArtifactByPath` and the local maps, made `positionsEqual` compare sorted lists, replaced the ghost filter `path !== undefined` by a test that a node has a record and a title, and added `commands/ingest.test.ts` (11 cases; 21 of 22 mutations caught, the 22nd equivalent), with `commit` 1029 of 1029 in 18.3 s by the Coder and 18.6 s by the orchestrator, `essential` 74 of 74 in 2.9 s and 3.2 s, `models` 165 of 165, `tools` 14 of 14 and the corpus group 17 of 17; two deliberate differences are recorded in [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7V4ETMG001); [the three behaviours of the order issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800D) is resolved and moved to Resolved, and the Coder's observation on the folder of `.threads` is added to [the dot-name issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D79JHQ40001), for the user to decide later. [Piece 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0007), writes and tombstones ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D7ZY25VG001); [done](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D8006A58001)), was found almost all done by the flip (the engine's `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` under `applyTombstone` and `tombstoneLiveSubtree`, the tombstone out of its container, the emptied container tombstoned at the removal, the boot rule alone in `tombstoneVacuousContainers`), and added the tests of its Done-when that were missing: a model of 20 seeds over `runRemove` against a ten-line model of the removal rule, `toPath()` null for a tombstone, the mirror a flush writes holding no tombstone in a `children` list (with the helper `tests/support/mirrorLists.ts`) and a move out of a list (11 mutations, all caught), with `commit` 1032 of 1032 in 20.0 s by the Coder and 20.6 s by the orchestrator, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.0 s and 3.3 s, `models` 186 of 186, `tools` 14 of 14 and the corpus group 17 of 17; it adds no deliberate difference to Layer 4, and a move or a reconcile that empties a list leaves it live until the boot sweep, the confirmed boot rule. The engine accepts an insert of an already-tombstoned node and the working service's `update` handler (and its three siblings) never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty: each is a dated entry on its issue, [the plain write on a tombstone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001) and [a write to a thread node never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001), the second a risk for the working service until the cutover and closed in the new one by piece 10; [tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001) gains a dated entry (the callers' share is built; it stays open for the mirror at the cutover). Steps 1, 2 and 4 of [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) are reworded to the leftover, the frozen set with its tests and the `oxigraph` dependency. [Piece 10](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0008), the sweeps and the service lifecycle ([checked](#id/BlockNode:00D80EG6Z8001); [done](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D80J973R001)), replaced the two sweeps by the engine's `sweep` of each graph (`sweepTombstones`; 16 lines to 0 outside the tests), gave each graph its own flush (a set of changed graphs filled by the write layer and one timer for each graph at the interval of the table of settings, so an update of a thread node alone reaches `.state/`), added the option `--start-anyway` of `aperas service start`, `service restart` and `aperas reload` with a side copy `<file>.rejected-<UTC stamp>.json` of the skipped documents, a client that says why a refused start did not start, the dangling ids logged as one warning, and a reload that loads once and frees the old handle as far as the engine lets it (on the real mirror the views graph only), with `service/flush.test.ts` (6 cases) and `corpus/sweeps.test.ts` (4 cases on the migrated copy of the real mirror: the first sweep removes 225 tombstones and no live node); 23 of 23 mutations caught, with `commit` 1049 of 1049 in 19.6 s by the Coder and 21.2 s by the orchestrator, `essential` 74 of 74 in 2.9 s and 3.2 s, `models` 187 of 187, `tools` 14 of 14 and the corpus group 21 of 21; six deliberate differences are recorded in [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001); [no test calls most commands of the CLI or the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC8001) and [the `danglingRefs` entry](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001) are resolved and moved to Resolved, and [a write to a thread node never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001) gains a dated entry (closed on the new engine, open on the working service until the cutover). Batch 11 is done ([the done record](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D80JWQKR001), in the plan's Archive with Batches 3 to 10): the shell of `Aperas.dev` runs on the engine, and the ten pieces, the split of the suites and the twenty-seven deliberate differences of Layer 4 are recorded there. Next is [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S), deleting what the flip froze (the six old Oxigraph files with their tests and support files and `shell/oldEngine.test.ts`, then the `oxigraph` dependency), then [Batch 13](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0010), the measurements against `d794060` and the differential run. The cutover follows them: the migration of the real mirror, applied after a fresh dry run on a clone, and the switch of the working service and of `Aperas/` to the new code, which is the user's decision from the record of Batch 13; until then the working service and `Aperas/` run the old code and keep the defects of the resolved issues. The folder scan that skips dot-names stays filed for the user to decide ([the issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D79JHQ40001)). The real mirror is not touched until the cutover. The real mirror is not migrated: the migration is applied at the cutover only. The design and the plan were completed before them, on 2026-10-16: the [decisions on the dependency survey](#id/BlockNode:00D4MJBY98001) and [the five answers](#id/BlockNode:00D4NN1G50001) ([recorded](#id/BlockNode:00D4NQ73AR001)). The [one-time migration of the mirror](#id/BlockNode:00D3Y1N5Y8001) is settled ([Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001)) and its dry run on a clone passed ([the dry run](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4JYSYZ0001)); the live blocks and the artifact that have no parent stay as they stand, as the test of [the garbage-collection issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D1A2AY68001) ([decided](#id/BlockNode:00D4NX8JHR001)), and what Batch 9 still leaves open is in its [open points](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8001). The migration is applied to the real mirror at the cutover only ([the rule in step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4JYSYZ0003)), after a fresh dry run on a clone. The dry run raised [`concepts.md` has no file under `artifacts/`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4JZ0A7R001). The fix of [the ghost folder](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001) and [the `ingest` prompt](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001) is committed on branch `oxigraph` of `Aperas/` as `eb352f5`. Deferred: [the fix of the busy service that looks stopped](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D457SD1R001), with its directions not chosen, and the single write measurement at full speed ([the cost of a write](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D457M2F8001)). The working service has looped twice on a move of a node into its own subtree (the loop is in the next walk of the parent chain, not in the move): for a day and 20 hours until the orchestrator stopped it on 2026-10-19, and again on 2026-10-20 until it was killed and started again, each time with the mirror on disk intact; [the issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) is resolved in `Aperas.dev` by piece 6 of Batch 11 (the working service runs the old code until the cutover and keeps the loop), and [the skills' recipe of a move](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAJNRR001) has said since v4.8 that `< /dev/null` is for a move only. [The `danglingRefs` entry](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001), related to the ghost, is resolved by piece 10; the dangling `children` reference of the ghost itself stays worked around. The [tests](#id/BlockNode:00D40RVX68000) that no group has today are written at the batch that requires them, not before.",
