    "title": "**Batch 9 and the `predicate`**",
    "text": "**Batch 9 and the `predicate`**: drop the mirror's `predicate` on every `Link` as the example in Batch 9's Enforcement gate.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YB0MCG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YB0MCG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No manual links**",
    "text": "**No manual links**: the feature of a manual link, one told from a wikilink by its `predicate` (the `kg:link` that `aperas link` added and `aperas unlink` removed), is dropped; it was imagined and never used. A `Link` is a wikilink, and the `predicate` leaves it. The six caller sites that tell the two apart, `aperas unlink` and the `tree` text that depends on it are removed in Batch 11.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YB0MCG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YB0MCG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The three questions about the trial and the mirror**",
    "text": "**The three questions about the trial and the mirror**: the orchestrator decides. The trial service is stopped, a fresh clone is made with the working-tree files and `.state/` copied in before any service starts, and the two defects the trial found (the 5 s start timeout, the `ingest` prompt) are filed as issues together with the survey's findings.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YB0MCG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YDAQH0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Shape of the one-time migration, 2026-10-15**",
    "text": "**Shape of the one-time migration, 2026-10-15**: the user settled it: drop the `predicate` from every `Link`, empty the 52 tombstones (they lose `children`, `links` and `props`), and remove the stray `README.md` artifacts, the six that stand outside any folder, instead of giving them a parent. This replaces the shape proposed earlier, which would have parented them. Whether \"remove\" is a tombstone or an outright deletion from the mirror, and what to do with links that point at them, are not stated yet.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
