    "title": "**The 12 helpers of `storeAccess.ts` against the engine's interface** ([the interface](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0003))",
    "text": "**The 12 helpers of `storeAccess.ts` against the engine's interface** ([the interface](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0003)): `objectsOf` (4 production sites: `node.ts:137,210,268`, `dehydrate.ts:44`) and `firstLiteralOf`/`firstRefIriOf` (1 each, `threadScope.ts:20,37`) are \"the values of field F of subject S\"; `orderedChildIds` (3: `node.ts:71,107`, `dehydrate.ts:75`) is \"the children in order\"; `deleteMatches` (11 sites, all in `node.ts`; one unbound subject at `:235`, the `unfolds` sweep, which is \"remove the pairs that name a value in a field\") and `addQuad` (11 in `node.ts`, 5 in `store.ts`) are the writes; `subjectsWhere` with a reference object (`node.ts:242,2132`) and `firstSubjectWhere` with a reference (`node.ts:1397`) are \"the subjects whose field holds node V\". Not offered by the interface and so not re-implementable on it: `subjectsWhere`/`firstSubjectWhere` with a **literal** object (`tree.ts:21` for `path`, `artifacts.ts:189` for `path`, `node.ts:2013` for `handle`, `node.ts:2022` for `name`: four sites, all Batch 10); `allSubjectIds` (1 site, under `allIdsOfKind`, 21 production callers) and `allObjectRefIds` (1 site, `store.ts:144`), which become the kind collections and \"referenced and never defined\"; `countMatches` (1 production site, `node.ts:90`, the sibling count of `appendOrderedChild`), which the ordered-field splice replaces.",
