    ],
    "title": "**Order of set-field values**",
    "text": "**Order of set-field values**: `readField` returns the values of a `set` field in match order (`node.ts:138`; the set fields are `links` and `props` in `BASE_NODE_SHAPE` and `LINK_SHAPE`, `preferences` in `PROFILE_SHAPE` and `unfolds` in `TREE_VIEW_SHAPE`, all in `shape.ts`). The mirror does not depend on it (`dehydrate.ts:58` sorts a set by `localeCompare`). Three readers do: (a) `artifacts.ts:371-373` `positionsEqual` compares the `position` list of a reused `Link`, read in match order, with the fresh ascending list, element by element (`artifacts.ts:611`); if the order differs the `Link`'s `props` are rewritten and the `position` `StringProp`s change id, without a change in content; (b) `buildRenderTree` collects `unfolds` in match order (`node.ts:1975-1987`) and `discoverCone` lets the first escaping link in that order claim the target (`:1530-1569`, `if (!zs.canonical.has(targetId))` at `:1538,1560`), so the place of a node reached through two unfolded links is the order's choice, which is [the canonical-render order check](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q); (c) the order of a block's links in `tree`, `unfold` and the web (`node.ts:1745,1807`, `kgUnfold.ts`), which is [the tree view lists a block's links newest first](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001), gated by [the order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000P",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000P:links:Link:00D3YFAPE0002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D24N87T0007",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000P:links:Link:00D3YFAPE0002:props:StringProp:00D3YFAPE0003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "625"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Order of single values**",
    "text": "**Order of single values**: the first of a `one` or `optional` field (`node.ts:140`, `dehydrate.ts:61`, `threadScope.ts:20,37`). Only `findByExactPath` (`tree.ts:20-21`, `firstSubjectWhere(…, 'path', …)`) can have several: it takes the first subject with that `path` whether tombstoned or live (its callers: `resolve.ts:69`, `resolveCreate.ts:98`, `kgProject.ts:46`, `linkIntegrity.ts:323`, 12 test and tool sites). The artifact side already filters (`findLiveByKindAndPath`, `artifacts.ts:188-191`); `kgProject.ts:46` and `linkIntegrity.ts:323` do not. the Coder did not reproduce a wrong pick; the pointer is the risk, and [the design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0007) says \"a caller that must name one node asks for the live one\".",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000Q",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Order of subjects**",
    "text": "**Order of subjects**: `backlinks` (`node.ts:2131-2133`) gives `kgBacklinks.ts:32` its printed order, `kgProfile.ts:69` its list of views and `removeProfile` its cascade; `orderedChildIds` (`storeAccess.ts:188-196`) sorts by `siblingIndex` with a stable sort, so a child with a `parent` and no index (index 0) or two children with one index keep match order.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000R",
