    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000V:props:StringProp:00D3YFAPD8000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000V:props:StringProp:00D3YFAPD8001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D3YFA81000V",
    "text": "**The archive is not runnable alone.** `Aperas.dev/monorepo/.archive/oxigraph/` holds 40 files (13 `apeironNgn/` modules of core that name a store, 17 `kg*.ts`, `service.ts`, the smoke test, 5 tests and support files, the 2 `verify*.ts` tools; not `shape.ts`, `astParser.ts`, `reconcile.ts`, `snowflake.ts`, `graphConfig.ts`, `aperas.ts` or `serviceClient.ts`), byte-identical to `d794060`. Its imports (`../astParser`, `../snowflake`, `../graphConfig`, `./apeironNgn/serviceClient`, `aperas.ts`) point to files the archive does not hold. The runnable reference is a **checkout** of `d794060`: `/home/will/source/Aperas` itself (it has `node_modules`, `@aperas/*` workspace links and `oxigraph@0.5.11`; the real service runs from it), or a second worktree of that commit with `monorepo/node_modules` copied or linked.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000W",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Two services on two copies**",
    "text": "**Two services on two copies**: the isolation exists and is used. `/proc/<pid>/environ` of a second service shows `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, `APERAS_HTTP_PORT`, `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT`, `APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT` and `APERAS_GRAPH_NAME` set apart from the real service's (which has `/run/user/1000`, port 2736 and the real roots). The lock, socket and token are per `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` (`serviceLock.ts:41-56`), the port per `APERAS_HTTP_PORT` (`:69`), the roots per the two root variables (`resolveEffectiveApeironRoot` and `resolveEffectiveArtifactsRoot` in `graphConfig.ts`), which win over `aperas.config.json`. So a second pair is four variables and one scratch directory each.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000X",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The `aperas` command is bound to one checkout**",
    "text": "**The `aperas` command is bound to one checkout**: `/home/will/.local/bin/aperas` runs `cd /home/will/source/Aperas/monorepo && node_modules/.bin/tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts`. The new engine is run as `cd /home/will/source/Aperas.dev/monorepo && env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH node_modules/.bin/tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts …` with its own variables; the reference gets the same with the `Aperas` path and a second set of variables.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000Y",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The copies**",
    "text": "**The copies**: `AperasKG/Apeiron` is 7.8 MB with `.state/` and `artifacts/` is 4.5 MB. Both copies must come from one snapshot, taken after `aperas flush` on the real service (the files on disk lag its memory by up to 10 s, `FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS`, `service.ts:97`) or from `git` at one commit, and then cloned: `makeCorpusCopy` (`corpus.ts:36-62`) copies only `Apeiron` and leaves `artifacts/` empty, which is enough for graph-only commands but not for `track`, `ingest` and `project`, which read the markdown tree.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000Z",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the harness has to normalise** (none of it exists)",
    "text": "**What the harness has to normalise** (none of it exists): (a) ids minted by a command come from `snowflake.ts` (a clock, the machine number and a sequence), so two runs mint different ids; the comparer has to map the k-th new id of one run to the k-th of the other, and `APERAS_MACHINE_NUMBER` must be one value for both; (b) timestamps (`lastTrackedAt`, `lastIngestedAt`, `tombstonedAt`, `new Date().toISOString()` at 11 production sites) differ between runs; (c) both dumps are sorted by `@id`, with `localeCompare` on one side and code point on the other (deliberate), and sets are sorted by the same rule, so the comparer parses both and compares by id and as sets, and `children` as lists; (d) the stdout of a command lists ids of a kind or subjects in an order that differs (the lists in (4)), so each listing is either sorted before comparing or recorded as a deliberate difference.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFA810010",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**A script of commands** has to be written",
    "text": "**A script of commands** has to be written: the 22 of the 27 verbs of `aperas.ts` that reach the service (`init`, `service`, `serve`, `identity` and `skill` do not), each with `--flush`, then a final `flush` and a compare of `Apeiron/` and `.state/`. Anything not reachable by a verb (the sweeps at boot, reload and shutdown) is reached by `reload`, `flush --clobber` and a restart of the isolated service.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFA81000T",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YFXDC8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
