    "title": "Five listings take their order from the engine's",
    "text": "Five listings take their order from the engine's: the report of `checkLinkIntegrity` (`linkIntegrity.ts:112`, so the output of `check-links` and the `linkWarning` text of the service); `track --reverse` (`kgTrack.ts:82-110`); the profile and view lists (`kgProfile.ts:65,111`); `backlinks` (`node.ts:2131-2133`, which gives `kgBacklinks.ts:32` its printed order, `kgProfile.ts:69` its list of views and `removeProfile` its cascade); and the links of a block in `tree`, `unfold` and the web ([the newest-first issue](#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001)). Two more depend on first-seen order: `buildLiveSlugPathIndex` (`node.ts:957-965`, \"first writer wins per name\", which decides the block a collision error names) and `orderedChildIds` (`storeAccess.ts:188-196`, whose stable sort leaves a child with no sibling index, or two with one index, in match order).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800E",
