    "title": "**Removal is deletion**",
    "text": "**Removal is deletion**: removing the stray `README.md` artifacts from the mirror is an outright deletion. A tombstone would only need the engine to run again to wipe it, with the same net result.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YG30JR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YG30K0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Nothing points at them (checked by the orchestrator on the census clone `/home/will/scratch/AperasKG-clone2`)**",
    "text": "**Nothing points at them (checked by the orchestrator on the census clone `/home/will/scratch/AperasKG-clone2`)**: of the six `README.md` artifacts and their six paragraphs, the only references in `Apeiron/` are each artifact's own `children` entry and its paragraph's `parent`. No `Link` targets any of the twelve, no `FolderNode` lists an artifact as a child, and no `TreeView` unfolds or roots at one. In `.state/` they appear only as ids in the text of thread blocks, not as a `Link`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YG30JR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3YTQJ4R001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YG30K0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What they are**",
    "text": "**What they are**: each artifact is `type: root`, holds one paragraph whose text is the folder's own description, and is parentless. A folder projects to its own `README.md` (`aperas project <folder>` writes to its README), so these artifacts duplicate a file the folder already owns. The dry run must check that a `track` or `ingest` after the deletion does not register them again.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YG30JR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YG30K0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The stop of the trial service was refused by the classifier**",
    "text": "**The stop of the trial service was refused by the classifier**: the coder's command `source trial-env.sh && npm run aperas -- service stop`, run from `Aperas.dev/monorepo`, was denied under the reason \"Interfere With Workloads\". It stops a service the coder had started itself, on port 2799, but the command line alone reads as a stop of the shared service. The coder did not retry or work around it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YG30JR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
