    "title": "**9. Manual links removed**",
    "text": "**9. Manual links removed**: a `Link` is a wikilink and has no `predicate`. The feature of a manual link, one told from a wikilink by its `predicate` (what `aperas link` added and `aperas unlink` removed), is dropped: it was never used and the mirror holds none ([every `Link` carries a `predicate`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG001)). The question of whether the shell keeps the field until a linking design gives the types of links is answered: it does not. The step is done before steps 3 and 5, whose render and ingest read the `predicate`. It removes the six sites that tell the two kinds apart (`artifacts.ts:606`, where `resolveBlockLinks` keeps the non-wikilink links of a block and regenerates the wikilink ones; `node.ts:1067`, `collectOldWikilinksByBlock`; `node.ts:343-345` and `:369`, `addLink` and `mintWikilink`; `kgLink.ts:56`, where `aperas unlink` removes only `references` links; `kgUnfold.ts:113,144` and `node.ts:1936,1940`, the text `[Link]  <predicate> → <target>` of `tree` and `unfold`, with the `predicate` of the render JSON that `web/src/render.ts:42` and `FolderDiv.tsx:534` read); the verbs `aperas link` and `aperas unlink` (`kgLink.ts`, `kgUnlink.ts` and their entries in `aperas.ts`); the text of `tree` and `unfold` that depends on the predicate; and its uses in the tests (`ingest/chain.test.ts:134,148,159`, `gc/collection.test.ts:63`, `store/views.test.ts`). The dropping of the `predicate` from the mirror is [Batch 9, step 6](#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YG50B0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Open points of the batch**",
    "text": "**Open points of the batch**: four points that the survey of the callers raised, all settled: the mirror of the differential run, and, by the answers of 2026-10-20, the other three; each gated the steps it names.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
