    "title": "**Which mirror the differential run starts from**",
    "text": "**Which mirror the differential run starts from**: settled. The migrated mirror is not readable by the reference code, which needs the `predicate` to tell wikilinks from manual links (`artifacts.ts:606`) and reads removed nodes through the `children` of their container; on a mirror migrated as [step 6 of Batch 9](#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001) migrates it, the reference would treat every existing link as manual and add a second wikilink per target at the next ingest, and its dump would differ from the new engine's for a reason that is not a finding. The two designs have no mirror in common, so the reference starts from an unmigrated copy of the mirror and the new engine from the migrated copy of it, and the dumps are compared after the differences that the migration and the design make on purpose are normalised; the migration's own changes are in the list of deliberate differences of [Verification Plan layer 4](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002). The drop of manual links in step 9 changes the new code and the migrated mirror and not the frozen reference.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YG50B0000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
