    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), on a service of the checkout `Aperas.dev` over a clone of the current graph**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), on a service of the checkout `Aperas.dev` over a clone of the current graph**: the start took 6 to 7 s (the clone held about 78.7k quads and 8,700 blocks), against the `READY_TIMEOUT_MS = 5_000` of `serviceClient.ts`. `aperas service start` and `aperas service restart` printed \"did not become ready in time\" and exited 1 in 3 of 3 starts, although the service came up and the lock turned `ready`; a script that trusts the exit code reads the start as failed. For scale on the same clone, a read verb took 0.85 to 1.15 s through `npm run` (about 0.85 s of it `npm` and `tsx`), a write with `--flush` 2 to 4 s, a `project` write 2.6 s, `check-links` 3.6 to 3.8 s, a `reload` 7.8 to 8.3 s, and the resident memory was 209 to 219 MB after a collection, 360 to 410 MB just after the start and 430 to 495 MB after writes and a full-size load. Nothing was changed. Judged in [Batch 13](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0010), step 2 (the time to ready at boot against the client's waits); no step of the plan changes the constant.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W05P08001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
