    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), on a document and not the corpus**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), on a document and not the corpus**: on a service of the checkout `Aperas.dev` over a clone of the current graph, `aperas ingest discussion/trial-scratch.md` (one new document) stopped on an interactive confirmation that named a folder \"permanently removed: 'null' (folder)\", the folder's name printed as the string `null`, and waited on standard input for 211 s. It did not repeat for a second document, and with `</dev/null` the later runs did not prompt. The root cause is not found: why a folder with no name was proposed for removal at all is not traced, so the prompt may not be only the one of a corpus-wide ingest. An unscripted caller hangs here. The removal detection moves with the ingest in [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), step 5; the prompt itself (a `--yes` flag or a `stdin.isTTY` check) belongs to no step of the plan.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YH8H08001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), three more times**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), three more times**: in the survey of the callers, `aperas tree design/core.md` and `aperas unfold BlockNode:00D24N87T0003` answered \"No ApeironNgn service running\" while the service processes were alive, for about 40 s and then about 20 s, and waiting and retrying worked each time. In the isolated service trial, one `ingest` right after another call returned the same message on the trial's service, whose ping timeout of 300 ms the busy service had missed; the retry worked. Nothing was started, stopped or restarted in either case.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The trial and the survey, filed 2026-10-15**",
    "text": "**The trial and the survey, filed 2026-10-15**: what the isolated service trial of `Aperas.dev`'s `aperas` and the Coder's survey of the callers before Batch 11 found, copied up from the Coder's thread.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
