    "title": "**The isolated service trial**",
    "text": "**The isolated service trial**: `Aperas.dev`'s `aperas` works end to end against its own service on a clone of the current `AperasKG`: `tree`, `show`, `backlinks`, `resolve`, `path`, `unfold`, `zoom`, `profile` (list, create-view), `track`, `ingest`, `insert`, `update`, `remove`, `project` (dry run and write), `flush`, `reload`, `check-links` and `service start` and `stop` all ran, and the read output matched the real graph byte for byte. The service was isolated by its own `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` and `APERAS_HTTP_PORT` and by the graph roots set in the environment.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G003",
      "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G004",
      "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G005",
      "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G006"
    ]
  },
  {
