        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D3YHF20G003",
    "text": "**Timings and memory** on the clone (about 78.7k quads, 8,700 blocks): a read verb 0.85 to 1.15 s through `npm run` (about 0.85 s of it `npm` and `tsx`; the real shim takes 0.5 to 0.9 s), a write with `--flush` 2 to 4 s, a `project` write 2.6 s, `check-links` 3.6 to 3.8 s (as on the real service), a `reload` 7.8 to 8.3 s and a cold start about 6 to 7 s. Resident memory was 209 to 219 MB after a collection, 360 to 410 MB just after the start and 430 to 495 MB after writes and a full-size load; the real service holds about 350 MB for a similar graph.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Env-bound roots**",
    "text": "**Env-bound roots**: `Aperas.dev/AperasKG` is a symlink to the real graph, and `npm run` pins the working directory to `monorepo/`, so without `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT` and `APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT` the dev tree's service would silently bind the real `AperasKG` (the hop-counted fallback in `core/src/graphConfig.ts`). Running from the clone's directory so that its own `aperas.config.json` applies is not possible through `npm run aperas --`; the environment variables were used. Not filed as an issue; a Question to the orchestrator.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3Z1RJ8R001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Clone fidelity**",
    "text": "**Clone fidelity**: a `git clone` has neither the uncommitted staged changes nor `.state/`, which holds about 40% of the real graph (threads and views), so the first runs (47.6k quads, 5,220 blocks) were a lighter test than the real graph; `.state/` has to be copied in before the first start, or the first collection prunes a tombstone the real graph keeps.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
