    "title": "00D3YHF20G009",
    "text": "The first Question of the survey, the predicate of a `Link`, is answered by [No manual links](#id/BlockNode:00D3YB0MCG003): option (b) of the survey, drop it now and remove `aperas link` and `aperas unlink`. The other four (tombstones leave their container, the mirror of the differential run, the order differences, the regrouping) are recorded as [open points of Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0000) and decided by no one yet.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YHF20G007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decisions on the migration and the differential run, 2026-10-15**",
    "text": "**Decisions on the migration and the differential run, 2026-10-15**: the user settled the rest of the migration and the shape of the comparison.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG002",
      "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG003",
      "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG004"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG002:props:StringProp:00D3YN5Y2R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG002:props:StringProp:00D3YN5Y2R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Tombstones are stripped from the tree**",
    "text": "**Tombstones are stripped from the tree**: the migration takes the full reading. A tombstone loses its content (the `props` that 40 of the 188 in the mirror still hold, and the `children` and `links` that some in `.state/` hold) and also its `parent` and its entry in its container's `children`, as the design's Containment states. So the migration is: drop the `predicate` from every `Link`, strip the tombstones from the tree, delete the six `README.md` artifacts and their paragraphs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3YTNE2G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No shared mirror for the two engines**",
    "text": "**No shared mirror for the two engines**: the migrated mirror is not readable by the old engine, which needs the `predicate` and reads removed nodes through `children`; two incompatible designs have no common mirror. The differential run therefore starts the reference from an unmigrated copy and the new engine from the migrated copy of it, and compares the dumps after normalising the differences that the migration and the design make on purpose.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3YTPFER001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The stop of the trial service**",
    "text": "**The stop of the trial service**: the orchestrator ran the command the classifier had refused for the coder, and it passed without a refusal (pid 739924 stopped, port 2799 free, the real service on 2736 untouched). The refusal was a quirk of the classifier. The user asked that the memory rule on retrying a refused command cover any interference by the harness, and it now does.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YN5FWG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YS41VR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**42 live `BlockNode`s have no `parent` and no container lists them**",
    "text": "**42 live `BlockNode`s have no `parent` and no container lists them**: found 2026-10-15 in the Coder's census of a clone of the mirror, which counted the parentless nodes. Filed 2026-10-15.",
