    "title": "**The live blocks and the artifact that have no parent, settled 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The live blocks and the artifact that have no parent, settled 2026-10-16**: besides the six `README.md` artifacts that step 6 deletes, a census of a clone of the mirror (the files of `Apeiron/` and `Apeiron/.state/`) finds 42 live `BlockNode`s and one live `ArtifactNode`, `concepts.md`, with no `parent`, and the root folder, which has none by definition. No container lists any of the 42 blocks or `concepts.md` in its `children`, so none is reachable by containment; no `Link` targets them and no `TreeView` names them. Eight of the blocks have children of their own (3 to 7 each), whose `parent` points at them, and no other node refers to them. Elsewhere `parent` and `children` agree (no disagreement, no repeated id, no node in two containers). The 42 are 8 headings, 29 list items and 5 paragraphs; the list is in [42 live blocks have no `parent` and no container lists them](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YS41VR001) and, for the artifact, in [one live artifact, `concepts.md`, has no `parent`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3F6RJCG001). Decided 2026-10-16 (the user): the migration leaves all 43 as they stand, `concepts.md` included, so that they test how the new engine handles nodes that nothing reaches, the case of [garbage collection never collects an unreachable block that was never tombstoned](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D1A2AY68001). Nothing uses `concepts.md` now and it could be removed, but it is kept for that test. The migrated mirror of step 6 holds them as they stand, and so does the baseline of Layer 3 on the real mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
