    "title": "Tombstones also stay in the tree",
    "text": "Tombstones also stay in the tree: 187 of the 188 in `Apeiron/` still carry a `parent` and are listed in the `children` of their container (the one without a `parent` is `BlockNode:00CR9SRMW8002`), and all 31 in `Apeiron/.state/` carry a `parent`, where [Tombstones](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01V) and [A removed node leaves its container](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000R) say a tombstone has none and is in no container's list. 142 of the 188 in `Apeiron/` keep a `text`, as the design allows. Two `Link`s in `Apeiron/` target a tombstoned node (`BlockNode:00CN1PKAQG001:links:Link:00CN1PKEW8002` and `BlockNode:00D24NRBSR001:links:Link:00D24NRQBG002`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D252W7VG002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3YTEXXR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3YTEXXR001",
    "text": "Checked 2026-10-15 on a clone of the mirror (`Apeiron/` and `Apeiron/.state/`, read with `jq`): the six are `ArtifactNode:00CN1QE950000` (`README.md`), `ArtifactNode:00CN4ZQ8Y0000` (`design/README.md`), `ArtifactNode:00CN4ZSF58000` (`discussion/README.md`), `ArtifactNode:00CN4ZTZRR000` (`issues/README.md`), `ArtifactNode:00CN4ZWHCG000` (`planning/README.md`) and `ArtifactNode:00CN4ZXWJ8000` (`history/README.md`). All are live and of `type` `root`; each has a `description` that is its abstract and a `text` that is its summary, and one child, a `paragraph` with no children and no links (`BlockNode:00CN1QEAGG001`, `BlockNode:00CN4ZQAPG001`, `BlockNode:00CN4ZSHMG001`, `BlockNode:00CN4ZV1G8001`, `BlockNode:00CN4ZWJMG001`, `BlockNode:00CN4ZXXRR001`), and no other block. Nothing points at the twelve nodes: the only references in `Apeiron/` are each artifact's own `children` entry and its paragraph's `parent`; no `Link` targets an artifact or its paragraph, from any owner in `Apeiron/` or `Apeiron/.state/`; no `FolderNode` lists an artifact as a child; no `TreeView` unfolds or roots at one. In `Apeiron/.state/` the ids occur only in the text of thread blocks, never as a `Link`. A folder projects to its own `README.md` (`aperas project <folder>` writes to it), so the six artifacts duplicate files that the folders already own.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WTZG9G002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
