    "title": "00D3YV43Q0007",
    "text": "Decided 2026-10-15 (the user), in two parts. (1) The hash and timestamp fields that projection or ingest sets (`projectedHash`, `fileHash`, `ingestedHash`, `lastIngestedAt` and `lastTrackedAt`) and the `kind` of a `Profile` become optional in the shapes. The design edit is made (2026-10-16): [Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M) declares them optional and [the sentence on the `one` fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Y) no longer names them. (2) The migration of the mirror ([Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001)) fills only `kind: human` of `Profile:00CJC4S69R000` (`dinhlx`), which lacks `kind`. `Profile:00CA03JXD8000` (`default`) lacks `kind` and `name`: it is the auto-generated fallback for everyone, so it has no `kind` and none can be given, because it cannot know. Decided 2026-10-16: [`Profile.name` is optional](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00W) too, so `default` is a valid document without a `name`, and the open point of Batch 9 on it ([Whether `default` has a `name`](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D41MK9N0001)) is closed. What remains, so the issue stays open: the real mirror gets the `kind` of `dinhlx` at the cutover (done on a clone only).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3YV43Q0006",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
