    "title": "**Which of them can be waived**",
    "text": "**Which of them can be waived**: only `runLinkCandidates`, which only `aperas link` calls, so it goes with that verb in step 9, done before steps 3 and 5. Every other command is tested. [The differential script](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0013) of Layer 4 runs the 22 verbs of `aperas.ts` that reach the service, each with `--flush`, and compares the dumps and the output, but it is Batch 13, after the flip, and between the flip and Batch 13 nothing else checks the commands. So `runPath`, `runFold`, `runZoom` and `runProfile*` are written as well, since they cost two files together (`views.test.ts` and `resolve.test.ts`) and sit with step 11, which moves them; the render (`runTree`, `runShow`, `runUnfold`, about 690 lines of `node.ts` whose order the script compares only after normalising), `runResolve` (it moves onto the primitives of Batch 10), `runRemove`, `runProject`, `runTrack`, `runReverseTrack` and the service, whose sweeps at boot, reload and shutdown the script reaches only through `reload`, `flush --clobber` and a restart, were never proposed for a waiver.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Z01YER001",
    "type": "listItem",
