    ],
    "title": "00D3Z1PHRR003",
    "text": "`resolveFallbackGraphRoot()` in `packages/core/src/graphConfig.ts` resolves `<repo root>/AperasKG`. In the checkout `Aperas.dev` that path is a symlink to the real graph, so the unset case of `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT`, `APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT` and `APERAS_GRAPH_NAME` binds the real graph, with no error and no sign.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3Z1PHRR004",
    "text": "`resolveEffectiveApeironRoot` takes the environment variable first, then an `aperas.config.json` found by walking up from the start directory, then the fallback. `npm run aperas --` pins the working directory to `monorepo/`, so the walk starts there and a clone's own `aperas.config.json` is not found through it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3Z1PHRR005",
    "text": "The trial used the variables, so it did not bind the real graph; a run without them would have.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D3Z1PHRR006",
    "text": "**Fix directions** (listed, not chosen)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR007",
      "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR008",
      "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR009"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR007:props:StringProp:00D3Z1Q020000",
