      }
    ],
    "title": "**The service had been started twice**",
    "text": "**The service had been started twice**: the user started a second service after searching `ps` for the wrong name. The second instance replaced the socket, the lock and the token, then died on the HTTP port that the first held, leaving the first running and unreachable, and every command answered \"No ApeironNgn service running\". The user killed both and restarted. It is not a defect of the agents' use of `service start`, and the start-timeout issue stays as it is; whether `service start` should refuse when a service process is alive is not decided.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D40RVX48000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D40RVX5R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the ghost folder is**",
    "text": "**What the ghost folder is**: `FolderNode:00CR5AN248000` is the `.threads` folder; its document, with `holder: true`, lives only in `.state/`. The root folder's `children` in the tracked mirror names it. The user had thought of the threads subgraph as isolated from the main graph through `parent` and had missed `children` as a reference from the main graph into it. Without `.state/` the id loads as a live folder with no path and no `holder`, and `ingestFolderTree` lists it for removal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D40RVX48000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D40RVX60000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Fix now, in the working engine**",
    "text": "**Fix now, in the working engine**: the multi-graph design is not in scope, so the dangling reference is worked around with the enhanced filter (keep only live `FolderNode`s that have a document and a path), and fixed now together with the stdin prompt: a flag that answers every removal prompt of `ingest` and `track` with no, and no refusal on a missing terminal. This is on branch `oxigraph` of `Aperas/`, the engine the workflow uses.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D40RVX48000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D40RVX68000",
