    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D40RVX6G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Profiles**",
    "text": "**Profiles**: `dinhlx` is a human, the user. `default` is the auto-generated fallback for everyone and cannot have a `kind`, because it cannot know.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D40RVX48000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D410ZGN8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The machine is overloaded, and the service may burn CPU while idle, 2026-10-15**",
    "text": "**The machine is overloaded, and the service may burn CPU while idle, 2026-10-15**: the user reported that the whole computer is sluggish with the CPU always at 100%. At 18:55 the load average was 12 on 4 cores. The orchestrator saw the coder's `npm run verify` runs (parallel test workers, bursts of about 25 s), the desktop programs (Paseo, Chrome, the system monitor), and the real service (pid 781595) at a steady 23% (12 minutes of CPU in 52 minutes of life); the orphaned service of earlier (pid 776226), which no client could reach, had also sat at 29%, so the service seems to use CPU while idle. The user decided to start from the clone with its own `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` and `APERAS_HTTP_PORT`, to measure that in isolation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001:links:Link:00D4185H9G000",
