        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001:links:Link:00D4185H9G000:props:StringProp:00D4185HA0000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "298"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**A `children` entry of the root folder in the tracked mirror names the `.threads` folder, whose document lives only in `.state/`: a dangling reference from the main graph into the threads graph, which `ingest` reads as a ghost folder to remove**",
    "text": "**A `children` entry of the root folder in the tracked mirror names the `.threads` folder, whose document lives only in `.state/`: a dangling reference from the main graph into the threads graph, which `ingest` reads as a ghost folder to remove**: found 2026-10-15 by the Coder in the debugging of [the `ingest` prompt](#id/BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001). Filed 2026-10-15.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG00J",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D417WK80002",
      "BlockNode:00D417WK9R000",
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA0001",
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA8001",
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA8003",
      "BlockNode:00D4579FMR001",
      "BlockNode:00D7V4WWG8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002:props:StringProp:00D4185GVG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002:props:StringProp:00D4185GVR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D417WK80002",
    "text": "**Symptom**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D417WK80003",
      "BlockNode:00D417WK98000",
      "BlockNode:00D417WK9G000",
      "BlockNode:00D417WK9G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80003:props:StringProp:00D4185GWG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK80003:props:StringProp:00D4185GWR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D417WK80003",
    "text": "`FolderNode:00CR5AN248000` is the `.threads` folder; its document, with `holder: true`, lives only in `Apeiron/.state/`, and the `children` of the root folder in the tracked mirror (`Apeiron/`) names it. The threads graph was thought isolated from the main graph through `parent`, and `children` is a reference from the main graph into it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK98000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D417WK98000",
    "text": "Without `.state/` (a `git clone`, a CI run, a fresh harness copy) the id loads as a live folder with no path and no `holder`, and `ingestFolderTree` lists it for removal. Every `ingest` reaches it, with paths or without and with `--track` or without, because the folder sweep runs each time; `track` with paths cannot, for it never runs the removal sweep. The proposed removal prints the folder's name as `null`, since JSON turns a missing path into `null`, and the prompt waits on standard input because nothing checks for a terminal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK9G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "With standard input closed (`</dev/null`) the answer is no",
    "text": "With standard input closed (`</dev/null`) the answer is no: nothing is removed, the rest of the ingest still lands, the exit code is 0 and the hold-back is only a message in the output; with standard input open and silent the prompt blocks for good. `--force` is no way round it, since it tombstones the ghost and writes a `FolderNode:00CR5AN248000` tombstone into the tracked mirror. A copy without `.state/` also drops the root's `children` entry on its first ingest.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK9G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D417WK9G001",
    "text": "It cannot fire on the real graph or on a copy that carries `.state/`; it can fire in the harness and the dry runs of the new engine's plan if their copies are made without `.state/`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK9R000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D417WK9R000",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code by the Coder)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D417WK9R001",
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA0000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK9R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK9R001:props:StringProp:00D4185GZG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WK9R001:props:StringProp:00D4185GZR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D417WK9R001",
    "text": "`ingestFolderTree` in `core/src/apeironNgn/folders.ts` (lines 20 to 22 and 56 to 57) treats any id with the prefix `FolderNode:` that is a subject in the store as a live folder. The ghost has no path, so `pendingRemovals` carries `undefined`, which JSON turns into `null` (`folders.ts:152`, `kgIngest.ts:148`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK9R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0000:links:Link:00D4185HB8000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0000:links:Link:00D4185HB8000:props:StringProp:00D4185HBG000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "221"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D417WKA0000",
    "text": "The reference exists because the multi-graph design that would keep the threads graph apart is not built: the tracked mirror lists the id in the `children` of its container, and the document is written to `.state/` only ([Containment](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z) states what a container lists).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK9R000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D417WKA0001",
    "text": "**Fix directions**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA0002",
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA8000"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0002:links:Link:00D4185HCG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0002:links:Link:00D4185HCG000:props:StringProp:00D4185HCR000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "338"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0002:props:StringProp:00D4185H1R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0002:props:StringProp:00D4185H28000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "Decided 2026-10-15 (the user)",
    "text": "Decided 2026-10-15 (the user): the multi-graph design is out of scope, so the dangling reference is worked around and not removed. The workaround is the enhanced filter, which keeps only the live `FolderNode`s that have a document and a path (the one-line change at `folders.ts:56`), and it is fixed now together with the stdin prompt of [the `ingest` prompt issue](#id/BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001): a flag that answers every removal prompt of `ingest` and `track` with no, and no refusal on a missing terminal (a refusal on a missing terminal would break `echo yes | aperas project` and the piped answers that `lineReader.ts` states as a design goal). It is made on branch `oxigraph` of `Aperas/`, the engine the workflow uses. A coder is making it now; this issue stays open until the coder reports.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D417WKA8000",
    "text": "The multi-graph design that would remove the reference is not in scope.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WKA0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D417WKA8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D417WKA8001",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D417WKA8002"
    ]
  },
  {
