        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D419V27R001:links:Link:00D41A1EX0000:props:StringProp:00D41A1EX8000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "0"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "[The ghost folder](#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001)",
    "text": "[The ghost folder](#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001): the `children` of the root folder in the tracked mirror names the `.threads` folder, whose document lives only in `.state/`, so a load of the mirror without `.state/` meets an id that is referenced and never defined, the case this list is for; what the caller does with it is the service lifecycle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D258W09800D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D41A7ZR8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-15, the user)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-15, the user)**: no code change is intended, and none of the fix directions (a), (b) and (c) is pursued; the symlink is left as it is. The mechanism is the one that (a) names for a cloned mirror: running `tsx packages/cli/src/aperas.ts` from the clone's directory, whose portable `aperas.config.json` the walk of `resolveEffectiveApeironRoot` finds (the orchestrator checked that the roots resolve to the clone from there, with no variable set). A second service still needs its own `XDG_RUNTIME_DIR` and `APERAS_HTTP_PORT`, because the lock, the socket, the token and the port are per user.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D41MK9N0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D41MK9N0001:links:Link:00D41MRG80000",
        "@type": "Link",
