    "title": "Promoted to [Core — Planning](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF23FB1G001) and [issues](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG001)",
    "text": "Promoted to [Core — Planning](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF23FB1G001) and [issues](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG001): the ghost folder is filed as [a dangling reference from the main graph into the threads graph](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001), with its cause and decision recorded in [the `ingest` prompt issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001) and the second `service start` in [the start issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W05P08001); the roots decision resolves [the issue on the unset roots](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Z1PHRR001); the tests decision is in [no test calls most commands](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC8001), [step 10 of Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Z01YER001) and [Layer 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AG001); the profiles decision is in [Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001), its [open points](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8001) and [the issue of the missing fields](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YV43Q0001); the harness requirements are in [Batch 13, step 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0013) and [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D40RVX48000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The slowdown was a CPU clamp, 2026-10-15**",
    "text": "**The slowdown was a CPU clamp, 2026-10-15**: the user rebooted, the machine recovered, and the evidence from the day was re-read.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D454XWTG002",
      "BlockNode:00D454XWTR000",
      "BlockNode:00D454XWTR001",
      "BlockNode:00D454XWTR002"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG002:props:StringProp:00D454YBCR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG002:props:StringProp:00D454YBCR001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**What was measured**",
    "text": "**What was measured**: before the first reboot the CPU held its minimum clock of 400 MHz under full load (all four cores, `powersave` governor with the `performance` energy preference, a 4.2 GHz ceiling, no OS-visible limit, no change in the package throttle counter during a 6 s burn), and a 10M-iteration Python loop took 7.85 s. After the reboot the cores held 4.1 to 4.2 GHz through a 70 s burn at 72 to 74 °C, and the same loop took 0.62 s, 12.7 times faster. The journal shows three boots that day (the 5-day one ended 20:44, then 20:45 to 22:43, then the current one); in the second the user ran `turbostat`, `cpupower frequency-set`, stopped `power-profiles-daemon` and `thermald`, and read MSR `0x1FC`, so the slowdown seems to have returned within the hour. The cause below the OS (firmware or the embedded controller; the laptop is an Acer Aspire Go 15, BIOS 1.03) is not known; the user has a logger (`cpulog.sh`, in `~/.local/bin`, output in `~/tmp/cpulog`, started from `.profile`) to catch the next onset.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What it changes in this work**",
    "text": "**What it changes in this work**: every timing taken between about 18:00 and the reboot was taken on a CPU running about 12.7 times slower than normal: the service's 30 s inserts and its 99% CPU, the 57 s of service CPU for one insert in the idle-CPU trial (5,693 ticks), the 57 s start of the real service, the 294 s `commit` suite and the \"No ApeironNgn service running\" answers when the 300 ms ping timed out. 57 s divided by 12.7 is about 4.5 s, which fits the filed profile (1.6 to 3.2 s of CPU per insert on 7,433 live blocks; the graph is about 30% bigger now). The orchestrator had called it about 18 times the profile; that reading was wrong. The idle result stands (0% over four 60 s windows, counted in ticks, which do not depend on the clock speed): the service has no timer that works while idle.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Checked at normal speed**",
    "text": "**Checked at normal speed**: the `commit` suite passed 70 of 70 in 19.6 s (budget 60 s), `essential` 27 of 27 in 2.9 s (budget 5 s), the groups `folder,prompt,ingest` 19 of 19 in 1.4 s; reads of the real service take 0.52 s and `aperas check-links` 3.7 s; the service starts in about 7 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D454XWTR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The user's decision**",
    "text": "**The user's decision**: do the graph work (record the ghost-folder and prompt fix as resolved, record the clamp correction) and make a fresh clone of the graph after it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D454XWTG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D4583SDG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4579FMR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-15)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-15)**: both private `allLiveIdsOfKind` helpers now keep only the live nodes that have a `path`, so the ghost is no longer a live node: the filter `path !== undefined` is at `core/src/apeironNgn/folders.ts:20` (it feeds `ingestFolderTree`, so the removal sweep no longer lists the `.threads` folder, and `existingByPath`, `folderIdByPath`, `liveArtifactIds` and `getFolderRecord`) and at `core/src/apeironNgn/artifacts.ts:197` (it feeds `trackAllArtifacts`, so a full `track` no longer reports it). The ghost `ArtifactNode` was reproduced the same way: named in the root's `children`, it made a full `track` return `pendingRemovals: [undefined]` before the fix and no longer does. Folders really gone from disk and folders flagged `holder` that have a document behave as before (both tested).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D417WK80001",
