  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D457ANWR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-15)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-15)**: `aperas ingest` and `aperas track` take `--no-prompt`. `confirmRemoval` in `cli/src/removalPrompt.ts` (new) then returns no at once, before any readline and any write of the question, so standard input is never read; the removals are still listed and the \"Skipped\" line is printed. `--force` is checked first and still wins. There is no `isTTY` check, so `echo yes | aperas ingest` keeps working and a closed stdin still counts as no. The flag is parsed, kept out of `<path>...` and documented in the help of each command. The prompts of `project` and of `link` are untouched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001",
