    "title": "**Every timing carries its calibration**",
    "text": "**Every timing carries its calibration**: a timing is taken with a calibration beside it, the clock of the cores (`scaling_cur_freq`, read under the load) and the time of a fixed 10M-iteration Python loop (about 0.6 s at normal speed). A timing taken when the calibration is off is discarded, not corrected. A clamped CPU, held at its 400 MHz minimum, made the timings of one evening 12.7 times too slow and passed for a defect of the service ([the cost of a write](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D457M2F8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), a figure taken on a clamped CPU**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), a figure taken on a clamped CPU**: between about 18:00 on 2026-10-15 and the first reboot the CPU held its 400 MHz minimum clock under full load, and a fixed 10M-iteration Python loop took 7.85 s against 0.62 s after the reboot, 12.7 times slower. The 57 s of service CPU for one insert in the idle-CPU trial of that evening (5,693 ticks) was measured on that CPU, so at normal speed it is about 4.5 s, which fits the profile of this entry (1.6 to 3.2 s of CPU per insert on 7,433 live blocks; the graph is about 30% bigger now). The live service was not profiled.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D457M2F8002",
      "BlockNode:00D457M2F8003"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D457M2F8002",
