    ],
    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), the 57 s start was the clamp**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), the 57 s start was the clamp**: the start of 57 s of the real service in the evening of 2026-10-15 was taken on a CPU clamped to its 400 MHz minimum, 12.7 times slower than normal (a fixed 10M-iteration Python loop took 7.85 s against 0.62 s after the reboot). At normal speed the service listens about 7 s after its launch, in line with the 6 to 7 s of the observation above on the clone. The command still prints \"did not become ready in time\", because the wait stays 5 s by the user's decision, and the target stands that the new engine's start is ready within it. The rule that a timing is taken with a calibration beside it is in [Layer 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D457HDWG001) of the Verification Plan.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D0W05P08001",
