    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), a busy service looked stopped, and the message led to a second start**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-15), a busy service looked stopped, and the message led to a second start**: reads and writes answered \"No ApeironNgn service running\" again and again while the service process was alive and listening. At its slowest the CPU was clamped ([the clamp](#id/BlockNode:00D457M2F8001)), but any request that keeps the service busy for over 300 ms does it: `PING_TIMEOUT_MS = 300` (`cli/src/apeironNgn/serviceClient.ts:23`), and `ensureServiceRunning` (line 149) throws the message at line 151 whenever the ping fails, a busy service included. A person who followed the message ran `aperas service start` a second time, and it replaced the socket, the lock and the token and left the first service running and unreachable ([the second `service start`](#id/BlockNode:00D4198VGG001)). Read from the code, not run: `runStart` (`cli/src/kgService.ts:50-56`) pings with the same 300 ms and, when the ping fails, clears the lock without asking whether its pid is alive and spawns another service; that fits the observation.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CVMPABY8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D457SD20000",
      "BlockNode:00D457SD20001"
    ]
