        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Fix directions, listed and not chosen**",
    "text": "**Fix directions, listed and not chosen**: a longer or adaptive timeout; a retry; telling a refused connection (no service) from a timeout (a busy one) in the message; checking that the lock's pid is alive (`isProcessAlive` exists in `serviceLock`) before the message and before `runStart` clears the lock; making `service start` refuse when a service process is alive. They add to the \"Fix to try\" above.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D457SD1R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
