  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4JR88A0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Go for the migration dry run, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Go for the migration dry run, 2026-10-16**: the user said to go with the dry run: a coder writes the migration as a script and runs it only on the clone `/home/will/scratch/AperasKG-dryrun` (byte-identical to the real graph when made), and shows the result; the real mirror is touched only after the user has seen the diff and approved a second time. The migration is the one the user settled: drop the `predicate` from every `Link`; strip the tombstones from the tree (content, `parent` and the entry in the container's `children`, keeping the literals `title`, `text`, `tombstonedAt`); delete outright the six `README.md` artifacts and their six paragraphs; set `kind: human` on `dinhlx`. Whether a `track` or `ingest` after the deletion registers the READMEs again is tested separately, on a copy that has only the deletion applied, because the old engine needs the `predicate`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**After the dry run, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**After the dry run, 2026-10-16**: the dry run on `/home/will/scratch/AperasKG-dryrun` passed (round trip exact before any change; 3,934 links lost their `predicate`; 218 tombstones stripped and 107 containers edited; 12 README documents deleted; `dinhlx` got `kind: human`; 0 differences outside the four rules over 9,584 documents; a second run changed nothing; the README test on a copy with only the deletion applied showed that `ingest --no-prompt` and `track` do not bring a README back), and the real tracked files kept their hashes. The orchestrator re-checked the migrated clone (0 `predicate`, 0 dirty tombstones, 0 containers listing a tombstone).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8002",
      "BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8003",
      "BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8004",
      "BlockNode:00D4JZXA1R001"
    ]
  },
