    "title": "**Apply at cutover only**",
    "text": "**Apply at cutover only**: the migrated mirror cannot be read properly by the working engine, which needs the `predicate` and reads removed nodes through `children`, so the migration of the real mirror is a step of the cutover, as Batch 9 step 6 says; before it the dry run is repeated on a fresh clone, since the real mirror moves on, and the real one is migrated after a flush and with the service stopped.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D4JZYCJG001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`concepts.md`**",
    "text": "**`concepts.md`**: `track` offered to permanently remove `concepts.md` because no such file exists under `artifacts/` (in the real graph or the clone) while the graph keeps its node `ArtifactNode:00CR5AEJ88000`; it is harmless unless a prompt is answered yes.",
