    ],
    "title": "**The dry run, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The dry run, 2026-10-16**: the migration was run on a clone of the mirror (the files of `Apeiron/` and `Apeiron/.state/`) and passed. Its script `migrate-mirror.py` and its checker `verify-migration.py`, both standard library only, are in `Aperas.dev/monorepo/scripts/`. The writer of the script round-trips the eight files exactly (8 of 8 identical in bytes) before any rule is applied. Part (1): 3,934 `Link`s lost their `predicate` (2,332 in the mirror and 1,602 in `.state/`, in 2,256 live documents), and another 10 vanished with their tombstones, so 3,944 are all the `Link`s; none carries a `predicate` after. Part (2): 218 tombstones were stripped (187 in the mirror and 31 in `.state/`), the 219th (one `BlockNode` with only `children`) being already clean, and 107 containers were edited (98 in the mirror and 9 in `.state/`); after it every one of the 219 tombstones has no `parent`, `links`, `props` or non-empty `children`, and no container lists one. Part (3): 12 documents were deleted (the six artifacts and their six paragraphs, all in the mirror, none in `.state/`), and no `README.md` artifact is defined after. Part (4): `Profile:00CJC4S69R000` (`dinhlx`) now holds `handle`, `name` and `kind: human`, and `default` is as it was. The mirror holds 9,584 documents before and 9,572 after, with 0 differences outside the four rules over a key-by-key comparison that includes the order of keys, and 7,016 documents are byte-for-byte unchanged. A second run changes 0 documents and writes 0 files. No id named by `children`, `parent`, `target`, `root` or `unfolds` is left undefined. The live documents without a `parent` are 44, as [the open point](#id/BlockNode:00D3YSA5T8002) leaves them: the root folder, `concepts.md` and the 42 blocks.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4JYSYZ0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The README question, answered**",
    "text": "**The README question, answered**: on a copy with only part (3) applied, `aperas ingest --no-prompt` and `aperas track` registered no `README.md` artifact and no README paragraph, so the deletion holds after a `track` or an `ingest`; the folders keep the content of their README as sub-blocks (children), and their `text` stays their frontmatter `description` (11 folders have a `README.md` on disk), and the service read the copy without trouble.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4JYSYZ0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Applied to the real mirror at the cutover only**",
    "text": "**Applied to the real mirror at the cutover only**: the working engine cannot read the migrated mirror, since it needs the `predicate` and reads removed nodes through `children`. This was not tested; it is read from the design and from the earlier survey of the code. The migration of the real mirror is therefore a step of the cutover and is not done before it. Before it, the dry run is repeated on a fresh clone, because the real mirror moves on (its `BlockNode.jsonld` already differs from the clone's), and the real mirror is migrated after a flush and with the service stopped.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4JZ0A7R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`concepts.md` has no file under `artifacts/`, so `track` offers to remove its node permanently, and a yes would delete it**",
    "text": "**`concepts.md` has no file under `artifacts/`, so `track` offers to remove its node permanently, and a yes would delete it**: found 2026-10-16 in the dry run of the migration of the mirror, on a clone and on the real graph. Filed 2026-10-16.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CF1WZ4JG002",
    "type": "listItem",
