    ],
    "title": "00D4JZ0A7R003",
    "text": "`ArtifactNode:00CR5AEJ88000` (`concepts.md`) is live, holds one child block and a `text` that describes it as the shared vocabulary promoted up by the grapher, and has no `parent` and none of the hash and timestamp fields ([it was never tracked](#id/BlockNode:00D3YV43Q0003)). No file `concepts.md` exists under `artifacts/`, in the clone or in the real graph. `aperas track` therefore offers to remove the node permanently, with \"no matching file found on disk\"; run with a yes, it would delete the node and its block. The node is the graph's own copy, and the graph is the source: its projection is missing, and the projection is not what is wrong. The offer is harmless unless the prompt is answered yes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4JZ0A7R002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
