      }
    ],
    "title": "**The fix**",
    "text": "**The fix**: `verify-migration.py` with no argument prints its header and exits 2, as its own header says, instead of dying with an `IndexError` and exit 1.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4K347M0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4K347M0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The design edits (one batch, only what is settled)**",
    "text": "**The design edits (one batch, only what is settled)**: in `design/core.md`, the fields that the code leaves unset until a projection or an ingest, `projectedHash` of `FolderNode` and `fileHash`, `lastTrackedAt`, `ingestedHash`, `lastIngestedAt` and `projectedHash` of `ArtifactNode`, become optional, and `kind` of `Profile` becomes optional because the `default` profile is the auto-generated fallback for everyone and cannot know it; the sentence that every document holds the `one` fields is corrected to match. Whether `default` has a `name` stays an open point of Batch 9. With the edit made before Batch 3 starts, Batch 3 needs no gate on it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4K347M0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4K347M0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Not decided, so not in the batch**",
    "text": "**Not decided, so not in the batch**: the ping fix (five fix directions are filed under the ping issue and none is chosen), and the stale wording about README artifacts in the design's open point on deriving the path, which the grapher is to list and not edit.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4K347M0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4KA0VRR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Second batch of design edits and the script loose ends, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Second batch of design edits and the script loose ends, 2026-10-16**: the user answered the question on folders and said yes to all.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
