    "title": "**A reference across graphs**",
    "text": "**A reference across graphs**: the root folder's `children` in the tracked mirror names the `.threads` folder, whose document is in the threads graph (`threads.tree`, mirrored in the git-ignored `.state/`), so the main graph (`tree`) holds a reference into another graph. It exists today and is known ([the ghost folder](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001)); the working engine works around it with a filter that leaves out documents without a `path`. The engine keeps a pair across graphs working, as [Reads and rules across graphs](#id/BlockNode:00D5AYGHJ0001) states, and for the same reason it refuses to drop the threads graph while this reference stands (see [Dropping a graph](#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8004)); the reference may dangle after the sweep of the threads graph. It is the one pair that goes against the order of the graphs (see [Addressing](#id/BlockNode:00D5AYBPWR001)). Because an id defined in any graph counts as defined (see [Persistence](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001)), the main graph's entry for the `.threads` folder is not returned as an id referenced and never defined. The multi-graph design that would remove it is outside this document.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
