    "title": "**The boundary mapped to the folders, in the design, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The boundary mapped to the folders, in the design, 2026-10-16**: the user asked that the design be updated to map [the boundary](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJFB7G001) to the folder structure of `src`, with the names they decided ([the code structure](#id/BlockNode:00D4M417RG000)): `monorepo/packages/core/src/apeironNgn/` is the engine in memory, `monorepo/packages/core/src/shell/` is the caller on disk. Settled and in this edit: those two names and their roles, and that the engine's directory imports nothing of the shell. Not settled and not in the edit: whether the rest of `src/` (parsing, config, the walk of the disk) is shell or a layer of its own, and how and when the current code moves; the coder's dependency survey answers them first.",
