    "title": "**The shell**",
    "text": "**The shell**: the shell is the part that calls the engine. It holds `wrap`, the class hierarchy, the Aperas schema that it hands to the engine (see [The Aperas schema](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001)), and all the code that calls the engine: persistence, ingest and project, resolve, render, link integrity, the sweeps of the service and the views. It lives in `monorepo/packages/core/src/shell/`, beside the engine's directory `monorepo/packages/core/src/apeironNgn/`; the shell calls the engine, and the engine's directory imports only files inside it: no `node:` module and no package at all, so nothing of the shell, no file system and no store library (see [The boundary](#id/BlockNode:00D3CJFB7G001)).",
