    "title": "**Decisions on the dependency survey, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Decisions on the dependency survey, 2026-10-16**: on the [coder's dependency map](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4M417RG000) and the orchestrator's recommendations, the user decided: the design renames \"the caller\" to \"the shell\", described as what calls the engine; the shell holds `wrap`, the class hierarchy and every caller (persistence, ingest and project, resolve, render, link integrity, the sweeps, the views); the uncovered code goes as proposed (a Batch 11 step for the profile and view operations, `runMigrateFrontmatter` deleted, `lineReader.ts` moved to `cli`, `compareMigration.ts` and `index.ts` deleted in the move, `cli/src/apeironNgn/` renamed `cli/src/service/`); and the two questions of the grapher go as proposed (the code-versus-rule difference filed with the plan, closed by the move; \"no file system and no store library\" stated in the design). Not settled: (1) persistence: the user's main concern behind the boundary between memory and disk; they observed that the current code makes the engine depend on the store in the shell, and want the reverse: the engine advertises an API that the shell uses for its own persistence, the engine not caring how the raw data is got and only giving a way to build the graph up; (2) ids: the user asked for the id question to be elaborated, finding it messy. No design or plan edit is made until these two are settled; then one batch.",
