    "title": "**The meta-model**",
    "text": "**The meta-model**: the engine is generic and names no class or field of its own. The shell passes it a schema when it constructs it, and the schema is closed at construction, fixed for the engine's life. The schema is written in the engine's meta-model: kinds, each of which can extend another and inherit its fields; for each field of a kind, its [storage kind](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00H) and its [cardinality](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00G), a literal field declaring no type (its value is a string, a number or a boolean) and an embed field naming the kind it embeds, which the embedded node's id carries; the reference and embed fields, whose pairs the engine keeps, each with the name of its reverse side where the engine must expose that side as a field (the name is optional, and every other reverse side is read by the field and the value: see [A field is a relation](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00F)), a reverse name taking a place in the field order of the kinds that have it as a derived entry, which the engine reads from the reverse side and for which it stores no pair; the [ordered](#id/BlockNode:00D255WVK0001) and [partitioning](#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001) fields; the field of [containment](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z); the field that marks a [tombstone](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01V); the reference fields whose value is dropped when its target is removed (see [Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013)); and the root kinds of [the sweep](#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8001) and the fields it follows. A rule of the engine that needs a particular field names the role that the schema assigns, and which field holds the role is the schema's choice. The Aperas schema, its classes and their fields, is the shell's (see [The Aperas schema](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR00D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
