    "title": "**Handed to the engine**",
    "text": "**Handed to the engine**: the shell holds the Aperas schema and passes it to the engine when it constructs it, closed for the engine's life (see [The meta-model](#id/BlockNode:00D4MYZ6Q0000)). The schema is written in the engine's meta-model, and the shell's classes (`wrap` and a class for each kind) read and write their fields through the engine.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Persistence**",
    "text": "**Persistence**: the API that the shell's persistence uses to build the engine's graphs from the mirror and to read them out at a flush; the engine does not care how the data is got or where it goes.",
