    "title": "**(2) The shell**",
    "text": "**(2) The shell**: \"the caller\" and \"callers\" are \"the shell\" throughout the body: the heading [The shell, on disk](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHMYQG001), and [The shell](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4M7YEZG001), which now says that the shell is the part that calls the engine and holds `wrap`, the class hierarchy, the Aperas schema and all the code that calls the engine (persistence, ingest and project, resolve, render, link integrity, the sweeps of the service, the views). [Outside this document](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00C) adds that the mapping of markdown, the addressing and the views are parts of the shell. The frontmatter `description` of the document still says \"the interface callers use\".",
