    "title": "**(3) Persistence**",
    "text": "**(3) Persistence**: a new group of the interface, [Persistence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001): build (a node with a given id, kind and graph, its fields, a reference to a node not yet built accepted), read out (all ids of a kind in a graph, the record of a node in the order of the schema), and the ids referenced and never defined, moved there from the Reads with its id. [Not offered](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000H) keeps \"no load or dump of its own\", the shell building through the API; [The boundary](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJFB7G001), [A reflection of the mirror](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR007), [Written by graph and kind](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01Y), the lead of [The index](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR015) and the lead of [the interface](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0003), which now says the shell constructs the engine with its schema, say the same.",
