    "title": "**Stale after the edits, not edited**",
    "text": "**Stale after the edits, not edited**: in the plan, [Batch 3 step 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG002) (the directory `engine/`, \"the caller\"); [Batch 3 step 2](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG003) (`shape.ts` declares the fields of each class, where the engine now declares the meta-model and is handed the Aperas schema by the shell); [Batch 3 step 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG004) (the interface as Reads, Writes and Ports, without the construction with a schema and the persistence group); the Design line of Batch 3 ([00D3XQQ2VR002](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR002)), which cites Fields per class as the engine's; [Batch 4 step 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR007) (\"the class shape\", \"One schema, the class\"); [Batch 6 step 2](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00X), if the mark of a partitioning field moves into the schema; [Batch 6 step 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00Y) (\"`children` is declared ordered and partitioning\"); [Batch 9 step 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01Q) (\"the engine is filled from the files\", the load returning the undefined ids to its caller); [Batch 11 step 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000D) (`NODE_BASE` kept as one of the caller's id rules, though it only builds IRIs); and \"the caller\" in [Batch 10 step 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0005), [Batch 14 step 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W8002) and the Design lines of Batches 9 and 11, which cite \"The caller, on disk\". In the design, the Open point [An invalid id and a non-canonical integer](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000S) still asks whether the engine refuses an id that is not a valid IRI.",
