    "title": "**The seven questions of the design edits, decided 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The seven questions of the design edits, decided 2026-10-16**: the user accepted the orchestrator's seven recommendations on the [grapher's questions](#id/BlockNode:00D4N298WG002): (1) the meta-model gets a role for a reference field whose value is dropped when its target is removed (the `unfolds` entries); (2) tombstoning is the engine's operation, the schema assigns the tombstone-marker role (`tombstonedAt`), the shell passes the timestamp in so the engine needs no clock, the engine offers the tombstone of a subtree over containment and the rule that a removed artifact tombstones its subtree is the shell's; (3) the schema marks the root kinds of the sweep and the fields it follows; (4) the partitioning mark is in the schema only, closed at construction, so Batch 3 types no run-time mark operation; (5) \"The artifact is its own root document\" and \"Links are outgoing ports\" move under the Aperas schema, \"Ids are stable\" to the shell; (6) the id half of \"An invalid id and a non-canonical integer\" is settled (the engine refuses an id that fails the grammar), the integer half stays open and still gates Batch 4; (7) the grapher fixes the frontmatter `description` of `design/core.md`, restoring from the staged index if the update touches the artifact's text. The plan edits follow on these.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D4NEENS0001",
      "BlockNode:00D4NEENS0002"
    ]
  },
