    "title": "**4. The old engine gone from the shell**",
    "text": "**4. The old engine gone from the shell**: what is left in `src/shell/` of the old engine after Batch 11 has flipped the shell is the frozen set, and it is deleted: `storeAccess.ts`, `shape.ts`, `store.ts`, `dehydrate.ts`, `threadScope.ts` and `vocab.ts` (the IRI and literal codec with `NODE_BASE` and `nodeExists`; `nodeKindFromId` and `isNodeRef` already live in `shell/nodeIds.ts`, so the whole file goes), with their tests and the two support files (step 1). The engine access of `node.ts` is not part of it: piece 6 of Batch 11 replaced those functions in place, so nothing is left to delete there. The test `shell/oldEngine.test.ts` of piece 6, which lists the frozen set and fails if any other module imports `oxigraph` or a frozen file, is removed with it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
