    "title": "**Recorded in `design/core.md`**",
    "text": "**Recorded in `design/core.md`**: the seven answers, in one pass. (1) [The meta-model](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MYZ6Q0000) names the role of a reference field whose value is dropped when its target is removed, and [Embedded nodes have ids and are removed outright](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013) drops a removed node from every such field (`unfolds` in the Aperas schema). (2) [Tombstones](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01V): tombstoning is the engine's operation, with a timestamp that the shell passes in, written in the field of the tombstone-marker role; the engine tombstones a node or a subtree over containment, and the rule that a removed artifact tombstones its subtree is the shell's; the write [Tombstone a node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CKXC6G001) says the same. (3) [The sweep](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8001) marks from the root kinds and through the fields that the schema marks. (4) [Partitioning fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001) and [A partition hierarchy](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2T5XBH0001): the mark is in the schema only, closed at construction. (5) [The artifact is its own root document](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR010) and [Links are outgoing ports](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR011) moved, with their ids, under [The Aperas schema](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ15AR001), after a new item, [The roles it assigns](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NB5FSR001) (containment to `children`, the tombstone marker to `tombstonedAt`, the drop with the target to `unfolds`, and the root kinds and fields of the sweep); [Ids are stable](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01Q) moved into the shell's part, after [The shell](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4M7YEZG001), and says that the shell mints the ids. (6) [An invalid id and a non-canonical integer](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000S) keeps its title and records the id half as settled, and [Ids](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01N) says that the engine refuses an id that fails the grammar. (7) The frontmatter `description` of `design/core.md` names the meta-model, the shell and its persistence instead of \"the interface callers use\"; the artifact's `text` is unchanged. [Status](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR005) lists the new issue.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4N6VYZ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
