    "title": "**Recorded in `planning/core.md` and `issues/core.md`**",
    "text": "**Recorded in `planning/core.md` and `issues/core.md`**: item (6) of [the batch](#id/BlockNode:00D4MVJXY0001). [Batch 15](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBFKAG001), the move of the current code to `src/shell/`, takes the next number under the plan's [Numbering](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQM4X0001) and comes first, before Batch 3: the move with its 128 imports in 41 `cli` files, the deletion of `compareMigration.ts`, `index.ts` and `runMigrateFrontmatter`, `lineReader.ts` moved to `cli`, `cli/src/apeironNgn/` renamed `cli/src/service/`, and the test of a dev checkout in `graphConfig.ts` made independent of the directory name; it is done when `npm run verify` passes with no change of behaviour. Updated with it: [Batch 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG001), retitled (the engine in `src/apeironNgn/` itself, the boundary test over the whole directory, the meta-model, a test schema and the Aperas schema in the shell, a graph argument with one default graph, the persistence group, the id grammar, no run-time mark); Batches 4 to 7 (the schema handed in, the refusal of an id that fails the grammar, the drop with the target, the mark in the schema, containment by its role, the tombstone with its timestamp passed in and the subtree tombstone, the sweep by roles); Batches 9 and 10 (the shell's persistence and maps, in `src/shell/`); Batch 11 (the classes and `wrap` in the shell, `NODE_BASE` gone with the codec, and [a step for the profiles and views](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NE1A7R001)); Batch 12 ([a step that deletes the old engine from the shell](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NE2D98001), done when nothing under `src/shell/` imports `oxigraph`); and \"the caller\" renamed \"the shell\" throughout the plan. Filed: [the code differs from the boundary](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBNCF8001), closed by Batch 15 and cross-referenced both ways with [the thread-scope issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2590B2R001), which Batch 9 still closes.",
