    "title": "**The grapher's five questions on the plan edits, decided 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The grapher's five questions on the plan edits, decided 2026-10-16**: on the [plan edits](#id/BlockNode:00D4NEENS0002), three answers follow from earlier decisions: the design's interface list gets the graph argument, the creation of a node and the creation and dropping of a graph, which Batch 3 types ([Batch 3 questions](#id/BlockNode:00D4KSHCD8001)); \"the new deletions\" of Batch 12 are what is left of the old engine in `src/shell/` after Batch 11, as the grapher read them; the shell imports the engine's id grammar and keeps no copy ([the decided batch](#id/BlockNode:00D4MVJXY0001), item 4). The user decided the other two: the oracle of Batch 3 step 4 is constructed with the same schema as the engine, and the step says so; dangling `unfolds` entries are dropped in the mirror and not by the engine, so the write that removes the pairs naming a value leaves the interface and `pruneStaleUnfolds` leaves Batch 11 step 7. The user asked whether the mirror had been migrated: it has not. The real mirror still holds 2,519 `predicate` fields, and the migration is applied at the cutover only ([apply at cutover only](#id/BlockNode:00D4JX0EM8002)). The orchestrator counted the `unfolds` entries of the real mirror on 2026-10-16: 19 views, 443 entries, 0 dangling, kept so by the working service's `pruneStaleUnfolds`. So nothing is to drop today; the one-time migration (Batch 9 step 6) gets a fifth rule, stripping any `unfolds` entry whose target is not defined, and its checker verifies none is left. Batch 15 keeps its number.",
