    "title": "**Recorded in `design/core.md` and `planning/core.md`**",
    "text": "**Recorded in `design/core.md` and `planning/core.md`**: the five answers, in one batch. In the design, [the interface](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0003) says that every read and write names the graph it acts on, and its Writes gain [the creation of a node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NP6EWG001) and [the creation and dropping of a graph](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NP7NSG001); the write that removed the pairs naming a value in a field across subjects is removed. In the plan, [Batch 3 step 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR000) constructs the oracle with the same schema as the engine; [Batch 11 step 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000K) keeps `tombstoneVacuousContainers` alone, `pruneStaleUnfolds` being dropped; [Batch 9 step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001) has a fifth part, every `unfolds` entry whose target is not defined stripped and checked, with `migrate-mirror.py` and `verify-migration.py` to gain the rule and the dry run repeated before the cutover; [Batch 11 step 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000D) says that the shell imports the engine's grammar and keeps no copy. [Batch 12 step 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NE2D98001) already read as the answer states and is unchanged. Edited with them, as text the answers made stale: [Batch 5 step 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00M) no longer removes the pairs naming a value, [Batch 11 step 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000M) names the sweeps instead of \"the three sweeps\", and the [Gated by](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0002) and [Done when](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0003) of Batch 9 count five parts and require no `unfolds` entry whose target is not defined.",
