    "title": "**The move's stdin hang, a third time, and its stopgap, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The move's stdin hang, a third time, and its stopgap, 2026-10-16**: in the filing of Batch 15 the grapher's move (`aperas insert <id> --after <anchor>` with no body) hung about two minutes until it was rerun with `< /dev/null`. It is a recurrence of [the move waits on standard input when it is an open pipe](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001) (first seen 2026-09-27), of the same root as [the `ingest` prompt hang](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CNX1T4XG001), fixed in `eb352f5` by `--no-prompt`. The orchestrator proposed a code fix (an explicit move signal, so that a move never reads standard input) and, as a stopgap, `< /dev/null` in the skills' move recipes. The user decided the stopgap now, on branch `oxigraph` of `Aperas/`; the user commits it and rebases `js-apeironngn` before Batch 3 goes on. The code fix is not decided. On the two other questions of the [filing of Batch 15](#id/BlockNode:00D4NYBTD0001) the user agreed: no issue for the sampler of each checkout matching its own service, and the stale comment of `core/src/artifacts.ts` fixed in Batch 11.",
