    "title": "**The stopgap checked by the orchestrator**",
    "text": "**The stopgap checked by the orchestrator**: in `Aperas/` (`oxigraph`, staged, not committed) the diff is 5 files: the move recipes of `skills/aperas/SKILL.md` (the quick reference row, a new move line in the patterns) and `skills/aperas-grapher/SKILL.md` (two recipes) end in `< /dev/null` with the reason; `skills/aperas/references/mechanics.md` gains a section \"Moving a Node (`insert` with No Body)\" and goes from v4.2 to v4.7; the four skills go to v4.7 (the coder and orchestrator skills have no move recipe, only the Status line). `skill_drift.py` fails as expected at this step, naming exactly the edited units (4 Status lines, 6 added, 6 dropped); `aperas check-links` is clean. The coder asked three questions; the orchestrator put them to the user.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4PDAWZ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
