    "title": "**v4.7 — every move recipe closes standard input, a stopgap for the move that waits on it**",
    "text": "**v4.7 — every move recipe closes standard input, a stopgap for the move that waits on it**: recorded as [the v4.7 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D4PMGJJR001). A move (`aperas insert <id> --after <anchor>` with no body) reads standard input to its end before acting, and a harness can leave standard input open, so a move run from a harness can wait indefinitely; it did three times (2026-09-27, 2026-10-13, 2026-10-16), as recorded on [the move that waits on standard input](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001). Every move recipe now ends in `< /dev/null` and says why: the base skill's quick-reference row and a new move line in its command patterns, and the Grapher skill's two recipes (step 3 of the edit loop and *Move nodes cleanly*). `skills/aperas/references/mechanics.md` goes from v4.2 to v4.7, the skill release it ships with, and gains a section, *Moving a Node (`insert` with No Body)*, with its entry in the reference's Table of Contents. The Coder and Orchestrator skills have no move recipe, so only their `Status:` lines move to v4.7; no in-place promote recipe appears in the skills or the reference, so none changed. The stopgap was decided by the user; the fix in the code, an explicit move signal so that a move never reads standard input, is proposed and not decided.",
