    "title": "**Batch 3: the grapher's eight questions, 2026-10-16** (the [brief](#id/BlockNode:00D4PZ2SJG008))",
    "text": "**Batch 3: the grapher's eight questions, 2026-10-16** (the [brief](#id/BlockNode:00D4PZ2SJG008)): by the [narrowed stop rule](#id/BlockNode:00D4PXQJSR001) the orchestrator decided three that are not about the design, with the grapher's defaults: (1) the oracle implements every operation whose meaning the design states in full, each of Batches 4 to 8 extends it only where the batch adds an operation, and the open meanings (existence, an out-of-shape write) are one function each that throws \"undecided: <Open point>\"; its own test `tests/engine/oracle.test.ts` is added, in `commit`; (2) `createEngine` refuses an inconsistent schema (unknown or cyclic parent kind, a field redeclared in a descendant, an embed field without a known embedded kind, a clashing reverse name, a containment field that is not a reference field, ordered and partitioning, a tombstone marker that is not an optional literal, a drop-with-target field that is not a reference, a sweep root or followed field that does not exist), every role is optional, a role named twice is refused, a schema with no roles is valid; (7) the typed-only operations throw an error that names their batch, the ports take the plainest rows the design sentence allows with a comment naming Batch 14, and the signatures are reviewed by the orchestrator at the verification. Put to the user as design: (3) what a field declaration holds, (4) `parent`, (5) `Profile.name`, (6) the engine side of Persistence, (8) how strict the boundary test is.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
