        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Batch 3: the five design questions, decided 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Batch 3: the five design questions, decided 2026-10-16**: the user answered \"yes to all\" to the orchestrator's defaults for the [five questions](#id/BlockNode:00D4PZETT0001): (3) a reverse name is optional and given only where the engine must expose it as a field; a literal field declares no type for now (values are `string | number | boolean`); an embed field names its embedded kind, and `Profile.preferences` is `StringProp`; (4) the schema holds `parent` as the reverse name of `children` with a place in the field order, the read-out lists it from the reverse side, and a build that supplies a `parent` is an assertion by the shell, never a stored pair; (5) `Profile.name` is optional, and the design's \"present on every document\" sentence is read for `TreeView.name`; (6) the read-out is a Batch 4 read, the build is one operation made of Batch 4's create and Batch 5's pairs with a dangling reference accepted, the referenced-and-never-defined list stays in Batch 9, and the plan says so in each of those batches; (8) the engine imports only files inside its own directory, no `node:` module and no package at all, and the design's sentence is tightened to match. The design and plan edits are one batch for the grapher.",
