    "title": "**The engine side of Persistence**",
    "text": "**The engine side of Persistence**: the build and the read-out are made by [Batch 4](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR006) and [Batch 5](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H), and steps 1 and 3 use them; this batch built the list of the ids referenced and never defined, its computing half (`danglingRefs(graph)` in `engine.ts`, the one persistence operation left as `NotBuiltError`), the service's reading of it staying the service's. It reads across graphs: an id defined in any graph counts as defined, so the root folder's entry for the `.threads` folder, defined in the threads graph, is not returned for the main graph ([A reference across graphs](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4KD44M8001)). A `parent` that the load supplies is an assertion by the shell and never a stored pair, and the read-out lists `parent` at its place from the reverse side of `children` ([Persistence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001)).",
