    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 3 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Batch 3 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-16**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built `core/src/apeironNgn/{schema,interface,engine}.ts`, `core/src/shell/aperasSchema.ts`, the `engine` test group (`boundary`, `schema`, `aperasSchema`, `oracle`) and the support files `engineSchema.ts` and `oracle.ts`, and joined the suites. The orchestrator ran them: `npm run verify` (`commit`) 177 of 177 in 19 s, `--suite essential` 51 of 51 in 3 s (budget 5 s), `--group engine` 107 of 107; the engine's files import only files of their own directory; the 29 operations of the interface are typed and throw an error naming their batch. Signatures reviewed and accepted (the coder's list: `size(graph)`, the three reads of the subjects, `items` and `placeOf`, `insertItem`/`moveItem`/`removeItem`, `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree`, a record listing only the fields that hold a value, `idsOfKind` serving the Reads and the read-out, the ports over a `Bucket`); they may be amended by the later batch that builds each. Four of the coder's five questions are about the design and go to the user: a field restated in a descendant, the sweep with no operation, clearing an embed field that keeps some of its nodes, and the rules the schema check read in; the fifth (the signatures) is answered here.",
