    "title": "**The interface's choices, accepted at the orchestrator's check**",
    "text": "**The interface's choices, accepted at the orchestrator's check**: `size(graph)` takes a graph although \"the size of the store\" names none; the read of the subjects is three calls (`subjectsOf`, `firstSubjectOf`, `countSubjectsOf`); an ordered field is read by `items(host, field)` and `placeOf(host, field, item)`; `insertItem`, `moveItem` and `removeItem` are three methods, not one splice value; `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` are two; a record lists only the fields that hold a value, in schema order; `idsOfKind` serves both the Reads and the Persistence read-out; the ports take a `Bucket` of (field, value) and return nested `PortTreeRow`s (boundary, count, splits). The id grammar is not in the oracle, which checks only uniqueness; it is [Batch 4 step 3](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR009). The later batch that builds each operation may amend its signature.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8000",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
