    "title": "**A field restated in a descendant**",
    "text": "**A field restated in a descendant**: [`ArtifactNode` in Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00R) extends `BlockNode` with `type` optional, where `BlockNode.type` is `one`, and the Coder's default had `createEngine` refuse \"a field redeclared in a descendant\"; both cannot hold as worded. `closeSchema` takes the narrowest reading that keeps both: a descendant may restate an inherited field only with `redeclares: true`, only to relax `one` to `optional`, with the storage kind, the embedded kind, the reverse name and the partitioning mark unchanged, and the field keeps its inherited place in the field order; any other restatement, or `redeclares` with nothing to restate, is refused (4 variants in `schema.test.ts`). Open: whether that is the rule, and whether [the meta-model](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MYZ6Q0000) says it. If not, `closeSchema` and `ArtifactNode.type` change in two places. Settled (2026-10-16): the hierarchy is straightened, with `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` as siblings of `BlockNode` under `TreeNode`, `type` on `BlockNode` only and `ArtifactNode` with no `type` ([Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M)), so no class restates an inherited field; the restated-field rule and `redeclares` go, and the Coder reworks `closeSchema` and the Aperas schema accordingly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
