    "title": "**Clearing an embed field and the embedded nodes it keeps**",
    "text": "**Clearing an embed field and the embedded nodes it keeps**: [Embedded nodes](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013) says that assigning an embed field removes every embedded node the new value does not keep, and [Writes](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000E) says that a write of a field is a clear then adds. In the oracle `clearField` on an embed field removes the held embedded nodes at once, so a write that keeps some of them cannot be a clear then adds, since they would be gone before the add. Open: how a keeping write is expressed, a replace operation or a clear that leaves orphans for the add to claim with a cleanup at the end of the write; [Batch 5 step 4](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00N) must say. Nothing in Batch 3 depends on it. Settled (2026-10-16): the writes gain `removePair(graph, subject, field, value)`, which removes the pair and, on an embed field, the embedded node recursively; a keeping write of an embed field is `removePair` for the dropped values and `addPair` for the new ones, so the nodes kept keep their ids ([Remove a pair](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4R9WX7R001), [Clear a field](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000E)); Batch 5 step 4 builds it and types it with the oracle. Built (2026-10-16): [Batch 5](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00H) step 4 builds `removePair` for a reference or an embed field, and a write that keeps some of the embedded nodes is `removePair` for each value dropped and `addPair` for each added.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The rules the schema check read in**",
    "text": "**The rules the schema check read in**: the meta-model names no target kind for a reference, so `closeSchema` checks a reverse name for the whole schema (it is no field's name, and one field name owns it, as `children` does in two kinds); a partitioning mark is refused only on a literal field; \"a role named twice\" is read as a repeated entry in a list of a role; and a derived entry must be the reverse name of some field. Each is one line in `closeSchema`. Open: whether any of the four is to change.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4QHTCBG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "tombstonedAt": "2026-10-16T15:43:56.257Z",
    "title": "**Open point**",
    "text": "**Open point**: settled (2026-10-16). A write that keeps some of the embedded nodes of an embed field is `removePair` for the values it drops and `addPair` for the new ones, so it needs no replace operation and no cleanup of orphans; the write of a `one` or `optional` field stays a clear then add ([Clear a field](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000E)). See [the open point of Batch 3](#id/BlockNode:00D4QHPDV8007).",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
