    "title": "**Since (2026-10-16), the `type` shape part closed, the data part not resolved**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-16), the `type` shape part closed, the data part not resolved**: [Batch 3](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VG001) wrote the Aperas schema with the `type` of an `ArtifactNode` optional, and the hierarchy was then straightened: [an `ArtifactNode` has no `type`](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00R) (the `type` is `BlockNode`'s alone), and the sixth rule of [the migration](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001) strips the `type` (`root`) from every artifact. So an artifact with no `type` is the valid document, and whether the 9 artifacts that carry none are given one no longer arises. Why 7 of them carry an `ingestedHash` and no `type` is a question of the data and stays open here; the cause of the path that produced them is still not found.",
