    "title": "**Batch 3 design questions: two decided, two open, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Batch 3 design questions: two decided, two open, 2026-10-16**: on the [four open design points](#id/BlockNode:00D4QFMSDG001) the user answered \"yes\" to the orchestrator's recommendations for (2) the sweep is an engine operation, added to the interface and the design's list in Batch 7, and (4) the four rules the schema check read in (a reverse name unique across the schema with one field name allowed to own it in several kinds, a partitioning mark refused only on a literal field, \"a role named twice\" as a repeated entry in a role's list, a derived entry the reverse name of some field). On (1) the user asked whether `ArtifactNode` really extends `BlockNode`, since they thought `BlockNode`, `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` were three siblings extending `TreeNode`: [Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00R) says `ArtifactNode` extends `BlockNode` (and `FolderNode` extends `TreeNode`, not `BlockNode`), and so does the old `shape.ts`; the question (1) rests on that. On (3) the user did not understand the problem; explained by the orchestrator. Both stay open.",
