  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4QW4JXG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 4 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Batch 4 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-16**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built records, literal fields, cardinalities, ids (`core/src/apeironNgn/ids.ts`), the collections and the orders (`records.ts`, `order.ts`, `errors.ts`) with the tests `ids`, `records`, `order` and `literals.model` (the seeded random sequence against the oracle); step 6 (existence and size) and the deletion half of step 4 are recorded as waiting. The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 316 of 316 in 22 s, `essential` 51 of 51 in 3.5 s, `--group engine` 246 of 246; the engine's files import only files of their own directory. The coder's two questions, decided as not about the design: a write to a derived entry throws Enforcement as the oracle does (not `NotBuiltError`), and `idsOfKind` on a missing graph returns an empty list as the oracle does. The grapher's question is answered yes: Batch 4's Done when also records the deletion half of step 4 as waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4QXWJFR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-16**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed. Steps 1 and 2: `core/src/apeironNgn/records.ts` (new) and `engine.ts` (173 lines, was 60), a record for each node with its literal fields in a `Map`, and `createNode`, `addPair`, `clearField`, `values` and `first` for a literal field of cardinality `one`, `optional` or `set`, read from the closed schema at each write; a value is kept as given, and `values` and `record` return copies. Step 3: `ids.ts` (new) with `isId` and `kindOfId`; `createNode` refuses (`Refused`) a graph that does not exist, an id that fails the grammar, a kind not in the schema, a kind that differs from the id's, and an id already taken; an embedded-shaped id is accepted whether or not its owner exists. Step 4: `records.ts` holds the master map and one collection of records for each graph and kind; `idsOfKind` iterates the collection of that exact kind (so `idsOfKind('Entity')` is empty for a `Leaf` node), in order of insertion. Step 5: `order.ts` (new) with `compareIds` and `compareByKey(key)`. Errors: `errors.ts` (new) holds `Undecided` and `Refused`, exported by `engine.ts`. Tests in `cli/src/tests/engine/`: `ids`, `records`, `order` and `literals.model` (a seeded random sequence of 20 seeds of 200 operations against the oracle, compared after every one), named in `commit.suite.mjs` and none in `essential`.",
