    "title": "**Choices of the batch, accepted at the orchestrator's check**",
    "text": "**Choices of the batch, accepted at the orchestrator's check**: a write to a derived entry throws `Undecided('Enforcement')`, as the oracle does for it (it is no pair), where a read of one (`values`, `first`) throws `NotBuiltError` naming [Batch 6](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V); `idsOfKind` of a graph that does not exist returns an empty list, as the oracle does, while `createNode` and the graph check of a write still refuse or throw; `compareByKey` throws `Refused` for a number against a string key, and a missing-key mix uses the heading of the open point as its `point`. Built (2026-10-16): [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V) built the read of a derived entry (`values`, `first` and `record` read `up` from the reverse of `children`); it no longer throws `NotBuiltError`, and a write to a derived entry still throws `Undecided('Enforcement')`.",
