    "title": "**Since (2026-10-16), the reading of the kind of an id closed, the id-like string at load not resolved**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-16), the reading of the kind of an id closed, the id-like string at load not resolved**: [Batch 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR006) built the reading in the new engine (`core/src/apeironNgn/ids.ts`): `isId` counts a string as an id only if a valid snowflake follows `Kind:`, and `kindOfId` reads the kind from the last `field:Kind:` segment or from the prefix when there is none, so an embedded id `owner:field:Kind:snowflake` has its own kind; `createNode` refuses an id that fails the grammar. A table test (`ids.test.ts`) covers a folder or an artifact named after a kind, which is never taken for an id. The id-like string in a field at load is not built: it closes in [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M), and this entry stays open until then.",
