    "title": "**1. The path derived**",
    "text": "**1. The path derived**: the shell derives the path of an artifact or a folder from its parent chain ([The path is derived from the parent chain](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01S)) and every read of the stored `.path` is replaced by the derivation: ingest, track, project, link integrity, the anchor of reference resolution, the deep path of a block and the tie to the file on disk, with the lookup by path over the maps of [Batch 10](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0004). Ingest and project throw \"path undeterminable: no parent\" for a node whose chain does not reach the root folder, and the load warns once, listing them; `concepts.md` is such a node and is kept as the test of the refusal ([A path that cannot be derived](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4R9VPGR001)). The stored `path` then leaves the Aperas schema, the Format and the mirror; how the mirror loses it is not planned yet. The count of the readers, made by the Coder on 2026-10-16: 47 lines read or write the stored field of `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` outside the schema (38 in 8 files of `core`, 9 in 4 files of `cli`, none in `web`), plus 4 declaration lines and 4 test lines. Of the 47, 27 can take the derived path as it is, 8 can but throw for a node with no chain, 9 need something else, and 3 are writes that go away. By role: ingest and track 11, rename detection and the removal sweep 13, project 1, resolve and lookup by path 10, render and the CLI commands 7 (and 14 calls through `toPath`), link integrity 2, thread scope 1, the service 0, the web package 0, tests and tools 6 (and their call sites). The stored path is the title chain for every attached node today; it is not for the 7 live artifacts with no parent, and the largest hole is a tracked artifact that has no parent until the next folder ingest (see the open points below).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4RNDQVG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4RBGG18001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Which artifacts hold a `type`, checked 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Which artifacts hold a `type`, checked 2026-10-16**: the orchestrator counted the real mirror: 54 live `ArtifactNode`s, 48 hold `type: \"root\"` (the mark of the old `root` node merged into `ArtifactNode`) and no other value occurs; the 6 without a `type` are `history/packaging.md`, `discussion/webapp.md`, `design/webapp.md`, `planning/webapp.md`, `history/webapp.md` and `concepts.md`, that is the artifacts ingested after the merge, not the `README.md` artifacts (the orchestrator first said so by mistake and corrected it). The user concluded that the data question of artifacts without a `type` is answered: once `ArtifactNode` has no `type`, the sixth migration rule strips the 48 and the 6 need nothing.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
