  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4RJ4XDR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`path` stays stored for now, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**`path` stays stored for now, 2026-10-16**: on the five holes the coder's count found in removing `path` (the tracked artifact with no parent, the tombstones, the thread scope, the seven parentless artifacts, the root folder), the user decided to keep the stored `path` for now, for the technical reasons, and said that in the design it must go anyway. So: the design keeps the derived path as the target (the chain of `title`s from the root folder; a path that cannot be derived is refused, with one warning at load) and states the stored `path` as transitional; the Aperas schema, the Format and the migration keep `path` (the seventh migration rule leaves Batch 9); the removal becomes its own later batch, after the engine is in place, with the five holes as its open points and the coder's count as its start; Batch 11 step 12 moves there.",
