    "title": "**The `title` of an artifact or a folder is its file or directory name, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**The `title` of an artifact or a folder is its file or directory name, 2026-10-16**: the user stated that the `title` of a folder or an artifact is its file name (the artifact `design/core.md` is titled `core.md`, its folder `design`), which is why the path is the chain of titles. The orchestrator checked the design: [the derived path](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01S) says \"the chain of its `title`s\" and so implies it, but no block states it as a rule of `TreeNode.title` for the two kinds; the only mention in the graph is the issue [`aperas update` re-derives an `ArtifactNode` target's own title from pushed text, corrupting its file-basename identity](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CGM54FX0001), which treats it as an invariant. To be written by the grapher into Fields per class after the current design turn: for `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` the `title` is the name of the file (extension included) or of the directory, and is the identity the path is built from; for a `BlockNode` it is the text of the heading or the block.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
