  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4RN38H0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Write the title rule down, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Write the title rule down, 2026-10-16**: the user said to write all of it down: the `title` of an artifact or a folder is its file or directory name, and the shell sets it only from that name (never from pushed text), a rename of the file or directory being the only change of it; the engine knows nothing of the rule, since it is the shell's. To go into Fields per class and the shell's part of the design, and onto the issue that treats it as an invariant.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
