    "title": "**The title of an artifact or a folder is its name**",
    "text": "**The title of an artifact or a folder is its name**: the `title` of an `ArtifactNode` is the name of its file, extension included, and the `title` of a `FolderNode` is the name of its directory (the artifact `design/core.md` is titled `core.md`, and its folder `design`), as [Fields per class](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M) states. It is the identity that [the path derived from the parent chain](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01S) is built from, since that path is the chain of these titles. The shell sets the `title` of an artifact or a folder only from that name, never from pushed text: a rename of the file or of the directory is the only change of it. The engine knows nothing of the rule, since it is the shell's: to the engine `title` is a literal field like another.",
