    "title": "**Since (2026-10-16), the design states the rule that the corruption broke**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-16), the design states the rule that the corruption broke**: [The title of an artifact or a folder is its name](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4RSAZ3G001) now says it as a rule of the shell: the `title` of an `ArtifactNode` is its file name and the `title` of a `FolderNode` its directory name (also in [Fields per class](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00M)), the identity that [the derived path](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01S) is built from, and the shell sets it only from that name, never from pushed text, a rename of the file or directory being the only change of it. The issue treated that as an invariant before any block stated it. This does not resolve the issue: the entry records only that the design now states the rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00CGM54FX0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4RTZKK8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 5 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Batch 5 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-16**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built pairs and the reverse side built on first use, node removal, embedded nodes, `removePair`, links and backlinks, and the build of Persistence, with the decided defaults (the reverse side of a node with no record in a map the coder named `waiting`, since `aperasSchema.test.ts` forbids the word `holder` in the engine's directory, a `BaseNode` field). The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 446 of 446 in 24 s, `essential` 51 of 51 in 3.2 s (the coder saw it warn at 5.5 to 7 s under a load of 5 to 7.5, and it adds no file to it), `--group engine` 376 of 376; the engine's files import only files of their own directory. No question of the coder blocks. Next: the grapher files Batch 5 and surveys Batch 6, after its current turn on the title rule.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
