    ],
    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-16**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed. The reference and embed fields of the engine, with the reverse side and the removal of a node. Steps 1 and 2: `addPair`, `removePair`, `clearField`, `values` and `first` for a reference or embed field, and `subjectsOf`, `firstSubjectOf` and `countSubjectsOf` for the reverse, which is built the first time a field is asked in reverse, held as a set on the record of each object, and kept by every later write. Steps 3 and 4: `removeNode` removes the pairs of a node, its record from its collection, its entries in every reverse that was built, and drops it from each field the schema marks to be dropped with its target (`pinned` in the test schema, `unfolds` in the Aperas schema); `removePair` on an embed field removes the embedded node the pair names, recursively. Step 5: the owner and the field of an id are read from the id (`ownerOfId` and `fieldOfId` in `ids.ts`), not by a scan. The build of [Persistence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001): `build` creates the nodes and the pairs of a plan in one operation, accepts a reference to a node not yet built, and checks the whole plan before the first change. Files: `core/src/apeironNgn/engine.ts` (358 lines, was 174), `records.ts` (129, was 55) and `ids.ts`; tests in `cli/src/tests/engine/`: `pairs` (21 cases), `reverse` (15), `removal` (16), `relations.model` (21; the model-based test, which holds the reverse equal to the inverse of the forward side and to the oracle) and `persistence` (30), named in `commit.suite.mjs`; `records.test.ts`, `schema.test.ts` and `ids.test.ts` changed. `interface.ts` is unchanged and the boundary test passes.",
