    "title": "**Recorded as waiting**",
    "text": "**Recorded as waiting**: [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) is one function, `inShape`, now with the rule of the embed field, and [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) is one function, `existence`, which every write of the batch reaches; each throws `Undecided` where the oracle does. `exists` and `size` still throw `Undecided('Existence')` (`WAITING_ON` in `engine.ts` holds them, and `BUILT_BY` still names Batch 4 for them). A node that has only incoming pairs has a bucket in the map of the reverse of nodes with no record and no record of its own, and no read of the batch counts the bucket as existence. The deletion half of Batch 4's step 4, recorded there as waiting, is `removeNode` of step 3. An ordered field is [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V)'s: a removal that has to drop from an ordered field builds the reverse of each such field before it changes anything, so it throws with nothing changed. Built (2026-10-16): [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V) builds the ordered fields, so a removal that drops from an ordered field no longer throws; it takes the node out of the lists that hold it and keeps the order of the others.",
