    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-16**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed. The ordered fields, the partitioning mark, containment with the parent derived from the reverse of `children`, and the tree of the records. Step 1: `items`, `placeOf`, `insertItem`, `moveItem` and `removeItem` on an ordered field, in the order of checks Existence, shape, ordered (else `Refused`), item a string, item not already there, `at` an integer from 0 to the length, then one splice; `removeNode`, `clearField` and `build` take a whole ordered field out or in without a splice for each item, and `build` keeps a `Set` of the strings of a field so that a long array is not scanned for each value. Step 2: `partition` refuses a write that gives an item a second subject on the climbed side or closes a cycle, called from `addPair` (after the cardinality check), `insertItem` (after the place check) and the plan of `build`; the climb is bounded by the number of records, so a cycle already in the lists is an `Error` and not a hang. Step 3: `values`, `first` and `record` read a derived entry (`up`) from the reverse of the field that carries its name (`items`), filtered to the subject's graph; `subjectsOf`, `firstSubjectOf` and `countSubjectsOf` of a derived name give `[]`, `undefined` and 0 as the oracle does; taking a node out of a list detaches it and does not delete it. Step 4: `records.ts` gained `under`, `beneath`, `roots`, `nest`, `rootIds` and `count`, and `engine.ts` gained `parentOf`, `place` and `replace`, called from `createNode`, `build`, `attach`, `detach` and `release`, so every write that changes a list or an embed field re-places the one node it names. The read-out of [Persistence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001) lists `up` at its place from the reverse of `children`, and `build` accepts an ordered field and checks a whole plan, a second container, the host in its own list and a cycle through the waiting buckets, before its first change. Files: `core/src/apeironNgn/engine.ts` (497 lines, was 358) and `records.ts` (164, was 129); tests in `cli/src/tests/engine/`: `ordered` (22 cases), `partitioning` (15), `containment` (26), `containment.model` (the model-based test) and `support/engineTree.ts`, named in `commit.suite.mjs` and none in `essential`; `pairs`, `records`, `reverse`, `removal`, `persistence` and `schema` rewritten to what is built (`schema.test.ts` takes `tombstone` and `createGraph` as the unbuilt examples, of which [Batch 7](#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014) moved `tombstone` to `danglingRefs` and added `dropGraph`). `interface.ts` and the oracle are unchanged and the boundary test passes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V",
