    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: the Coder's run: `tsc` of `core` and `cli` clean, group `engine` 460 of 460 in 6.6 s, `essential` 51 of 51 in 3.1 s (no file added to it), `commit` 530 of 530 in 23.8 s (Batch 5: 446 in 24 s). The orchestrator's run: `commit` 530 of 530 in 24 s, `--suite essential` 51 of 51 in 3.0 s (budget 5 s), `--group engine` 460 of 460. The model-based test, `containment.model.test.ts`, runs 20 seeds (701 to 720) of 250 operations over the test schema (6 `Box`, 7 `Leaf`, 3 `Stub` and 3 ids that never get a record), compares the engine with the oracle by value, or by the class and the point of the error, after every operation and the whole state every 12th, and holds after every operation the checks independent of the oracle: a single container for each node, no cycle (a climb by `first(up)` with a bound), `up` equal to the host whose list holds the node, the place equal to the index, `items` equal to `values`, the reverse of `items` with its first and count equal to the hosts, and the tree equal to a scan of the lists and the embed fields (`checkTree`); a second test holds that the sequences reach what they are for (insertions that held, moves, refusals, hosts and listed nodes removed, builds with items, a tree three deep, the three kinds of error). All 20 seeds equal the oracle. Mutation checks on the engine, each reverted: dropping the cycle check, the second-container check or the re-placement in `release` fails the model test from seed 701.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SKPNR8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
