    "title": "**The two reproductions of the Done when**",
    "text": "**The two reproductions of the Done when**: each was written first as a scratch script outside the repository, run on the reference copy of the shell, and failed there; each is now a test of `containment.test.ts` under \"the two issues of the old engine\", and passes on the engine. [Sibling indexes are not kept dense](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252Y7WR001): on the reference copy, after A, B, C under P, B moved to Q and a new child D appended on P, `P children = A@0 D@2 C@2` and the script exits 1 (`two children of P share an index (0 | 2 | 2); a dense list would be 0,1,2`); this one fails when run and not only when read. On the engine the list of P is [A, C, D] with places 0, 1, 2 and Q holds [B]. [A child can end with two `parent` pairs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2532JJR001): on the reference copy, the generic setter `container2.children = [...container2.children, child]` leaves `parent pairs of child = [container2,container1]` and the script exits 1 (`the child has 2 parent pairs`); `appendChild` and `insertChild` no longer reproduce it, because they detach the child's prior containment, and the issue's text names lines of `node.ts` that have moved. On the engine, `insertItem` of the child into a second container and the clear-then-add write are `Refused`, the child has one container, and after `removeItem` and `insertItem` it has the other.",
