    "title": "**Recorded as waiting**",
    "text": "**Recorded as waiting**: [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) is one function, `existence`, which every ordered read and write that names a host with no record reaches, and [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) is one function, `inShape`, which every ordered read and write reaches for the shape (an undeclared field, a derived entry, an item that is not a string) and for the second value of a `one` or `optional` partitioning field; each throws `Undecided` where the oracle does, and the partitioning refusals are `Refused`, not `Undecided`. `exists` and `size` still throw `Undecided('Existence')` (`WAITING_ON` in `engine.ts` holds them). A list entry that names a node with no record stays in the list, its bucket waits in the map of the reverse of nodes with no record, and no read counts the bucket as existence; `items` and `placeOf` of a host with no record are `Undecided('Existence')` while `values` of it is empty, as in the oracle. A splice on a field that is not ordered is `Refused`, as in the oracle; whether that is Enforcement's waits for that open point.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SKPNR8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
