    "title": "**Gaps seen, not decided**",
    "text": "**Gaps seen, not decided**: two are written as [Open points](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000J) of the design: [a node both embedded and listed](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z) (choice 1 above is the engine's reading) and [the order of the checks on a partitioning field of cardinality `one` or `optional`](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001) (cardinality, then the rule, as the oracle does, held by a test); both settled on 2026-10-17, the links pointing at where the design now states them. Also seen by the Coder and neither tested nor changed: `insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string, because the oracle checks the embedded-id rule in `addPair` only, so a node could be held by two owners, and no schema declares an ordered embed field; and the oracle's `mustPartition` and `holds` cross graphs and the engine's bucket read does the same, while the derived entry and the tree look at the subject's own graph, which no test can tell apart while there is one graph, until [Batch 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D). Filed 2026-10-16 as two open issues: [`insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001) and [the buckets of a reverse side are read across graphs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRWNPR001).",
