    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-16)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-16)**: [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V) built the ordered fields of the new engine in `Aperas.dev` (branch `js-apeironngn`), staged and not committed, and the engine keeps no sibling index: the place of a child is read from the list of its container, so a move leaves no gap and an append cannot repeat an index. The reproduction (children A, B, C under P; B moved to Q; a new child D appended on P) failed on the reference copy, where it prints `P children = A@0 D@2 C@2` and exits 1, and is now a test of `containment.test.ts` that passes on the engine: the list of P is [A, C, D] with places 0, 1, 2 and Q holds [B]; the model-based test `containment.model` holds the place equal to the index after every operation of 20 seeds. The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps the defect until [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) moves the shell onto the engine and [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes it. The question under Not proven, a moved child with no sibling index when a reconcile moves a block, concerns the reference copy's `writeField` and is not answered by the engine; it goes with the reference copy. The density of sibling indexes, an Open point of the design when this issue was filed, is no longer one: there is no index.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
