    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-16)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-16)**: [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V) built containment in the new engine in `Aperas.dev` (branch `js-apeironngn`), staged and not committed: the containment field is ordered and partitioning, so a write that gives a node a second container is refused, and `parent` is not stored but read from the reverse of `children`. The reproduction (a child written into the `children` of a second container through the generic setter) failed on the reference copy, where it prints `parent pairs of child = [container2,container1]` and exits 1 (`appendChild` and `insertChild` no longer reproduce it, since they detach the child's prior containment), and is now a test of `containment.test.ts` that passes on the engine: `insertItem` of the child into a second container and the clear-then-add write are `Refused`, the child has one container, and after `removeItem` and `insertItem` it has the other. The model-based test `containment.model` holds a single container for each node and no cycle after every operation of 20 seeds. The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps the defect until [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) moves the shell onto the engine and [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes it. Whether a production path of the reference copy writes a child into a second container without first taking it out, under Not proven, was not looked for and goes with the reference copy.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
