  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SNN1X0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 6 filed, the grapher's two questions, 2026-10-16**",
    "text": "**Batch 6 filed, the grapher's two questions, 2026-10-16**: the grapher filed Batch 6 and resolved the two issues whose reproductions now pass on the engine (the sibling gap and the second `parent`; the reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps the defect until Batches 11 and 12). Decided by the orchestrator: (1) the two gaps the coder saw (`insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string, so a node could be held by two owners; the oracle and the engine read buckets across graphs, which no test can tell until Batch 8) are filed as open issues under `issues/core.md`, each pointing at the batch that closes it (Batch 8 for the graphs; the ordered embed field has no schema using it, so a later batch or the schema check); (2) the `BUILT_BY` table stays as it is: it records the batch that built each operation, built ones included.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
