      }
    ],
    "title": "00D4SRT8KR003",
    "text": "Read from the code, not run. `addPair` on an embed field applies the rule for the value of an embed field: the value must be the id of a node whose owner is the subject and whose field is this one (otherwise `Refused`), of the embedded kind or a descendant (otherwise `Undecided('Enforcement')`). `insertItem` checks its item with `inShape(field, item)` and does not pass the host, so on an ordered embed field it takes any string. Two hosts could then list the same embedded id, which [the design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR013) says one node owns, and a host that is not the owner could list a node that its id gives to another owner.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D4SRT8KR004",
    "text": "The oracle and the engine do the same (`oracle.ts` `insertItem`, `engine.ts` `insertItem`), so a comparison of the two cannot find it. No schema declares an ordered embed field, neither the test schema nor the Aperas schema, and `closeSchema` accepts one, so no test reaches the case; it would need an inline schema.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D4SRT8KR005",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from the code)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR006:props:StringProp:00D4SRTQZG004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR006:props:StringProp:00D4SRTQZG005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D4SRT8KR006",
    "text": "The subject reaches the shape check only from `addPair` and `build`; the three splices (`insertItem`, `moveItem`, `removeItem`) never pass it. `build` and `addPair` of the same field are checked.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
