    "title": "What each read and rule should do across graphs",
    "text": "What each read and rule should do across graphs: [the design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8002) says that every read and write names the graph it acts on, and that a pair from one graph can point into another ([a reference across graphs](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4KD44M8001)), and is silent on whether the reverse side of a node shows the subjects of the other graphs, and whether a second container or a cycle is counted across graphs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4SRWNQ0001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4SRWNQ0003",
