    "title": "**Batch 7: the grapher's three questions, 2026-10-16** (the [brief](#id/BlockNode:00D4SV1J48000))",
    "text": "**Batch 7: the grapher's three questions, 2026-10-16** (the [brief](#id/BlockNode:00D4SV1J48000)): decided by the orchestrator to go on, none about the design rules already settled: (1) `tombstoneSubtree` is all-or-nothing when a member's kind has no marker, and the oracle changes to match; (2) the sweep's root kinds include the kinds that extend a root kind (inheritance of the meta-model); (3) generic writes of the marker field, or to a tombstone, stay allowed for now, and the grapher files that as an issue when Batch 7 is filed (a tombstone that can be written to is the revive gap the plan leaves open). The sweep is `sweep(graph): Id[]` returning the removed ids sorted by code point; the two filed issues, the cross-graph reads (Batch 8 should name it) and the ordered embed field, are not Batch 7's.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
