    "title": "**Batch 7 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**Batch 7 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-17**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built the tombstone and the tombstone of a subtree, embedded removal and `sweep(graph): Id[]`, with the oracle and the two reproductions written first, failing on the old engine in `Aperas/` and passing as engine tests in `tombstone.test.ts`, and `sweep.test.ts`. The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 605 of 605 in 26 s, `essential` 51 of 51 in 3.1 s, `--group engine` 535 of 535; the engine's files import only files of their own directory. The coder ran four mutations: three are caught by the model test or a hand-written case, and removing the `pinned` cleanup is caught only by the hand-written `sweep.test.ts` cases (accepted). The coder's question, answered by the orchestrator: the model test's reading of \"no live node refers to a tombstone's removed fields\" as the reverse reads and the lists checked right after each operation is accepted. For the grapher's filing: the design's interface list gains the `sweep(graph): Id[]` item; the plan's Batch 7 step 3 open point that the Freeflow settled is removed; the tombstoning issue's stale lines are refreshed; Batch 8's text names the cross-graph issue; the issue on writes to a tombstone or its marker is filed.",
