    "title": "00D4T7JDAR003",
    "text": "Built, and tested in `tombstone.test.ts`, `sweep.test.ts` and `tombstone.model.test.ts` in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (staged, not committed). The engine's `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` leave a node with no reference and out of every list, but nothing stops a generic write that follows. `insertItem` accepts a tombstone as an item, so a tombstone is listed in a container again (the test of a tombstone `dead` inserted into `top` after its stamp); a second `tombstone` of it then changes nothing, because the marker is set, so it stays listed until its container is tombstoned. `addPair` and `build` give a tombstone references again (the test \"a node written after the tombstone holds references again, and a second tombstone does not take them\"). `clearField` and `removePair` of the marker field make the node live again, with the references it lost gone and its literals kept; the model-based test makes 95 tombstones by a generic write of the marker and 33 generic clears of it in its sequences.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D4T7JDAR004",
    "text": "Both the engine and the oracle behave so, so a comparison of the two cannot find it. The engine has no revive operation and the design says none exists, so the clear of the marker is a revive that is not offered and cannot be told from a plain write.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
