    "title": "00D4T7JDAR008",
    "text": "Whether the shell ever writes the marker or writes to a tombstone through the generic operations. The Aperas schema holds `tombstonedAt` on three kinds, and the shell's own tombstoning goes through the engine's operation only once [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) moves the callers.",
