    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: the Coder's run: `tsc` of `core` and `cli` clean, group `engine` 535 of 535 in 6.5 to 9.3 s, `essential` 51 of 51 in 3.1 s (no file added to it), `commit` 605 of 605 in 26.2 s (Batch 6: 530 in 23.8 s). The orchestrator's run: `commit` 605 of 605 in 26 s, `--suite essential` 51 of 51 in 3.1 s (budget 5 s), `--group engine` 535 of 535; the engine's files import only files of their own directory. The model-based test, `tombstone.model.test.ts`, runs 20 seeds (721 to 740) of 250 operations over the test schema, compares the engine with the oracle by value, or by the class and the open point of the error, after every operation and the whole state every 12th, and holds the checks independent of the oracle: right after each `tombstone` or `tombstoneSubtree`, for each node newly tombstoned, `record` shows literals and the marker only, `up` is empty, no list holds it, its embedded nodes have no record, the reverse reads of the values it held no longer include it, its incoming `likes`, `mate`, `pinned` and `to` are as they were but for the pairs of the nodes tombstoned with it, every other node is unchanged but for the entries of containers that listed a tombstoned node, a second tombstone changes nothing and a refused one (a refused subtree included) changes nothing; the sweep removes exactly the unmarked tombstones, computed from reads before it by a mark through `values` of `items`, `refs` and `to` from the live `Box` records, the ids returned equal that set, each is gone from `record` and `idsOfKind`, each marked tombstone is kept, their `pinned` entries are gone, the other live nodes are unchanged and a second sweep gives `[]`; a tombstone keeps its literals; and at every step the reverse of `items`, `likes`, `mate`, `refs` and `to` equals a scan of the forward sides and `checkTree` holds. A second test holds that the sequences reach what they are for, with these counts in a run: tombstoned nodes 406, subtrees 194 (14 of several members, 8 refused), tombstones of a tombstone 60, builds of a tombstone with references 74, generic writes of the marker that made a tombstone 95, generic clears of it 33, sweeps 250 (169 removed something, 98 a tombstone holding references, 31 an island), marked tombstones kept 107; the file takes 2.9 s. Four mutations of `engine.ts` by the Coder, each reverted and the restore checked by `diff`: the removal from the container dropped fails 18 cases of the model test and 10 of `tombstone.test.ts`; the embedded nodes not dropped by the tombstone fails 20 and 6; the mark not going through a tombstone it reaches fails 5 and 1 of `sweep.test.ts`; the `pinned` cleanup of the sweep (`prepareRemoval()`) removed fails 0 of the model test and 2 of `sweep.test.ts`, because the model reads the reverse of `pinned` at every step and so builds it; the orchestrator accepted that, and a model run with the reverse of `pinned` unread would be a stronger check and is not built.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The reading of the Done when**",
    "text": "**The reading of the Done when**: \"no live node refers to a tombstone's removed fields\" is held as the reverse reads and the lists checked right after each operation, as listed above, and not as a property that stands after later writes, since a write after the tombstone (the marker's generic write, a `makeRef`, a `build`) gives the node references again. The orchestrator accepted this reading at its check.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
