    ],
    "title": "**The reproductions of the Done when**",
    "text": "**The reproductions of the Done when**: each was written first as a scratch script outside both repositories (`/tmp/batch7/repro1.mts` and `repro2.mts`), run on the old engine of the `Aperas/` checkout (`core/src/apeironNgn/node.ts`, the code that `Aperas.dev` keeps as the reference copy `core/src/shell/node.ts`), and failed there; each is now a test of `tombstone.test.ts` under \"the reproductions of the issue of the tombstone\" and passes on the engine. [Tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001), first: a container P with a child B1 that has a child B2, `tombstoneLiveSubtree(B1)` ends with `P children = [B1]`, B1 still having its `parent`, B2 having lost its `parent` as a side effect of the clearing of B1's `children`, and both stamped; the script exits 1 (`a tombstone is in no container's list, but B1 is in P's children`). On the engine P's list loses B1, and B1 and B2 have no `parent` and no `children` and are stamped. Second: a childless `list` block with a `StringProp`, `tombstoneVacuousContainers` stamps it and leaves the prop (`the node is tombstoned and still holds 1 prop(s); a tombstone keeps its literals only`); the script exits 1. On the engine a childless `list` block is left with its stamp and its literals (`type`) only. The third site of the issue, the folder removal, was not scripted, as asked. The tests assert the engine's rule and not the old defect, so nothing goes with the reference copy in Batch 12 except the scratch scripts, which are outside the repository.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
