    "title": "**Closed, in part**",
    "text": "**Closed, in part**: [tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001) for the nodes the engine tombstones, with a dated entry; the tombstones that the mirror holds (52 of 219 still hold `children`, `links` or `props`) are [Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001)'s, and the callers that tombstone are [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C)'s. Not closed, as the plan said: [no operation revives a tombstoned node](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CN1PT1B0001) and [a block that is unreachable and was never tombstoned is never collected](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D1A2AY68001). The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps the old tombstoning until Batch 11 and Batch 12.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided before the batch**",
    "text": "**Decided before the batch**: the sweep is an operation of the engine, `sweep(graph): Id[]`, as the interface now types it. `tombstoneSubtree` is all or nothing when a member's kind holds no marker, and the oracle was changed to say the same. The roots of the sweep are the root kinds and the kinds below them (the inheritance of the meta-model), tested with a root kind that has a child and a grandchild kind, in the engine and the oracle. The generic write of the marker, or to a tombstone, stays allowed for now.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Choices of the batch, reported by the Coder**",
    "text": "**Choices of the batch, reported by the Coder**: (1) `tombstoneSubtree` checks the role, then the record, then every member's kind, as `tombstone` does (the brief listed the record first for the subtree; the model cannot tell the two apart since its schema has the role). (2) `prepareRemoval()` runs in `tombstone` when the node holds an embed value, and in `sweep` only when there is a tombstone to remove, so a sweep with nothing to do builds nothing. (3) The sweep's candidates are the records of the kinds that declare the marker, collected before the first removal; a candidate that went with an embedding owner is skipped at its turn and its id is still returned (no schema gives an embedded kind the marker, so this is a guard, untested). (4) The walk of the subtree is in pre-order with an explicit stack and a visited set, the engine's and the oracle's. (5) `Registry.recordsOf(graph, kind)` is the one addition to the records, for the mark and the sweep to read one graph's collection. (6) The mark follows a followed field only through `rec.fields`, so a field the kind does not declare is never read.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
