    "title": "**Gaps seen, not decided**",
    "text": "**Gaps seen, not decided**: a tombstone made by the engine leaves no container, but a generic `insertItem` of it lists it again and a second `tombstone` then does nothing, so it stays listed until its container is tombstoned; this is part of [the writes to a tombstone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001). A member of a subtree that is a tombstone holding a list written after its tombstone is walked through, and keeps its stamp (tested). The tombstone removes the node from the containers in its bucket whole, and the sweep marks inside the graph it names, so a live node of another graph that points at a tombstone does not keep it; both belong to [the buckets read across graphs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRWNPR001), which [Batch 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D) closes and now names.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Stale places, corrected**",
    "text": "**Stale places, corrected**: the Open point of step 3 (whether the sweep is an operation of the engine), removed as settled; the Gated by of this batch, which named Existence and not Enforcement; the design's list of the interface's writes, which gained the sweep; the lines of the tombstoning issue that cite the old code; the Open point of Batch 3 that the sweep has no operation (it now carries a \"Built\" line); the sentence of Batch 6's done record that said `schema.test.ts` takes `tombstone` as the unbuilt example.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG00B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Changes outside the engine's new code**",
    "text": "**Changes outside the engine's new code**: `schema.test.ts` takes `danglingRefs` and `dropGraph` as the unbuilt examples; `suites/commit.suite.mjs` names the three new files; the oracle's `tombstoneSubtree` and `sweep` and its header changed as listed above, `interface.ts` gained the sweep, and `exists`, `size`, the generic reads and writes and the ports are untouched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T85FNG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
