    "title": "**Since (2026-10-17), the engine tombstones as the rule says; the mirror and the callers do not yet**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-17), the engine tombstones as the rule says; the mirror and the callers do not yet**: [Batch 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014) built `tombstone`, `tombstoneSubtree` and `sweep` in the engine. The reproductions of the Root cause were written first and run on the old code, where both fail: `tombstoneLiveSubtree(B1)` leaves B1 in the `children` of its container P with its `parent`, and takes the `parent` of B2 away as a side effect; `tombstoneVacuousContainers` stamps a childless `list` block that has a prop and leaves the prop. Both pass as tests of the engine in `tombstone.test.ts`: P's list loses B1, B1 and B2 have no `parent` and no `children` and are stamped, and the childless block is left with its stamp and its literals only. The third site, the folder removal, was not scripted. The issue stays open: the 52 tombstones of the mirror wait for [Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001), the callers that tombstone for [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), and the old code stays in the reference copy under `core/src/shell/` until [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S).",
