    "title": "**Since (2026-10-17), two more reads across graphs, built in Batch 7**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-17), two more reads across graphs, built in Batch 7**: [Batch 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR014) added two places that read across graphs, the same in the engine and the oracle. The removal of a tombstoned node from the lists that hold it reads the bucket of the containment field whole, whichever graph the container is in. The sweep marks inside the graph it names, from the live nodes of that graph through that graph's records, so a live node of another graph that points at a tombstone does not keep it, and the sweep of the tombstone's graph deletes it and leaves the pair of the other graph pointing at an id with no record, which `dropGraph` refuses to do to a whole graph. Neither is tested with two graphs. [Batch 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D) lists both among the reads it decides.",
