    "title": "**The change**",
    "text": "**The change**: in `core/src/apeironNgn/`, `engine.ts` gaining `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` (a tombstone leaves every list that holds it, loses every reference and embedded node, and keeps its literals) and `sweep(graph): Id[]`, which the interface gained; `records.ts` gaining `recordsOf(graph, kind)`. In `cli/src/tests/`, the oracle's `tombstoneSubtree` made all or nothing and its `sweep` written by scan, and in `engine/` the tests `tombstone`, `sweep` and `tombstone.model`, named in the `commit` suite and none in `essential`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T9MBEG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T9MBEG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The model-based test**",
    "text": "**The model-based test**: `tombstone.model` runs 20 seeds of 250 operations and holds the engine equal to the oracle after every operation, with the checks independent of the oracle: a tombstone holds literals and the marker only, is in no list, and keeps its incoming references; the sweep removes exactly the tombstones that a mark from the live nodes does not reach, an island included.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T9MBEG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T9MBEG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The two reproductions**",
    "text": "**The two reproductions**: each was run on the old engine and failed there (a subtree tombstoned by `tombstoneLiveSubtree` stays in its container's list; a childless `list` block tombstoned by `tombstoneVacuousContainers` keeps its prop), and each is now a test of `tombstone.test.ts` that passes on the engine. The reference copy keeps both behaviours until it is deleted.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D4T9MBEG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D4T9MBEG005",
