    "title": "**3. Reads and rules across graphs**",
    "text": "**3. Reads and rules across graphs**: the reads that give a node's relations (`subjectsOf`, `firstSubjectOf`, `countSubjectsOf`, the derived entry and the tree) are filtered to the graph they name; the rules that guard an invariant of the whole store (one container, no cycle, the second-value and cycle rule of a partitioning field, the check of `dropGraph`) read across graphs; a sweep marks and deletes within the graph it names and never keeps another graph's tombstone alive, so a reference across graphs may dangle after the sweep of the graph it points into ([Reads and rules across graphs](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D5AYGHJ0001)). The oracle and the engine are made to say the same, each read tested with a subject in each of two graphs.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
