    "title": "**4. The graph that holds a node**",
    "text": "**4. The graph that holds a node**: `graphOf(id)` joins the interface's reads, so that `aperas://id/<ID>` resolves through the engine without naming the graph; it reads the `graph` field of the engine's record (`Rec.graph` in `records.ts`), which already exists ([the interface's Reads](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D5AYTCJR001)). It is proposed by the orchestrator and awaits the user's confirmation; it is built (2026-10-17) and stays unconfirmed, and the steps to remove it are in [the done record](#id/BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
