    "title": "**5. An embedded id in a containment field**",
    "text": "**5. An embedded id in a containment field**: an id of the embedded shape cannot be listed in a containment field, in `addPair`, `insertItem` and `moveItem` alike, so a node is owned or contained, never both ([Containment](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR00Z)). The check of a partitioning field (`partition`) then meets no embedded id. By itself it does not close [the `insertItem` issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001), which is the other way round: an ordered embed field taking any string, so that a node could be held by two owners; the follow-up of the Coder closed it (see the done record).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5B19E9G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The names `id` and `tree`, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**The names `id` and `tree`, 2026-10-17**: the user asked where the graph of a record is stored; the orchestrator checked the code: the record of the engine carries its `graph` as a field beside its id and kind, and the records are also filed in a collection for each graph and kind, so `graphOf(id)` reads that field. The user then decided: the name `id` is hard excluded as a graph identifier, and the name `tree` is soft excluded: a future graph named `tree` is warned of a possible collision with the default graph that has no identifier (today's default); the graph identifier is to be set in `aperas.config.json`, which is not designed yet, so today's default is `tree`. The orchestrator's reading: the reserved `id` is part of the grammar of a `graph.domain` that the engine enforces (a graph identifier is an authority, and `id` is the one authority that `aperas://` gives a fixed meaning), so no layer can create it; the warning about `tree` is the shell's, since \"the default graph without an identifier\" is the shell's notion (the engine has no default graph).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D5B422T0001"
    ]
  },
