    "title": "**Several graphs applied, the grapher's two questions, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**Several graphs applied, the grapher's two questions, 2026-10-17**: the grapher applied [the decisions](#id/BlockNode:00D5AHW09G001) and [the names `id` and `tree`](#id/BlockNode:00D5B19E9G001) to the design and the plan (`check-links` clean). Decided by the orchestrator: (1) \"the partitioning check\" in Batch 8 is read as the grapher read it: the refusal of an embedded id in a containment field makes the check meet no embedded id; the check itself does not change in Batch 8, and the forward climb of a single-valued field stays in Batch 14; (2) the grammar of a `graph.domain` is the hostname rule of RFC 1123: letters, digits and hyphens inside a label, no hyphen at a label's ends, at most 63 characters a label and 253 a name, a label may start with a digit, lowercase only, and `id` refused. The origin link of the `id` and `tree` rule in the design is to be added by the grapher at the filing of Batch 8, now that the entry exists.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5B3C4E8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**No `graph` field in the mirror, clarify the two folds, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**No `graph` field in the mirror, clarify the two folds, 2026-10-17**: the user decided the mirror needs no `graph` field in its documents, and asked that the design clarify \"records by kind and by graph\" in both folds: in the mirror a document's graph is given by file containment (the file for its graph and kind holds it), and in memory by a field (the record carries its `graph` and is filed in the collection of its graph and kind). The load gives each record the graph of the file it reads; the dump writes each record to the file of its graph and kind.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D5BEXM70001"
    ]
  },
