    "title": "00D5B422T0001",
    "text": "Promoted (2026-10-17) to [Graphs in memory](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CHJXK8003), where the engine enforces the grammar of a `graph.domain` and refuses `id`, and to [Addressing](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D5AYBPWR001), where `aperas://id/` has its fixed meaning and the shell warns of a graph named `tree`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5B19E9G001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BATEM0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 8 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**Batch 8 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-17**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built the graph name grammar (`graphName.ts`), the registry of graphs, `createGraph` and `dropGraph`, `graphOf` (unconfirmed by the user, built, with the steps to remove it in the Report), the decided cross-graph reads (only `subjectsOf` visibly differed in the first run; `firstSubjectOf` and `countSubjectsOf` read the same unfiltered bucket and are made to filter), and the refusal of an embedded id in a containment field (one old `containment.test.ts` case that asserted the opposite was rewritten). The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 702 of 702 in 36.8 s (budget 60 s), `essential` 51 of 51 in 4.0 s (budget 5 s), `--group engine` 632 of 632; the engine's files import only files of their own directory. Of the coder's mutations all were caught except removing the `moveItem` refusal (step 5). Decided by the orchestrator: (1) a correction of the orchestrator's: refusing an embedded id in a containment field does not close the gap of `insertItem` into an ordered embed field; that gap is the other way round (an embed field accepting any string, so a node could be held by two owners), and is closed by `insertItem` into an embed field checking the embedded-id rule as `addPair` does, which the coder does in a follow-up with a test that fails without it, together with the `moveItem` refusal left uncaught by the model; (2) `countSubjectsOf` being O(bucket) once more than one graph exists is accepted and noted in the done record, no issue. The grapher's filing also adds the origin link for the \"no `graph` field in the mirror\" decision and checks the plan's \"4. The master map and the collections\" and \"2. Written by graph and kind\" for staleness.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
