    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-17**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed. The grammar of a graph's name, the registry of graphs, `createGraph` and `dropGraph`, the reads of a node's relations filtered to the graph they name, `graphOf` (built, unconfirmed by the user) and the refusal of an embedded id in a containment field. In `core/src/apeironNgn/`: `graphName.ts` (new), `records.ts`, `engine.ts` and `interface.ts`; in `cli/src/tests/`: `support/oracle.ts`, `support/engineTree.ts`, and the new `engine/graphs.test.ts`, `graphReads.test.ts`, `embeddedId.test.ts` and `graphs.model.test.ts`. A follow-up of the Coder, checked the same day, closed [`insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001) and added a case for the `moveItem` refusal: `engine.ts` and `support/oracle.ts` (one line each) and the new `engine/embeddedOrdered.test.ts`. `exists`, `size`, `danglingRefs` and the ports are unchanged, and the boundary test passes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01D",
    "type": "listItem",
