    "title": "**Closed, in whole**",
    "text": "**Closed, in whole**: [the buckets of a reverse side are read across graphs](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRWNPR001), in whole by step 3: its reproduction is the test, `graphReads.test.ts`, which failed on the engine before the change and passes. Closed by the follow-up of the Coder, and not by step 5: [`insertItem` into an ordered embed field accepts any string](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4SRT8KR001). Step 5 refuses an embedded id in the containment field and the issue is the other way round (an embed field accepting any string, so a node could be held by two owners); the follow-up has `insertItem` into an embed field check the embedded-id rule as `addPair` does, with a test that fails without it (see below).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decided before the batch**",
    "text": "**Decided before the batch**: the name of a graph follows the host of a URL authority (lowercase DNS labels, hyphens only inside a label) with `id` refused, and no other name is special; the reads that give a node's relations are filtered to the graph they name, the rules that guard a whole-store invariant read across graphs, and the sweep deals within one graph; the partitioning check is unchanged; the engine holds no settings of a graph. `graphOf` is the orchestrator's proposal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBG007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBG007:links:Link:00D5BD4CKG000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0019",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBG007:links:Link:00D5BD4CKG000:props:StringProp:00D5BG8FKR000",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "478"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Decided at the check**",
    "text": "**Decided at the check**: (1) a correction of the orchestrator's own reading: refusing an embedded id in a containment field does not close the gap of `insertItem` into an ordered embed field (see above); the Coder's follow-up closes it. (2) `countSubjectsOf` is O(bucket) once more than one graph exists (the three reverse reads filter the bucket); this is accepted and noted here, with no issue. A count kept for each graph would change the shape of the buckets; the ports of [Batch 14](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0019), which count large buckets, are the place to revisit it if it matters.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBG008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Choices of the batch, reported by the Coder**",
    "text": "**Choices of the batch, reported by the Coder**: the check of a drop scans the forward sides of the records of the other graphs and does not build every reverse (a build costs on a graph that never needed the reverses, and a drop is rare); the drop takes the graph's pairs out of the buckets directly and deletes the records wholesale, not `release` for each (`release` also re-places children, which a wholesale drop does not need); the three reverse reads skip the filter while one graph exists, so a single-graph count stays O(1); `graphName.ts` is a file of its own beside `ids.ts` so that the shell can import it as it will `ids.ts`; the names `Registry.addGraph`, `removeGraph`, `recordsIn`, `records`, `hasSeveralGraphs` and `bucketedSubjects` are the Coder's, as the brief said, and `inspectEngine.bucketedSubjects` is for tests only; `checkTree` takes a graph argument (default `default`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBG009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Gaps seen, not decided**",
    "text": "**Gaps seen, not decided**: none new. The `moveItem` refusal not seen by a run was covered by the follow-up, and the O(bucket) count is in the entries above.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
