    "title": "**Stale places, corrected**",
    "text": "**Stale places, corrected**: the text of steps 4 and 5 (`graphOf` built and unconfirmed; step 5 not closing the `insertItem` issue, which the follow-up closes), Closes, Gated by and Done when of this batch; Numbering (\"The nine are done\") and the Task Breakdown text; steps 2 and 3 of [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M), which now say that a document holds no `graph` field and that the load gives each record the graph of the file it reads. [Batch 4's step 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00A) (one map from id to record, one collection for each graph and kind) is not stale against the design's two folds, and is left as it stands.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DBR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Changes outside the engine's new code**",
    "text": "**Changes outside the engine's new code**: `schema.test.ts` lost its two `NotBuiltError` assertions for `createGraph` and `dropGraph`; `ids.test.ts`'s uniqueness case now runs on the engine and the oracle; `containment.test.ts` (the rewritten case above); `suites/commit.suite.mjs` names the four new files and none is in `essential`; the oracle gained the name grammar, `graphOf` and `notOwned`. The follow-up added `engine/embeddedOrdered.test.ts` to `suites/commit.suite.mjs` (after `embeddedId.test.ts`; not in `essential`) and changed `inShape(field, item)` to `inShape(field, item, host)` in `engine.ts` (and the comment of `inShape`) and in the oracle's `insertItem`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
