    "title": "**The follow-up of Batch 8 checked, and the suites' timings, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**The follow-up of Batch 8 checked, and the suites' timings, 2026-10-17**: the coder closed the gap of `insertItem` into an ordered embed field (the embedded-id rule in the engine and the oracle, with a test that fails without it) and added a test that fails when the `moveItem` refusal is removed. The orchestrator ran the suites: `--group engine` and `commit` 708 of 708 in 41.6 s (the coder saw 49.6 s), `essential` 51 of 51 in 4.4 s and 3.9 s (the coder's first run took 6.6 s, over its 5 s budget, with a grapher and the service working at the same time, a load average of 3 to 4; the calibration of [Layer 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D457HDWG001) is that a timing carries its load). Decided by the orchestrator: the suites stay as they are; `essential` is within its budget on a quiet machine (about 4 s), `commit` has room (about 42 s of 60 s); the budgets are watched at each batch, and Batch 9 adds nothing to `essential` beyond one second. The `insertItem` issue is closed by this follow-up, not by Batch 8's refusal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BGVC20001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The follow-up of the Coder, checked 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**The follow-up of the Coder, checked 2026-10-17**: two small fixes after the orchestrator's check of the batch. (1) `insertItem` into an ordered embed field checks the embedded-id rule (owner, field and kind of the id) as `addPair` does: `engine.ts` line 603 `inShape(field, item)` became `inShape(field, item, host)`, and the oracle's `insertItem` the same (the diff is two lines in the engine, with the comment of `inShape`, and one in the oracle). (2) The `moveItem` refusal has a test that fails without it. The tests are the new `engine/embeddedOrdered.test.ts`, 6 cases each run on the engine and the oracle, named in `commit.suite.mjs` and not in `essential`, over a test schema of `Pack` (two ordered embed fields, `parts` and `spares`, both embedding `Part`), `Part`, `Big extends Part` and `Other`: `insertItem` takes an id the host embeds (at the end, at a place, a descendant kind); refuses the embedded node of another owner (the reverse `subjectsOf` stays `[a]`), an id of the other field, a top-level id, a non-id and an id of another owner, the list unchanged; is `Undecided('Enforcement')` for an embedded node of another kind; gives the outcome `addPair` gives for seven values on fresh stores (reaching ok, `Refused` and `Undecided`); and `moveItem` of an embedded id in `items` is refused with a message matching \"embedded node\", while an absent non-embedded id gives \"is not in items\". The `moveItem` case reads a message because the refusal cannot be seen by its class (the id is never in the list, so \"not in the list\" is `Refused` first, with the same class); a rewording of either message breaks it, and the alternative the Coder named, dropping the check from `moveItem` as unreachable, was not taken. Mutations, each under `timeout 100` over 88 cases (baseline 88 of 88): the engine's `inShape` without the host 4 failures, the same in the oracle 4, the engine's `moveItem` without `notOwned` 1, the oracle's 1; each restored from a copy. Checks: `tsc --noEmit` of `cli` clean, `--group engine` 638 of 638, `essential` 51 of 51, `commit` 708 of 708 (the timings are in the Done when, checked). Staged: `engine.ts`, `oracle.ts`, `commit.suite.mjs` and `embeddedOrdered.test.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D5BD3DB8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BM7928001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BM7928001:links:Link:00D5BM7SFR000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D5BKMV0G005",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BM7928001:links:Link:00D5BM7SFR000:props:StringProp:00D5BM7SFR001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
