  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5BXSWD8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The views graph is `views.tree`, the table is in `graphs`, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**The views graph is `views.tree`, the table is in `graphs`, 2026-10-17**: the user decided the name of the graph of the views is `views.tree`, not `views.threads.tree`: the order of \"under\" is the topology of the linking design: design > {issues, planning, history} > discussions > threads > views, so `views.tree` is a sibling of `threads.tree` under `tree`, lower in the order and not a subdomain of threads; and the table of settings goes in a `graphs` key of `aperas.config.json`, keyed by graph name, the existing `graph` keys giving the main graph's defaults when the table is absent. So the graphs are `tree` (tracked kinds, `Apeiron/`, 10 s), `threads.tree` (thread-scoped tree kinds, `Apeiron/.state/`, 3 s) and `views.tree` (`TreeView`, `Apeiron/.state/`, 3 s).",
