    "text": "**The views graph is `treeviews`, 2026-10-17**: the user changed the name again: `treeviews`, not `views.tree`, because the views can index many other graphs and not only `tree`; it is a graph of its own at the top level of the names, not under `tree`. It is a valid `graph.domain` (one label) and does not collide with `tree`. The order of \"under\" of the topology stays: design > {issues, planning, history} > discussions > threads > views; the graph that references every other and is referenced by none. The names are therefore `tree`, `threads.tree` and `treeviews`; wherever the previous entry says `views.tree` read `treeviews`.",
