    "@id": "BlockNode:00D5C44ZSG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 9 steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**Batch 9 steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-17**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built the format and the dump (`mirrorDump.ts`), the load (`mirrorLoad.ts`), the exact round trip, the writers and the two missing rules of the migration scripts (rules 5 and 6), with the mapping from (graph, kind) to a file taken as an argument; step 2 is not built. The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 821 of 821 in 40.6 s, `essential` 53 of 53 in 3.5 s (the new fixture round trip took the old one's slot at 27 ms for its slowest case, the old `store/roundtrip.test.ts` moved to `commit`). The coder reports: both scripts hold rules 5 and 6 and `verify-migration.py` reports 0 unexpected differences on a fresh scratch clone with a second run changing nothing; the new load and dump return the migrated copy of the real mirror byte for byte, except the two `FolderNode` files (the mirror lists `path` before `children`, the Format `children` first); that copy loads in about 360 ms with no errors, warnings or dangling ids. Decided by the orchestrator: (1) the Format puts `path` before `children` for a `FolderNode`, as the real mirror does (no migration rule: `path` goes in Batch 16 anyway), and the coder sets the order in code; (2) the `localeCompare` issue is closed with the simulated collation test, no real id differing; (3) a `parent` naming no document is returned by the load in its own list of undefined ids, the engine's `danglingRefs` not seeing a derived entry, and the design's sentence on the load is worded for that. The two answers on the `tree` warning (warn once when the table has an entry keyed `tree`, the entry is used) and on `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT` (it keeps winning for the main graph's directory) were confirmed by the user. A stray scratch service of the coder's loaded the real mirror (pids 569794 and 569809, runtime directory `/home/will/scratch/run6`), received nothing, is not dirty and exits by its idle timer at about 21:28; the user decides if it is stopped sooner; the orchestrator did not touch it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D6HCYP58001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6H5V1BR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The hung service stopped, Batch 9 step 2 checked, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**The hung service stopped, Batch 9 step 2 checked, 2026-10-19**: a command of the coder (an `aperas insert` with `</dev/null` where a pipe was meant, so with an empty body: a move of the Turn 13 heading into its own subtree) left the service (pid 498193) in a loop at about 97% of a CPU from 2026-10-17 21:20 to 2026-10-19 16:20 (1 day 20 hours of CPU time). The user, back from the weekend, said to stop it; `aperas service stop` timed out after 10 s of SIGTERM (busy loop), then the orchestrator sent SIGKILL to that one pid, checked the mirror on disk (all files parse, no unstaged diff, no parent cycle, the Turn 13 heading under its task with its Ask as the only child: the bad move never reached disk, since the loop kept the flush timer from firing), and started the service again by the standing arrangement for a stopped service: it rehydrated 105,476 quads and answers. The coder's prepared Work and Report for Turn 13 was inserted by pipe. Step 2 checked by the orchestrator on 2026-10-17 with the in-process suites: `commit` 862 of 862 in 44 s, `essential` 52 of 52 in 3.6 s, `--group mirror` 126 of 126 (the coder: the corpus round trip of the migrated copy of the real mirror is byte for byte for all 8 files, 14 mutations killed). Decided by the orchestrator on the coder's three questions: (1) the design is worded for the confirmed rule, a warning for a table entry keyed `tree`, the entry used; the case of a fourth graph named `tree` is not wanted; (2) in Batch 11 the service calls only `loadMirror`, whose mapping names the same three graphs; `createMirrorGraphs` stays for a start with no load and for tests; the load is unchanged; (3) a config with a `graphs` key and no `graph` key stays invalid, as a config has always needed `graph`. Two defects to file: a move into its own subtree is not refused by the working engine and loops the service (the new engine's no-cycle rule of partitioning fields refuses it, so Batch 11 closes it), and the skills should say that `< /dev/null` belongs to a move only, never to an `insert` with a body.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D6HD03M8001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6H8QJXR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Skills v4.8: `< /dev/null` is for a move only, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**Skills v4.8: `< /dev/null` is for a move only, 2026-10-19**: the user found it nonsense that a coder wrote `cat file | aperas insert … </dev/null` (the redirect replaces the pipe, the insert has an empty body, the CLI takes it for a move) and said to fix it. The change: one sentence, \"`< /dev/null` belongs to a move only (no body); never on an `insert` that has a body or a pipe, because the redirect replaces the pipe and turns the insert into a move\", in the move line of the base skill's quick reference, in the move recipes of `aperas-grapher` and in the \"Moving a Node\" section of `references/mechanics.md`; the four skills go to v4.8; the grapher records the delta so that `skill_drift.py` passes; skill-only, no `npm run verify`; the user commits on `oxigraph`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HA6M7G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Skills v4.8 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**Skills v4.8 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-19**: in `Aperas/` (`oxigraph`, staged, not committed) the diff is 5 files: the rule that `< /dev/null` is for a move only, with its reason, in the base skill's quick reference row and patterns, in the two move recipes of `aperas-grapher`, in a note of `aperas-coder` (an insert with a body takes the pipe and no redirect), and in `references/mechanics.md` with the wrong form (`cat file | aperas insert <id> </dev/null`, marked as wrong) and the right one; the Status of the four skills and of `mechanics.md` is v4.8. `skill_drift.py` fails as expected (the grapher has not recorded v4.8) and `aperas check-links` is clean; `npm run verify` was not run (skill-only). Next: the grapher records the v4.8 delta once its Batch 9 filing is done.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
