    ],
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR003",
    "text": "A command of the Coder, an `aperas insert` with `< /dev/null` where a pipe was meant, had an empty body and so ran as a move: it moved the Turn 13 heading of `.threads/coder.md` into its own subtree. The service (pid 498193) then ran in a loop at about 97 percent of a CPU from 2026-10-17 21:20 to 2026-10-19 16:20, 1 day 20 hours of CPU time. `aperas service stop` timed out after 10 s of SIGTERM (a busy loop), and the orchestrator sent SIGKILL to that one pid.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "The mirror on disk was checked after the kill",
    "text": "The mirror on disk was checked after the kill: every file parses, there is no unstaged diff, there is no cycle in `parent`, and the Turn 13 heading stood under its task with its Ask as the only child. The bad move never reached disk, since the loop kept the flush timer from firing. The service started again by the standing arrangement and rehydrated 105,476 quads.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR005",
    "text": "**Root cause** (read from a search, and run in the reproduction of piece 3 of Batch 11)",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR006"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR006:props:StringProp:00D6HAEZY8004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR006:props:StringProp:00D6HAEZY8005",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR006",
    "text": "The move path of `kgInsert.ts` (lines 67 to 102) repositions the node after the anchor, and a search of the file for a check of the anchor against the moved node's subtree (cycle, ancestor, descendant) finds none. The loop is not in the move: the Coder's reproduction of 2026-10-20 (`commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts`, run on the old code) shows `runInsert` of a heading after its own child returning in under 1 s (`moved after`), `runShow` and `runTree` returning, and `runPath` of the moved heading never returning (probed per step under `timeout 8`: `show` and `tree` rc 0, `path` rc 124). The loop is the walk of the parent chain (`toPath`) over the cycle that the move makes, so any command that walks the chain after the move freezes the service, not only the next `insert`. With a one-line guard in `kgInsert.ts` that walks the anchor's parents up to the target and throws, the reproduction ends by itself in 1.8 s; the guard was not kept.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR005",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR007",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR008",
      "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR009"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR008:props:StringProp:00D6HAEZYG000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR008:props:StringProp:00D6HAEZYG001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR008",
    "text": "Which other commands that walk the parent chain loop over the cycle: `path` was shown to, `show` and `tree` of the artifact returned, and the others were not run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR007",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR009",
    "text": "Whether `--before` and a move between artifacts fail the same way; only the one move was run.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR007",
