    "title": "The new engine refuses it",
    "text": "The new engine refuses it: containment is a partitioning field, and the engine ensures that the relation has no cycle ([Partitioning fields](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3CJDGH8001), built in [Batch 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR00V)). [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) closes this issue by that no-cycle rule of the engine, when the move reaches the engine's `moveItem` and `insertItem` (piece 6, the flip), and by the reproduction `commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts`, which piece 6 renames and names in `commit.suite.mjs`: it has to end by itself with a refusal that names the cause and the service answering. No change to the working engine is decided.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00A",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR00C",
    "text": "**Workaround**",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00D"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00D:props:StringProp:00D6HAEZYG004",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00D:props:StringProp:00D6HAEZYR000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D6HAEDCR00D",
    "text": "Until then, do not move a node after an anchor that is in its own subtree. If the service loops, the orchestrator stops it with the user's approval and checks the mirror on disk before starting it again.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR00C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
