  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-17**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-17**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed (58 files in all). Steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6 were built first, and step 2 after the user's answers on the table of settings, together with the `FolderNode` order fix. The format and the dump of the engine's records, the load of the mirror into the graphs, the exact round trip, the writers, the two missing rules of the migration scripts, the table of settings and the mapping from a graph and a kind to a file, the creation of the three graphs, the rule that gives a new node its graph, and `danglingRefs` in the engine. New in `core/src/shell/`: `mirrorFiles.ts`, `mirrorDump.ts`, `mirrorLoad.ts` and `graphOfPath.ts`; `graphConfig.ts` gained the reader of the table, and `aperasSchema.ts` gave `FolderNode` an explicit field order. In `core/src/apeironNgn/`, `engine.ts` gained `danglingRefs` (and `BUILT`, and one import of `compareIds`). In `scripts/`, `migrate-mirror.py` and `verify-migration.py` gained rules 5 and 6. In `cli/src/tests/`, the group `mirror/` (`format`, `load`, `files`, `roundtrip`, `roundtrip.model`, `settings`, `graphOfPath`), `engine/danglingRefs.test.ts`, `corpus/mirror.test.ts` (`demand`), `support/mirrorFixture.ts` and the three suites. `dehydrate.ts`, `store.ts`, `threadScope.ts`, `service.ts` and `kgInit.ts` are not touched, and the boundary test passes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
