    ],
    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: the Coder's runs after step 2: `tsc --noEmit` of `core` and `cli` clean, `--group mirror` 126 of 126 in 1.5 s, `--suite essential` 52 of 52 in 3.1 s, `npm run verify` (`commit`) 862 of 862 in 35.0 s of its 60 s budget. After steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6: `--group mirror` 85 of 85 in 1.2 s, `essential` 53 of 53 in 3077 to 3471 ms (51 of 51 in 3769 ms before any edit), `commit` 820 of 820 four times (51.8 s at a load average of 2.9, 42.9 s at 4.5 to 5.0, 41.5 s, and 48.7 s on the first run, which had one failing case). The orchestrator's runs: after steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6, `commit` 821 of 821 in 40.6 s and `essential` 53 of 53 in 3.5 s (the new fixture round trip took the old `store/roundtrip.test.ts` slot at 27 ms for its slowest case, and the old file moved to `commit`); after step 2, `commit` 862 of 862 in 44 s of 60 s, `essential` 52 of 52 in 3.6 s of 5 s and `--group mirror` 126 of 126. A timing carries its load ([Layer 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D457HDWG001)): the Coder's slower `commit` runs were taken with the real service at 90 percent of a core. The corpus round trip on the migrated copy of the real mirror is byte for byte for all 8 files, `FolderNode.jsonld` and `.state/FolderNode.jsonld` included (`--group corpus` 15 of 15 in 52.0 s, `corpus/mirror.test.ts` 1.26 s); the copy loads in about 360 ms (11,312 documents and 15,744 embedded entries) with no error, warning, rejected id or dangling id, and the dump takes about 110 ms.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**1, the dump**",
    "text": "**1, the dump**: `mirrorDump.ts` (`dumpDocuments`, `dumpText`, `dumpMirror(engine, root, mapping)`) writes a document as `@id`, `@type` and the fields of the kind in the order of `engine.schema` (so the Format), the value of each from `record()`; `children` is always written, every other empty set or unset field is left out; the values of a reference set and the embedded entries are sorted with `compareIds`, an embedded entry written inline from the `record()` of the embedded node; documents are sorted with `compareIds`; the text is `JSON.stringify(docs, null, 2)` and a newline. Nothing is rebuilt from pairs. `mirror/format.test.ts` (25 cases): the golden text, the field order of each of the five kinds against the Format list stated again in `support/mirrorFixture.ts`, the omissions, strings with quotes, a newline, U+2028, control characters and an emoji, integers (`1e21` gives `1e+21`, `-0` gives `0`), 10 shuffled seeds of 40 ids, shuffled reference and embedded sets, the order of a container's list, the derived `parent` at its place, and a hostile `localeCompare`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**3, the load**",
    "text": "**3, the load**: `mirrorLoad.ts` (`loadMirror(engine, root, mapping)`) skips an absent file; a file that is not JSON or not an array throws `MirrorFileError` (a dump over it afterwards would lose it); a document without a string `@id` and `@type` is an error and skipped. A repeated `@id` is counted over the top level and the embedded entries of all the files together, and every document that carries one is rejected, reported in `rejected` and in a warning. Containment is resolved over all the documents of all the graphs before any build (`resolveContainment`): the owner of a node is the container its `parent` names if a document that can hold it stands there, else the first container (file order) that lists it; a node whose `parent` names a container that did not list it is appended at its end, and every drop or append is a warning that names the node and both containers; `parent` is never put in the fields of a build. Then `startGraphs` (a `createGraph` for each graph, `default` dropped unless the mapping names it or it holds a record) and one `build` for each document, the embedded entries built after their owner with the id they carry and the graph of the owner. The errors of `build` go through `problemOf` alone (class, open point, id), a non-engine error being rethrown. The result holds the counts, `rejected`, `warnings`, `errors`, and `dangling`: the engine's `danglingRefs` of each graph plus the ids that a `parent` names with no document. `mirror/load.test.ts` (29 cases), among them the two reproductions and the ghost folder.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**4 and 5, the round trip and the writers**",
    "text": "**4 and 5, the round trip and the writers**: `support/mirrorFixture.ts` holds canonical documents as literals for every kind, in three graphs, with a tombstone, a `Link` with a `StringProp`, a `TreeView` with `unfolds`, an empty container, an empty file, the root folder listing the `.threads` folder of the other graph, and escapes. `mirror/roundtrip.test.ts`: the fixture byte for byte, loaded and dumped again, and a second case with the views file emptied. `mirror/roundtrip.model.test.ts`: 20 seeds (3001 to 3020) of random canonical mirrors, load then dump equal and dump, load, dump idempotent. `dumpMirror` writes every file of the mapping whole (an empty array for a kind with no record), makes the directories and checks the mapping before it writes, and decides nothing about when; `mirror/files.test.ts` covers it, and the service's `stampAll` and `diverged` are untouched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**6, the migration**",
    "text": "**6, the migration**: `migrate-mirror.py` and `verify-migration.py` hold six rules (`--rules` takes 1 to 6, default `123456`, no argument exits 2, `--dry` writes nothing). Rule 5 strips each `unfolds` entry whose target is not defined (a view left with none loses the key); rule 6 strips the `type` of every `ArtifactNode`; the checker classifies both and reports a clone that still holds an undefined `unfolds` entry or an artifact with a `type` as unexpected. On a fresh clone (`/home/will/scratch/mig1`): `--roundtrip` 8 files identical; the run changed 2963+2522 links, 191+32 tombstones, 100+10 containers, 12 deleted documents, 1 profile, 0 `unfolds` entries and 42 artifact types; `verify-migration.py` exit 0 with 0 unexpected differences, 11,324 documents before and 11,312 after, every conformity count zero; a second run changed 0 documents and 0 files. The real mirror holds no undefined `unfolds` entry, so rule 5 was exercised on a clone with 3 planted ones (3 stripped, a view with only undefined ones loses the key, 0 unexpected, a second run 0 files), and on an unmigrated clone `verify --rules 56` exits 1 and names both leftovers. `track` and `ingest` on a clone with only rule 3 applied registered 32 artifacts and rebuilt the folders, none with a `README.md` path and none of the six ids. `verify-migration.py` with a subset of rules applied rule 2's container edit whatever the rules; it was fixed, and each rule alone now gives 0.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**2, the table of settings and the graphs**",
    "text": "**2, the table of settings and the graphs**: `graphConfig.ts` gained `MAIN_GRAPH`, `THREADS_GRAPH`, `VIEWS_GRAPH`, `MIRROR_GRAPHS`, the two default intervals, `GraphSettings`, `GraphTable`, `warnTreeEntry` and `resolveGraphSettings(startDir?)`, which returns `{ graphs, warnings }` (the three settings in the order of the graphs, absolute directories). The config is the nearest above `startDir` or the one beside the fallback root; the checks of the table run before any path is made and each refusal names the file and the entry (14 cases, plus an interval past the double range and the malformed-JSON error kept); `tree` is `resolveEffectiveApeironRoot` (the variable wins over an entry of `tree`), the other two are `<root>/.state` unless their entry has a `mirror`, a relative `mirror` being taken from the config's directory; the entry has `mirror` and `flushIntervalMs`. With no `graphs` key the table gives `Apeiron/` at 10 s and `Apeiron/.state/` at 3 s twice. `mirrorFiles.ts` gained `KINDS_OF_GRAPH`, `mirrorMapping(settings)` (eight files, `<directory>/<kind>.jsonld`, in the order of the graphs) and `createMirrorGraphs(engine)` (the three graphs in order, `default` dropped unless it holds a record). `graphOfPath.ts` holds `isThreadsPath` and `graphOfNewNode(engine, { kind, path?, under? })`: a `Profile` is `tree`, a `TreeView` is `treeviews`, an `ArtifactNode` or `FolderNode` goes by its `path` (`.threads` or under `.threads/`, backslashes and a leading `./` normalised), anything else takes `engine.graphOf(under)`, and a missing path, a missing container or a container in no graph is an error; it is not wired. `mirror/settings.test.ts` (28 cases) and `mirror/graphOfPath.test.ts` (6) are new, and `files.test.ts` gained the shell's mapping, the graphs at start and the three-graph dump and load.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The mutations**",
    "text": "**The mutations**: steps 1, 3, 4, 5 and 6, each under `timeout 100` with the file restored after, all caught: the dump's sort back to `localeCompare` (1 failure, the hostile-collation case only), the repeated id merged (5), `parent` ignored (6), the empty `children` left out (8 or more), embedded entries unsorted (1), a reference set unsorted (2), no bridge across graphs for the derived `parent` (6 or more), the final newline dropped (4), fields written in reverse (6 or more), no append of a node to its parent's list (5), the other container's entry kept (5), a `parent` with no document not returned as dangling (1), the last container keeping a node listed twice (1), `danglingRefs` defined only by the graph named (5 or more), literals counted (1), unsorted (5 or more) and the pairs of every graph read (5 or more). Step 2, 14, all failing the tests: `threads.tree` at the tracked directory (4), `TreeView` mapped into `tree` (5), `default` not dropped (1), the graphs created in another order (1), a relative `mirror` resolved against the working directory (5), the 10 s and 3 s swapped (4), an entry for a fourth graph accepted (2), `.threadsx` taken as threads (2), the variable not winning for the main graph (1), no warning for a `tree` entry (1), an explicit `mirror` ignored for the other two (4), the `FolderNode` order back to `children` before `path` (23), a block taking the main graph (2) and a view taking the main graph (1).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The two reproductions on the reference copy**",
    "text": "**The two reproductions on the reference copy**: the last block of `load.test.ts` shows that `rehydrateStore` keeps both titles of a repeated id and gives a disagreeing node two parents, and the load rejects the repeated id and gives the node one; the block goes with the reference copy at Batch 12. The `localeCompare` issue has no reproduction on a real mirror (for ASCII ids every collation agrees with the code points), so `format.test.ts` shows `dehydrateToJsonLd` out of code-point order under a collation that reads digit runs as numbers (`String.prototype.localeCompare` patched for the case) and the dump in code-point order, and a second case with kinds `Item` and `Item2` under a hostile collation, the only case that fails when the dump's sort goes back to `localeCompare`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D6HANDAG004",
    "text": "**Choices of the load that the decision left to the Coder**, each in `mirrorLoad.ts` and a case in `load.test.ts`: a node listed by two containers with no `parent` stays in the first in file order and is dropped from the other with a warning; an entry listed twice in one container is kept once, with a warning; a `parent` that names a document that cannot hold a node (a kind with no `children`) leaves the node with no container, and that id is not dangling since a document stands there; a `parent` that is not a string is ignored with a warning; a document in the file of another kind is built as its `@type` says, with a warning; a file that is not a JSON array stops the load.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
