    ],
    "title": "**The bridge for the derived `parent`**",
    "text": "**The bridge for the derived `parent`**: the record of a node holds its `parent` only if the container is in the same graph (a read of the derived entry is filtered to the graph), so the record of the `.threads` folder in the threads graph has none, while its document in `.state/FolderNode.jsonld` states `parent` (the root folder of the main graph). The dump bridges it, as [A flush is a dump](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D39EAKW0001) allows: for a node with no `parent` in its record it asks the other graphs of the mapping for the subjects of `children` (one `subjectsOf` per graph) and writes the one it finds. Tested, and the mutation that removes it fails the model seeds. It is an implementation choice that the design may say.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HANDA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG006:links:Link:00D6HAP228002",
