        "target": "BlockNode:00D24N87SR01Z",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HANDAG006:links:Link:00D6HAP228002:props:StringProp:00D6HAP228003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "209"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Decided at the checks**",
    "text": "**Decided at the checks**: (1) the Format puts `path` before `children` for a `FolderNode`, as the real mirror does (the schema carries the order, no migration rule, since `path` goes in Batch 16 anyway), and [Format](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01Z) says so; (2) the `localeCompare` issue is closed with the simulated collation test, no real id differing; (3) a `parent` naming no document is returned by the load in its own list, the engine's `danglingRefs` not seeing a derived entry, and the design's sentence on the load says so; (4) the warning is for a table entry keyed `tree`, the entry used, and the case of a fourth graph named `tree` is not wanted (confirmed by the user, with the variable `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT` still winning for the main graph's directory); (5) in Batch 11 the service calls only `loadMirror`, whose mapping names the same three graphs, and `createMirrorGraphs` stays for a start with no load and for tests, the load being unchanged (`createGraph` refuses a graph that exists, so an engine prepared by `createMirrorGraphs` cannot be passed to `loadMirror`); (6) a config with a `graphs` key and no `graph` key stays invalid, as a config has always needed `graph`.",
