    "title": "**Incidents of the batch**",
    "text": "**Incidents of the batch**: a scratch service of the Coder, started with a runtime directory and a port but without the roots, loaded the real mirror (pids 569794 and 569809, runtime directory `/home/will/scratch/run6`), received nothing and was not dirty, and left by its idle timer; a coder's `aperas insert` with `< /dev/null` where a pipe was meant had an empty body, which is a move, of a heading into its own subtree, and left the working service in a loop for a day and 20 hours until the orchestrator stopped it on 2026-10-19, with the mirror on disk untouched (two issues are filed: [a move into its own subtree loops the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) and [the skills' recipe of a move does not say that `< /dev/null` is for a move only](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAJNRR001)).",
