    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-17)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-17)**: [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) wrote the dump of the new engine (`mirrorDump.ts` in `Aperas.dev`, branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed), which sorts its documents, its reference sets and its embedded entries with `compareIds`, the plain code-point comparison that [Batch 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR006) built, and never calls `localeCompare`. The issue observed nothing on the real mirror, and for ASCII ids every collation agrees with the code points, so no run on the mirror can fail on it; the reproduction is a simulated collation. `format.test.ts` patches `String.prototype.localeCompare` to read digit runs as numbers, shows the reference copy's `dehydrateToJsonLd` out of code-point order and the dump in code-point order, and a second case with kinds `Item` and `Item2` under a hostile collation is the one case that fails when the dump's sort goes back to `localeCompare` (the mutation, at 3 sites, gives 1 failure). The orchestrator decided at the check that this closes the issue. The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps its `localeCompare` (`dehydrate.ts` lines 58, 106, 130 and 138) until [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) replaces it with the layer of Batch 9 and [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes it.",
