    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-17)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-17)**: [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) wrote the load of the new engine (`mirrorLoad.ts` in `Aperas.dev`, branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed), in which `parent` wins ([A file whose `parent` and `children` disagree](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PV8GC0001)): the node is appended at the end of the `children` of the container its `parent` names, its entry in the other container is dropped, and a warning names both; a `parent` that names an id with no document leaves the node with no container, and the id is returned in the load's own list `dangling` with a warning; a node that a container lists and that has no `parent` stays in that container. A `parent` is never put in the fields of a build, since it is derived from the reverse of `children`. The reproduction is the last block of `load.test.ts`: on the reference copy's `rehydrateStore` a node whose `parent` and container disagree ends with two `parent` pairs, and on the load it has one container. The real mirror has none of the three cases, so only fixtures reach them. Mutations: `parent` ignored (6 failures), no append to the parent's list (5), the other container's entry kept (5), a `parent` with no document not returned as dangling (1). The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps its loader (`store.ts`'s `encodeDoc`) until [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) replaces it and [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes it.",
