    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-17)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-17)**: [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) wrote the load of the new engine (`mirrorLoad.ts` in `Aperas.dev`, branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed), which rejects every document that carries a repeated `@id` ([A repeated `@id` at load](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PC3ZG8001)): it keeps none of them, reports the id in `rejected` and in a warning, and goes on. The repeat is counted over the top level and the embedded entries of all the files together, since ids are unique across graphs. The reproduction is the last block of `load.test.ts`: on the reference copy's `rehydrateStore` a repeated id keeps both titles on one subject, and on the load no document with that id is built. The real mirror has no repeated id. Mutation: the repeated id merged (5 failures). The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps merging and the service keeps logging `duplicateIds` until [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) step 8 swaps the load, where a mirror with a repeated id then fails or needs a rule, and [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) deletes the reference copy.",
