    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-17), in `Aperas.dev` only**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-17), in `Aperas.dev` only**: [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) replaced the scope test by `graphOfPath.ts` in `src/shell/`: a node's scope is the graph it belongs to, so `isThreadsPath` tests the file-system path (`.threads` or under `.threads/`, backslashes and a leading `./` normalised) and `graphOfNewNode(engine, { kind, path?, under? })` gives an artifact or a folder its graph by that path, a block, a `Link` or a `StringProp` the graph of its container, a `Profile` `tree` and a `TreeView` `treeviews` (`mirror/graphOfPath.test.ts`, 6 cases; mutations: `.threadsx` taken as threads gave 2 failures, a block taking the main graph 2, a view taking the main graph 1). The engine's directory holds no scope test: [Batch 15](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4NBFKAG001) moved `threadScope.ts` to `src/shell/`. The new rule is built and tested and not wired, since the shell has no creation path before [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), which wires it and replaces `threadScope.ts` (step 1). The working checkout `Aperas/` keeps the test in `core/src/apeironNgn/`, so the issue is true there until the cutover.",
