    "title": "2026-10-17, [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) in `Aperas.dev`",
    "text": "2026-10-17, [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) in `Aperas.dev`: the mirror, the shell's first batch: the format and the dump of the engine's records, the load of the mirror into the three graphs, the exact round trip, the writers, the table of settings and the mapping from a graph and a kind to a file, the rule that gives a new node its graph, `danglingRefs` in the engine, and rules 5 and 6 of the migration scripts, staged on branch `js-apeironngn` and not committed. It resolves [`dehydrate` sorts with `localeCompare`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D39EY5B0001), [the loader writes `parent` from its own pair](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2538VKR001), [a repeated `@id` is logged and merged](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2595QAG001) and, for `Aperas.dev` only, [the thread-scope test inside the engine's directory](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2590B2R001), and builds the computing half of [`danglingRefs` computed and not read by the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001).",
