    "title": "**The change**",
    "text": "**The change**: in `core/src/shell/`, `mirrorFiles.ts`, `mirrorDump.ts`, `mirrorLoad.ts` and `graphOfPath.ts` (new), `graphConfig.ts` gaining the reader of the table of settings and `aperasSchema.ts` giving `FolderNode` an explicit field order, `path` before `children`; in `core/src/apeironNgn/`, `engine.ts` gaining `danglingRefs`; in `scripts/`, the two migration scripts gaining rules 5 and 6; in `cli/src/tests/`, the group `mirror/`, `engine/danglingRefs.test.ts`, `corpus/mirror.test.ts` and the fixture. Nothing in the reference copy is changed and nothing reads or writes the live mirror.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HC6K28001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HC6K2G000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The round trip**",
    "text": "**The round trip**: a load followed by a dump returns the fixture byte for byte, and 20 seeds of random canonical mirrors, and the migrated copy of the real mirror byte for byte for all 8 files (about 11,300 documents loaded in about 360 ms with no error, warning or dangling id), once the `FolderNode` order is the mirror's.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HC6K28001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HC6K2G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The migration**",
    "text": "**The migration**: the scripts hold six rules; on a fresh scratch clone `verify-migration.py` reports 0 unexpected differences and a second run changes nothing. The real mirror is migrated at the cutover only.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HC6K28001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
