    "title": "**Batch 9 filed, Batch 10 surveyed, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**Batch 9 filed, Batch 10 surveyed, 2026-10-19**: the grapher filed Batch 9 (the done record, the resolved issues, the two new defects: a move into its own subtree, in `issues/core.md`, and `< /dev/null` for a move only, in `issues/aperas-skill.md`) and wrote [the Batch 10 brief](#id/BlockNode:00D6HF2D30009). Decided by the orchestrator on its questions: (1) the maps are an object with one function for each write that changes them, which Batch 11's write layer calls after the engine accepted the write, with the model test driving them (the plan's words); (2) a key held by two live nodes: the map answers the first holder in `compareIds` order and lists the keys with more than one holder, for the load to warn about; (4) one path map over the graphs of the mapping, with an optional graph filter on a lookup (the real mirror's 71 artifacts and folders of `tree` and the 3 of `threads.tree` are one namespace; the filter serves `aperas://graph.domain/<deep_path>`). The user's, as design: (3) the gate of step 2, [How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001): whether every lookup by path goes through the one primitive of the live node (the orchestrator recommends yes); the coder builds the primitive either way.",
