    "title": "## v4.8 additions — delta on the v4 snapshot",
    "text": "Records the v4.8 edits to the skills: [the user's decision](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6H8QJXR001) that `< /dev/null` is for a move only, and [the Orchestrator's check of the diff](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HA6M7G001), against [the issue that the skills give `< /dev/null` as the recipe of a move without saying it belongs to a move only](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAJNRR001). A Coder wrote `cat file | aperas insert <id> </dev/null`: the redirect replaced the pipe, the body was empty and the CLI took the insert for a move. The rule now stands next to every move recipe: `< /dev/null` is for a move (an insert with no body) only, never for an insert that has a body or a pipe, because the redirect replaces the pipe and the CLI takes the insert for a move. The base skill carries it in its quick-reference row and in its move line of the command patterns, the Grapher skill in its two move recipes (step 3 of the edit loop and *Move nodes cleanly*), and the Coder skill in a new note under the Work and Report insert of *Every Invocation*, since the Coder writes inserts with a body and has no move recipe. The `Status:` lines of all four skills move to v4.8, with four `Status` entries, one per skill; the Orchestrator skill has no move recipe and no insert recipe of this kind, so only its `Status:` line moved. `skills/aperas/references/mechanics.md` goes from v4.7 to v4.8, the skill release it ships with, and its section *Moving a Node (`insert` with No Body)* gains a second rule. The drift check reads only the `SKILL.md` files, and a recorded block absent from them reads as dropped, so the reference's text is recorded here, in the delta's commentary, as it has been since its extraction in v4.2: the rule **`< /dev/null` is for a move only** says never to put the redirect on an insert that has a body or a pipe, because the redirect replaces the pipe, the body is empty and the CLI takes the insert for a move, so the content is never inserted; and it shows the wrong form, `cat file | aperas insert <id> </dev/null` (the redirect replaces the pipe; this is a move of `<id>` and the file's content is lost), and the right one, `cat file | aperas insert <id> --flush` (an insert with a body takes the pipe and no redirect). The move recipes of v4.7 stay as they were; v4.8 adds the sentence to each. Each entry that rewrites text recorded in an earlier delta or the v4 snapshot carries a `Supersedes:` line naming the blocks it replaces.",
