    "title": "**v4.8 — `< /dev/null` stated as belonging to a move only, after a Coder put it on an `insert` that had a body to pipe**",
    "text": "**v4.8 — `< /dev/null` stated as belonging to a move only, after a Coder put it on an `insert` that had a body to pipe**: recorded as [the v4.8 delta](../discussion/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HJWKQG001). The v4.7 move recipes ended in `< /dev/null` and gave the reason for a move, and none said the other half: on an `insert` that has a body or a pipe the redirect replaces the pipe, the body is empty and the CLI takes the insert for a move. A Coder ran `cat file | aperas insert <id> </dev/null` and moved a heading into its own subtree, as recorded on [the issue that the skills do not say the redirect belongs to a move only](../issues/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAJNRR001). The rule now stands in the base skill's quick-reference row and its move line in the command patterns, in the Grapher skill's two move recipes (step 3 of the edit loop and *Move nodes cleanly*), and in a new note under the Work and Report insert of the Coder skill's *Every Invocation*; `skills/aperas/references/mechanics.md` goes from v4.7 to v4.8 and its section *Moving a Node (`insert` with No Body)* gains the rule with the wrong form and the right one. The `Status:` lines of all four skills move to v4.8; the Orchestrator skill has no recipe of this kind, so only its `Status:` line moved. What stays open: the code fix of the move's signal, an explicit move that never reads standard input, which would remove the need for the redirect and the risk with it, is proposed on [the move that waits on standard input](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001) and not decided; which text the Coder followed when it wrote the command is not proven; and [a move into its own subtree is not refused by the engine](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001).",
