    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-19)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-19)**: [v4.8](../history/aperas-skill.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HK42K0001) puts the rule next to every move recipe: `< /dev/null` is for a move only, never for an `insert` that has a body or a pipe, because the redirect replaces the pipe and the CLI takes the insert for a move. It stands in the base skill's quick-reference row and move line, in the Grapher skill's two move recipes, in a note of the Coder skill's *Every Invocation*, and in `references/mechanics.md` with the wrong form and the right one; the Orchestrator skill has no such recipe. Still open: [the code fix of the move's signal](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2PVVMWG001), which would remove the need for the redirect, is proposed and not decided; which text the Coder followed when it wrote the command is not proven; and [a move into its own subtree is not refused](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001).",
