    "title": "**How a path names one node, settled, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**How a path names one node, settled, 2026-10-19**: after the orchestrator's explanation (a tombstone keeps its stored `path`, so two nodes may hold one path and one is live; the code has two readers that disagree, `findByExactPath` taking the first node and `findLiveByKindAndPath` filtering the tombstoned; and the map is the shell's, from a literal value to an id, the engine offering no match on a literal), the user said to keep only live nodes in that map. The orchestrator's reading, taken as the user's yes: the path map holds only live nodes' ids, a tombstone is never in it, and every lookup by path goes through the one primitive \"the live node at this path\" (an optional kind, an optional graph), so the answer never depends on the order of the store; Batch 11 moves each reader of the old lookups onto it. The open point [How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001) is settled; Batch 10 step 2 is built and not recorded as waiting.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6HRZD8G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Batch 10 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**Batch 10 checked by the orchestrator, 2026-10-19**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built the maps of a literal value in `core/src/shell/` (handle to id, view name to id filtered by kind, path to id, holding only live nodes), the update functions the write layer will call, and the function `liveAtPath` (an optional kind and graph), with the model test and 16 mutations all killed. The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 904 of 904 in 50.0 s (budget 60 s; it has grown 36.8, 41.6, 40.6, 44, 50 s over the batches, partly load), `--group lookups` 42 of 42, `essential` 52 of 52 in 4.6 to 6.1 s under a load average of 5 to 6 (the grapher working at the same time; about 3.5 s on a quiet machine); to be re-timed when the machine is quiet, and `commit` is the suite to split first if it passes 60 s. The engine's files import only files of their own directory. Decided by the orchestrator on the coder's four questions: (1) the gate of step 2 is settled by the user's decision above, step 2 is built and not waiting; (2) the subtree tombstone is found by a scan of the graph's entries (`subtreeTombstoned(graph)`), the safe form, and Batch 11's write layer may replace it; (3) `swept` stays as a defensive no-op, the plan listing it; (4) Batch 11 step 5 replaces the ingest's local maps by path (`folders.ts` 41 to 114 and the ones in `artifacts.ts`) with the one map, the write layer telling the maps right after each accepted write.",
