    "title": "**A key held by two live nodes**",
    "text": "**A key held by two live nodes**: a handle and a view name are unique by design, and a path names one node while live siblings have distinct titles (see [How a path names one node](#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001)), but a mirror edited by hand or a failed ingest can hold a key twice among live nodes; the real mirror has no such repeat today. The map keeps every live holder of a key in `compareIds` order and answers the first, so the answer never depends on the order of the store, and it lists the keys that have more than one holder, for the load to warn about; the load does not refuse the mirror and a later write does not win. A view created with the name of a live view is refused, as the code refuses it today.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHMYQG004",
