    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: the Coder's runs: `tsc --noEmit` of `core` and `cli` clean, `--group lookups` 42 of 42 in 1.4 s, `--suite essential` 52 of 52 in 3.4 to 4.9 s (load average 4), `npm run verify` (`commit`) 904 of 904 in 41.6 s of its 60 s budget, the boundary test passing (the engine's directory imports nothing of the shell); `demand` was not run, the one new corpus file was run alone (3 of 3, about 1 s). The orchestrator's runs: `commit` 904 of 904 in 50.0 s, `--group lookups` 42 of 42, `essential` 52 of 52 in 4.6 to 6.1 s under a load average of 5 to 6 (the grapher working at the same time); re-timed with the load average at 4 to 5 and no agent running, `essential` 3.8 s and 4.6 s of 5 s and `commit` 49.5 s of 60 s. A timing carries its load ([Layer 7](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D457HDWG001)). `commit` has taken 36.8, 41.6, 40.6, 44 and 50 s over the last five batches, partly load.",
