    "title": "**What was built**",
    "text": "**What was built**: `createLookups(engine, graphs)` gives an object with `profileByHandle`, `viewByName`, `liveAtPath(path, { graph?, kind? })`, `duplicates`, `size`, `rebuild` and the update functions `built`, `fieldWritten`, `tombstoned`, `subtreeTombstoned`, `removed`, `swept` and `graphDropped`. One pass of `rebuild` over `idsOfKind` of `Profile`, `TreeView`, `ArtifactNode` and `FolderNode` in the graphs given reads each `record` and leaves out a node with the tombstone marker; the view map is over `TreeView` only, so the view `default` and the profile `default` are told apart; each key holds its live holders sorted with `compareIds` and the answer is the first; the path map is one map over all the graphs of the mapping, the graph and the kind being filters; `pathKeyOf(record)` is the one place that gives the key, so [Batch 16](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4RNDQVG001) changes that place and nothing else.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The reproduction and the model**",
    "text": "**The reproduction and the model**: `maps.test.ts` (22 cases) writes the reproduction first: the reference reader returns the tombstoned node when the live one was stored first (asserted, and marked as going with the reference copy at Batch 12), and `liveAtPath` returns the live one for both orders of building, for both orders then a told tombstone, and for a path reused after a tombstone; then the maps built from a loaded fixture (handles `will` and `default`, views `main`, `bare` and `thread view`, six paths in two graphs, ten absent keys including `constructor` and `__proto__`, the graph and kind filters, a tombstone holding a path), a key held by two live nodes (the first by `compareIds` under three orders of building, listed per map and by key), each update function, the updates for four writes the engine did not take, and `pathKeyOf`. `lookups.model.test.ts`: 20 seeds of 200 operations on the engine and the oracle together over `tree`, `threads.tree` and `treeviews` (build, some tombstoned, bare create then writes, a second value, clear, `removePair`, contain, tombstone, subtree, remove, sweep, `createGraph` and `dropGraph`), the maps told only after a write the engine took; after every operation the three maps, the filtered lookups for 14 keys, `duplicates` and `size` equal a scan of the oracle written apart; every 60 operations a dump, a load and new maps equal the scan, and every 45 four writes are made untold and a `rebuild` equals the scan; about 1.2 s. `corpus/lookups.test.ts` (`demand`, 3 of 3, about 1 s): the migrated copy of the mirror at `REAL_GRAPH`, which from `Aperas.dev` is `Aperas.dev/AperasKG`, loaded and the maps rebuilt in 2 ms: 9 profiles, 19 views, 67 live paths and 1 tombstone holding a path, no duplicate, each map equal to a scan, the tombstone found by no path.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The mutations**",
    "text": "**The mutations**: 16, each under `timeout 100`, all killed by `--group lookups`: insertion order instead of `compareIds` (23 failing cases), the kind filter off the view map (23), a tombstone left in the map (26), removal not dropping (21), sweep not dropping (1), a changed `path` not moving the entry (22), a changed `handle` not moving it (21), a reload not clearing the maps (7), a tombstone not dropping (24), a subtree tombstone not dropping (21), a dropped graph not dropping (17), the graph filter ignored (22), the kind filter of a path ignored (21), `built` not filing (24), an update made before the engine's answer (17), and `removed` trusting the call and not the engine (1). The sweep mutant is killed by one hand case only.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The Coder's choices**",
    "text": "**The Coder's choices**: the names `lookups.ts`, `createLookups`, `Lookups`, `liveAtPath` (the plan's \"the live node at this path\"), `pathKeyOf`, `Duplicate`, `PathFilter` and the group `lookups/`; an update reads the engine for the node it is told of and files what the engine holds, so a call for a write the engine did not take, or one told twice, leaves the maps as the engine is; a key with more than one live holder answers the first by `compareIds`, and `rebuild` and `duplicates` give the list for the load to warn about (no warning text is made here, the load is not changed); `subtreeTombstoned(graph)` finds the subtree by a scan of the nodes the maps hold for that graph (about 100 in the real mirror), since `tombstoneSubtree` takes the nodes out of the containment and the subtree cannot be walked from its root afterwards; `swept` drops the ids it is given and has no effect once every tombstone has been told.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
