    "title": "**Decided at the checks**",
    "text": "**Decided at the checks**: (1) the gate of step 2 is settled by the user's decision ([How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001)), so step 2 is built and not waiting; (2) the subtree tombstone stays a scan, the safe form, and Batch 11's write layer may replace it by the ids it collects before the write; (3) `swept` stays as a defensive no-op, the plan listing the ids a sweep returns among the writes; (4) Batch 11 step 5 replaces the ingest's local maps by path with the one map, the write layer telling the maps right after each accepted write. Settled earlier, as the Coder built them: the maps are an object with one function for each write, which the write layer calls after the engine accepted the write; two live nodes holding one key answer the first holder and list the keys with more than one ([A key held by two live nodes](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6J3N65R001), now in the design); one path map over the graphs, with the graph as an optional filter.",
