    "title": "**What Batch 11 takes from this batch**",
    "text": "**What Batch 11 takes from this batch**: the write layer calls the update functions right after each accepted write (and may replace the scan of `subtreeTombstoned` by the ids it collects); the load calls `rebuild` and warns for each key in `duplicates`; each reader of the old lookups moves onto `liveAtPath`, `profileByHandle` and `viewByName` in the step that moves its file ([the readers of the old lookups](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HTH5ZR001): `findByExactPath` with `resolve.ts:69`, `resolveCreate.ts:98`, `kgProject.ts:46`, `linkIntegrity.ts:323` and `verifyLinkRefusals.ts`; `findLiveByKindAndPath` and `findLiveArtifactByPath`; `findProfileByHandle` and `findTreeViewByName`), and the folder ingest's local maps (`folders.ts` 41 to 114 and the ones in `artifacts.ts`) are replaced by the one map. The old readers stay in the reference copy because the working service runs on them, and Batch 12 deletes what is left.",
