  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6J42610002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Incidents of the batch**",
    "text": "**Incidents of the batch**: the Coder's mutation script restored a file with `git checkout --`, which restores the staged copy, and lost an edit made since the files were staged; it saw the loss by a count of new lines, made the edit again, staged, and ran all 16 mutations again (stage before a mutation run). The first model had most writes refused (113 of 200) and a reload that lost nodes of a kind placed in a graph with no file for it; both were its own generator and were fixed, and the acceptance check in the test (more than half the writes taken, some refused, some duplicates) stays so that a sequence that does nothing fails. The service answered \"No ApeironNgn service running\" once on a read while the node process was alive at high CPU; the Coder waited 10 s at a time and it answered on the third try, with no command run to start or stop it. The Coder's count of the real mirror (67 live paths and 1 tombstone, from `Aperas.dev/AperasKG`) differs from the grapher's census of `Aperas/AperasKG` (71 artifacts and folders in `Apeiron/`, 3 in `.state/`, 1 tombstone): the two mirrors are not the same copy, and the corpus test states no count and compares with a scan.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6J4260R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D6J4S2X0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Paused before the survey of Batch 11, 2026-10-19**",
    "text": "**Paused before the survey of Batch 11, 2026-10-19**: the user paused because the quota was at 100%. Done: Batches 3 to 10 built in `Aperas.dev` and committed by the user; Batches 3 to 9 filed; Batch 10 partly filed (the design item \"A key held by two live nodes\", the plan's done record in the Archive). Not done, to finish in the next turn of the grapher (its Turn 30 Report lists them): the \"Since\" entries on the `findByExactPath` issue, the three-behaviours issue and the full-store-scans issue; the Batch 10 milestone and Current Status in the history; the Dashboard's In flight, the Planning entry, Numbering and the Task Breakdown text; the \"Promoted\" lines under the two Batch 10 Freeflow nodes. Not started: the survey of Batch 11 (12 steps: split into pieces of one coder turn each, with gates and open points for the user) and the split of the `commit` suite (about 41 to 50 s of 60 s; the grapher's timings point at the engine group, the runner's own test and the shell groups as the parts to cut). Waiting for the user, as design: nothing blocks Batch 11's survey; the open points of Batch 11 will come with it. The real mirror is not migrated (the cutover only).",
