    "title": "**Since (2026-10-20), the primitive for the live node at a path built, the readers not moved**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-20), the primitive for the live node at a path built, the readers not moved**: [Batch 10](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W0004) built in `core/src/shell/lookups.ts` the one primitive `liveAtPath(path, { graph?, kind? })`, over a map that holds only live nodes' ids, so a tombstoned and a live node at one path return the live one under both orders of building and of the tombstone ([How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001), [A key held by two live nodes](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6J3N65R001)); `lookups/maps.test.ts` writes the reproduction first, against the reference reader, which returns the tombstoned node when the live one was stored first, and the model test holds the maps equal to a scan of the oracle after every write (20 seeds, 16 of 16 mutations killed). The defect is not resolved: the reference copy under `core/src/shell/` keeps the first-match reader `findByExactPath`, and its callers (`resolve.ts:69`, `resolveCreate.ts:98`, `kgProject.ts:46`, `linkIntegrity.ts:323`, `verifyLinkRefusals.ts`) move onto `liveAtPath` in [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), step 3; the reference copy goes at Batch 12. This entry stays open until then.",
