    "title": "**Piece 1 closed, piece 2 next, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Piece 1 closed, piece 2 next, 2026-10-20**: the coder made case 7 of `corpus/roundtrip.test.ts` exact (the difference is exactly the `predicate` quads of the mirror, counted from it); `--group corpus` 18 of 18, `essential` 52 of 52 in 3.4 s, `commit` 904 of 904 in 39.5 s. Piece 1 is done. Piece 2 (the tests before the reads, three files in a group `commands/`) starts, with the rule of the brief for the assertions: where the order of an unordered read shows (the five listings, the place of a node reached through two links, the links of a block) the test compares sets or the invariant, not today's order, so it passes on both engines; the tombstone and order answers of [the four design answers](#id/BlockNode:00D766N4RR001) change the assertions only at the pieces that apply them (7 and 9).",
