    "title": "**A node exists when a document stands for it**",
    "text": "**A node exists when a document stands for it**: the shell asks the engine whether a node exists with one function, `nodeExists(id)`, which is `graphOf(id) !== undefined` (see [Reads](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T0004)), so a change of the engine's answer changes one line. A node exists when a document stands for it, that is, when a graph holds a record with the id. An id that only a container's `children` names, with no document of its own, is a ghost and does not exist (the load returns such ids in the list of ids referenced and never defined, see [Persistence](#id/BlockNode:00D4MZ7DZG001)). The engine's `exists` and `size` stay undecided for a node that has incoming pairs and no record (see [Existence](#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K)), a case the shell never asks.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3CHMYQG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001",
