    "title": "**How every piece stays green with both engines in the tree**",
    "text": "**How every piece stays green with both engines in the tree**: (1) The working service and the reference copy run from the checkout `Aperas/` at `d794060`, a directory apart from `Aperas.dev/`; no piece edits it, reads or writes the live mirror, or restarts the service, and every run uses a scratch mirror ([Scratch mirrors only](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQM4X8000)). So \"the working service keeps running on the old code until the cutover\" is a fact of the two checkouts, and the pieces only have to keep `Aperas.dev` green. (2) Inside `Aperas.dev`, pieces 1 to 5 change nothing that the shell runs on: piece 1 removes a feature from the old code, pieces 2 to 4 add tests that run on the old code, piece 5 adds files that nothing imports (the pattern of Batches 9 and 10). (3) Piece 6 is the flip: `node.ts` and everything that reaches it runs on the engine. The old Oxigraph files stay in the tree as a **frozen set**, unchanged and compiled, with their own tests, until Batch 12 deletes them: `storeAccess.ts`, `shape.ts`, `store.ts`, `dehydrate.ts`, `threadScope.ts` and the codec half of `vocab.ts`. They import nothing that piece 6 changes (`node.ts` imports `dehydrate.ts`, not the reverse), so they stay green. Piece 6 adds one test, `shell/oldEngine.test.ts`, that lists the frozen set and fails if any other module imports `oxigraph` or a frozen file, so the old engine cannot creep back. (4) The tests of pieces 2 to 4 touch the store only through `fx.store`, `wrap` and the `runX` functions (a grep of the new files for `oxigraph`, `storeAccess`, `vocab` or `.match(` finds nothing), so piece 6 changes the fixture and leaves them as they are; any difference they show after the flip is either a bug of the flip or an entry of the list of deliberate differences ([Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002)), which is the use the plan wants of them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
