    "title": "**Piece 2: tests before the reads**",
    "text": "**Piece 2: tests before the reads**: ([step 10](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Z01YER001) for steps 3 and 11; Layer 1). A new group `commands/` (the coder's name), each file standalone and named in `commit.suite.mjs`; three files, one for each cluster, because a file costs about 0.58 s of start whatever it holds: `render.test.ts` (`runTree`, `runShow`, `runUnfold`: plain, with a view, `--tombstoned`, `maxDepth`, `noHolders`, a node reached through two unfolded links has one canonical place and a pointer elsewhere, the links of a block), `resolve.test.ts` (`runPath`, `runResolve`: the deep-path grammar, `..` at each tier, `aperas://id/`, the root `.`, an ambiguous slug, a path held by a live node and a tombstone, which is the reproduction of [`findByExactPath` takes the first node found](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001), asserted on the reference and turned into the regular test at piece 6, which puts `findByExactPath` onto `liveAtPath`) and `views.test.ts` (`runFold`, `runZoom`, `runUnfold` with a view, `runProfile*`: create, list and remove a profile and a view, the first-use `default` view, the removal cascade, a refused duplicate). Replaces nothing. Rule for the assertions: where the order of an unordered read shows (the five listings of [the order issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800D), the place of a node reached through two links, the links of a block), the test compares sets or the invariant, not the order of today, so it can pass on both engines. Done when: each command has a case that succeeds and a case that is refused; green on the old code; the coder breaks the core line of each command (8 to 10 mutations, each under `timeout 100`, staged first) and each is caught; the added time is measured. Gated by: nothing. Waived here: `runLinkCandidates` only, which goes with its verb in piece 1; every other command is tested.",
