    "title": "**Piece 3: tests before the writes, ingest, track and project**",
    "text": "**Piece 3: tests before the writes, ingest, track and project**: (step 10 for steps 4 and 5). Same group, four files: `remove.test.ts` (`runRemove` of a block, of an artifact and of a folder: the subtree is tombstoned, `tree --tombstoned` shows it, the root is refused, `track --reverse` after it, the path reused by a new artifact), `insert.test.ts` (`runInsert` placement before and after an anchor and as the last child, a move to another parent and within the same parent, `runUpdate` with `textOnly`, `runRetype`; and the reproduction of [a move after an anchor inside the node's own subtree](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) in a child process killed after a few seconds: today it loops, and the test is written to expect a refusal and is named in a suite only in piece 6, so `commit` stays green), `track.test.ts` (`runTrack`, `runReverseTrack` with its three lists `neverProjected`, `changed` and `staleOnDisk`, `kgTrack.ts:82` to `:110`, a rename on disk, held-back removals), `project.test.ts` (`runProject`: a folder's `README.md`, `projectedHash`, the purity gate of `node.ts` after `:880`, a path that does not resolve). `runIngest` is covered by `ingest/chain.test.ts`; add to it the case that a second ingest of unchanged text leaves the `Link`s' `props` ids as they were (the `positionsEqual` behaviour of `artifacts.ts:371`, which step 5 changes). Same rule for orders; the same grep rule for the store. Done when, mutations and Gated by: as piece 2. The reproduction of the move is run once on the old code and its outcome (killed after N s) recorded in the coder's thread, as the proof that it fails first.",
