    "title": "**Piece 4: tests before the service**",
    "text": "**Piece 4: tests before the service**: (step 10 for step 8). A group `service/` (the coder's name), two files: `lifecycle.test.ts` (start; boot with a mirror that has a vacuous container and an unreachable tombstone, so the startup sweep counts show; flush; the divergence guard refusing to overwrite a file changed outside; `flush --clobber`; `reload` and `reload --discard`; the standing `linkWarning` at boot and reload; shutdown flush and sweep; the thread size cap path of `service.ts:312`) and `ops.test.ts` (each of the 29 `case` arms of `handle()` at `service.ts:489` to `:695` reached once through `serviceClient`, or named as waived: the three link arms are gone after piece 1). The service is started from source by the test with a runtime directory, a port and the two roots all in a scratch directory (the isolation settled in [Isolated service trial](../discussion/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y1N5Y0002) and used by the coder's second service in Turn 5); the test asserts those variables before it starts anything, stops its own service in `after` by its own socket and leaves no process, and never touches the runtime directory or the port of the working service. Done when: every arm is reached or waived by name; the sweeps at boot, reload, clobber and shutdown are seen through the counts in the response or the log; no process is left (the test checks); `service/` runs in 8 s or less in all (a file over 4 s in-file goes to the `tools` suite, see the split of `commit`); mutations on the divergence guard and on one sweep are caught. Gated by: nothing. The service tests run on the old boot, so piece 6 changes the fixture of the service (a migrated scratch mirror) and not the tests.",
