    "title": "**Piece 5: the engine-side handle, beside the old code**",
    "text": "**Piece 5: the engine-side handle, beside the old code**: (steps 1 and 2, the additive half; the pattern of Batches 9 and 10). New file(s) in `core/src/shell/` (the coder's names; I use `db.ts`), nothing imports them, and a new group `shell/` of tests. It builds, on `Engine`, `Lookups`, the mapping and the three graphs: the **handle** (`Db`: the engine, the maps, the mapping, the graph list) with `openDb(root)` (settings, mapping, `loadMirror`, `rebuild`, a warning for each key of `duplicates` and each of `warnings`, and `rejected` and `errors` returned to the caller) and `newDb()` for tests (`createMirrorGraphs`); `graphOfId(db, id)`; **`nodeExists(db, id)`** as the one function, `graphOf(id) !== undefined` ([A node exists when a document stands for it](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76AAE8G001)); `allIdsOfKind(db, kind)` over the graphs of the mapping in code-point order and `liveIdsOfKind(db, kind)` (the 16 live callers drop the tombstoned ids afterwards, so one filtering helper and no separate set of live ids); `backlinksOf(db, id, field)` asking each graph and returning the union sorted by id, since `subjectsOf` names a graph; `isThreadScoped(db, id)` as `graphOf(id) === 'threads.tree'` (the rule of [Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2VR01M) gives a thread node its graph at creation, so the walk of `parent` in `threadScope.ts` is not rebuilt); and the **write layer**: one object whose functions are the engine's writes that the shell makes (`createNode` in `graphOfNewNode`'s graph, `addPair`, `clearField`, `removePair`, `insertItem`, `moveItem`, `removeItem`, `tombstone`, `tombstoneSubtree` (it collects the subtree's ids before the write and tells the maps by id, replacing the scan of `subtreeTombstoned`), `removeNode`, `sweep`) and tell the maps right after the engine accepted each, never before. Replaces: nothing in `shell/` (the old files are untouched). Deletes: nothing. Tests: `shell/db.test.ts` (open and new; a ghost id is not an existing node; `liveIdsOfKind` drops a tombstone; `backlinksOf` crosses graphs; a write the engine refuses leaves the maps as they were) and `shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts` (the model of `lookups/lookups.model.test.ts`, 20 seeds, driven through the write layer and compared after every operation with a scan; about 1 s, so it goes in the `models` suite). Done when: those tests pass with 8 or more mutations caught (an update before the engine's answer, a subtree not told, a graph skipped by `allIdsOfKind`, a ghost counted as existing, the union of `backlinksOf` unsorted, and so on); `tsc` clean; the boundary test passes; `commit` within its budget; the old files are untouched (`git diff --stat` names only new files and the suites). Gated by: [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) for `nodeExists`, [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) for the writes (the write layer lets `Undecided('Enforcement')` through: the shell obeys the schema, and a throw is a finding), [No set of live ids](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000X) lightly.",
