    "title": "**Piece 6: the flip**",
    "text": "**Piece 6: the flip**: (steps 1 and 2; the boot, reload and flush of step 8; the wiring of Batch 10's maps; the fixtures). The only piece that moves what the shell runs on, and the largest; it is one change because `wrap(store, …)` is the entry of everything else and `node.ts` makes about 45 calls into `storeAccess`, so no cut inside it leaves `commit` green. Replaces in `core/src/shell/`: in `node.ts` the engine access in place (`childrenOf`, `appendOrderedChild`, `insertOrderedChild`, `decodeObj`, `readField`, `idOf`, `clearField`, `mintEmbedded`, `hardDeleteNode`, `removeDanglingUnfolds`, `writeField`, `ApeironInstance`, `defineAccessors`, `wrap`, `backlinks`), each going through the write layer and the engine's reads of piece 5 (ordered children by `items`, `appendChild` and `insertChild` by `insertItem` and `moveItem`, an embed field by `removePair` for each dropped value and `addPair` for the new ones, `hardDeleteNode` by `removeNode`, which takes the embedded nodes with it and drops the `unfolds` entries by the role `dropWithTarget`), `findProfileByHandle` and `findTreeViewByName` (`node.ts:2012`, `:2021`) onto the maps, `tree.ts:20` `findByExactPath` onto `liveAtPath` (the callers keep the name until their own pieces), the one `subjectsWhere` of `artifacts.ts`, every `Store` in a signature outside the frozen set (the 17 `kg*.ts`, `node.ts`, `artifacts.ts`, `folders.ts`, `linkIntegrity.ts`, `resolve.ts`, `resolveCreate.ts`, `tree.ts`) by `Db`, the 20 `nodeExists` lines and the 16 `allIdsOfKind` lines by the functions of piece 5, `vocab.ts` split (`nodeKindFromId` and `isNodeRef` stay, reading ids by the grammar imported from `apeironNgn/ids`; `nodeExists`, `NODE_BASE` and the codec stay only in the frozen half); in `cli/`: `kgInit.ts:43` to `:47` (it writes the empty files itself: it takes `fileNameOfKind` and `EMPTY_FILE_TEXT`), `service.ts:161` and `:377` (`loadMirror` and `rebuild` for `rehydrateStore`; one flush interval, the table of settings comes in piece 10), `:236`, `:327`, `:420` and `:424` (`dumpMirror` for the two `dehydrate` functions), `:312` (`isThreadScoped`), the `stampAll` file lists from the mapping, the `quadCount` log lines. Tests: `fixture.ts` builds a `Db` with the three graphs and keeps the property name `store`, so the 14 test files that use it keep their text; `makeCorpusCopy` copies the real mirror and runs `scripts/migrate-mirror.py` on the copy (as `corpus/lookups.test.ts` does), because the new load cannot read an unmigrated mirror; the cases that touch raw quads are rewritten (`linking/integrity.test.ts:78` removes a `links` pair with `removePair`) and `store/dangling-unfolds.test.ts` and `corpus/dangling-unfolds.test.ts` are retired, the engine's `dropWithTarget` tests covering them; `shell/oldEngine.test.ts` is added; the reproduction of the move (piece 3) is named in `commit` and passes. Deletes: `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts` (referenced by nothing, [it asks for a dead predicate](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZV0FG001)); `verifyLinkRefusals.ts` and `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts` are ported or retired here (they build a raw `Store` and call `wrap`, so `tsc` of `cli` fails otherwise; this takes forward the second clause of Batch 12 step 2). Batch 12 then deletes the frozen set: `storeAccess.ts`, `shape.ts`, `store.ts`, `dehydrate.ts`, `threadScope.ts`, the codec of `vocab.ts` with `NODE_BASE`, `oxigraph` from the `package.json` files and the `--external` of `build.mjs`, and the tests of the frozen files (`store/storeAccess.test.ts`, `store/roundtrip.test.ts`, `corpus/roundtrip.test.ts`, `support/roundtripChild.ts`, the reproduction blocks of `mirror/load.test.ts` and `mirror/format.test.ts`). Done when: every test of the groups that moved passes on the engine, unchanged except where the list of deliberate differences says; the move reproduction is refused and the service answers; the service tests of piece 4 pass on the new boot (a migrated scratch mirror); `tsc --noEmit` of `core` and `cli` clean; `oldEngine.test.ts` passes; `essential` and `commit` within their budgets; `git diff --stat` shows no edit in a frozen file. Gated by: [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K) (the shim of piece 5), [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) (writes obey the schema; the old tests that write made-up predicates are Batch 12 step 1), and `graphOf`, which the shim uses (built and tested, [confirmed by the user on 2026-10-20](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D5AYTCJR001)); the tombstone open point does not gate it, because `applyTombstone` and `tombstoneLiveSubtree` keep their present effect (the node stays in its parent's list) through the accessors until piece 9, and `addPair` checks only the shape, so a plain write of `tombstonedAt` is accepted. Closes: [a move of a node after an anchor inside its own subtree](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) (the plan names step 4, but the no-cycle refusal comes with `insertItem` and `moveItem`, which `insertOrderedChild` of step 2 now calls); [the store is read outside the helpers](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2536E1R001), first part. If the coder finds it too large for a turn, there is no green cut inside it: the answer is more of piece 5, not a half-flip.",
