    "title": "**Piece 7: reads, link integrity, profiles and views**",
    "text": "**Piece 7: reads, link integrity, profiles and views**: (steps 3, 6 and 11; the readers of the old lookups in `resolve.ts`, `resolveCreate.ts`, `kgProject.ts`, `linkIntegrity.ts`, `kgProfile.ts`). After piece 6 the commands already read through the engine; this piece moves what is still the old behaviour or the old name. Replaces: the callers of `findByExactPath` onto `liveAtPath` by name (`resolve.ts:69`, `resolveCreate.ts:98`, `kgProject.ts:46`, `linkIntegrity.ts:323`) and `tree.ts:20` deleted; the order of `unfolds` at `node.ts:1975` to `:1987` and the first-escaping-link rule at `:1530` to `:1569` by the rule that the canonical place is the first in code-point order of the unfolded ids ([The canonical place in the render](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q)); the links of a block in `tree`, `unfold` and the web by `position`, then id, a link with no position after those with one ([The order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P)) (`node.ts:1745`, `:1807`, `kgUnfold.ts:109` to `:115`), which closes [the newest-first issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001); the other four listings (`checkLinkIntegrity` at `linkIntegrity.ts:112`, `track --reverse`, the profile and view lists, `backlinks`) sorted by id in the shell; `removeTreeViewByName` and `removeProfile` (`node.ts:2049`, `:2238`) through the write layer's `removeNode`; `rejectSlugPathCollisions`' full scan stays a scan over `liveIdsOfKind`. Deletes: `findByExactPath`. Tests: the three files of piece 2 stay green, with their set assertions turned into exact-order assertions where the shell now promises an order, plus `commands/order.test.ts` (the canonical place is the same under every order of `unfolds` and of building; the links of a block in position order; each of the five listings sorted; a link with no position placed after those with one) and a check of `check-links` on a fixture. Done when: those pass; no `findByExactPath` remains; mutations on each sort and on the canonical rule are caught; `tsc`, `essential` and `commit` as before. Gated by: [The canonical place in the render](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q), [The order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P), [No set of live ids](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000X) and the open point [Which order differences are accepted](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0003), all settled. Closes: [the newest-first issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001), and with piece 8 [three behaviours of the caller depend on the order](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800D).",
