    "title": "**Piece 9: writes and tombstones**",
    "text": "**Piece 9: writes and tombstones**: (step 4). The open point [Tombstones leave their container](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0001) is settled: the design wins. Replaces: `applyTombstone` and `tombstoneLiveSubtree` (`node.ts:850` to `:878`; callers `kgRemove.ts:42`, `artifacts.ts:272`, `kgUpdate.ts:332`, `folders.ts:104`, `node.ts:803`) by the engine's `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` through the write layer, the copying of `type`, `title` and `text` from the reconcile record staying the shell's; the tombstone leaves its container, so `tree --tombstoned` loses its source for a removed child, `toPath()` of a tombstone is `null` (13 sites in `core` and 15 in `cli`; the fallbacks at `node.ts:1876`, `:1900` already take `null`), a removal ends by tombstoning a container it empties (a rule at the time of the removal, in the same write), and `tombstoneVacuousContainers` keeps only the boot-time rule over a list or a textless item with no live child; `kgRemove.ts`, `kgInsert.ts`, `kgUpdate.ts`, `kgRetype.ts` onto the write layer's `insertItem`, `moveItem` and `removeItem` directly. Deletes: the clearing of `children`, `links` and `props` by the shell (the engine's tombstone does it). Tests: `commands/remove.test.ts` and `insert.test.ts` of piece 3 with their expectations on `--tombstoned` and on the vacuous container changed by the decision, a model case in `shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts` (a tombstone is in no list; a removal that empties a container tombstones it), and a test that `tree --tombstoned` shows what the decision says. Done when: those pass; the mirror a flush writes holds no tombstone in a `children` list (checked on a fixture); mutations on the cascade and on the list removal are caught; `tsc`, `essential`, `commit`. Gated by: the open point named, settled, which also gated piece 10.",
