    "title": "**Piece 10: the sweeps and the service lifecycle**",
    "text": "**Piece 10: the sweeps and the service lifecycle**: (steps 7 and 8). Replaces: `pruneUnreachableTombstones` (`node.ts:2159` to `:2189`) by the write layer's `sweep` for each graph (the step is one sweep, not three); `pruneStaleUnfolds` (`node.ts:2063` to `:2075`) dropped (the engine drops an `unfolds` entry with its target, and the migration strips the ones that already dangle); `tombstoneVacuousContainers` kept as the boot rule of piece 9; in `service.ts` the three sweep sites at `:201` to `:203`, `:364` to `:372`, `:417` to `:419` and `:473` to `:476`; the two timers (`:96`, `:97`, `:444`, `:447`) by one timer for each graph at the interval of the table of settings (`tree` 10 s, `threads.tree` and `treeviews` 3 s); `stampAll` and `diverged` over the mapping's files; the boot or reload with `rejected` or `errors` in the load's result by the rule of [Packaging — Design](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001) (a load that rejects a document is refused, with a start-anyway option and a side copy of the raw rejected documents); `reloadStore` building a new `Db` and dropping the old one (`dropGraph`, Batch 8) instead of replacing a store without freeing it; `quadCount` (`:163`, `:387`, `corpus.ts`, `copy.test.ts`, the round-trip tests) by the count of records; `danglingRefs` read or left unread (it waits on [The service lifecycle](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000W)). Deletes: `pruneStaleUnfolds`, `pruneUnreachableTombstones`, `removeDanglingUnfolds` and the old `reloadStore` path. Tests: `service/lifecycle.test.ts` of piece 4 with the sweep counts, the intervals (a write in `threads.tree` is flushed at its interval; read through the setting, not by sleeping), the refusal on a mirror that the load cannot read in full, and a reload that frees the old graphs; `tombstone` and `sweep` cases in `shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts`. Done when: those pass; nothing in `service.ts` names `dehydrate`, `rehydrateStore` or a quad; the differential run of [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002) is Batch 13's and is not run here; `tsc`, `essential`, `commit`. Gated by: the open point on tombstones (settled), the rule for a load that rejects a document (settled, in [Packaging — Design](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001); [The service lifecycle](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000W) in the design points to it) and [Enforcement](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000M) (the load's `errors`).",
