    "title": "**The suites**",
    "text": "**The suites**: Batch 11's tests would push `commit` toward its budget (904 of 904 in 34.2 s of 60 s on an idle machine before the cut, 40.9 s under load, and about 10 s more with the roughly 20 files and 8 s in-file that Batch 11 adds; the cost of a file is about 0.58 s of start whatever it holds, and two files run at a time), so the suite is cut in three, as [the tiers](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64000K) list, and the cut is built. (a) `models` (budget 30 s) holds the seven seeded model files, `engine/graphs.model`, `engine/tombstone.model`, `engine/containment.model`, `engine/relations.model`, `engine/literals.model`, `mirror/roundtrip.model` and `lookups/lookups.model`, plus `shell/writeLayer.model` from piece 5: 145 cases in 12.0 s; a model file over about 1 s in-file goes there, a smaller one stays in `commit`. (b) `tools` (budget 30 s) holds `runner/runner.test.ts`, one file of 14 cases that start the runner as a process, 14.0 s; it is run when `run.mjs`, `support/suite.mjs`, `support/reporter.mjs` or a suite file changes. (c) `commit` keeps everything else, including the fast engine files and `engine/boundary`: 53 files, 888 cases, 15.4 s of its 60 s at a load average of 0.9 to 2.5, before the files of pieces 4 to 10, so most of the budget is free for them and for Batches 12 to 14. (d) `demand` lists `commit`, `models`, `tools` and the six corpus files. (e) `essential` takes at most two of the new files, one of `commands/` and one of `shell/`, only if each runs in 300 ms or less; it has 74 cases in 3.6 s of 5. A new test file is named in exactly one of `commit`, `models` and `tools` (or in `corpus/` for `demand` only); `runner/suites.test.ts`, in `commit`, fails if a test file is in none or in two. `models` is run by whoever edits `core/src/apeironNgn/`, `lookups.ts`, `mirror*.ts` or the write layer, and by the orchestrator at Step 7 of such a batch and before Batch 13's baseline; `tools` is run by whoever edits the runner, the suite helper, the reporter or a suite file. The figures for the files of pieces 4 to 10 are estimates until the pieces are built.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQW6AG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
