        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D76D48C0001",
    "text": "**`models`:** the seeded model-based files, with a budget of 30 s: `engine/graphs.model`, `engine/tombstone.model`, `engine/containment.model`, `engine/relations.model`, `engine/literals.model`, `mirror/roundtrip.model` and `lookups/lookups.model`, and the model file of the write layer once it exists: 7 files, 145 cases, 12.0 s wall at a load average of 0.9 to 2.5. A model file over about 1 s in-file goes here and a smaller one stays in `commit`. It is run by whoever edits `core/src/apeironNgn/`, `lookups.ts`, `mirror*.ts` or the write layer, and by the orchestrator at Step 7 of such a batch and before the baseline of the differential run. `commit` does not list these files. *(built, measured; one run, by the orchestrator)*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D5F64000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76D48C8000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**`tools`:** `runner/runner.test.ts` alone, with a budget of 30 s",
    "text": "**`tools`:** `runner/runner.test.ts` alone, with a budget of 30 s: 1 file, 14 cases that start the runner as a process, 14.0 s wall at a load average of 0.9 to 2.5. It is run by whoever edits `run.mjs`, `support/suite.mjs`, `support/reporter.mjs` or a suite file, and by the orchestrator at Step 7 of such a change. `commit` does not list it. *(built, measured; one run, by the orchestrator)*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D5F64000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76D48C8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D76D48C8001",
    "text": "**`commit` and the split:** `commit` keeps every other file, including the fast engine files and `engine/boundary`, so that the tests of the layers above the engine fit in its 60 s with room for the batches still to come; `demand` lists `commit`, `models`, `tools` and the six corpus files. `essential` may take at most two of the new files, one of `commands/` and one of `shell/`, only if each runs in 300 ms or less; it holds `commands/render.test.ts` and no file of `shell/` yet. Every test file outside `corpus/` is in exactly one of `commit`, `models` and `tools`, and `runner/suites.test.ts` fails if one is in none or in two. *(built, measured)*",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D1D5F64000K",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
