    "title": "Promoted (2026-10-20) to the design",
    "text": "Promoted (2026-10-20) to the design: [`graphOf` confirmed](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D5AYTCJR001), [A node exists when a document stands for it](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76AAE8G001), [Existence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000K), [Tombstones](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR01V), [A removed node leaves its container](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000R), [The order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P), [The canonical place in the render](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q), [No set of live ids](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000X), [The service lifecycle](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000W) and, where the service's rules are kept, [the rule for a load that rejects a document](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001); to the plan: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) with its [open points](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YG50B0000) settled, [Batch 12](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000S) reworded, and [the suites](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76D2W00000) of the Verification Plan; to [the tiers](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64000K).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D766N4RR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76GDRD0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 2 checked, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Piece 2 checked, 2026-10-20**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder wrote the group `commands/` on the old code: `render.test.ts` (21 cases), `resolve.test.ts` (19) and `views.test.ts` (19), 59 in all; 17 of 17 mutations caught; `render.test.ts` joined `essential`. The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 963 of 963 in 43 s, `essential` 73 of 73 in 3.1 s, `--group commands` 59 of 59; a grep of the new files for `oxigraph`, `storeAccess`, `vocab` and `.match(` finds nothing. Decided by the orchestrator on the coder's two questions: (1) `runPath` on a `Link` throws \"toPath is not a function\" instead of a message of its own: a defect of the old code, filed as an issue for piece 7 (the reads) to give a proper refusal; the test asserts that the command is refused and does not pin the message; (2) the reproduction of the first-match path lookup is asserted on the reference and is turned into the regular test (the live node is returned) at piece 6, the flip, which puts `findByExactPath` onto `liveAtPath`, not at Batch 12; the grapher notes it in the entries of pieces 6 and 7.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D770QD5G001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76GZQAG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The Batch 11 answers written, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**The Batch 11 answers written, 2026-10-20**: the grapher wrote the four answers into the design, the plan, the Verification Plan, the tiers list and the Dashboard (the load-rejection rule is in `design/packaging.md`'s Workflow, the one design document that states what the service does, and the open point in `design/core.md` points to it). Decided by the orchestrator on its question: Batch 11 keeps its eleven steps below the ten pieces, since done Batches 8 and 9 and other items link to the step ids; the pieces are the order of work and the steps are the record of what each replaces.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
