    "title": "**The corpus case**",
    "text": "**The corpus case**: the Done when asked the Coder to run `--group corpus` once. The old load takes the unmigrated mirror (17 of 18 cases passed, `mirror.test.ts` byte for byte included), and one case failed: `corpus/roundtrip.test.ts` case 7, the whole-mirror round trip, by 5906 quads (103890 against 109796), exactly the `predicate` quads of the mirror's `Link`s (3147 in `BlockNode.jsonld`, 2756 in `.state/BlockNode.jsonld`, 3 in `ArtifactNode.jsonld`, counted by `grep -c '\"predicate\"'` of the real files, read only). A dump of the unmigrated mirror loses the field, which is the intended end state and what [step 6 of Batch 9](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001) does to the mirror. The Coder's two options were to accept the failure until the mirror is migrated or to keep `predicate` in `LINK_SHAPE`; the orchestrator took neither: case 7 was made exact (\"keeps every quad but the predicate of a Link\"), counting the mirror's `predicate` quads and asserting that the difference equals them, nothing else missing and nothing extra, with a comment on the cutover (two files, +39 -9: `corpus/roundtrip.test.ts` and `support/roundtripChild.ts`, whose `read` phase now returns the missing and extra quads as sets).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76JZXJ8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
