    ],
    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: each command has a case that succeeds and a case that is refused. The Coder's runs: `tsc --noEmit -p packages/cli` clean; the group alone 59 of 59 in 1.3 to 1.9 s wall at concurrency 2 (140 to 290 ms in-file for each file at load 3); `essential` 3.1 s before and 3.5 s after (three runs each, the same load); `commit` 963 of 963 in 40.2 s at load 3.2, no warning. The orchestrator ran the suites: `commit` 963 of 963 in 43 s, `essential` 73 of 73 in 3.1 s, `--group commands` 59 of 59. The mutations: 17 of 17 caught (the brief asked for 8 to 10), each under `timeout 100`, staged first, the file restored from a copy after each. Tree: `showTombstoned` ignored (1 case fails); `noHolders` ignored (1); the view ignored (7). Show without its existence check (1). Unfold without its tombstone refusal (1); unfold that does not add to the view (8). Resolve ignoring `base` (1); `..` at the artifact tier going two up (3); `findChild` that never reports an ambiguity (2). Path with a prefix added (2). Fold that folds nothing (3). Zoom that sets no root (2); zoom without its tombstone refusal (1). Profile create without the duplicate check (2); profile removal that keeps the owned views (2). The pointer of the text render without its target (1). View creation without the owner check (2).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Added time**",
    "text": "**Added time**: the three files add about 0.6 s in-file and 1.4 to 1.9 s wall to `commit` (three starts of 0.58 s, two files at a time), under the 4 s that was allowed; `essential` goes from 3.1 to 3.5 s (the one file, 140 to 160 ms in-file alone).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the files cover**",
    "text": "**What the files cover**: `render.test.ts`: `runTree` (the structure under its parents; every form of a reference gives the same subtree and the path as breadcrumb; `maxDepth`; `noHolders`; a view shows the abstract of an unfolded node only; the links of an unfolded block; one canonical place and one pointer for a target reached by two unfolded links; `render-tree` as data; refusals), `runShow` and `runUnfold` (with and without a view, after a `runRemove`: a tombstoned node hidden or tagged, `unfold` refusing it). `resolve.test.ts`: the deep-path grammar (folder, file, heading by prefix and by exact slug, `aperas://id/` and `aperas://tree/`, bare codes, full id, root, several paths in one call, a base), `..` at each tier and refused at the root, the refusals (an ambiguous slug named with its path, a miss at each tier), `--create-holder`, `runPath` (every node of the render has a path that resolves back to it), a path reused after a removal (resolves to the live node, the bare code of the tombstone to nothing), and the reproduction of the first node found at a path. `views.test.ts`: profiles and views (create, list, detail, duplicates and unknown names refused), `runUnfold` with a view, `runFold` (cascades over what is reached from the node and leaves a target reached by another path), `runZoom`, the first use of a view (the default view and the default profile, made once), the removal cascade (a profile takes the views it owns and nobody else's; a freed name can be used again).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
