            "@id": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8007:links:Link:00D76KPHV8000:props:StringProp:00D76KPHV8001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "306"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Decided by the orchestrator on the Coder's two questions**",
    "text": "**Decided by the orchestrator on the Coder's two questions**: (1) `runPath` of a `Link` id does not refuse with the message the code means (`has no walkable parent chain`, `kgPath.ts:17`) and throws `wrap(...).toPath is not a function`, because a `Link` has no `toPath`: a defect of the old code, filed as [`aperas path` on a `Link` throws a TypeError](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76KJ728001) for piece 7 to give a proper refusal; the test asserts that the command is refused (any `Error`) and does not pin the message. (2) The reproduction is asserted on the reference reader and is turned into the regular test (the live node is returned) at piece 6, the flip, which puts `findByExactPath` onto `liveAtPath`, and not at Batch 12; the entries of pieces 6 and 7 say so.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76KP0D8008",
