    "title": "**Set by piece 2, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Set by piece 2, 2026-10-20**: `commands/resolve.test.ts` holds the reproduction of [the first node found at a path](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001), asserted on the reference reader: two holders of one path built with `wrap` in both orders, and `findByExactPath(fx.store, path)` returns the tombstone when the live node was stored first. This piece puts `findByExactPath` (`tree.ts:20`) onto `liveAtPath`, so that case then fails by design. It is turned into the regular test at this piece, not at Batch 12: the same two holders in both orders, asserting that the live node is returned, through `liveAtPath` (the callers still call `findByExactPath` by name until piece 7), and its title no longer says that it goes with the reference reader.",
