    "title": "**Set by piece 2, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Set by piece 2, 2026-10-20**: (1) the regular test that piece 6 made of the reproduction of [the first node found at a path](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001) calls `findByExactPath`; when this piece deletes the function, the test calls `liveAtPath` and asserts the same (the live node, whatever the order of the holders). (2) `runPath` of a `Link` id gets a refusal of its own, the message the code means (`has no walkable parent chain`) or one the piece settles, in place of the `TypeError` \"toPath is not a function\" ([`runPath` of a `Link` id throws](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76KJ728001)); `commands/resolve.test.ts` asserts only that the command is refused, so the piece may tighten that case to the message it settles on. Closes that issue.",
