    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-20)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-20)**: [Batch 11, piece 1](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2MR003) removed the `predicate` of a `Link` from the code of the shell in `Aperas.dev` (branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed): `LINK_SHAPE` and `Link` have no such field, `mintWikilink` sets none, `resolveBlockLinks` writes the links from the wikilink ids alone, `WIKILINK_PREDICATE` is gone from `astParser.ts`, the render item and the JSON of a link carry none, and `tree` and `unfold` print `[Link]  → <target>`; `aperas link` and `aperas unlink` are deleted with `kgLink.ts` and `kgUnlink.ts`, their entries in `aperas.ts`, the three `case` arms of `service.ts` and the three request types. A grep of `core/src`, `cli/src` and `web/src` for `predicate` finds no use of the field of a `Link` (only RDF predicate terms); `tsc --noEmit` is clean for `core`, `cli` and `web`; `essential` 52 of 52 and `commit` 904 of 904 in 39.5 s. The reproduction of the cost is `corpus/roundtrip.test.ts` case 7, \"keeps every quad but the predicate of a Link\": the round trip of the unmigrated real mirror differs by exactly its 5906 `predicate` quads, counted from the mirror. The data part is not touched by the code: the real mirror keeps its `predicate` until the cutover, where the one-time migration ([Batch 9, step 6](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3Y3DMTR001), dry run passed) removes it. The checkout `Aperas/` at `d794060`, which the working service runs, keeps writing the field and the two verbs until the cutover.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D76YFZ0G001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The second loop of the service, piece 3 checked, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**The second loop of the service, piece 3 checked, 2026-10-20**: the grapher, filing pieces 1 and 2, gave the move command the id of the parent instead of the node to move; that moved the `## Resolved` heading after one of its own children, and the old engine's service (pid 11794) looped on the next walk of the parent chain (the coder's reproduction showed the move itself returns at once and the loop is in `runPath`, `runShow` and `runTree` returning but the next walk of the chain never returning). The user approved the stop at once; `aperas service stop` timed out after 10 s of SIGTERM, the orchestrator sent SIGKILL to that pid, checked that the mirror files on disk had no parent cycle, started the service again (about a minute to load) and inserted the coder's prepared Turn 18 Work and Report by pipe. Piece 3 checked by the orchestrator (in-process, no service): `commit` 1043 of 1043 in 49.5 s (the four files add 2 to 3 s; `commit` is near its 60 s budget, so the split into `commit`, `models` and `tools` is the next work), `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.6 s, `--group commands` 138 of 138; the coder's 22 of 23 mutations caught; no process left by the move reproduction (`commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts`, named in a suite at piece 6). Decided by the orchestrator, as not about the design: the reproduction file name `.repro.ts` is fine; the issue on the move into its own subtree is reworded: the loop is in the walk of the parent chain, not in the move; the quirks of the old code the coder listed (a `runUpdate` of a heading with two or more top-level blocks clearing its own text; `runUpdate` not refusing a tombstoned node while `runRetype` does; the deep-path wikilink that makes no `Link`; eight behaviours left unpinned) are filed as one issue for the pieces that move those commands (7 to 9) to decide which the new engine pins; the grapher reads each id twice and checks that the anchor is not inside the node it moves before any move.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
