        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D7710E58003",
    "text": "A `runUpdate` onto a heading with a document of two or more top-level blocks (so `--text-only`, or a leading paragraph before a subheading) clears the heading's own text (`text` becomes absent) and makes the leading paragraph a child of its own. The header of `kgUpdate.ts` (lines 6 to 13) says the first paragraph becomes the target's `text`. Seen in text-only mode on a heading that had text; the default mode with several blocks was not read for the text. The tests do not pin the text in that case.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7710E58002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "`runUpdate` of a tombstoned node is not refused",
    "text": "`runUpdate` of a tombstoned node is not refused: a block removed by `runRemove` and then updated takes the new title and text, read through `show` with `tombstonedAt` still set. `runRetype` refuses a tombstoned node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7710E58002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7710E58005",
    "text": "A wikilink written as a deep path (`[c]([[cmd_demo/beta.md/Beta/Beta Section]])`) in an ingested paragraph produces no `Link`, while the same target written as a bare code does; the corpus uses bare codes. Seen in the Coder's exploration of piece 2, not traced to a line.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7710E58002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58006:links:Link:00D7711158002",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58006:links:Link:00D7711158002:props:StringProp:00D7711158003",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "355"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58006:links:Link:00D7711158004",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D24N87T000R",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58006:links:Link:00D7711158004:props:StringProp:00D7711158005",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "525"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D7710E58006",
    "text": "Eight behaviours of the old code that the tests do not pin, listed by the Coder: (1) `runRemove` of a full id that names no node answers `{ id }` and does not refuse; (2) a second removal of a removed node stamps a later `tombstonedAt`; (3) after a removal the path of the artifact still resolves to the dead node until a new file takes it, the family of [`findByExactPath` takes the first node found](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001); (4) the removed node stays in the `children` of its parent in `show`, which [the design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000R) changes and piece 9 applies; (5) a create-mode `runInsert` whose anchor is not a child of the parent is refused (`is not a child of`) only after the new blocks were hydrated, read in `kgInsert.ts` and not seen in a command; (6) `--after` an `ArtifactNode` moved a block out of the artifact, and where it landed was not read; (7) the counts of `runUpdate`'s reconcile (`matched`, `moved`, `changed`, `added`, `removed`) say `added 0, removed 0` for a piped block that took the id of a removed one, so the tests pin ids and trees and not counts; (8) the `staleOnDisk` of `track --reverse` names a path once for each tombstoned artifact that had it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7710E58002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7710E58007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7710E58007",
    "text": "**Not proven**",
