    "title": "**The diff**",
    "text": "**The diff**: `commands/remove.test.ts`, `insert.test.ts`, `track.test.ts`, `project.test.ts` and `moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts` (new); `support/moveIntoOwnSubtreeChild.ts` (new); `support/commandsCorpus.ts` (adds `projectToDisk`); `ingest/chain.test.ts` (adds `5g` and a helper, `positionPropIds`); `suites/commit.suite.mjs` (+4 lines: remove, insert, track, project). None is added to `essential`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: each command has a case that succeeds and a case that is refused or held back (`runRemove`, `runInsert` create and move, `runUpdate`, `runRetype`, `runProject`; `runTrack` has the held-back removal and the README it will not track; `runReverseTrack` only reads). Green on the old code. The Coder's runs: `tsc --noEmit -p packages/cli` clean; `commit` 1043 of 1043 in 49.2 s at load 2.4, and 53.0 s at load 4.3 (49.8 s without the four files at load 3.1); `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.5 s; `--group commands` 138 of 138 in 3.9 s. The orchestrator ran the suites in-process: `commit` 1043 of 1043 in 49.5 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.6 s, `--group commands` 138 of 138. The mutations: 23, each file under `timeout 100`, staged first, the source restored by writing the original back; 22 caught. They are: root refusal, removable kinds, the tombstoning, move side, bare promote, create-mode collision check, list-run stripping, anchor placement, text-only mode, depth check, update promotion, retype's dropped props, retype's tombstone check, stale-on-disk list, `changed` comparison, the sweep's `force`, project's conflict hold-back, purity gate, `projectedHash` of an artifact and of a folder, the dry run, `positionsEqual`. The first run left a survivor in the text-only promotion of `kgUpdate.ts`; the case \"with --text-only makes it real as well\" was added and the mutation is caught.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The mutation that survives**",
    "text": "**The mutation that survives**: create mode without the `assertLinksAcceptable` pre-check in `kgInsert.ts` still refuses, because `resolveBlockLinks` keeps the same check as its backstop and gives the same message. What differs is that the new blocks were already hydrated when it throws, which shows only in the store and not in a command, so the rule for the tests forbids a case for it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Added time**",
    "text": "**Added time**: the four files add 2 to 3 s to `commit`, which is now about 50 of 60 s at this load (piece 2 left it at 40 s to 43 s). In-file the files take 0.13 s (project), 0.16 s (track), 0.20 s (remove) and 0.64 s (insert), 0.8 to 1.4 s wall each alone with the 0.58 s start. The split of `commit` into `commit`, `models` and `tools` is the work that comes before piece 4.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the files cover**",
    "text": "**What the files cover**: `remove.test.ts`: refusals (the root, a path that resolves to nothing, a link); a block with a subtree (every descendant dead, siblings, parent and other artifacts live, `tree` hides it and `showTombstoned` tags it, a deep path, a bare code, a full id and `base` all name the node, a second removal is not refused); an artifact (dead with its blocks, the folder live, `staleOnDisk`, a new ingest of the path makes a new artifact and new blocks); `track --reverse` after a removal; a folder (dead with its artifacts and blocks, the root live, a new file at the path makes a new folder). `insert.test.ts`: `runInsert` create (last child, before, after, by path, bare code and full id for parent and anchor, several blocks, under an artifact, a nested document, links resolved with their counts, a lone list item continuing a bullet run, a wrong number in an ordered run refused, refusals that leave the rendered tree as it was), move (before and after in the same parent, to another parent with its subtree, onto a top-level heading, a placeholder promoted in place, a placeholder folder promoted and refused with an anchor, six refusals), `runUpdate` (text-only prepends and keeps ids, the default reconciles, one paragraph becomes the text, a retitle of the same depth with the path following, a checkbox set, kept and cleared, a placeholder made real in both modes, frontmatter of an artifact and of a folder, links kept across the same text, four refusals) and `runRetype` (depth, heading to paragraph and back, list item props dropped, no lead-in, seven refusals). `track.test.ts`: a sweep of unchanged files, a path, a new file by path and by sweep, a directory, an edited file (`fileHash` moves, `ingestedHash` stays until ingest), a README given as a path, a rename found by a sweep and by a track of the new path (same node id), a file gone (other paths remove nothing, the sweep lists it and holds it back, `force` applies it), and `track --reverse` (never projected, projected, changed by an edit, a folder with frontmatter, stale on disk, writes nothing); lists are compared as sets. `project.test.ts`: the dry run records nothing, a real projection (the same markdown, `projectedHash` = `fileHash` = `ingestedHash`), a track after the write finds nothing, a hand-edited file held back (`conflict: true`, nothing recorded), `force`, a folder README (frontmatter and body, a hand edit held back), the root, the purity gate (artifact, folder and root held back, then promoted), a placeholder artifact made real by its first projection, with a file already at its path a conflict until forced, three refusals of a path. The caller's file write is `projectToDisk` in `support/commandsCorpus.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Case 5g**",
    "text": "**Case 5g**: the paragraph with the self-link keeps its text, a heading is added elsewhere, the file is ingested again, and the `Link` has the same id and the same `position` prop ids as captured in `5c` (the `positionsEqual` behaviour of `artifacts.ts:371`, which step 5 changes). `ingest/chain.test.ts` is 9 of 9 on the old code; the mutation `positionsEqual` forced false fails exactly `5g`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0005:links:Link:00D7717M48000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
