            "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0005:links:Link:00D7717M48000:props:StringProp:00D7717M48001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "1371"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The reproduction of the move**",
    "text": "**The reproduction of the move**: the move into its own subtree does not loop in the reposition. `runInsert` of a heading after its own child returns in under 1 s (`moved after`), and `runShow` and `runTree` of the artifact return; the loop is the first walk of the parent chain over the cycle the move makes: `runPath` of the moved heading never returns (probed per step under `timeout 8`: `show` and `tree` rc 0, `path` rc 124). The test `commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts` with `support/moveIntoOwnSubtreeChild.ts` (the child makes its scratch roots under the test's own scratch directory through `TMPDIR`; `spawnSync` with `timeout: 6000` and `SIGKILL`) expects the child to end by itself with a refusal that names the cause, and no step after it. Outcome on the old code, run twice: the child was killed after 6.0 s (SIGKILL) instead of ending, with `outcome: moved`, and the steps that returned were `show` and `tree`. With a one-line guard in `kgInsert.ts` (walk the anchor's parents up to the target, throw) for one run it passes in 1.8 s; the file was restored with `git checkout` and has no diff. After each run no process of the child was left and `/tmp` held no `aperas-test-*`. It is a `.repro.ts` file, not `.test.ts`, because a group run finds every `.test.ts` in the directory and would turn red; piece 6 renames it and names it in `commit.suite.mjs`. [The issue on the move](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) is reworded accordingly.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D77170G0006:links:Link:00D7717M48002",
