    ],
    "title": "**Decided by the orchestrator on the Coder's questions**",
    "text": "**Decided by the orchestrator on the Coder's questions**: the name `.repro.ts` is kept and piece 6 renames it; the issue on the move says the loop is in the walk of the parent chain and not in the move; the quirks of the old code and the eight behaviours left unpinned are filed as [one issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7710E58001) for pieces 7 to 9 to decide which the new engine pins.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D77170FR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D771BZ38001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D771BZ38001",
    "text": "The second time, on 2026-10-20, was a move by the Grapher that was given the id of the heading `## Resolved` of `issues/core.md` instead of the node to move, with an anchor that was one of that heading's own children: it moved the heading after its own child. The move itself answered, and the service (pid 11794) looped at 100 percent of a CPU on the next walk of the parent chain, answering \"No ApeironNgn service running\" to every command. `aperas service stop` timed out after 10 s of SIGTERM, the orchestrator sent SIGKILL to that pid with the user's approval, checked that the mirror files on disk had no cycle of `parent`, and started the service again; it took about a minute to load.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR002",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
