    "title": "**Set by piece 3, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Set by piece 3, 2026-10-20**: `commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts` (with `support/moveIntoOwnSubtreeChild.ts`) is the reproduction of [a move after an anchor inside the node's own subtree](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001), run on the old code in a child process killed after 6 s (`outcome: moved`). It is a `.repro.ts` file so that no group run finds it; this piece renames it `.test.ts` and names it in `commit.suite.mjs`, where it has to end by itself with a refusal that names the cause, the engine's no-cycle rule, and the service answering.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0004",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D772VH78001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Paused after piece 3 of Batch 11, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Paused after piece 3 of Batch 11, 2026-10-20**: the user paused (a move to a new office) and asked for no commit messages; the work resumes as normal. State: Batches 3 to 10 built and committed; Batch 11 pieces 1 to 3 built, verified and filed, staged and not committed in `Aperas.dev` (`commit` 1043 of 1043 in 49.5 s of 60 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.6 s of 5 s, `--group commands` 138 of 138), the graph staged in `AperasKG` with the documents projected. Next: the split of `commit` into `commit`, `models` and `tools` (the budget is near), then piece 4 (the tests before the service), piece 5 (the additive engine-side handle), piece 6 (the flip), then pieces 7 to 10. No design question is open: the four answers of Batch 11 are written. The grapher moves a node only after reading its id twice and checking the anchor (the old engine's service froze twice, on 2026-10-17 and 2026-10-20, by a move into its own subtree, which Batch 11 closes). If the service has stopped on its idle timer, start it by the standing arrangement; it takes about a minute to load. The real mirror is not migrated: that is the cutover.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D78XYFTR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Resumed after the pause, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Resumed after the pause, 2026-10-20**: the user, stable after the move, said to resume as normal. The service had stopped on its idle timer and was started again by the standing arrangement (about a minute to load). The work continues in the order of the pause note: the split of the `commit` suite into `commit`, `models` and `tools` first (the grapher's brief for it is the entry \"Brief — the split of `commit`\" of its Batch 11 Report, written into the Verification Plan and the tiers list of `design/testing.md`), then piece 4. The coder does the split in `Aperas.dev`; it is a change of the suite files and the runner's lists, no engine or shell behaviour changes.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D790YQZ8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The `commit` suite split, checked, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**The `commit` suite split, checked, 2026-10-20**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder split the suites: `models` (7 model files) and `tools` (the runner's own test) are built, `commit` keeps 53 files, and a new test `runner/suites.test.ts` fails if a test file is in none or in two of `commit`, `models` and `tools` (the coder broke a suite on purpose and the test failed). The orchestrator ran them with the load average beside: `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.6 s (load 0.6), `commit` 888 of 888 in 15.4 s, `models` 145 of 145 in 12.0 s, `tools` 14 of 14 in 14.0 s (load 0.9 to 2.5). The coder's Report says `design/testing.md` disagrees with the code in one place, for the grapher to put right; a tombstoned ghost line under the coder's Turn 19 (a mistyped turn id) is left, hidden by default, for a later cleanup when the coder is not writing to its thread. Next: piece 4, the tests before the service, by the coder; the grapher files the split and puts `design/testing.md` right.",
