    "title": "**The `commit` suite split: done, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**The `commit` suite split: done, 2026-10-20**: not one of the ten pieces, it is the preparation the survey asked for before piece 4 ([the cut in the Verification Plan](#id/BlockNode:00D76D2W00000), [the tiers](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64000K)). In `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed, the suites `models` (the seven model files, budget 30 s) and `tools` (`runner/runner.test.ts`, budget 30 s) are built, `commit` keeps 53 files, and `demand` lists `commit`, `models`, `tools` and six corpus files (67 files). A new test, `runner/suites.test.ts`, in `commit`, holds each test file outside `corpus/` in exactly one of `commit`, `models` and `tools` and fails when one is in none or in two. No script was added: `npm run verify -- --suite models` and `-- --suite tools` run them. Run by the orchestrator, one run each, with the load average beside: `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.6 s of 5 s (load 0.6), `commit` 888 of 888 in 15.4 s of 60 s, `models` 145 of 145 in 12.0 s of 30 s, `tools` 14 of 14 in 14.0 s of 30 s (load 0.9 to 2.5 over the three). Piece 4 adds its files to `commit`, or to `tools` when one runs over 4 s in-file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D799Z790001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 4 checked, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Piece 4 checked, 2026-10-20**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder wrote the group `service/` on the old boot: `lifecycle.test.ts` and `ops.test.ts`, 50 cases in about 3 s; all 26 arms of `handle()` reached, none waived (the three link arms went with piece 1); 9 of 9 mutations caught; the service the tests start is the coder's own in a scratch runtime directory and port, stopped by its own socket. The orchestrator ran: `commit` 938 of 938 in 18.2 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.5 s, `--group service` 50 of 50, `--group runner` 18 of 18 (the suite-membership test holds); only the working service is running (pid 34166), so no process is left. Next: piece 5 (the additive engine-side handle, nothing imports it yet) by the coder, and the grapher files piece 4 and puts the stale counts of `design/testing.md` right (the \"19 files\" and \"15 files\" examples, \"8 to 20 s\" for `commit`, \"56 cases in 19 files\" for `demand`, using the runner's `--help` and `--list` read-only); the ghost line under the coder's Turn 19 stays (hidden by default).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
