    "title": "**The diff**",
    "text": "**The diff**: `service/lifecycle.test.ts`, `service/ops.test.ts` and `support/serviceHarness.ts` (new); `suites/commit.suite.mjs` (+2 lines, after `commands/project.test.ts`). None is added to `essential`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The Done when, checked**",
    "text": "**The Done when, checked**: every arm reached or waived by name: 26 of 26 arms of `handle()` are reached (the brief's 29 less the three link arms that piece 1 removed; the line numbers moved from `:489`-`:695` to `:486`-`:672`), the `WAIVED` list is empty, and the last case of `ops.test.ts` reads the `case` labels out of `service.ts` and fails if one is neither reached nor waived or if a waived arm is reached. The sweeps at boot, reload, clobber and shutdown are seen through the counts and the log. No process is left: both files assert it in `after`, and a `pgrep` afterwards finds none of `Aperas.dev`. `service/` runs in 3.0 s of the 8 s. Mutations on the divergence guard and on a sweep are caught. The checks: `tsc --noEmit -p packages/cli` clean; `--group service` 50 of 50 in about 3.0 s, run 22 times and green after the one fix below; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.5 s; `commit` 938 of 938 in 18.1 s (the orchestrator's run: 18.2 s; it was 888 of 888 in 15.4 s), no warning; `--group runner` 18 of 18, so the suite-membership test holds. Afterwards only the working service is running (pid 34166, from `Aperas/`, never signalled), and `/tmp` holds no `aperas-test-*` directory.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The isolation**",
    "text": "**The isolation**: the harness follows the isolation settled in the brief of this piece (the isolated service trial). `isolateService` sets a scratch run directory (`XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`), a free port (`APERAS_HTTP_PORT`), both roots (`APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT`, `APERAS_ARTIFACTS_ROOT`) and the thread cap (`APERAS_THREAD_SIZE_CAP`), and records what the working service would use. `assertIsolated` throws unless the run directory, socket, lock, token, port and both roots are scratch ones and none is the working run directory, the default port 2736, the ambient port or the real mirror. `startService` asserts first, refuses if a lock or an answer already exists in the scratch directory, calls `runStart`, then checks the lock names the scratch socket, roots and port. `stopService` asserts, checks the lock's socket is the scratch socket and inside the scratch directory, sends SIGTERM to the pid of the scratch lock (it never reads the working service's lock) and waits for the process and its `tsx` wrapper to be gone. `leftoverProcesses` scans `/proc` for a command line with `service.ts` and an environment with `APERAS_APEIRON_ROOT=<scratch>`. A `process.once('exit')` kills any scratch service still running. The mirror the service boots on is built by `dumpMirror` and `buildSeed` through the old `rehydrate` and `dehydrate`, so piece 6 changes that builder (a migrated scratch mirror) and not the cases.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What the 50 cases cover**",
    "text": "**What the 50 cases cover**: `ops.test.ts` (29 cases, one real service on the corpus of the command tests): each of the 26 arms (`ping`, `reload`, `flush`, `track`, `trackReverse`, `ingest`, `unfold`, `fold`, `zoom`, `resolve`, `insert`, `update`, `remove`, `retype`, `project`, `tree`, `path`, `backlinks`, `show`, `profileCreate`, `profileList`, `profileRemove`, `profileCreateView`, `profileListView`, `profileRemoveView`, `checkLinks`) reached through `request` of `serviceClient` with its result checked; the `reload: true` and `flush: true` flags on `tree`, `update`, `insert`, `resolve`, `ingest`, `unfold` and `checkLinks`; refusals (`profileCreate` twice, `resolve` of a bad path, `remove .`, `update` of a bad path); the `default` arm (`unknown op 'bogus'`); and the coverage case. `lifecycle.test.ts` (21 cases): the seed is the corpus plus a vacuous `list` (its only item tombstoned), an unreachable tombstoned block, a view that unfolds an id with no node, four fodder pairs, a thread artifact `.threads/t.md` over a cap of 3 and one dropped `links` pointer. The cases: the isolation checks refuse a wrong port, run directory or root; nothing runs before the start; start gives a ready lock bound to the scratch roots; the log carries `Startup GC: cleaned 1 unreachable tombstone(s), 1 vacuous container(s), 1 stale unfold(s).` and the files are already swept; a flush after the boot writes nothing; a second start prints `Already running` and starts nothing; the standing `linkWarning` rides on a response of any op and is printed by the client; reload clears it when the file has the link and sets it when the file loses it; the thread insert carries `threadSize {count, cap 3, artifactPath .threads/t.md}` and the same size on a non-thread artifact carries none; the divergence guard (a file changed outside refuses `flush`, `insert --flush` and a plain `reload`, the file stays as the outside wrote it, the local change stays in memory, `conflict.content` rides on the next `ping` and the client prints `UNRESOLVED CONFLICT`); `flush --clobber` writes both local changes and clears it; `reload --discard` takes the file, drops the pending change, sweeps nothing and clears it; sweep counts `[1, 1, 0]` (pruned, vacuous, stale unfolds) at clobber and at reload, with the reload log line `Reloaded ... GC: 1 unreachable tombstone(s) pruned, 1 vacuous container(s) tombstoned.`; at stop the pending sweep is done and flushed and the lock is gone; the second boot has no new `Startup GC` line; a stop with a pending change and a changed file logs `Shutdown WARNING: content mirror flush refused`, keeps the file and ends the process; no process is left.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The mutations**",
    "text": "**The mutations**: 9, each file under `timeout 100`, a script restoring `service.ts` from a copy (`cmp` confirms it identical, and `git status` shows no working-tree change to it); 9 caught. M1 `diverged()` returns `[]`: 6 cases fail (the whole guard). M2 `clobberFlush` skips the tombstone prune: 2 fail. M3 `shutdown` skips the prune: 2 fail. M4 the boot skips `pruneStaleUnfolds`: 3 fail. M5 reload never clears `linkWarning`: 1 fails. M6 the `flush` arm ignores `clobber`: 6 fail. M7 reload skips the vacuous sweep: 1 fails. M8 a new `case 'zzz'` no test reaches: the coverage case fails. M9 the `path` arm returns a wrong value: its case fails.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Added time**",
    "text": "**Added time**: `commit` goes from 888 cases in 15.4 s to 938 in 18.1 to 18.2 s, 55 files; the budget is 60 s.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Left open, the Coder's questions**",
    "text": "**Left open, the Coder's questions**: branches of `service.ts` that every arm reaches but the cases leave unreached: the 10 s and 3 s flush timers and the 30 minute idle exit (the file runs in seconds); `linkBreakage` of `withLinkCheck` (no way found to make a write break a link on demand); a non-zero `prunedUnfolds` at clobber, reload and shutdown (a hard delete clears the dangling unfolds of the id at once, so only the boot, which reads a mirror written with a stale one, shows the count); `reload: true` on most of the 26 arms (the same line `if (req.reload) reloadStore()` in each, reached on `tree`, `update`, `insert` and `resolve`); the `force` flags of `track` and `ingest` and the `--force` retry of the clients; decided by the piece 4 filing: each unreached branch of an arm that reads or writes the store gets a case, the others are waived by name, as done in the follow-up below. A thread in a scratch graph: `runIngest(['.threads/t.md'])` ingests the artifact but the folder scan skips every name starting with `.` (`core/src/folders.ts:67`), so no `FolderNode` `.threads` exists and the artifact cannot be reached by the path `.threads/t.md`; the test reaches it by its id (`threadSize` and `isThreadScopedId` work), while the real mirror has threads reachable by path; piece 6 or 10 should look at this case if it changes how a thread is placed. The stop by its own socket: there is no shutdown op, so `stopService` sends SIGTERM to the scratch lock's pid; a stop through a request on the socket needs a new op in `service.ts`, which is not in this piece.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Findings of the Coder along the way**",
    "text": "**Findings of the Coder along the way**: the first `stopService` returned when the lock's pid was gone, but the `tsx` process that started the service ends a few ms later, so `no process of the test is left` failed once in 8 runs; it now waits for `leftoverProcesses` to be empty too. A `remove` of an artifact tombstones the artifact and its blocks but leaves it reachable from its folder, so a sweep prunes only its blocks (the count is 1 for a one-heading artifact, not 2); the cases assert the heading gone and the artifact tombstoned in the file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D79C5M38001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
