    "title": "Promoted (2026-10-20) to the plan and the design",
    "text": "Promoted (2026-10-20) to the plan and the design: the done record in [Piece 4: tests before the service](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0002) with the Coder's open questions (the unreached branches of the arms, a thread in a scratch graph, the stop by its own socket) left for the orchestrator to decide before piece 6; the counts of [the groups](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64000F), [the per-commit tier](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F648000), [the on-demand tier](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F648001), [the options and `--list`](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F648009), [`--help`](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1EXMKPG001), [the header line](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1EXNME8001) and the [workflows before a commit](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64800H), [on demand](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64800J) and [the migration](../design/testing.md#id/BlockNode:00D1D5F64800M), put right against `npm run verify -- --help` and `--list`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D799Z790001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79DCNPR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 4 filed, the grapher's three questions, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Piece 4 filed, the grapher's three questions, 2026-10-20**: the grapher filed piece 4 and put nine items of `design/testing.md` right against the runner (`commit` 55 files, 938 cases, 18.2 s; `demand` 69 files; 15 groups). Decided by the orchestrator, as not about the design: (1) before piece 6 the coder closes piece 4's gaps in a small follow-up: every unreached branch of an arm that reads or writes the store gets a case, the others (argument errors and the like) are waived by name in the test file; (2) the folder scan skipping dot-names (`folders.ts:67`), which makes a thread reachable only by id in the service tests, is filed as an issue for piece 8 (ingest) to decide whether the scan sees `.threads`; (3) no shutdown op is added: the service already flushes and exits on SIGTERM, the lifecycle is outside the design, and the tests keep stopping their scratch service by that signal.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D79G81AR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 5 checked, 2026-10-20**",
    "text": "**Piece 5 checked, 2026-10-20**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built the handle and the write layer beside the old code: `core/src/shell/db.ts` and `writeLayer.ts` (nothing else imports them), `tests/shell/db.test.ts` (37 cases, `commit`) and `tests/shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts` (20 seeds, `models`); no old file changed; 23 of 24 mutations caught, the survivor (`sweep` not telling the maps) an equivalent mutant since a tombstone is already unfiled before the sweep. The orchestrator ran: `commit` 975 of 975 in 18.1 s, `models` 165 of 165 in 13.7 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.5 s, `--group shell` 57 of 57. Decided on the coder's two questions: `Lookups.subtreeTombstoned` stays until the flip and piece 6 removes it with its two test uses (`lookups/maps.test.ts`, `lookups/lookups.model.test.ts`); the equivalent mutant is left as it is and noted in the record of the mutations. Before piece 6: the coder closes piece 4's gaps (the follow-up decided at the piece 4 filing) and the grapher files piece 5 and the dot-name issue. Then the flip, the riskiest change of the plan; the orchestrator recommends the user commits the staged work as a checkpoint before it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D79K9158001"
    ]
  },
