    "title": "**The folder scan skips every name that starts with a dot (`core/src/folders.ts:67`), so no `FolderNode` `.threads` is ever built by `ingest`, and a thread artifact ingested in a scratch graph can be reached only by its id, not by the path `.threads/t.md`**",
    "text": "**The folder scan skips every name that starts with a dot (`core/src/folders.ts:67`), so no `FolderNode` `.threads` is ever built by `ingest`, and a thread artifact ingested in a scratch graph can be reached only by its id, not by the path `.threads/t.md`**: found 2026-10-20 by the Coder, in writing the service tests of piece 4 of [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) (`runIngest(['.threads/t.md'])` ingests the artifact, `threadSize` and `isThreadScopedId` work, but the path does not resolve); filed 2026-10-20, as decided by the orchestrator at the filing of piece 4. The real mirror has threads reachable by path, so the folder of `.threads` is made some other way than by the scan (it is the same folder that [the `children` entry of the root folder](#id/BlockNode:00D417WK80001) names). Whether `ingest` should see `.threads`, and so build the folder and the path of a thread, is for [piece 8, ingest, track and project](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0006) to decide; until then the service tests keep reaching a thread by its id. Piece 6 or 10 should look at it too if it changes how a thread is placed.",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
