  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7S9A300001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Go for the flip, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Go for the flip, 2026-10-21**: the user committed the checkpoint (`Aperas.dev` `1b15432`: Batch 11 pieces 1 to 5 and the split of the suites; `AperasKG` `bb7792b`) and said to go: the coder implements piece 6, the flip, the one change that moves what the shell runs on (steps 1 and 2 of Batch 11, the boot, reload and flush of step 8, the wiring of Batch 10's maps, the fixtures). Piece 4's gaps were closed (`service/` 66 cases, 52 of 52 mutations of `service.ts` caught; four branches waived by name) and checked by the orchestrator (`commit` 991 of 991 in 18.1 s, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.4 s, `models` 165 of 165 in 13.3 s). The flip is judged against these suites and the tests already written on the old code (the three of `commands/`, the four of piece 3, `service/`, the corpus), which must stay green or be an entry of the list of deliberate differences. The old Oxigraph files stay as a frozen set, guarded by a test, until Batch 12; the working service and the reference copy run from `Aperas/` and are not touched.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T09ZXG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The flip (piece 6) checked, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**The flip (piece 6) checked, 2026-10-21**: the coder was cut off by the session limit, resumed after the reset and finished. In `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, 65 files staged, not committed) the core and cli sources run on the engine through the `Db` and the write layer, the service boots, reloads and flushes on it, `Lookups.subtreeTombstoned` is removed, the first-match reproduction is the regular test (the live node under both orders), `commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.test.ts` is named in `commit` and passes by the engine's no-cycle rule, `shell/oldEngine.test.ts` guards the frozen set (the six old files have no diff), and two tests are added (`commands/containers.test.ts`, `service/refusal.test.ts`). The orchestrator ran: `tsc` clean for core, cli and web; `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.0 s, `commit` 999 of 999 in 25.6 s, `models` 165 of 165, `tools` 14 of 14, `--group shell` 61 of 61, `--group corpus` 17 of 17 (migrated scratch copy), load 1 to 2.5; the coder's 12 of 12 mutations on the main seams caught; 12 deliberate differences, each with its reason, in the coder's Report (the main one: a tombstone leaves its list, a removal also tombstones the container it empties, and a removed node is pruned at the next sweep). Decided by the orchestrator on the coder's two questions: (1) a removed artifact's tombstone does not survive the sweep: it is the consequence of the user's tombstone answer, `track --reverse` forgets it once pruned and a later track makes a new artifact: a deliberate difference; (2) a textless list item written with no child is tombstoned at boot: intended, it is the boot rule over a container with no live child the user confirmed. The coder started the working service (down with no process, the standing arrangement) though its Ask said not to; it is up. Next: the grapher files piece 6, rewords Batch 12 steps 1, 2 and 4 to the leftovers as decided, and records the deliberate differences; then piece 7.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
