    "title": "**What moved in `core`**",
    "text": "**What moved in `core`**: in `node.ts` the engine access was replaced in place: `childrenOf`, `appendOrderedChild`, `insertOrderedChild`, `decodeObj`, `readField`, `idOf`, `clearField`, `mintEmbedded`, `hardDeleteNode`, `writeField`, `ApeironInstance`, `defineAccessors`, `wrap`, `backlinks`. The accessors are generated from the closed Aperas schema (`FIELDS_OF_KIND`), the reads go by `engine.items`, `values`, `graphOfId` and `backlinksOf`, the writes by `db.write`. The list of a container is written as the engine's splices (`setOrderedChildren`, `placeUnder`, which leaves the old container first and puts the child back when the engine refuses). A node is made by the new `createNode` and `wrapOrCreate`, and a write to an id with no record throws. `tombstoneNode`, `applyTombstone` and `tombstoneLiveSubtree` run on the engine's `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree`; `tombstoneEmptiedContainers` and the new `tombstoneVacuousContainers` rule are the two container rules. `findProfileByHandle`, `findTreeViewByName` and `tree.ts` `findByExactPath` read the maps (`findByExactPath` is `liveAtPath` under its old name). A new file `shell/nodeIds.ts` holds `nodeKindFromId` and `isNodeRef` by the grammar of `apeironNgn/ids`, so `vocab.ts` is not edited (the plan split `vocab.ts` in place). `Store` is replaced by `Db` in `artifacts.ts`, `folders.ts`, `linkIntegrity.ts`, `resolve.ts`, `resolveCreate.ts` and `tree.ts`; the creation sites (`trackArtifact`, the holders of `resolveCreate.ts`, the folder tree) call `createNode` with a path or an `under`. `Lookups.subtreeTombstoned` is removed with its two test uses; `mirrorDump.ts` gains `documentOf` and a `select` filter; `db.ts` gains `loadRefusal`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**What moved in `cli` and the service**",
    "text": "**What moved in `cli` and the service**: the 16 `kg*.ts` are on `Db`; `kgShow` prints `documentOf`; `kgRemove` ends by `tombstoneEmptiedContainers`; `kgInsert`, `kgUpdate` and `kgProfile` make their nodes with `createNode`; `kgInit` writes the empty files from `KINDS_OF_GRAPH` and `EMPTY_FILE_TEXT`. `service.ts` boots by `openDb` (it exits with status 1 and a cleared lock, logging the ids and files, when the load returns `rejected` or `errors`), stamps and flushes the files of the mapping (the content is the main graph, `.state/` is the threads and the views), reloads by `openDb` and refuses to replace the graph when the load is not whole (also for `--discard`, which reads the disk first), and logs and returns record counts. Deleted: `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts` and `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts`; ported: `verifyLinkRefusals.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The frozen set and its guard**",
    "text": "**The frozen set and its guard**: `storeAccess.ts`, `shape.ts`, `store.ts`, `dehydrate.ts`, `threadScope.ts` and `vocab.ts` stay in the tree, compiled, with no diff (`git diff --cached --stat` on the six is empty). `shell/oldEngine.test.ts` (4 cases, named in `commit`) holds them: the set is in the tree; no module outside the set and outside the tests imports `oxigraph` or a frozen file; a frozen file imports only the frozen set, `oxigraph`, `graphConfig` and the node builtins; and the scanner finds what it should (a probe of import specifiers). It goes with the frozen set at Batch 12.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The fixtures**",
    "text": "**The fixtures**: `support/fixture.ts` builds a `newDb()` with the three graphs, keeps the property name `store` so the test files that use it keep their text, and writes the empty mirror; `support/corpus.ts` copies the real mirror to a scratch directory and runs `scripts/migrate-mirror.py` on the copy; `support/oldFixture.ts` and `support/oldCorpus.ts` (new) keep the frozen files' own tests (`store/storeAccess.test.ts`, `store/roundtrip.test.ts`, `corpus/roundtrip.test.ts`) running on an old `Store` made from the dump of the handle and on an unmigrated copy; `serviceHarness.dumpMirror` dumps the handle.",
