    "title": "**The tests turned**",
    "text": "**The tests turned**: `commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.repro.ts` is renamed `.test.ts` and named in `commit`, and it ends by itself with a refusal that names the cause, the engine's no-cycle rule, with the service answering; its child also checks that a refused move changes nothing. The first-match case of `commands/resolve.test.ts` is the regular test (the live node under both orders, through `liveAtPath`), and the reproduction of the reference reader in `lookups/maps.test.ts` is retired with its subject. `store/dangling-unfolds.test.ts` and `corpus/dangling-unfolds.test.ts` are retired (the engine's `dropWithTarget` case in `engine/removal.test.ts` and `store/views.test.ts` 9 cover them). The tests that changed with a deliberate difference are named under each difference in [Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002); every other test of the moved groups passes with its text unchanged. After the edits of part 3, by group: commands 139 of 139, service 66 of 66, store 16 of 16, linking 10 of 10, links 3 of 3, gc 2 of 2, folder 6 of 6, ingest 9 of 9.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7T3QAV8007",
    "text": "**The checks and timings, with the load** (load average of 1, 5 and 15 minutes in brackets): the baseline before the piece, on a clean tree at `1b15432`, was `tsc` of `core` 0 errors, `web` 0, `cli` 1 (the type of a `find` in `service/ops.test.ts:334`, already there), and `commit` 991 of 991 in 19.4 s [0.70 before]. After, by the Coder: `tsc` of `core`, `cli` and `web` (`tsconfig.app.json`) 0 [2.2 at the three]; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.9 s of 5 s [2.33 1.41 1.12 before]; `commit` 999 of 999 in 19.8 s of 60 s [2.62 1.49 1.15 before, 3.19 after]; `models` 165 of 165 in 14.6 s of 30 s [3.19 before]; `tools` 14 of 14 in 14.6 s [3.29 before]; `--group corpus` 17 of 17 in 41.0 s on a migrated scratch copy [2.64 before, 2.80 after]. By the orchestrator: `tsc` clean for `core`, `cli` and `web`; `essential` 74 of 74 in 4.0 s; `commit` 999 of 999 in 25.6 s; `models` 165 of 165; `tools` 14 of 14; `--group shell` 61 of 61; `--group corpus` 17 of 17 on a migrated scratch copy; load 1 to 2.5. The two figures for `commit` (19.8 s and 25.6 s) were taken on different loads and are not compared.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7T3QAV8008",
    "text": "**The 12 mutations**, each applied by a scratch script that runs `npm run verify -- --group <g>` under `timeout 100` and restores the file; 12 of 12 caught: (1) a literal write that bypasses the write layer so the maps are not told (commands, 137 failed); (2) a tombstone that only sets the marker and stays in its list (commands, 3); (3) `isThreadsPath` false for the graph of a new node (service, 2); (4) `trackArtifact` creating the artifact without its path (ingest, 9); (5) the boot not refusing on `rejected` or `errors` (service, 2); (6) the reload not refusing (service, 1); (7) a refused move that does not put the child back (commands, 1: the check added to the child); (8) a child that does not leave its old container before the insert (commands, 5); (9) the removal that does not tombstone the container it empties (commands, 3); (10) a divergence guard that never diverges (service, 7); (11) an `oxigraph` import in the shell (`oldEngine`, 1); (12) `findByExactPath` answering the first node found (commands, 1). No survivor.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3QAV8009",
