    "title": "**Decided on the Coder's two questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21)",
    "text": "**Decided on the Coder's two questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21): (1) the tombstone of a removed artifact does not survive the sweep: it is the consequence of the tombstone answer in [Core — Design](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87SR001), `track --reverse` forgets the artifact once it is pruned and a later `track` of the path makes a new artifact with new ids, and this is a deliberate difference; (2) a textless list item written with no child is tombstoned at boot: intended, it is the boot rule over a container with no live child, which the user confirmed.",
