    "title": "00D7T3XZA8002",
    "text": "**Difference 1, a tombstone leaves the list of its container** (design answer 2): `tree` and `unfold` show nothing in place for a removed child, with `--tombstoned` too; the tombstone is shown by its id (`tree <id> --tombstoned`, `unfold <id> --tombstoned`), and a link to a tombstoned target keeps its `(tombstoned)` tag. Tests adapted: `commands/render.test.ts` (2), `commands/remove.test.ts` (3), `service/ops.test.ts` (2).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7T3XZA8003",
    "text": "**Difference 2, a removed node is unreachable, so a sweep prunes it** (it follows from 1): a removed artifact, folder or block leaves its list and is pruned at the next boot, reload, clobber or stop (it was kept before because its container reached it). The boot line of `service/lifecycle.test.ts` reads `3 unreachable tombstone(s), 1 vacuous container(s), 1 stale unfold(s)` (it was 1, 1, 1: the removed item and the vacuous list itself are now in no list); `FODDER_PRUNED` is 4 (it was 1: artifact, heading, item, list); the case that waited for the vacuous list and the artifact to stay in the file now expects them pruned; a case that asked for a removed artifact's tree after the sweep now expects the refusal; `service/ops.test.ts` can no longer unfold a removed child by its id after an earlier sweep in the file.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7T3XZA8004",
    "text": "**Difference 3, a removal tombstones the container it empties, in the same write** (design answer 2; `tombstoneEmptiedContainers` in `kgRemove`): a `list`, or a textless `listItem`, left with no live child goes with the removal, and so on upward, so the sweep's vacuous count is 0 after a removal (`lifecycle.test.ts` expects `[FODDER_PRUNED, 0, 0]`). The boot rule `tombstoneVacuousContainers` is now \"a `list`, or a textless `listItem`, with no child\" (before: with children, all tombstoned). The log words `1 vacuous container(s) tombstoned` for a reload or a clobber after a removal no longer appear.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8005:links:Link:00D7T3YJRR002",
