        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D7T3XZA8005",
    "text": "**Difference 4, the first node found at a path is the live one** (the Ask's decision, [How a path names one node](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D25686RR001)): `findByExactPath` is `liveAtPath`; `commands/resolve.test.ts` asserts the live node under both orders; the reproduction of the reference reader in `lookups/maps.test.ts` is retired, its subject, the old reader, no longer existing in the shell (the primitive's own cases stay).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 5, a move into its own subtree is refused by the engine's no-cycle rule**",
    "text": "**Difference 5, a move into its own subtree is refused by the engine's no-cycle rule**: the shell words the refusal (`cannot be moved into its own subtree`) and puts the child back, so a refused move changes nothing; `commands/moveIntoOwnSubtree.test.ts` is a regular test in `commit`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7T3XZA8007",
    "text": "**Difference 6, a node must be made before it is written, and its id must be of the engine's grammar** (13 Crockford characters; a reference field still takes any string, so a ghost in a `children` list is allowed): tests that built nodes with `wrap` on a fresh id use `createNode` (`gc/collection`, `store/views`, `links/backlinks`, `folder/ghost` with a generated id, `service/lifecycle` `addList`); a block is made `under` a node, so a test with no node first makes an artifact.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 7, removing an embed pair removes the embedded node**",
    "text": "**Difference 7, removing an embed pair removes the embedded node**: `linking/integrity.test.ts` drops the link with `removePair` (the `Link` goes with the pair; the raw delete left it orphaned).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7T3XZA8009",
    "text": "**Difference 8, `ArtifactNode` has no `type`** (the schema and rule 6 of the migration): it reads `undefined` and a write is ignored.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 9, no quads**",
    "text": "**Difference 9, no quads**: the service logs `Rehydrated N record(s)` and `Reloaded N record(s), M document(s)` and returns `recordCount` and `documentCount` (it was `quadCount` and `nodeCount`); `lifecycle.test.ts` and `ops.test.ts` follow (`> 20` and `> 10`, since the fixture is smaller than the quad counts were); `verifyLinkRefusals` counts records. The raw-quad cases are rewritten: `integrity.test.ts` (`removePair`); `lifecycle.test.ts` `buildSeed` (the stale unfold is an `unfolds` entry written for an id never made, since the engine drops an entry with its target; the dropped link by `removePair`; the dumps by `dumpMirror`); `store/storeAccess` and `store/roundtrip` (frozen files) run on an old `Store` made from the dump; `corpus/roundtrip` runs on an unmigrated copy.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800B",
