    ],
    "title": "**Difference 10, the load is whole or the service does not run**",
    "text": "**Difference 10, the load is whole or the service does not run**: a boot with `rejected` or `errors` logs `REFUSING TO START` with the ids and files, clears the lock and exits 1 (the client then reports \"did not become ready in time\" after its 5 s, and the log says why); a reload refuses with `Refusing to reload: the mirror was not read in full` and keeps the memory, and so does `--discard`, which reads the disk first, so a discard now loads twice. The start-anyway option and the copy of the rejected raw documents are piece 10 ([the rule](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800C",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 11, retired and deleted**",
    "text": "**Difference 11, retired and deleted**: `apeironNgnSmokeTest.ts`, `verifyDanglingUnfolds.ts`, `store/dangling-unfolds.test.ts` and `corpus/dangling-unfolds.test.ts` (the engine's `dropWithTarget` case in `engine/removal.test.ts` and `store/views.test.ts` 9 cover them); `Lookups.subtreeTombstoned` and its two test uses (the model test and `maps.test.ts` tell the maps of each member by id, as the write layer does).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800D",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 12, one sequencing change in a test**",
    "text": "**Difference 12, one sequencing change in a test**: in `lifecycle.test.ts` \"a stop sweeps and flushes\", a `flush --clobber` comes first, because the blocks removed in the thread test above are now pruned at the next sweep, which marks the state pending and would meet the file the test writes from outside.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800E",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The two decisions on the Coder's questions** (the orchestrator, 2026-10-21)",
    "text": "**The two decisions on the Coder's questions** (the orchestrator, 2026-10-21): (1) the tombstone of a removed artifact does not survive the sweep (Difference 2): `track --reverse` forgets it once it is pruned and a later `track` or `ingest` of that path makes a new artifact with new ids; it is the consequence of the tombstone answer, and it is a deliberate difference, not a defect. (2) A textless `listItem` written with no child is tombstoned at boot (Difference 3): intended, it is the boot rule over a container with no live child, which the user confirmed; the rule cannot tell an emptied wrapper from an item written empty (`-` alone).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800F",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Noted, not a difference of this piece**",
    "text": "**Noted, not a difference of this piece**: the set fields (`links`, `props`, `unfolds`) read in the engine's insertion order and `backlinks` in id order; no test pinned the old store order, and the order rules are piece 7's.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7T4PZ7R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Set by piece 6, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Set by piece 6, 2026-10-21**: (1) `findByExactPath` of `tree.ts` is already `liveAtPath` under its old name, so its callers (`resolve.ts:69`, `resolveCreate.ts:98`, `kgProject.ts:46`, `linkIntegrity.ts:323`) get the live node today; this piece changes their name and deletes the function, and the regular first-match test of `commands/resolve.test.ts` then calls `liveAtPath`. (2) The sort rules are all still this piece's: the set fields (`links`, `props`, `unfolds`) read in the engine's insertion order and `backlinks` in id order, and no test pinned the old store order, so the exact-order assertions of `commands/order.test.ts` are new. (3) `Lookups.subtreeTombstoned` is gone, and `findProfileByHandle` and `findTreeViewByName` read the maps.",
