    "title": "**Set by piece 6, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Set by piece 6, 2026-10-21**: the flip did the boot and the reload by `openDb`, with the refusal when the load returns `rejected` or `errors` (the boot logs `REFUSING TO START` with the ids and files, clears the lock and exits 1; a reload, `--discard` too, keeps the memory), the stamping and flushing of the files of the mapping, and record counts in place of quad counts; `service.ts` names no `dehydrate`, `rehydrateStore` or quad. Left to this piece, as the entry says: the engine `sweep` in place of `pruneUnreachableTombstones` and `pruneStaleUnfolds` (still called at the boot, the reload and the stop, `service.ts:209`, `:382`, `:437`, `:493`), the two timers in place of one for each graph, `dropGraph` of the old graphs on reload, and the start-anyway option with the side copy of the rejected raw documents. With the sweep a removed node is pruned at the next boot, reload, clobber or stop ([Layer 4](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQW6AR002), Difference 2); a refused boot shows to the client as \"did not become ready in time\", with the reason in the log only.",
