    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-21), the working service stopped with no process, and a refused load**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-21), the working service stopped with no process, and a refused load**: the Coder of piece 6 found the working service down with no process of it (the log's last start at 07:58; the idle timer, or the session reset), waited 48 s and ran `aperas service start` by the standing arrangement: it answered \"did not become ready in time\" after 5 s, the load of the real mirror taking longer (`Rehydrated 114061 quad(s)`, log 08:46:44), and the service was up 15 s later. That service runs the old code of `Aperas/`, so this is the reference engine's start on the real mirror. On the new boot of piece 6 a refused load (`rejected` or `errors`) logs `REFUSING TO START` with the ids and files, clears the lock and exits 1, and the client prints the same \"did not become ready in time\" after its 5 s, with the reason in the log only: a slow start and a refused one read the same.",
