    "title": "**Go to finish Batch 11, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Go to finish Batch 11, 2026-10-21**: the user committed the flip (`Aperas.dev` and `AperasKG`) and, judging the session quota enough, said to try to finish Batch 11: pieces 7 (reads, link integrity, profiles and views), 8 (ingest, track and project), 9 (writes and tombstones) and 10 (sweeps and the service lifecycle), one coder turn each, in order, each checked by the orchestrator before the next starts, each filed by the grapher while the next coder turn runs; if the quota runs out the work stops at the last green piece and the state is written here. Decided by the orchestrator on the grapher's last three questions: the smoke-test issue stays open until Batch 12; Current Status in `history/core.md` is reworded now (it says nothing runs on the new engine yet, which is false in `Aperas.dev`); piece 4's gaps follow-up (the coder's Turn 22: 16 cases, `service/` 50 to 66, 52 of 52 mutations of `service.ts`) was done and is added to piece 4's done record. The piece 7 entry's note stands: `findByExactPath` is already `liveAtPath` under its old name, so the piece renames its callers and deletes it, and the sort rules are all still to build.",
