    "title": "**Follow-up closing the gaps, 2026-10-20** (the coder's Turn 22)",
    "text": "**Follow-up closing the gaps, 2026-10-20** (the coder's Turn 22): in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed, `tests/service/ops.test.ts` and `tests/service/lifecycle.test.ts` changed and no change to `service.ts`. 16 cases added: `service/` goes from 50 to 66 cases in 3.2 s (3 runs: 3.13, 3.24, 3.20 s), against the 8 s of the piece. Branches given a case, by arm: `reload: true` on all 23 arms that take it; `flush: true` on insert, remove, retype, profileCreate, profileCreateView, fold, zoom and `profileRemove`; the flush arm's state flush and the case for a state-mirror divergence (`conflict.state`, an extra beyond the decision); `track` and `ingest` `force`; `checkLinks` repair with and without flush; `unfold` `showTombstoned`; `linkBreakage` (made on demand); `base` through `artifactForRef` for insert, update, remove, retype and the unresolvable base; `threadSize` on update, retype and remove; a non-zero `prunedUnfolds` at reload, clobber and shutdown. Four branches are waived by name in `WAIVED_BRANCHES` of `ops.test.ts` (its last case checks the marker is still in `service.ts`): `flushTimer` (10 s), `stateFlushTimer` (3 s) and `idleTimeout` (30 min), none a branch of an arm, each calling a function that a case reaches, and a case would wait past the group budget; and `withLinkCheckThrows`, the `catch` around the check after a write, which cannot be reached (the check does not throw on a folder, a removed artifact or an unknown id; each was run). Mutations: 52 of 52 caught. The first pass caught 48 and left 4 alive (the `checkLinks` repair flush and the `req.base` argument to `artifactForRef` in update, remove and retype, because the cases used an id, which resolves without a base); a repair-flush case and a thread case with `path` and `base` caught all four. Suites: `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.5 s, `commit` 991 of 991 in 18.3 s (budget 60 s, no warning), `models` 165 of 165 in 13.1 s; no process of `Aperas.dev` left after each run. Not covered, outside `handle()`: the `--force` retry and the removal prompt of the clients (client code; the service sees a plain `force: true`, covered) and the pass-through arguments of the read commands (covered by the `commands` group).",
