    "title": "00D7TSC16G003",
    "text": "Take a target T reached by a link Lb (id 4) of a container and by a link Lx (id 8) inside a cone that is nested through another link of the container, La (id 2). `discoverCone` recurses into the nested cone at the moment La wins, before it looks at the later links of the container, so Lx claims T first and Lb becomes the pointer, although Lb comes before Lx in id order. Within one cone the rule is exact: the first link by id claims the target, whatever the order of the view's `unfolds` and of building, for a target outside the cone and for one inside it (`commands/order.test.ts`). The result of the nested case is the same under every order of `unfolds` and of building, since the entries are sorted before the visit; only which link is canonical is in question.",
