    "title": "None decided; for the user. The Coder's options",
    "text": "None decided; for the user. The Coder's options: (a) leave it, the claim goes to the first link met in the depth-first visit in id order, which is what the code does and gives the same result under every order; (b) defer the recursion until all the links of the container are classified, so that the container's links by id win over a nested cone's; (c) the literal global minimum over every link the render reaches, which needs a fixpoint because the cones a link opens depend on who wins. Default if nothing is said: (a). Whichever is chosen, [the design sentence](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q) gets the case it names, and a case of `commands/order.test.ts` pins it.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSC16G009",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
