    "title": "**What moved**",
    "text": "**What moved**: `findByExactPath(store, p)` became `store.maps.liveAtPath(p)` at `resolve.ts`, `resolveCreate.ts`, `kgProject.ts` and `linkIntegrity.ts` and in 8 test and support files (`verifyLinkRefusals.ts`, `linking/{integrity,anchors,edits}.test.ts`, `commands/resolve.test.ts`, `ingest/chain.test.ts`, `support/linkedDemo.ts`, `service/lifecycle.test.ts`); the function, its import in `tree.ts` and three comments were deleted or reworded. `removeProfile` and `removeTreeViewByName` already went through `hardDeleteNode` and the write layer's `removeNode` since the flip, so nothing moved there. In `db.ts`, `allIdsOfKind`, `liveIdsOfKind` and `backlinksOf` were already sorted by id since piece 6, so four of the five listings were already sorted; what was open were the links of a block, the order of `unfolds` in the render, the profile and view details, and `compareByKey`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The order rules as built**",
    "text": "**The order rules as built**: (a) `apeironNgn/order.ts`: `compareByKey` puts an id with no key after those with one (several without by `compareIds`), and `MIXED_KEYS_POINT` and the import of `Undecided` are deleted; `engine/order.test.ts`'s `Undecided` case became the placement case, both sides, two start orders. (b) `node.ts`: the new exported `linksInOrder(node)` keys a link by the smallest of its `position` values as a number (`'9'` before `'10'`; a non-number counts as none) through `compareByKey`, so a link with no `position` goes last; it serves the links shown under an unfolded block (`buildNodeItem`), the links of an expanded link's target (`buildLinkItem`), `kgUnfold.ts`' `previewChildren` (the web reads `buildRenderTree`, so it gets the same) and `linkIntegrity.ts` for `storedLinks` (its `resolvedLinks` and the dangling list); the text at a dangling link's position reads the smallest position instead of the first listed. (c) `buildRenderTree` sorts the entries of `unfolds` by `compareIds` before it splits them into ids and links, so `discoverCone` meets the unfolded links in code-point order and the first claims the target, and a container's own claims (its structural homes) still come before any nested cone, as the old rule had it; the \"by luck\" comment of `ZoomState` is reworded. (d) `kgProfile.ts`: the unfolded ids of a view and the preferences of a profile are listed by id. (e) `buildLiveSlugPathIndex` scans `liveIdsOfKind` (the `tombstonedAt` check dropped). `track --reverse` (through `allIdsOfKind`), the profile and view lists, `backlinks` and `check-links` were already in id order from piece 6; the new tests pin them.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The refusal of `runPath`**",
    "text": "**The refusal of `runPath`**: in `kgPath.ts`, a node with no `toPath` gives `'<id>' is a <Kind>, which has no path: only a tracked artifact, folder or block does.`; the `null` case (a tombstone, or a block with no parent chain) keeps its own message, which no longer mentions a `Link`. `commands/resolve.test.ts` asserts the message and that it is not a `TypeError`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7TSHVMR002",
    "text": "**The checks and timings, with the load** (load average of 1, 5 and 15 minutes in brackets), by the Coder: `tsc` of `core`, `cli` and `web` (`tsconfig.app.json`) 0 errors; after part 1, `commit` 999 of 999 in 17.97 s [0.59 before]; at the end, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.0 s of 5 s [1.04 0.94 0.91 before], `commit` 1018 of 1018 in 17.7 s of 60 s [1.10 0.90 0.90 before], `models` 165 of 165 in 12.9 s, `tools` 14 of 14 in 14.1 s, `--group corpus` 17 of 17 in 38.7 s on a migrated scratch copy [1.48 1.07 0.96 before, 2.74 1.44 1.09 after]. By the orchestrator: `tsc` clean for `core`, `cli` and `web`; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.1 s; `commit` 1018 of 1018 in 18.9 s; `models` 165 of 165; `tools` 14 of 14; `--group corpus` 17 of 17; load 1.5. The added time in `commit` is the 18 cases of `order.test.ts` and one in `shell/db.test.ts`, under 0.3 s: the suite is where it was (17.5 s to 17.9 s by the Coder). The suite file counts are now `commit` 60 files and `demand` 74 (`npm run verify -- --help`, not a run).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7TSHVMR003",
    "text": "**The 21 mutations**, each applied by a scratch script (`/home/will/scratch/mutate.py`, `mutate2.py`) on one test file under `timeout 100`, the file restored after each: 18 caught at the first try and 3 survivors, each closed with a new case. Caught: the `unfolds` not sorted; sorted descending (the canonical rule reversed); `linksInOrder` returning the engine's order; by id only; the position as a string; the last position of several; a link with no position first (in `order.test.ts` and in `engine/order.test.ts`); a tie of absent keys left to 0; `allIdsOfKind` unsorted; `backlinksOf` unsorted; the profile's unfolds and its preferences unsorted; the peek of `unfold` on the raw links; `tree` on the raw links of a block; `check-links` on the raw links; `runPath` without the kind refusal and with another message. Survivors, then closed: the expanded link's target links on the raw order (the case \"the links of an expanded link\" added), the dangling text at `positions[0]` instead of the minimum (the two-position dangling link added), and `liveIdsOfKind` unsorted (applied by hand because the pattern of the script did not match; the case added in `shell/db.test.ts`). No survivor at the end.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The extra tests**",
    "text": "**The extra tests**: `commands/order.test.ts`, 18 cases, named in `commit`, with the `check-links` fixture inside it. Its fixture `ord_demo` has two documents built in two ingests, so that in `older.md` the tree lists X then Y and the id of Y is the lower, and in `newer.md` the two orders agree (the first case asserts that). The canonical place: a target outside the cone and a target inside it, in each document, under a view that lists the unfolds forward and one that lists them backward (a case asserts that their raw `unfolds` differ): the same render, exactly one `[*]` on the link of the lowest id and the other a `[*see <it> (link)]`; and the four links of both documents together. The links of a block: five minted links of ids rising in the order none, 100, 10, [40, 3], 9 come out as [40, 3], 9, 10, 100, none in `linksInOrder`, in `tree`, in `render-tree`, in the peek of `unfold`, inside an expanded link, and as the `resolvedLinks` of a discrepancy; two dangling links in position order with the text at their first position. The listings, made in the opposite order of their ids: profiles, the views of a profile, its preferences, all views, the unfolded ids of a view, `backlinks`, `track --reverse` (never projected and changed), and the discrepancies and dangling links of `check-links`. `shell/db.test.ts` gained the missing case for `liveIdsOfKind`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The tests turned exact**",
    "text": "**The tests turned exact**: `render.test.ts` (the links under an unfolded block in the order of the text; the two links to Beta Section in tree order with the canonical one the first by id; the structure's links; `show` by id; the peek's children then links; a bare peek leaves the unfolds as they were, no sort), `views.test.ts` (the `unfolds` of a view by id; the views by id), `track.test.ts` (the lists exactly) and `service/ops.test.ts` (backlinks `[alpha, gamma]`; `trackReverse` in the order beta, dup, alpha, gamma, then `.`, `cmd_demo`); the file headers that said \"compares sets\" are reworded. The \"Noted\" entry of piece 6 in Layer 4 (the set fields read in insertion order) is replaced by these assertions. By group after the turn: `--group commands,shell,engine` 888 of 888, `service/ops.test.ts` 41 of 41.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
