    "title": "**Decided on the Coder's questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21)",
    "text": "**Decided on the Coder's questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21): (1) a nested cone: the rule of the canonical place is exact within one cone and, with a nested cone, the first link met in the depth-first visit wins, not necessarily the lowest id; left as built and filed as [an issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7TSC16G001) for the user to decide later (the edge was never specified; the options are in the issue); (2) `aperas show` keeps listing a block's links in id order, the stored form, as the mirror (`mirrorDump.documentOf` sorts every set by id; `linksInOrder` is the reader's order, and nothing else reads `.links` into an output).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decisions noted by the Coder**",
    "text": "**Decisions noted by the Coder**: the first in code-point order of the unfolded ids means, in the code, that the render sorts the entries of `unfolds` by id and `discoverCone` visits the links of a cone in that order (a pure implementation choice); the place of a link with several positions is its smallest position, as a number (the design says \"by `position`\" and every wikilink has at least one; a link of two occurrences of its target has two `position` props); `compareByKey` no longer throws on a mixed pair, so `Undecided` and `MIXED_KEYS_POINT` left `order.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSHVMG001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
