    "title": "**Difference 2, the canonical place of a node reached through several unfolded links is the first link by id within a cone**",
    "text": "**Difference 2, the canonical place of a node reached through several unfolded links is the first link by id within a cone**: the render sorts the entries of a view's `unfolds` by id before the visit, so the place is the same under every order of `unfolds` and of building; the reference copy let the first escaping link in the store's order claim it. Reason: [The canonical place in the render](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q). With a nested cone the first link met in the depth-first visit wins, not necessarily the lowest id; left as built and filed as [an issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7TSC16G001). Tests adapted: `commands/render.test.ts` (the two links to Beta Section in tree order, the canonical one the first by id), `commands/order.test.ts` (new).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7TSPH88001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
