    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 7, in `Aperas.dev` (branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed), lists a block's links by the smallest of their `position` values as a number, then by id, a link with no `position` after those that have one ([The order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P)), in `tree`, in `unfold` (the peek and inside an expanded link), in the web's `render-tree` and in `check-links`, through the new `linksInOrder` over `compareByKey`, which no longer throws `Undecided` on a mixed pair (the entry above). The reproduction is the test: `commands/order.test.ts` mints five links of ids rising in the order none, 100, 10, [40, 3], 9 and asserts [40, 3], 9, 10, 100, none in each of those places; mutations on the engine's order returned as it is, by id only, the position as a string, the last of several positions, and a link with no position first are all caught. `commit` 1018 of 1018. `aperas show` keeps listing the links in id order, the stored form, as the mirror (decided by the orchestrator). The working service and the reference copy in `Aperas/` run the old code until the cutover and keep listing them newest first.",
