    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 7, in `Aperas.dev` (staged, not committed), gave `runPath` the refusal of its own: a node with no `toPath` ends with `'<id>' is a <Kind>, which has no path: only a tracked artifact, folder or block does.`, and the `null` case (a tombstone, or a block with no parent chain) keeps its own message, which no longer mentions a `Link`. `commands/resolve.test.ts` asserts the message and that the refusal is not a `TypeError`; the mutations without the kind refusal and with another message are caught. The test covers a `Link`; the check is by the absence of `toPath`, so it does not depend on the kind. The working service and the reference copy in `Aperas/` run the old code until the cutover and keep the `TypeError`.",
