    "title": "**Since (2026-10-21), two of the three behaviours and the five listings built**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-21), two of the three behaviours and the five listings built**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 7, in `Aperas.dev` (staged, not committed): the first-match behaviour is closed on the new engine (the callers read `liveAtPath`, `findByExactPath` is deleted; see [the live-or-tombstoned issue](#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001)); the canonical place of a node reached through several unfolded links is the first link by id within a cone, whatever the order of the view's `unfolds` and of building ([The canonical place in the render](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q)), with the nested cone filed as [its own issue](#id/BlockNode:00D7TSC16G001); the profiles, the views, a view's unfolded ids, `backlinks`, `track --reverse` and the `check-links` report are sorted by id, and the links of a block by `position` ([the newest-first issue](#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001)), each pinned by `commands/order.test.ts`. Not touched: `positionsEqual` (piece 8). `buildLiveSlugPathIndex` now scans `liveIdsOfKind`; whether that settles the first-seen order named above was not traced. This entry stays open until piece 8.",
