  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V14M08001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 8 checked, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Piece 8 checked, 2026-10-21**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder moved the lookups of `artifacts.ts` and `folders.ts` onto the one path map (the write layer telling it after each accepted write), made `positionsEqual` compare sorted lists, replaced the ghost filter by a record-and-title test, gave each created node its graph by `graphOfNewNode`, and added `commands/ingest.test.ts` (11 cases); 21 of 22 mutations caught, the 22nd equivalent (`createNode` not telling the map, because the path write afterwards does). The orchestrator ran: `tsc` clean for core, cli and web; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.2 s, `commit` 1029 of 1029 in 18.6 s, `models` 165 of 165, `tools` 14 of 14, `--group corpus` 17 of 17 (load 0.8). Decided on the coder's two questions: (1) the folder scan keeps skipping dot directories; the coder found that `listArtifactFiles` does walk into them, so a thread artifact is tracked and found by path while `ingest` never builds its `.threads` folder: added as an observation to the dot-name issue, for the user to decide later; (2) the tracked artifact with no parent until the next folder ingest stays as it is, for Batch 16. The coder's friction (it found no \"Brief — piece 8\" entry through `aperas show`, which cuts children) is a tool gap noted for the grapher's friction list. A link with several positions: the smallest position rules, one sentence to add to the design where the order of a block's links is stated.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D7V5SMJR001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-21**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed (eight files: seven changed and the new `commands/ingest.test.ts`, named in `suites/commit.suite.mjs`). The lookups of `artifacts.ts` and `folders.ts` read the one path map, the write layer telling it after each accepted write (it already did since piece 6, so it needed no change); `findLiveByKindAndPath`, `findLiveArtifactByPath`, `allLiveIdsOfKind`, `existingByPath`, `folderIdByPath` and `artifactIdByPath` are found nowhere in `packages` by a `grep` of the Coder; the real mirror and the checkout `Aperas/` were only read, and no service was started or stopped.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0006",
    "type": "listItem",
