    "title": "**What moved**",
    "text": "**What moved**: (a) `shell/artifacts.ts`: the two `find` functions are deleted; their 8 callers (`resolveBarePathCode`, `trackArtifact`, `trackArtifactsScoped`, `ingestArtifact`, `ingestAllArtifacts` and `kgIngest.ts:48`) call `store.maps.liveAtPath(path, { kind })` with `'ArtifactNode'` or `'FolderNode'`; in `trackAllArtifacts` the map `existingByPath` is gone (`liveAtPath` per file on disk, computed before any write as before); `positionsEqual` compares two sorted copies of the lists. (b) `shell/db.ts`: the new `liveDocumentIdsOfKind(db, kind)` lists the ids that have a record, a title and no tombstone marker, sorted by id, and replaces the two local `allLiveIdsOfKind` (the filter `path !== undefined` of the reference copy). (c) `folders.ts` (the pure builder): `buildFolderTree` takes one `FolderReaders` (`folderKeyAt`, `artifactKeyAt`, `existingAt`) in place of the three maps; `shell/folders.ts` answers each from `store.maps` (`existingAt` reads the `props` and the README children of the one folder asked about), takes `diskOnlyPaths` and `dbOnlyIds` from `liveAtPath` and the list of live folder paths, and `getFolderRecord` asks the map instead of scanning every folder. (d) `shell/node.ts`: one comment reworded; `kgIngest.ts`: `liveAtPath`. The graph of each created node was already `graphOfNewNode` since the flip (`createNode` goes through the write layer), so no code in the ingest paths decides a graph any more.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The checks and timings, with the load**",
    "text": "**The checks and timings, with the load**: by the Coder, baseline before any edit `commit` 1018 of 1018 in 19.3 s and `--group folder` 6 of 6; after parts 1 and 2 `tsc` clean, `essential` 74 of 74, `commit` 1018 of 1018 in 20.7 s; at the end `tsc` of `core`, `cli` and `web` clean, `essential` 74 of 74 in 2.9 s of 5 s, `commit` 1029 of 1029 in 18.3 s of 60 s (the 11 new cases add 0.14 s of file time, below the noise), `models` 165 of 165 in 13.3 s, `tools` 14 of 14 in 14.1 s, `--group corpus` 17 of 17 in 40.4 s (the Coder recorded the load as \"as before\", no figure). By the orchestrator: `tsc` clean for `core`, `cli` and `web`; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.2 s; `commit` 1029 of 1029 in 18.6 s; `models` 165 of 165; `tools` 14 of 14; `--group corpus` 17 of 17; load 0.8.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D7V463CR004",
    "text": "**The 22 mutations**, applied by a scratch script (`/home/will/scratch/p8/mutate.py`, which restores each file) on the whole `commit` suite under `timeout 100`: 21 caught and 1 equivalent. Caught: `positionsEqual` unsorted (the position props case of `ingest.test.ts`); the write layer's `tombstone`, `tombstoneSubtree`, `addPair`, `clearField`, `removePair` and `removeNode` not telling the map (`ingest.test.ts`, `shell/db.test.ts`, `remove.test.ts`, `views.test.ts`); `folderKeyAt` and `artifactKeyAt` returning nothing; the live list keeping tombstones (`track.test.ts`); the live list ignoring the title (`ingest.test.ts`); `liveAtPath` ignoring the kind or the graph (`ingest.test.ts`, `lookups/maps.test.ts`); `trackArtifact` and `ingestArtifact` never finding the node; `existingAt` returning nothing (`folders.test.ts` 6b); folder holders not kept (`ghost.test.ts`); `resolveBarePathCode` looking at folders only (`links/refusals.test.ts`). Three survived at first and each got a case: `diskOnlyPaths` of the folder ingest and of `trackAllArtifacts` taking every path (the two twin cases) and `getFolderRecord` ignoring the kind (an assertion on a file path); all three are caught now. The equivalent one: the write layer's `createNode` not calling `maps.built`, because the shell writes `path` after creating a node and that write tells the map.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The 11 cases of `commands/ingest.test.ts`**, in order, on one store",
    "text": "**The 11 cases of `commands/ingest.test.ts`**, in order, on one store: an artifact and a folder of one ingest found by the one map and listed by the folder; a path is a file or a directory (the kind and graph filters); a second ingest keeps the ids; a rename on disk (the map follows, the old path finds nothing); a path reused after a removal (a new artifact with new ids, the tombstone keeps its path and is not answered); a ghost is in no list; a node with a record and a path but no title is in no list; a vanished folder with the README of a live folder is a removal, not a rename; the same for an artifact; a thread artifact lands in `threads.tree` and is found there by its path; the `position` props of a `Link` stored in descending order keep their ids on a later ingest (the case asserts that the store reads them in the order written).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
