    ],
    "title": "**Decided on the Coder's questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21)",
    "text": "**Decided on the Coder's questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21): (1) the folder scan keeps skipping dot directories; the Coder found that `listArtifactFiles` (`core/src/artifacts.ts:42`, used by the full `track` sweep and by `ingest` of a directory) does walk into them and skips only dot files, so a thread artifact is tracked, lands in `threads.tree` and is found by its path, while `ingest` never builds its `.threads` folder; the Coder's three ways, (a) leave it, the folder being the mirror's own, (b) have the scan build `.threads` in the threads graph, (c) make `listArtifactFiles` skip dot directories like the scan, are not chosen: added as an observation to [the dot-name issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D79JHQ40001), for the user to decide later. (2) The tracked artifact with no parent until the next folder ingest stays as it is, for Batch 16: the next ingest finds it through the map by its stored path, and the problem arises only with a derived path.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7V463D0000",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Decisions noted by the Coder**",
    "text": "**Decisions noted by the Coder**: (1) the ghost filter is `liveDocumentIdsOfKind`, a record, a title and no tombstone marker; with the engine a ghost has no record at all, so the test that matters today is the record, and the title guards a node a write is still building; (2) `buildFolderTree` takes one `FolderReaders` of three functions and not the shell's `Db`, so the pure builder stays engine-agnostic and reads one folder's props and README children only when the disk walk reaches that folder; (3) `positionsEqual` sorts both lists numerically; the fresh list is always in text order, so the sort matters only for the stored list.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D7V463CR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
