    "title": "**Observed (2026-10-21), by the Coder in piece 8 of [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C)**",
    "text": "**Observed (2026-10-21), by the Coder in piece 8 of [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C)**: the scan of `buildFolderTree` skips every directory name that starts with a dot, but `listArtifactFiles` (`core/src/artifacts.ts:42`, used by the full `track` sweep and by `ingest` of a directory) walks into dot directories and skips only dot files. So a thread artifact is tracked (a full `track` finds `artifacts/.threads/*.md` on disk when it is projected), lands in `threads.tree` and is found by its path through the map (`liveAtPath`; `commands/ingest.test.ts` has the case), while `ingest` never builds a `FolderNode` `.threads` and never attaches the artifact to a folder; in the real mirror that folder exists by some other route, the `children` entry of the root. The title's \"only by its id\" holds for the walk through folders; whether `aperas resolve` or `aperas tree` reach the thread by that path was not run. Three ways, none chosen: (a) leave it, since threads are reached by path through the map and the folder is the mirror's own; (b) have the scan build `.threads` as a folder of the threads graph with its artifacts listed, which completes the folder tree and changes what `ingest` writes into the threads graph and what the root lists; (c) make `listArtifactFiles` skip dot directories like the scan, so the two agree. The orchestrator kept the scan as it was (piece 8 changes none of the three) and left the choice to the user, to decide later.",
