    "title": "**Since (2026-10-21), the filter that keeps the ghost out is a record and a title, in `Aperas.dev`**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-21), the filter that keeps the ghost out is a record and a title, in `Aperas.dev`**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 8 replaced the two private `allLiveIdsOfKind` helpers (`path !== undefined`) by `liveDocumentIdsOfKind` in `shell/db.ts`, which lists the ids that have a record, a title and no tombstone marker, sorted by id; with the engine a ghost has no record at all, so it is in no list, and a node that a write is still building (a record and a path but no title) is not listed either. `commands/ingest.test.ts` holds both cases (a ghost is in no list; a node with a record and a path but no title is in no list), and `folder/ghost.test.ts` passes with its text unchanged; the mutations on the live list (keeping tombstones, ignoring the title) are caught. What the load does with a `children` entry whose id has no document is still not read (Not proven above). The reference copy in `Aperas/` keeps the filter `path !== undefined`; this entry is a note on the new engine and does not reopen the issue.",
