    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 8, in `Aperas.dev` (staged, not committed), built the last of the three behaviours: `positionsEqual` compares two sorted lists, so a reused `Link` whose `position` props are stored in another order keeps its prop ids on a later ingest (`commands/ingest.test.ts`, the position props stored in descending order; the mutation with the sort removed is caught). With piece 7 the three behaviours and the five listings are built on the engine: the first-match lookups read `liveAtPath` (the callers of `findByExactPath` in piece 7, `findLiveByKindAndPath` and `findLiveArtifactByPath` in piece 8, all deleted), the canonical place is the first link by id within a cone ([The canonical place in the render](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000Q); the nested cone is [its own issue](#id/BlockNode:00D7TSC16G001)), and the profiles, the views, a view's unfolded ids, `backlinks`, `track --reverse` and the `check-links` report are sorted by id, the links of a block by `position` ([The order of links without a position](../design/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D24N87T000P)). `buildLiveSlugPathIndex` scans `liveIdsOfKind`, which is sorted by id. `commit` 1029 of 1029 in 18.3 s by the Coder and 18.6 s by the orchestrator. The reference copy in `Aperas/`, which the working service runs until the cutover, keeps the three behaviours as they were.",
