  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D7ZY25VG001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 9 checked, and a defect of the working service, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Piece 9 checked, and a defect of the working service, 2026-10-21**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder found almost all of step 4 already done by the flip and added the missing Done-when tests: a model of the removal rule (`tests/shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts`, 20 seeds over `runRemove`; the invariant that a tombstone is in no `children` list also in the existing model), a `toPath()` null case and a flushed-mirror case (`commands/remove.test.ts`, with the helper `support/mirrorLists.ts`), a move-out-of-a-list case (`commands/containers.test.ts`), two stale comments fixed; 11 mutations caught. The work was cut off once by an API connection error (a certificate error) and resumed. The orchestrator ran: `tsc` clean, `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.3 s, `commit` 1032 of 1032 in 20.6 s, `models` 186 of 186, `tools` 14 of 14, `--group corpus` 17 of 17 after the coder fixed four dangling links of its own Report (`../.threads/coder.md` is not a link form inside a thread: `#id/BlockNode:<ID>`); load 1.5 to 1.8. Decided on the coder's questions: (1) the four commands reach `insertItem`, `moveItem` and `removeItem` through the shell's `insertChild`, `appendChild` and the `children` setter in `node.ts`, one place: accepted; (2) the engine accepts an insert of an already-tombstoned node into a list: filed as an issue, nothing reaches it; (3) a move or a reconcile that empties a list leaves it live until the boot sweep: the boot rule the user confirmed, noted in the record. A defect of the working service found by the coder: its `update` handler (`Aperas/monorepo/packages/cli/src/apeironNgn/service.ts` lines 574 to 582) sets only `dirty` and never `stateDirty`, so an `update` that touches only a thread node is not written to `.state/` until something else marks the state dirty (re-zoom a view, then `aperas flush`, is the workaround): filed as an issue; piece 10's flush of each graph on its own flag closes it in the new service.",
