    "title": "**The extra tests and the helper**",
    "text": "**The extra tests and the helper**: `tests/support/mirrorLists.ts` (new) reads `ArtifactNode.jsonld`, `BlockNode.jsonld` and `FolderNode.jsonld` of a flushed mirror and gives the tombstones and the ids that a `children` list names. `commands/remove.test.ts` (23 lines more): `toPath()` and `parent` of a removed block and of the block under it are null and undefined, the container's `treeChildren` has no trace of it, and a live node still has a path; after the block removals, `dumpMirror` writes the tombstones of five removed nodes and no `children` list names one (the helper's `inLists` is empty, its `listed` is over 5; a first form of this case sat where every host was already dead and passed under the mutation, so it was moved before them). `commands/containers.test.ts` (16 lines more): a move is not a removal, the last item moved out of a list (`runInsert --after`) leaves the list live and empty, and `tombstoneVacuousContainers` then tombstones it, and it leaves its container. `shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts` (129 lines more): in the existing 20-seed model, after every operation, a node that the operation made a tombstone is in no `children` list; a new part of 20 seeds (3001 to 3020) builds a random tree of headings, paragraphs, lists, textful and textless list items with no vacuous container, removes at most 40 nodes by `runRemove` (75 percent leaves), and after each removal compares the tombstone state of every node and every `children` list with a model of the rule in ten lines (the subtree goes; the container above goes while it is a `list` or a textless `listItem` with no live child, upward), and a final case asserts that the seeds together made over 100 removals, over 20 emptied containers and over 3 chains of more than one container (121, 53 and 11). The invariant of the existing model is stated for the moment of the operation, not \"whatever came after\", because the engine accepts an insert of an already-tombstoned node ([the issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001)).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D8006A58001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
