    "title": "**Closes**",
    "text": "**Closes**: the piece's entry names no issue. The batch's Closes names step 4 only inside [no test calls most commands of the CLI or the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC8001), which closes with steps 3, 4, 5 and 8 and so waits for piece 10: it stays open. [Tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001) gains a dated entry: the callers that tombstone, its share of Batch 11, now go through the engine in `Aperas.dev`; it stays open for the 52 tombstones of the real mirror (migrated at the cutover) and for the reference copy (Batch 12). [The plain write on a tombstone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001) and [a write to a thread node never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001) gain a dated entry each, see the filing.",
