  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D8006A5800B",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Findings of the Coder along the way**",
    "text": "**Findings of the Coder along the way**: a vacuous `list` cannot come from a document (the parser flattens a list into `listItem`s under the heading), so the move case of `containers.test.ts` is built on the handle like the rest of that file, and an edit of `insert.test.ts` was reverted; the working service's `update` handler (and its three siblings) never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty, the issue above; waiting on the mutation run with an `until pgrep -f` loop (a pattern that could match its own shell) had to be stopped, and `tail --pid` and `kill -0` were used instead.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D8006A58001",
