    "title": "**Since (2026-10-21), the shell never lists a tombstone, and the model finds that the engine does**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-21), the shell never lists a tombstone, and the model finds that the engine does**: in piece 9 of [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) the Coder read the shell for the question under Not proven. No command writes the tombstone marker or inserts a tombstone: the four commands that place children (`kgInsert`, `kgUpdate`, `kgRemove`, `kgRetype`) reach the write layer's `insertItem`, `moveItem` and `removeItem` through the shell's `insertChild`, `appendChild` and the `children` setter (`node.ts:92` to `:160`), and `kgInsert` moves only live blocks; the tombstoning goes through the engine's `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` (`node.ts:792`, `:815`). The invariant \"a tombstone is in no `children` list, whatever came after\" failed in the existing 20-seed model of `tests/shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts` on the seeds 2009 to 2011, with an `insert` of an already-tombstoned node under a host: the engine accepts the insert. The invariant is now stated for the moment of the operation. So nothing reaches the symptom today; the case stays open with Enforcement, and the orchestrator decided at the check of the piece to leave it as built. No test pins the acceptance.",
