    "title": "**Since observed (2026-10-21), by the Coder in piece 9 of [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), on the `update` handler, and the same in its three siblings**",
    "text": "**Since observed (2026-10-21), by the Coder in piece 9 of [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C), on the `update` handler, and the same in its three siblings**: the working service's `update` case (`Aperas/monorepo/packages/cli/src/apeironNgn/service.ts`, lines 574 to 582) sets `dirty = true` and never `stateDirty`; the grapher read the file and found the same in `insert` (565), `remove` (583) and `retype` (595), so an `update` of a thread node alone is not written to `.state/` until something else marks the state dirty. Workaround: re-zoom a view (`zoom` sets `stateDirty`), then `aperas flush`. The three-part fix agreed on 2026-10-02 is not made in the working service, and the service runs the old code until the cutover. The new service closes it with piece 10 of Batch 11: its flush of each graph on its own flag ([step 8](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000M)). Until then the issue is a risk for the working service.",
