    "title": "**Since (2026-10-21), the callers that tombstone go through the engine in `Aperas.dev`; the issue stays open**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-21), the callers that tombstone go through the engine in `Aperas.dev`; the issue stays open**: [piece 9 of Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0007) found `applyTombstone` and `tombstoneLiveSubtree` already on the engine's `tombstone` and `tombstoneSubtree` since the flip, the tombstone out of its container, the shell clearing no `children`, `links` or `props`, and added the tests that pin it: a model of 20 seeds over `runRemove` against a ten-line model of the rule, a case that a removed block has a null `toPath()` and no `parent`, and a case that the mirror a flush writes holds the tombstones of five removed nodes and no `children` list names one; 11 mutations on the cascade, the list removal and the emptied container were all caught. The Batch 11 share of the issue (the callers) is therefore built and tested in `Aperas.dev`. It stays open for the 52 tombstones of the real mirror, which the migration changes at the cutover, and for the reference copy `Aperas/` and the working service, which keep the old code until the cutover and Batch 12. The third site, the folder removal, is not scripted by a reproduction of its own; it goes through `applyTombstone`.",
