  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80EG6Z8001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Piece 10 checked, Batch 11 built, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Piece 10 checked, Batch 11 built, 2026-10-21**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` (`js-apeironngn`, staged, not committed) the coder built the sweeps and the service lifecycle: the write layer's `sweep` for each graph, `pruneStaleUnfolds` dropped, the boot rule over a container with no live child kept, one flush timer for each graph at the interval of the table of settings (`tree` 10 s, `threads.tree` and `treeviews` 3 s) with its own dirty flag (so an update of a thread node alone reaches `.state/`), the refusal on `rejected` or `errors` with the start-anyway option and the side copy of the raw rejected documents, a reload that builds a new handle and drops the old graphs, `quadCount` replaced by the count of records; 23 of 23 mutations caught. The orchestrator ran: `tsc` clean for core, cli and web; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.2 s, `commit` 1049 of 1049 in 21.2 s, `models` 187 of 187, `tools` 14 of 14, `--group corpus` 21 of 21 (load 0.9 to 1.8); `check-links` clean. Decided on the coder's five questions, all as built: (1) `closeDb` drops the graphs that no pair of another graph points into (the views graph on the real mirror) and the old handle is collected anyway: best effort; (2) the settings table is read once at start from the configuration found from the mirror's directory, a change needs a restart; (3) the load's dangling ids are logged as one warning at start and at each reload, not a refusal; (4) the side copy is made when the load is accepted, as `<file>.rejected-<UTC stamp>.json` next to the mirror file (in `.state/` too), not written again if an equal copy exists, and the flag name and the file name go into `design/packaging.md`'s Workflow and the option into the skills' service recipes at the next skill release; (5) a removal in a thread rewrites the main graph's files at its next tick, as before. Batch 11 is built: the grapher files piece 10 and closes the batch (the Finishing Turn: the batch's done record, what it closes, the milestone, Current Status, the Dashboard, the deliberate differences of the batch in Layer 4, the flag and file names in `design/packaging.md`). Next: Batch 12, deleting what the flip froze.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D3XJ7GTR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D80N9028001"
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Done, 2026-10-21**",
    "text": "**Done, 2026-10-21**: in `Aperas.dev/monorepo` on branch `js-apeironngn`, staged and not committed (53 files staged in all, with the earlier pieces' staged files). The flip had done the boot and the reload on the handle; this piece replaced the two sweeps by the engine's, gave each graph its own flush, added the start-anyway option with the side copy of the skipped documents, and made a reload free the old handle as far as the engine lets it. The real mirror and the checkout `Aperas/` were only read; the working service (pids 578888 and 578899 under `Aperas/`) was not touched, and the Coder's own scratch services are gone (`ls /tmp | grep -c aperas-test`: 0).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D76BQ2N0008",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": [
      "BlockNode:00D80J973R002",
      "BlockNode:00D80J973R003",
