  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R002",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "props": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R002:props:StringProp:00D80J9T4R000",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "orderedList",
        "value": "false"
      },
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R002:props:StringProp:00D80J9T4R001",
        "@type": "StringProp",
        "key": "startIndex",
        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "00D80J973R002",
    "text": "**What the flip and the earlier pieces had done** (the Coder's Subturn 1, by `grep` and reading): `service.ts` (824 lines) already booted on `openDb(contentDir)`, refused to start on `loadRefusal(opened.load)` (lines 168 to 175), refused a reload (`reloadStore`, 394 to 399, and the `discard` probe, 368 to 370), dumped by `dumpMirror(store.engine, contentDir, store.mapping, …)` and stamped by `mirrorFilesOf` over the mapping; `grep -nEi \"quad\" service.ts` found 0 lines. What remained was 16 lines outside the tests that named `pruneUnreachableTombstones`, `pruneStaleUnfolds` or `removeDanglingUnfolds` (the two definitions in `node.ts` with their comments, the import and nine call sites in `service.ts`) and 10 in the tests (`gc/collection.test.ts` 3, `store/views.test.ts` 4, `service/lifecycle.test.ts` 3); the two flags `dirty` and `stateDirty` with the constants `FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS = 10_000` and `STATE_FLUSH_INTERVAL_MS = 3_000` and their two timers; an `update` handler (`:592` to `:600`) that set `dirty` only, which is the defect of an `update` of a thread node that reached no `.state/` file; a `reloadStore` that swapped the `Db` without freeing the old one; and no start-anyway option, side copy or logging of `load.dangling` (`grep -rn \"start-anyway\\|startAnyway\"`: 0 lines).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The sweeps of the shell** (Subturn 2, `core/src/shell/node.ts`)",
    "text": "**The sweeps of the shell** (Subturn 2, `core/src/shell/node.ts`): `pruneUnreachableTombstones` and `pruneStaleUnfolds` deleted; `sweepTombstones(db)` added, which calls the write layer's `sweep` for each graph of `db.graphs` in the order of the mapping and gives `{ pruned, byGraph }`; `tombstoneVacuousContainers` kept as the boot rule; the one comment of `TreeView.unfold` that named the deleted sweep reworded (the engine drops an `unfolds` entry with its target, role `dropWithTarget`). The 16 lines outside the tests became 0 and the 10 in the tests 0 (`gc/collection.test.ts` and `store/views.test.ts` call `sweepTombstones`; `views.test.ts` 9b shows an `unfolds` entry leaving with its swept target; `lifecycle.test.ts` rewritten). On a migrated copy of the real mirror (`makeCorpusCopy`): load 639 ms, 30,595 records, 12,522 documents, 0 dangling, 0 rejected, 0 errors; the boot rule tombstones 0; `sweepTombstones` removes 225 ids (tree 192, threads.tree 33, treeviews 0) in 20 ms.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The per-graph flush** (Subturn 3)",
    "text": "**The per-graph flush** (Subturn 3): the write layer (`shell/writeLayer.ts`) takes a `touch` callback and tells it, after the engine took each write, which graph changed (a write of a graph touches it; `insertItem` and `removeItem` also touch the graph of the item, whose document states its `parent`; `tombstone`, `tombstoneSubtree` and `removeNode` touch every graph, since they leave the lists and the `unfolds` of the others; a `sweep` that removed something touches every graph, one that removed nothing touches none); `Db` (`shell/db.ts`) gets `changed: Set<GraphName>` filled by it (a load changes none). `service.ts` is rewritten around it: `resolveGraphSettings(contentDir)` read once at boot (logged as `Flush intervals: tree 10000 ms, threads.tree 3000 ms, treeviews 3000 ms.`); the flags `dirty` and `stateDirty`, the two constants, the two timers and all 27 `dirty = true`/`stateDirty = true` lines of `handle()` are gone; `flushGraph(graph)` flushes a graph that is in `store.changed` after the divergence check of its own files, `flushAll()` tries every graph and throws the first refusal after, `writeGraph` is the dump of one graph, one `setInterval` for each graph at its interval, `clobberFlush` writes every graph, the shutdown flushes each graph apart; `standingConflict()` still gives the response its `content` (the main graph's) and `state` (the others'). `grep -nEi \"dehydrate|rehydrate|quad\" service.ts`: 0 lines (it was 6, comments and a log text). The reload result loses `prunedUnfolds` and gains `freedGraphs`; the boot and reload log `Loaded` and `Reloaded` lines and `Startup GC: cleaned N unreachable tombstone(s), M vacuous container(s).`",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R005:links:Link:00D80J9T58000",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R005:links:Link:00D80J9T58000:props:StringProp:00D80J9T58001",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "117"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**The refusal and the start-anyway option** (Subturn 4)",
    "text": "**The refusal and the start-anyway option** (Subturn 4): the boot and reload refusal were the flip's (`loadRefusal`, [the rule of Packaging](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001)); added the flag `--start-anyway` of `aperas service start`, `service restart` and `aperas reload` (the environment variable `APERAS_START_ANYWAY` for the spawned service, `startAnyway` in the `reload` request, `runStart({ startAnyway })`). With it the load that returned `rejected` or `errors` is accepted, logged as `START-ANYWAY: …`, and before anything can flush the service copies the raw documents the load skipped to a side file next to their file, `<file>.rejected-<UTC stamp>.json` (in `.state/` too); `skippedDocuments(root, mapping, load)` in `mirrorLoad.ts` re-reads the files and gives the documents that carry a rejected id, the id of an engine error, or, for an error on a file, the entries that are no document; a copy identical to one already beside the file is not written again. A refused start now ends the client's wait at once and says why (`waitForReady` sees the lock cleared and reads the last `REFUSING TO START` line of `service.log` since the start) instead of a 5 s timeout; without the option the reload error and the start line name the files, the ids and the option. The ids referenced and never defined (`load.dangling`) are logged as one warning at boot and at reload and nothing more (the real mirror has none).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D80J973R006",
    "text": "**The release of the old handle, and the tests** (Subturn 5): `closeDb(db)` in `shell/db.ts` drops a replaced handle's graphs through the engine in rounds (the views, nothing points into them; then every graph no remaining graph points into; when two graphs wait for each other it takes out of the lists the items that are nodes of another remaining graph, which is the root folder's entry for the `.threads` folder, and drops again); a graph the engine still refuses (a `Link` target across the graphs in both directions) is kept. `reloadStore` loads once (the old probe load on `discard` is gone), refuses and `closeDb`s the new handle when the load is refused, otherwise swaps and `closeDb`s the old one, and answers `freedGraphs`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The extra tests**, each named in a suite",
    "text": "**The extra tests**, each named in a suite: NEW `service/flush.test.ts` (6 cases, in `commit`: the intervals read from the table in `aperas.config.json` above the scratch mirror, 150 ms for `threads.tree` and 60 s for the others, so no case waits for a default; an update of a thread node alone reaches `.state/BlockNode.jsonld` by its timer and by `flush: true` with the other files' bytes and mtime unchanged; a main write waits for its interval; a flush of a graph not written writes nothing; a main file changed outside refuses the main graph and the threads graph is flushed all the same; a view op does not write the threads graph); `service/lifecycle.test.ts` (the stale-unfold counts gone, the sweep counts become two, `Loaded` for `Rehydrated`, `freedGraphs` 3, the dangling warning, the shutdown text names the graph); `service/refusal.test.ts` (+5: the client's start says why from the log, no lock, no process; `--start-anyway` on a reload copies both documents of a repeated id raw to `BlockNode.jsonld.rejected-<stamp>.json` before any flush, the unaffected parts work and flush, the first flush removes them from the file and the side file keeps them; a second reload copies nothing again, also against an older copy under another stamp; a document the engine refused is refused and copied likewise; the boot with the option); `service/ops.test.ts` (the two timer waivers removed, `freedGraphs`); `shell/writeLayer.model.test.ts` (in the 20 seeds, after every operation the graphs whose files the dump would write differently are all in `db.changed` and a refused write touches none; five `sweepTombstones` runs per seed equal the oracle's per-graph sweeps and touch every graph or none; one case that the seeds together swept something); `shell/db.test.ts` (+4 `closeDb`); `mirror/load.test.ts` (+3 `skippedDocuments`); `store/views.test.ts` 9b and `gc/collection.test.ts` on `sweepTombstones`; NEW `corpus/sweeps.test.ts` (4 cases on the migrated copy, in `demand`: the load reads in full, the sweeps remove 225 tombstones and no live node, a second sweep finds nothing, the swept mirror loads again with nothing to sweep, `closeDb` drops the views).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R008",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The checks and timings, with the load**",
    "text": "**The checks and timings, with the load**: by the Coder, `tsc --noEmit` of `core`, `cli` and `web` clean; `essential` 74 of 74 in 2.9 s; `commit` 1049 of 1049 in 19.6 s (was 1032 in 20.0 s; load average 2.9 before, 2.3 after); `models` 187 of 187 in 13.4 s (was 186); `tools` 14 of 14 in 13.9 s; `--group corpus` 21 of 21 in 40.2 s (was 17: the 4 cases of `corpus/sweeps.test.ts`). By the orchestrator: `tsc` clean for `core`, `cli` and `web`; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.2 s; `commit` 1049 of 1049 in 21.2 s; `models` 187 of 187; `tools` 14 of 14; `--group corpus` 21 of 21; load 0.9 to 1.8; `aperas check-links` clean. The first `commit` run after the refusal cases failed once, on the Coder's own race (`service start says why` read a leftover `tsx` wrapper process a moment after the service had exited); the case now waits up to 5 s for the process list to empty, and three runs of the group passed after.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R009",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "00D80J973R009",
    "text": "**The 23 mutations**, applied by a scratch script (`/home/will/scratch/mut10/run.py`, each under `timeout 100` on `--group service,shell,mirror,gc,store`, the source restored after each, `git status` showing only staged files): 23 of 23 caught; 21 at the first run and 2 alive, (19) `flushAll` stopping at the first refusal and (23) the side copy written again though one exists, which got a case each (the main graph refused while the threads graph is flushed; the older copy under another stamp). Caught by: the old defect (`flushAll` writes the main graph only) 6 cases (flush, lifecycle, ops); `insertItem` and `removeItem` not touching the item's graph 20 and 3 seeds; `tombstone` touching its own graph only 9 seeds; a sweep touching always or never 19 and 21 cases; `sweepTombstones` on the main graph only 21; every timer at the first interval 3 (`flush.test.ts`, each waiting 5 s for the file); divergence ignored 7; the old store not freed 2; `closeDb` without the cross-list step 1; start-anyway copying nothing 4 and ignored by a reload 3; `skippedDocuments` ignoring errors 2; no boot sweep 3; the client not seeing the refusal 1; `changed` not cleared 5; the dangling warning removed 4; the boot accepting without the option 7; clobber skipping unwritten graphs 1; no sweep at shutdown 2.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80J973R00A",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
