    "title": "00D80J973R00A",
    "text": "**Decided on the Coder's five questions** (by the orchestrator, 2026-10-21, all as built): (1) `closeDb` drops the graphs that no pair of another graph points into (on the real mirror the views graph only, since the main and threads graphs have `Link` targets into each other; on the commands corpus and the fixtures all three), and the old handle is collected anyway: best effort, the log and the reload answer say how many graphs were freed. (2) The table of settings is read once at start from the configuration found walking up from the mirror's directory (the real `AperasKG/aperas.config.json` has no `graphs` key, so the intervals stay 10 s and 3 s); a change needs a restart. (3) The load's dangling ids are logged as one warning at start and at each reload, not a refusal. (4) The side copy is made when the load is accepted, which is earlier than any flush and cannot be forgotten by a code path; its name is `<file>.rejected-<UTC stamp>.json` next to the mirror file and in `.state/`, not written again if an equal copy exists; the side files are untracked files (the `.state/` ones are ignored by git, the main directory's are not); the flag name and the file name are in [Packaging — Design](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001), and the skills' service recipes (`references/mechanics.md`) do not yet mention the option: for the next skill release. (5) A removal in a thread rewrites the main graph's files at its next tick, as before: a tombstone, a removal and a sweep that removed something mark every graph, because they leave the lists of the other graphs and the `unfolds` of the views, and narrowing it needs the write layer to know the hosts of the node.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80J973R001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
