        "value": "1"
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Difference 1, an `update` of a thread node alone reaches `.state/`**",
    "text": "**Difference 1, an `update` of a thread node alone reaches `.state/`**: each graph has its own set of changed graphs filled by the write layer, its own divergence check and its own timer (`tree` 10 s, `threads.tree` and `treeviews` 3 s, from the table of settings, read once at start); the reference service set `dirty` only on `update`, so such an update reached no `.state/` file until something else marked the state dirty ([the issue](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001)). A main file changed outside refuses the main graph only, and the others are flushed; `flushAll` tries every graph and throws the first refusal after. Test: `service/flush.test.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 2, the sweeps are the engine's, and a stale unfold is no longer swept**",
    "text": "**Difference 2, the sweeps are the engine's, and a stale unfold is no longer swept**: `sweepTombstones` calls the engine's `sweep` for each graph; the sweep of the unfolds that name no node is gone (the engine drops an `unfolds` entry with its target, and the migration strips the ones that already dangle), so an unfold of an id no node has stays in the view's file; the boot, reload and stop log `Startup GC: cleaned N unreachable tombstone(s), M vacuous container(s).` with two counts (they had three); the reload result loses `prunedUnfolds`. Tests: `service/lifecycle.test.ts`, `store/views.test.ts` 9b.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR004",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "links": [
      {
        "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR004:links:Link:00D80JF2MR003",
        "@type": "Link",
        "target": "BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800B",
        "predicate": "[[wikilink]]",
        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR004:links:Link:00D80JF2MR003:props:StringProp:00D80JF2MR004",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "200"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Difference 3, a refused start says why at once**",
    "text": "**Difference 3, a refused start says why at once**: the client sees the lock cleared and reads the last `REFUSING TO START` line of `service.log`, instead of the 5 s \"did not become ready in time\" of [Difference 10 of the flip](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D7T3XZA800B). Test: `service/refusal.test.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR005",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
