        "props": [
          {
            "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR005:links:Link:00D80JF2MR005:props:StringProp:00D80JF2MR006",
            "@type": "StringProp",
            "key": "position",
            "value": "365"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "title": "**Difference 4, the start-anyway option and the side copy**",
    "text": "**Difference 4, the start-anyway option and the side copy**: `--start-anyway` of `aperas service start`, `service restart` and `aperas reload` accepts a load with `rejected` or `errors`, and the service copies the raw documents the load skipped to `<file>.rejected-<UTC stamp>.json` next to their file (in `.state/` too) when it accepts the load, before any flush ([the rule](../design/packaging.md#id/BlockNode:00D76B1ZTR001)); a copy equal to one already there is not written again. Tests: `service/refusal.test.ts`, `mirror/load.test.ts` (`skippedDocuments`).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR006",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Difference 5, a reload loads once and frees the old handle as far as the engine lets it**",
    "text": "**Difference 5, a reload loads once and frees the old handle as far as the engine lets it**: the probe load of `--discard` is gone (Difference 10 of the flip said a discard loads twice), and `closeDb` drops the old graphs that no remaining graph points into; the reload answers `freedGraphs` (the real mirror frees the views graph only, since the main and threads graphs have `Link` targets into each other). Tests: `shell/db.test.ts` (+4), `service/lifecycle.test.ts`, `corpus/sweeps.test.ts`.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JEFKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
