    "title": "**What the batch closes**",
    "text": "**What the batch closes**: resolved and moved to Resolved, each with a dated entry saying that the working service and `Aperas/` run the old code until the cutover: [every `Link` carries a `predicate`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3WNBPPG001) in the code of the shell (piece 1), [a move of a node after an anchor inside its own subtree](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D6HAEDCR001) (piece 6), [the tree view lists a block's links newest first](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZK7C8001), [`runPath` of a `Link` id throws](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D76KJ728001) and [`findByExactPath` takes the first node found at a path](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22ZMTKG001) (piece 7), [three behaviours of the caller depend on the order of an unordered read](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC800D) (piece 8), and, with piece 10, [no test calls most commands of the CLI or the service](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3YFXDC8001) and [the load computes `danglingRefs` and the service never reads it](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D258W098001). Left open, each with its dated entries: [the store is read outside the helpers](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D2536E1R001) (the shell's side closed by piece 6; the frozen set goes in Batch 12), [tombstoning does not empty the node at every site](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D252W7VG001) (the callers' share built; open for the 52 tombstones of the real mirror, migrated at the cutover, and for the reference copy, Batch 12), [the plain write on a tombstone](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D4T7JDAR001) (waits for Enforcement), [a write to a thread node never marks the `.state/` mirror dirty](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00CVNZXVR8001) (closed on the new engine by piece 10, open on the working service until the cutover, or until the user fixes it there) and the filed costs of [one `insert`](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D22Z1HJ8001) and of [a full-store scan](../issues/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D0W02KPG001), which are Batch 13's to judge.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JWQKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80JWQKR007",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**The reference-copy notes**",
    "text": "**The reference-copy notes**: until the cutover the working service and `Aperas/` keep the defects that the resolved issues record, because they run the old code: the first-match readers and the unsorted listings, the loop on a move into the node's own subtree, the missing `stateDirty` on an `update` of a thread node, and a reload that swaps the store without freeing the old one. The reference copy under `core/src/shell/` goes with the frozen set in Batch 12.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80JWQKR001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
