    "title": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**",
    "text": "**Resolved (2026-10-21)**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 10, in `Aperas.dev` (staged, not committed), built the reading: the service logs the load's `dangling` list (the engine's list for each graph plus the ids that a `parent` names with no document) as one warning at the start and at each reload, and nothing more, so a load is not refused for it (decided by the orchestrator on the Coder's question, as built); the real mirror has none today. With the sweep of the stale unfolds dropped, an unfold of an id no node has stays in the view's file (the Coder: \"stays in the view's file and is reported there\"). Test: `service/lifecycle.test.ts` (the dangling warning; the mutation that removes it is caught by 4 cases). The working service and `Aperas/` run the old code and still never read the list until the cutover.",
