    "title": "**Since (2026-10-21), closed on the new engine, open on the working service**",
    "text": "**Since (2026-10-21), closed on the new engine, open on the working service**: [Batch 11](../planning/core.md#id/BlockNode:00D3XQQ2W000C) piece 10, in `Aperas.dev` (staged, not committed), flushes each graph on its own flag: the write layer fills `Db.changed` with the graphs a write changed, and `service.ts` has one timer for each graph at the interval of the table of settings (`tree` 10 s, `threads.tree` and `treeviews` 3 s), with `flush: true` writing the changed graphs at once; the flags `dirty` and `stateDirty` are gone. `service/flush.test.ts` shows that an update of a thread node alone reaches `.state/BlockNode.jsonld` by its timer and by `flush: true`, with the other files' bytes and mtime unchanged (the mutation that keeps the old `flushAll` is caught by 6 cases). The working service and `Aperas/` run the old code, so the issue stays open there until the cutover, or until the user fixes it there; the workaround above stands for them.",
