    "title": "**The change**",
    "text": "**The change**: the manual links removed (piece 1); the tests of the reads, the writes, `track`, `project` and the service written on the old code before their groups moved (pieces 2 to 4: `commands/` 138 cases after piece 3, `service/` 66 cases after the follow-up of piece 4); the engine-side handle and the write layer beside the old code (piece 5); the flip, which ran the shell, the cli and the service on the `Db`, the maps and the write layer, kept the six old Oxigraph files frozen and guarded by a test, and made a move into the node's own subtree refused by the engine (piece 6); the callers on `liveAtPath` and the order rules (piece 7); the lookups of ingest, track and project (piece 8); the writes and tombstones, found almost all done by the flip (piece 9); the sweeps as the engine's `sweep` of each graph, one flush timer for each graph at its own interval, the `--start-anyway` option with a side copy of the skipped documents, and a reload that frees the old handle as far as the engine lets it (piece 10).",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80M96P8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
  },
  {
    "@id": "BlockNode:00D80M96P8003",
    "@type": "BlockNode",
    "title": "**Checked by the orchestrator**",
    "text": "**Checked by the orchestrator**: at the end `tsc` clean for `core`, `cli` and `web`; `essential` 74 of 74 in 3.2 s (budget 5 s); `commit` 1049 of 1049 in 21.2 s (budget 60 s; 19.6 s by the Coder); `models` 187 of 187; `tools` 14 of 14; `--group corpus` 21 of 21; load 0.9 to 1.8. The mutation checks of pieces 2 to 10 (17, 23, 9, 24, 12, 21, 22, 11 and 23 mutations) caught all but three: one of piece 3 that no command can show, and one equivalent mutant each in pieces 5 and 8.",
    "parent": "BlockNode:00D80M96P8001",
    "type": "listItem",
    "children": []
